const CHAPTER_DESIGN = {
 0:{ title:'Tribute', type:'Opening Cinematic / Story Introduction', loc:'🏝 Tribute Island · 🏯 Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade Gold (introduction — the player does not control her yet)',
  introduced:['Jade Gold','King Greyson','Xima','Sage of Tribute'],
  sum:'Far across the eastern seas lies Tribute, a hidden island of cliffs, waterfalls and ancient mysteries, once a peaceful land of scholars and healers. Half a century ago the witch Xima cast a terrible curse upon it, and from her hatred sprang fifteen demonic evils that brought destruction, suffering and despair. Two years after ascending the throne, young King Greyson has gathered allies and restored the island\'s strength, and decides he can wait no longer: he summons Jade Gold. Jade was born beneath a lunar eclipse, carries the blood of the sword-bearing Gold family and the legacy of her mother Valor, a powerful psychic. She can see beyond the veil, sense spirits and withstand forces that would destroy others, which is why the evils fear her. The Sage of Tribute tells her a prophecy: a woman and two men will come to save the island, and their fates are bound with hers. Greyson gives her the mission to find the fifteen evils and end their torment.',
  art:'Artwork also shows: Jade is the youngest daughter of the Imperial Advisor family and grew up beside the crown prince, whom she treated as an older brother; she nearly drowned at ten, trained in martial arts, returned from the mountains at nineteen, and Greyson names her Imperial Guard before the court.',
  quote:'"The first test is love. Until you learn how to love, you cannot ascend." — the Sage of Tribute',
  events:['Tribute Island introduction','Xima\'s curse explained (fifteen evils)','King Greyson prepares retaliation','Jade\'s bloodline revealed (lunar eclipse, Gold family, mother Valor)','Sage\'s prophecy revealed (a woman and two men will come)','Jade receives her mission: find the fifteen evils and end their torment','Greyson gives Jade a dagger and a flail (she may not use them until the major battle)'],
  purpose:['Opening cinematic, about 5–8 minutes, before the player gains control of Jade','Introduce the world of Tribute and Xima\'s curse','Set up King Greyson\'s mission and Jade\'s destiny'],
  unlocks:['World Map','Main Quest','Jade Character Profile','Codex System'],
  reward:'Jade Gold joins the journey · Greyson\'s dagger and flail (kept, not yet usable)'},
 1:{ title:'The Recruitment Scroll', type:'Character Introduction / Recruitment Chapter', loc:'🏙 Tribute Capital — city streets, recruitment office, Jade\'s office',
  chars:['chad','sky'], charsNote:'Chad and Sky (playable) · Jade Gold (guest, first appears at the end of the chapter)',
  introduced:['Roc Chadwick (Chad): born Roc Chadstone, a prince of a faraway state who left his palace; living as a commoner, skilled fighter seeking purpose and adventure','Sky Yale: Chad\'s companion, found injured at sea with no memory of his past (a letter from his master and a jade pendant engraved with his mother\'s name); hardworking farmer, optimistic and adaptable','Jade Gold: first appearance at the end of the chapter'],
  sum:'Narrated by Chad. One year after he and Sky arrived on Tribute, he remembers how it began. Chad was born a prince of a faraway state, but his mother was of low status, so he was despised by his half-siblings and oppressed by palace rules. He left the suffocating palace, abandoned his birth name Roc Chadstone and took the name Roc Chadwick, boarding a small boat called the Explorer. Not long after setting sail he found Sky in the sea, severely injured and barely alive, and nursed him back to health with a skilled physician in a remote port town. Sky woke with no memories; the only things he had were a letter from his master and a jade pendant engraved with his mother\'s name. They decided to sail to Tribute to search for the truth about Sky\'s origins, crossed oceans and storms, and passed through a tunnel of light to the hidden island. After arriving, Chad and Sky live as commoners for a year, without noble titles or special privileges, slowly building a new life. Sky proves surprisingly capable at farm work and wins the locals\' trust. Chad finds steady work as an accountant at a local shop, but the ordinary routine leaves his restless heart longing for adventure. One day Chad travels to the capital looking for opportunities and finds a recruitment scroll: "Mercenaries Wanted". An anonymous employer seeks two capable individuals for a journey. It is vague but intriguing, and Chad decides to investigate, planning to bring Sky along if the job seems suitable. He follows the address to a small, respectable office guarded by two potted plants and a Kirin statue. Inside, the room is elegant, feminine and filled with foreign touches, and Chad realises his employer is a woman. Behind the curtains stands Jade Gold, the legendary daughter of Tribute, who calmly asks: "So, I presume you are here for the job?"',
  art:'Pages show: the chapter is narrated by Chad in the first person, speaking to Sky; the opening page gives the backstory (the Explorer, the tunnel of light, Sky\'s amnesia); Sky also grows bored of repetitive field work; Chad\'s voice recognises something familiar in Jade\'s, and the chapter ends on his line "It\'s you…".',
  quote:'"So, I presume you are here for the job?" — Jade Gold',
  events:['Backstory: Chad leaves his palace as Roc Chadstone and becomes Roc Chadwick','Chad rescues Sky at sea; Sky has lost his memories','They sail through a tunnel of light to Tribute, to search for the truth about Sky\'s origins','Chad and Sky\'s life on Tribute is established (one year as commoners)','Chad feels restless with ordinary life','Recruitment scroll discovered in the capital','Chad accepts the mysterious job offer','Chad arrives at Jade\'s office','First meeting between Chad and Jade'],
  purpose:['Introduce Chad and Sky before they meet Jade, and establish their life on Tribute','Begin the journey that brings them to Jade; set up the first party formation','Tutorial exploration, character introduction, first quest acceptance','Suggested: a flashback/tutorial. Play as Chad and Sky, then the camera switches to Jade at the end ("these are the people who answered Jade Gold\'s call")'],
  unlocks:['Chad profile','Sky profile','Main quest begins'],
  reward:'Chad and Sky profiles revealed (they join the party later)'},
 2:{ title:'The Mercenary Trial', type:'Story Chapter (Jade\'s point of view) — interview and trial setup', loc:'🏙 Jade\'s office → ⚔ Imperial Training Grounds (behind the palace office)',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade Gold (the chapter is narrated by Jade) · Chad (appears opposite her; Sky does not appear)',
  introduced:['Imperial Guards at the Training Grounds, who greet her as "Lady Jade"'],
  sum:'Told from Jade\'s point of view, picking up as Chad stands frozen in her office. Jade reads his shock: unlike most people, who stare at her appearance, status and reputation, he looks genuinely stunned. She decides to see what kind of man he is. Chad apologises: she reminds him of someone he knows. He says he is here for the mercenary position and is ready to be tested at any time, and Jade has him fill in paperwork first. His form reads: Name Chad, Age 21, Martial Arts Experience 15 years, practising since he was six. Jade suspects he may still be lying, as there are too many mysteries around him, but sets that aside: actions speak louder than words. She tells him that if he can parry three blows from her, she will take him on as her personal attendant. He follows without protest, his composure either genuine or very well practised. At the training grounds behind the palace office, where the Imperial Guards and younger recruits train every day, Jade explains she is skilled in archery and prefers weapons that give her distance, such as whips and spears; direct close combat is not her strength, so she relies on speed, precision and control of the battlefield. She changes into her Imperial Guard uniform, a reminder of who she must be: no more the sheltered daughter, a blade of the kingdom. The guards greet her formally and she answers with a polite, distant smile. She tells Chad to pick up a weapon. As he walks to the weapon rack, calm and observant, she watches him closely: three blows, to see what he is truly made of, Roc Chadwick.',
  art:'Pages show: no fight happens in this chapter. The sparring is only set up on the last page, and Sky does not appear. Jade already uses his full name, Roc Chadwick, although the form says only "Chad". Jade\'s own weapons here are archery, whips and spears.',
  quote:'"If you can parry three blows from me, then I will consider taking you on as my personal attendant." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Jade reads Chad\'s reaction to meeting her','Chad says she reminds him of someone he knows','Chad fills in the paperwork: Chad, 21, 15 years of martial arts since age six','Jade sets the Three Blows test: parry three blows and become her personal attendant','They go to the Imperial Training Grounds','Jade explains her fighting style and puts on her Imperial Guard uniform','Chad takes a weapon; the spar is about to begin'],
  purpose:['Show the first meeting from Jade\'s side and establish her public persona versus her private thoughts','Establish Jade\'s combat style (distance, speed, precision, control)','Set up the Three Blows duel, which plays out in the next chapter','Suggested: no combat here. Use the story popup, then hand off to the duel in Chapter 3'],
  unlocks:['Imperial Training Grounds (story scene)'],
  reward:'Story progress to the Three Blows duel'},
 3:{ title:'Three Blows', type:'Story Chapter (mostly Chad\'s point of view) — duel and hiring', loc:'⚔ Imperial Training Grounds → 🏙 Jade\'s office',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Chad (narrator) and Jade Gold · Sky is only mentioned',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'At the lively Training Grounds, Chad watches Jade take her stance with no hesitation and no recognition in her eyes, and wonders whether she truly has no memory of the past. He and Jade have met twice before: first at a crowded market, where they argued over the last chicken, and then over a job she wanted and he took, when she told him "I hate you to the core of my heart". Now she looks at him like a stranger, and he decides it may be a blessing: this time he might get on her good side before she has another reason to hate him. Jade shouts "Make your move now!" and is beaten in seconds. "That didn\'t count! Let\'s have another go!" In the rematch she vows not to hold back, but Chad moves too fast for her to follow and locks her acupoints. He tells her she only needs to acknowledge him as her hired mercenary and promises that his partner and he will protect her during her mission. She agrees ("You have my word") and he releases her. Back at the office Jade prepares a special pass that lets Chad and Sky Yale enter the restricted area of the city, tells Chad to perform up to standards, and orders them back in three days to be briefed; the Imperial Guards have no tolerance for lateness and will revoke the passes. When Chad flirts, she slaps him. "I\'ll be early," he says, and leaps over the wall, thinking this was only the beginning between them.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade is drawn with a sword at first and then a whip (the author\'s intent is whip and bow; the comic later gives her a dagger and flail); Chad wins both bouts (the first in seconds), the second by locking her acupoints, so it is not literally three blows. Jade has not met Sky yet ("your friend too, whatever his name is").',
  quote:'"Miss Gold, you just need to acknowledge me as your hired mercenary." — Chad',
  events:['Jade and Chad\'s duel at the Training Grounds (Chad wins in seconds)','Jade demands a rematch; Chad locks her acupoints','Jade acknowledges Chad as her hired mercenary','Chad\'s memories of their two earlier meetings (the chicken, the job)','Jade prepares a special pass for Chad and Sky Yale (restricted area of the city)','Briefing set for three days later; punctuality warning','Chad flirts, is slapped, and leaps over the wall'],
  purpose:['First fight: a story duel, Jade vs Chad. Defeat does not block progress, since Chad wins in the story','Establish the Jade and Chad dynamic: hidden history, her apparent amnesia, his flirting','Chad is hired; set up the briefing with Chad and Sky'],
  unlocks:['Combat: first duel','Chad hired as Jade\'s mercenary','Restricted-area pass (Chad and Sky)'],
  reward:'Chad hired; special pass issued'},
 4:{ title:'A Secret Mission', type:'Story Chapter — the secret mission is offered', loc:'🏯 Imperial Training Grounds → Jade\'s office',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad and Sky (Jade\'s point of view)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Three days pass in a blink. Jade throws herself into drilling the junior guards, pushing them harder than ever ("An Imperial Guard must be ready at all times!"). A guard tells her the two men she mentioned have arrived an hour early. She dismisses training and lets them in. In her office Chad introduces himself and "my friend and sworn brother Sky". Jade checks that no one is around, bolts the main door and the back exit, and warns them the mission is extremely important and perilous: there may be no one alive to tell of it. She does not want cowards who will run halfway, and gives them one last chance to refuse, because once she explains it she cannot let them leave. Sky answers "We are in." Chad promises he will do a good job: "it\'s a man\'s part to keep his woman safe". Jade, furious, thinks: "I want to kill him right now!!!"',
  art:'Pages show: Jade drills the guards with a sword here, so the comic art mixes her weapons. Chad and Sky arrive an hour early, which fits the punctuality warning from Chapter 3. This is the first time Jade and Sky meet in the story\'s present.',
  quote:'"I do not want cowards who will run halfway through." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Three days pass; Jade trains the junior guards hard','Chad and Sky arrive an hour early','Chad introduces Sky as his friend and sworn brother','Jade seals her office and gives them a last chance to refuse','Chad and Sky accept: "We are in"','Chad flirts; Jade is furious'],
  purpose:['Secret mission offered and accepted: the party forms','Show Jade as drill leader of the junior guards','Set up the briefing in Chapter 5'],
  unlocks:['Party formation: Jade, Chad and Sky','Main quest: the secret mission'],
  reward:'Chad and Sky join the mission'},
 5:{ title:'Unanswered Ties', type:'Story Chapter — briefing and a hint about Sky\'s past', loc:'🏯 Jade\'s office → 🌸 flower garden, about ten li from the office',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad and Sky (Jade\'s point of view)',
  introduced:['Yvette Sue (named by Sky as his mother; mentioned only)'],
  sum:'Jade finishes the briefing, pointing to a map unrolled before them. She pays extreme attention to the fifteen territories, the demonic presence in each, their behaviours and the measures needed. Chad sits on the floor, coolly watching her with no trace of seriousness, and getting furious at him is meaningless. Sky says, as his brother said, they will keep her safe. When Chad touches her she snaps "Get your filthy hands off me!" Sky then asks if she still remembers him: back at the cemetery, at his mother\'s grave, Yvette Sue. Jade realises "So, it\'s you" and asks how he can be sure Yvette Sue is his mother. Sky admits he does not know if he is her son: he lost his memory, and all he has is a jade pendant. They go to a flower garden about ten li from the office to talk privately. Footsteps reveal someone eavesdropping; Jade rushes after the person and finds Chad ("Bud, what are you doing here?"). His face is expressionless and he strides away without a word, puzzling Jade further.',
  art:'Page redrawn so the pendant matches chapter 94: a light green jade pendant. Pages show: Sky\'s jade pendant, first seen in Chapter 1, comes up again, and Sky and Jade have a past meeting at a cemetery that Jade remembers and Sky is asking about. Chad overhears part of their talk.',
  quote:'"I\'m wondering if you still remember me, Miss Gold." — Sky Yale',
  events:['Jade briefs them using a map of the fifteen territories','Jade, annoyed by Chad, rebuffs him','Sky asks if Jade remembers him from the cemetery (his mother\'s grave, Yvette Sue)','Sky says he lost his memory and only has a jade pendant','Jade finds Chad eavesdropping; he walks away without a word'],
  purpose:['Explain the main quest: fifteen territories, fifteen demonic evils','Seed Sky\'s mystery and the Jade and Sky link'],
  unlocks:['World map briefing: the fifteen territories','Relationship tension: Jade × Chad, Jade × Sky'],
  reward:'Briefing completed'},
 6:{ title:'Moonlit Confessions', type:'Story Chapter (Chad\'s point of view) — night training', loc:'🏕 Mercenaries\' quarters → ⚔ Training grounds under a full moon',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Chad (narrator) and Jade',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Chad cannot sleep in the stiff bed of the mercenaries\' quarters, still seeing Sky and Jade together in the flower garden. He walks the camp under a full moon and hears metal clinking at the training grounds: Jade stands firm in a martial stance, practising deep into the night. He offers to help and guides her into position; after some hesitation they spar together in the moonlight. She asks why he is so kind, and he answers "Because you are my employer." She misses a step and he catches her before she hits the ground. Then he asks: "Miss Gold, are you in love with my brother?" Jade, gasping, breaks away and runs off, saying "I… I don\'t know." Chad watches her vanish and wonders what just happened.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade here practises with a chain-like whip, in a red-and-white outfit. Chad refers to Sky as his brother again.',
  quote:'"Miss Gold, are you in love with my brother?" — Chad',
  events:['Chad cannot sleep after seeing Sky and Jade in the garden','Chad finds Jade practising at night','Chad guides her stance and they spar under the moon','Chad catches Jade when she stumbles','Chad asks if she loves Sky; Jade flees: "I don\'t know"'],
  purpose:['Develop the Jade and Chad dynamic through a night training scene','Suggested: a light sparring or training scene, a chance for bond points'],
  unlocks:['Relationship events (Chad)'],
  reward:'Bond scene: moonlit training'},
 7:{ title:'Restless Desire', type:'Story Chapter — Jade\'s restless night and a vision', loc:'🏕 Jade\'s quarters → 🛁 bath chamber',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade closes the door behind her, trying not to be daunted by the pounding in her chest. The man she claims to detest has that effect on her, and she cannot understand why. She reminds herself she is Jade Gold, the future Imperial Advisor and currently the only female Imperial Guard, and cannot let emotions take over. She reminds herself of her engagement to Levi Stanson and imagines him, but also worries he might judge her for who she is. Unable to sleep, she sneaks out to the quiet bath chamber, whose water has rejuvenating properties, adding herbs and lavender. As she relaxes, a vision appears: people running and screaming, pursued by green-coloured creatures, blood painting the scene red. She screams, moves too fast to the deep end of the tub and begins to drown.',
  art:'Pages show: future Imperial Advisor and the only female Imperial Guard are both Jade\'s titles here. The vision shows green-skinned demonic creatures attacking people, a first look at the kind of evil she must fight.',
  quote:'',
  events:['Jade tries to sort out her feelings for Chad','She recalls her engagement to Levi Stanson','Jade sneaks out to the bath chamber','A vision shows people attacked by green demonic creatures','She panics and begins to drown'],
  purpose:['Establish Jade\'s inner conflict: Chad versus her engagement to Levi','First vision of the fifteen evils at work'],
  unlocks:['Vision events (first vision)'],
  reward:'Vision scene: the demon attack'},
 8:{ title:'Unwanted Truths', type:'Story Chapter — a rescue and a painful truth', loc:'🛁 Bath chamber → Jade\'s chamber',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:['The goddess Miyu (Jade prays to her; mentioned only)'],
  sum:'Panicking underwater, Jade silently prays to the goddess Miyu. Two hands appear and someone lifts her to safety. When she comes to, her rescuer is the man she detests, Chad. He tells her to stay away from deep water if she cannot swim, and she asks if he is only here to blame her. He kisses her; her heart pounds and her body trembles. When he reaches for her garment she stops him, since the island\'s strict traditions forbid such actions between men and women. She asks whether he dressed her and saw everything; he says he had to save her and asks her to call him Chad. She tells him to get out, threatening to rip his tongue out if he ever tells a soul. Chad asks whether she has really forgotten what happened between them three months ago, then says they first met at the market, fighting over a chicken. Jade says she remembers the chicken but not him. She races to her chamber, bolts the door and breaks down in tears.',
  art:'Pages show: Chad says something happened between them three months earlier, which Jade does not remember. This is the clearest hint so far of the history Chad mentioned in Chapter 3. Chad later lies about it in Chapter 11.',
  quote:'"I remember the chicken, but I don\'t remember you." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Jade prays to the goddess Miyu as she drowns','Chad rescues her','Chad kisses her; Jade stops him, citing the island\'s traditions','Jade threatens him to keep quiet','Chad says they first met at the market, and something happened three months ago','Jade does not remember him; she breaks down in tears alone'],
  purpose:['Deepen the Jade and Chad history and her conflict','Island tradition: strict rules between men and women'],
  unlocks:['Relationship events (Chad)','Story choices (suggested)'],
  reward:'Story: Chad\'s secret revealed'},
 9:{ title:'Whispers and Jealousy', type:'Story Chapter (Chad\'s point of view) — the king arrives', loc:'🏯 Palace hall → 🌸 flower garden',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Chad (narrator), Jade, Sky and King Greyson',
  introduced:['King Greyson in person (first scene with the party)'],
  sum:'Chad, dressed in the magnificent mercenary robes provided by the Guard, cannot stop thinking about the night before. Sky looks cheerful and says Jade is the only woman he wants to spend his entire life with; Chad hopes his sworn brother is not serious. Jade appears bored, fidgeting with her plaits, unbothered by the king\'s lateness. King Greyson arrives, everyone kneels, and he helps Jade to her feet. He assigns them their duties and official passes for travel across the region. After a tea break the king and Jade head to the flower garden. Tired of waiting, Chad slips away with his martial arts and hides behind the shrubs to listen. Greyson asks whether Jade is confident, and she says the problem is Stanson: she does not know how long she can wait, whether she can keep herself pure for him, or whether she will return alive. She asks Greyson to keep it a secret. He offers to revoke the arrangement made between their families, and asks if she is afraid of dying or if Stanson is not what she wants him to be. Chad is relieved the king is not a threat but his heart tightens at the mention of Stanson: if her fiancé appeared, would she obey the arrangement set by the elders?',
  art:'Pages show: Greyson and Jade are close, as the Prologue art suggested. The king recommends Chad because he beat Jade in sparring, as he did in Chapter 3. Jade\'s fiancé is called Stanson here.',
  quote:'',
  events:['Chad and Sky dress as mercenaries; Sky declares his feelings for Jade','King Greyson arrives and assigns their duties and official travel passes','Greyson and Jade talk privately in the flower garden','Jade confides her worry about Stanson and the mission; Greyson offers to revoke the engagement','Chad eavesdrops behind the shrubs'],
  purpose:['Establish Greyson\'s mission and the travel passes','Reveal Jade\'s engagement and her fears about the mission'],
  unlocks:['Official passes for travel across the region'],
  reward:'Duties and passes from King Greyson'},
 10:{ title:'The Prophecy', type:'Story Chapter — the prophecy explained', loc:'🏯 Imperial Palace (Greyson\'s audience), altar',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky and King Greyson',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The three listen to King Greyson recount the island\'s history, most of which Chad already knows while Sky struggles to follow. Jade finds herself staring at Chad and stops when he notices. After the incident last night she is unsure whether she still hates him; the memory of their intimacy lingers and she feels butterflies when he approaches. Jade rejects Greyson\'s offer to break her engagement: she must honour the promise her family made, even if her future with Stanson is hazy. At the altar she lights incense for him. Greyson tells them that fifty years ago, after the curse laid on the island by the witch concubine Xima, his great-grandfather sent for ascetics and hermits, but they found no solution. Then, nineteen years ago on the fifteenth lunar day of the ghost month, a prophecy was told: two men from a different world and a woman of extraordinary abilities will save Tribute from disaster. That is the true reason for the trip: the three are to go down and eliminate as many of Xima\'s evil underlings as they can in fifteen territories around the island. The date is Jade\'s birthday; she is nineteen this year. She asks whether the prophecy concerns her. She realises this is a suicide mission whose outcome depends on how paramount their lives are, and as the destined Imperial Advisor she accepts, but she is human and afraid of death.',
  art:'Pages show: Xima is described as a witch concubine from Greyson\'s great-grandfather\'s time. The prophecy names two men from a different world, which fits Chad and Sky arriving through the tunnel of light in Chapter 1.',
  quote:'"The prophecy told of two men from a different world, and a woman of unordinary abilities." — King Greyson',
  events:['Greyson recounts the island\'s history','Jade refuses to break her engagement','Greyson explains the prophecy from nineteen years ago (Jade\'s birthday)','The mission: eliminate Xima\'s underlings in fifteen territories','Jade realises it may be a suicide mission'],
  purpose:['Lore chapter: Xima, the curse and the prophecy explained','Give the party its purpose: fifteen territories'],
  unlocks:['Codex entries: Xima, the prophecy','Main quest: the fifteen territories'],
  reward:'Codex: Xima and the prophecy'},
 11:{ title:'Dreams and Doubts', type:'Story Chapter — the journey begins; a dream', loc:'🚗 Carriage on the road to Faepool',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade (the carriage), Chad',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Two days later Jade looks back as the Guard\'s office vanishes from sight. Their first destination is Faepool, a village closest to the city. Absorbed in her thoughts, she is brought back when Chad takes the seat beside her and brushes her cheek: she has been silent for six hours and should drink some water. She hesitates, then accepts his waterskin; a sip leads to a mouthful and she soon falls into a deep sleep. In her dream she sees a village razed to the ground and a witch in a purple robe laughing, not hideous but seductive and powerful. The witch shows her a memory of her and Chad in the bath chamber, and an even more intimate image from her lewd dreams. She says Jade craves intense pleasure but ties herself to a hopeless engagement, that they have all lied to her, and offers to make her her successor, to impart power and knowledge. Someone calls her name and the carriage returns. Chad says she was mumbling strange words. She asks why he did that in the bath chamber; Chad says he does not remember any bath chamber and has never seen her there (a lie: he did rescue her in Chapter 8). She realises that, lusting after him, she may have mistaken someone else for him while dazed. Chad says it is his duty and promise to protect her; the rest of the day she is silent, in despair for the first time.',
  art:'Pages show: the witch in the dream is not named on the page. The denial of the bath chamber by Chad is a lie to cover that he rescued her in Chapter 8; Jade, believing it, concludes she mistook someone else for him. Their first destination is Faepool, a village near the city.',
  quote:'"Surrender to me, Jade Gold. I will make you my next successor." — the witch in Jade\'s dream',
  events:['The party leaves the capital by carriage; first destination Faepool','Chad gives Jade a waterskin and she falls into a deep sleep','Dream: a razed village and a seductive witch who offers Jade power','Jade wakes; Chad lies and denies any bath chamber incident','Jade realises she may have mistaken someone else for Chad'],
  purpose:['Start the journey; first dream-vision encounter with the witch','Dramatic irony: the player knows Chad is lying about the bath-chamber rescue'],
  unlocks:['World map travel (carriage)','Dream events'],
  reward:'Travel begins: carriage to Faepool'},
 12:{ title:'Shadows at the Inn', type:'Story Chapter (Chad\'s point of view) — a night at the inn', loc:'🏚 Inn near the Tribute–Faepool border',
  chars:['chad','jade','sky'], charsNote:'Chad (narrator) with Jade and Sky',
  introduced:['Levi Stanson (first appearance)'],
  sum:'The carriage stops at an inn near the border of Tribute and Faepool, where they stay the night before resuming their journey. Chad takes the lead and selects two spacious rooms on the top floor; he drove the carriage the last two days to give Sky and Jade some private time. That evening Jade and Sky have a heartfelt talk and she gives him an encouraging smile and a clenched fist. Chad watches from a distance, his heart heavy. Deep in the night he cannot sleep and overhears the innkeeper\'s men leering about a beautiful woman on the top floor. Soon after, a dark figure moves lightly to the upper level. Chad quietly checks each room until he reaches Jade\'s; after three knocks with no answer he casts a small gust of wind and the door opens with a creak. Inside, a man in black stands over the bed while Jade sleeps, unaware. He removes his scarf: it is Levi Stanson, incredibly handsome, with a long scar across his face. A tattoo on his back bearing a character confirms Chad\'s suspicion. Levi freezes, captivated by Jade\'s beauty, and whispers "Jade…"',
  art:'Pages show: Chad can use a small gust of wind. Levi Stanson, Jade\'s fiancé, is the intruder, with a long facial scar and a tattoo of the character 郎 on his back.',
  quote:'"Jade…" — Levi Stanson',
  events:['The party stops at an inn near the Tribute–Faepool border','Chad rents two rooms and watches Jade and Sky talk','Chad overhears the innkeeper\'s men leering at a woman on the top floor','A dark figure enters Jade\'s room; Chad opens the door with a gust of wind','The intruder is Levi Stanson, with a facial scar and a tattoo'],
  purpose:['Introduce Levi Stanson, Jade\'s fiancé, at the inn','Set up the incident at the inn in the next chapter'],
  unlocks:['Levi Stanson introduced','Inn location unlocked'],
  reward:'Levi Stanson appears'},
 13:{ title:'Uninvited Encounter', type:'Story Chapter — fight at the inn', loc:'🏚 The inn (Jade\'s room)',
  chars:['chad','jade'], charsNote:'Chad (narrator) and Jade',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Chad opens the door on the intruder, sword drawn: "Who the hell are you?" The man answers "I am the Hero of the Night." Levi calls out and inn employees rush up from downstairs ("There he is! Catch him!"). Chad pulls the blanket over Jade to protect her modesty and fights off the whole wave with his sword. When the clash ends Levi has already escaped into the night. Chad returns to Jade, who is still asleep, and smells the faint scent of a drug in the air. He uses his internal energy to draw the drug\'s effects out of her body. Jade slowly wakes, dazed: "...Chad? Please... stay with me." He stays, conflicted but protective. Unsure if it is a dream, she asks if he is really there; he pinches her cheek and she realises it is real.',
  art:'Pages show: Chad can draw a drug out of someone\'s body with his internal energy. Levi, calling himself the Hero of the Night, escapes by leaping out of the window; the inn\'s own employees attack Chad.',
  quote:'"I am the Hero of the Night." — the intruder',
  events:['Chad confronts the intruder in Jade\'s room','Inn employees attack; Chad fights them off with his sword','Levi escapes into the night','Chad draws the drug out of Jade with his internal energy','Jade wakes and asks him to stay'],
  purpose:['Story fight: Chad against the inn\'s employees','Show Chad\'s protective side and his internal energy'],
  unlocks:['Combat: Chad solo fight'],
  reward:'Story: the inn incident'},
 14:{ title:'Unwanted Choices', type:'Story Chapter — the morning after, and an ultimatum', loc:'🏚 Inn room',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade wakes in an unfamiliar room, the words "It\'s not a dream" repeating in her mind, and asks what happened and why Chad is in her room. He asks if she remembers what she asked of him and whether she is already going back on her words. She recalls ordering the most potent wine and finishing half a pot before losing consciousness. Chad explains the inn workers drugged the wine, targeting travellers who stayed the night; she was not the only victim. A memory returns: a pigeon with Greyson\'s emblem and a note: "Jade, I have found that Stanson is dead and therefore the engagement is revoked with further effect. — Greyson". She should feel relieved but feels uncertain. Sky has confessed his admiration, but they might be cousins, and their bloodlines cannot be bound together; she is not sure of her feelings. Chad tells her she must choose between Sky and him, or her betrothed. She says she does not want to decide; he threatens she will suffer by his hand and offers to show her what a secret employer and mercenary relationship is like: be his discreet lover and he promises to satisfy her to the fullest. If she refuses he cannot promise her secret is safe. Jade asks for time, since neither of them is thinking clearly under the drug, and if Sky finds out she is in a woman\'s room, things will get complicated. He gives her three days to accept or decline. After he leaves, her secret is the least of her worries; the witch\'s words echo in her mind, compelling her for an answer.',
  art:'Pages show: Greyson\'s message arrives by pigeon, which fits the pigeon post. Levi Stanson is reported dead and the engagement revoked. Jade believes she and Sky might be cousins. Her "secret" is her relationship with her aunt, hinted again in chapter 16.',
  quote:'"You need to make a choice. Between Sky and me. Or your betrothed." — Chad',
  events:['Jade wakes after the drugged wine','A pigeon from Greyson reports Stanson\'s death and revokes the engagement','Jade is torn between duty, Sky and Chad','Chad gives her three days to accept or decline his offer'],
  purpose:['Resolve the engagement and raise the stakes of Jade\'s choice','Introduce the three-day deadline'],
  unlocks:['Dialogue choices and relationship changes (suggested)'],
  reward:'Engagement revoked; a decision looms'},
 15:{ title:'The Storm Within', type:'Story Chapter — the boat', loc:'🏚 Empty inn → ⚓ harbour → ⛵ blue boat (sea)',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad and Sky (Jade\'s point of view)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade wakes with a troubled mind. Sky hugs her, saying he was worried, and she notes that the inn was a dark inn. She wonders who bears such a grudge against her, and why it happened right after the news of Levi\'s death. Unable to find clues, they leave the empty inn and head to the harbour. Jade looks at her reflection and wonders if she is suitable to become an advisor, or if someone is trying to bring her down. Chad sits beside her and asks what she thinks of his offer; she says she is pleased Sky rejected him but "it\'s his decision". Sky returns with a blue-painted boat arranged by Greyson. The cabin fits only two, so Sky insists on sitting outside because he gets seasick. Jade finds it strange that Sky has a remedy for seasickness, something no physician in Tribute possessed, and wonders where Chad is from. In the cabin she draws the curtain and asks Chad if he is from the island; he says he is from Lingering Vale. He asks her to choose not because of pressure but because it is what she truly wants. Outside, Sky looks at the darkening sky: he never suffered from seasickness, he only wanted Chad and Jade to speak honestly. Inside, Jade stares at the storm, knowing the greatest battle ahead is understanding her own heart.',
  art:'Pages show: Chad says he is from Lingering Vale. The blue boat is arranged by Greyson. Sky\'s seasickness is a ruse. Chad\'s offer is turned from an ultimatum into a request that she choose freely.',
  quote:'"I want you to choose because it is what you truly want." — Chad',
  events:['Jade questions who targeted her at the dark inn','The party leaves for the harbour','Greyson arranges a blue boat; Sky stays on deck','Jade asks Chad where he is from; he answers Lingering Vale','Sky reveals he faked his seasickness'],
  purpose:['Introduce sea travel by boat','Seed the mystery of Chad\'s origin (Lingering Vale)'],
  unlocks:['Boat travel unlocked'],
  reward:'Sea voyage begins'},
 16:{ title:'The First Village', type:'Story Chapter — arrival in Faepool and the festival', loc:'⛵ Sea → 🌊 Faepool → 🏘 Vigil Village',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade (also Chad, Sky, Sally)',
  introduced:['Sally (first appearance: seen at Chad\'s side in Vigil)'],
  sum:'They journey by sea for three days. On the second night Sky takes Chad\'s place in the cabin and confesses to her again, for the third time; Jade is exhausted and must reject him without hurting his feelings, and still cannot reveal her relationship with her aunt. That night she dreams of the ancient evil again, as a reminder of the message she had received. She wonders why her, her lusty nature or something more, and notes all her memories beyond a certain age are a blur. After three days they arrive at Faepool: a group of forest-filled, very traditional villages, quiet, but Jade feels something is wrong and her clairvoyance reveals nothing, as if a force is blocking her vision. To reach Frog Mahan they must pass through the forest on foot, which could take at least three weeks, and Greyson will send updates and instructions through his pet pigeon. The Shaman had told her about her tribulation, the test of love; she cannot see herself as someone full of love, but perhaps when the time is right she will have answers. During their stay in Vigil, Chad is noticeably absent, spending time with the villagers, especially a woman named Sally who often appears by his side; the more Jade sees them together, the more it bothers her. That night a festival is held where young single women choose their husbands, a Vigil tradition. Jade buys a traditional dress in red with thick red threads, and the proprietress asks if she has someone in mind: "No, I am still single." Girls toss blossoms of different colours at their chosen groom, blue being the highest caste. After two hours many girls leave hand in hand with partners. A boy in blue, not more than thirteen, hands her a message, and without thinking she heads to the address.',
  art:'Pages show: the Shaman (told her of the test of love) is the Sage from the Prologue, and the target is Frog Mahan. Jade\'s aunt is the secret. The boy in blue also appears in Chapter 17.',
  quote:'"No, I am still single." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Three days at sea; Sky confesses to Jade a third time','Arrival in Faepool; Jade\'s clairvoyance is blocked','The party must reach Frog Mahan on foot (about three weeks)','Chad spends time with Sally','The Vigil festival: single women choose husbands','A young boy gives Jade a message'],
  purpose:['Introduce Faepool and Vigil Village, and the festival','Establish the Frog Mahan objective and Greyson\'s pet pigeon updates','Introduce Sally'],
  unlocks:['New region: Faepool','Village exploration, local NPCs, regional quest board (suggested)'],
  reward:'Faepool reached'},
 17:{ title:'A Choice Beneath the Lanterns', type:'Story Chapter — the lanterns', loc:'🏮 Vigil festival → isolated hut beyond the eastern path',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:['The boy in blue (messenger)'],
  sum:'The Vigil festival continues into the night. The boy tells Jade someone is waiting for her at the address, and the note reads "Come to the old hut beyond the eastern path. — C." Curious, with a troubled heart, she goes. On the outskirts she spots Chad with Sally, follows them to an isolated hut and sees Chad hand Sally a silver nugget ("Thank you, Lord Chad! You are always so kind."). Sally leaves with a smile. Chad says "You sent that boy, didn\'t you? You arranged this." He asks: "So, you fell for it", and if she did not care about him, would she have come all this way. She has no answer, and her silence says more than words. She says that for once she wants to choose for herself, she is not here out of duty, and she wants to stay. Chad: if you only came out of duty or curiosity I will stop; stay only if it is what you truly want. They kiss, and the night passes. The next morning Jade wakes in the same hut beside him: "Good morning." "Don\'t look so pleased." "I didn\'t say anything. You were thinking it."',
  art:'Pages show: Sally is paid by Chad with a silver nugget. Chad sent the messenger, and the note signed "C." was his. Jade makes her choice by herself; this is the decision Chad offered in Chapters 14 and 15.',
  quote:'"For once… I want to choose for myself. I\'m not here out of duty." — Jade Gold',
  events:['The boy delivers Chad\'s note','Jade follows Chad to a hut and sees him pay Sally','Chad reveals he arranged it','Jade chooses Chad','The next morning in the hut'],
  purpose:['Resolve the three-day choice: Jade chooses Chad','Show Chad\'s hand in the festival arrangement'],
  unlocks:['Relationship milestone: Jade × Chad (Bond event)'],
  reward:'Bond event: Jade chooses Chad'},
 18:{ title:'The Price of Trust', type:'Story Chapter — Sky is taken', loc:'🏘 Cottage in Vigil → 🛒 Vigil Central Market',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad (Sky absent)',
  introduced:['Bandit Booyeon (named in the ransom note)','A bearded man in black (messenger)'],
  sum:'Jade returns to the cottage with a mind far more unsettled than she expected. One night had not settled her heart; it had made everything more complicated. Chad returns in unexpectedly high spirits and calls for Sky, but the silence feels wrong and Sky is gone. A dagger thuds into the table, pinning a note: "Your friend is in our hands. If you want him alive, bring 1000 silver pieces. Go to Vigil Central Market. A bearded man in black will give further instructions. — Bandit Booyeon." Chad calls Jade; she reads the note, saying Sky is missing. In minutes they are ready. The market looks ordinary, too ordinary. A disturbance breaks out at the edge, and a hooded figure slips Chad an envelope; Chad shouts "Wait!" but the figure vanishes. "This wasn\'t a meeting." "They wanted us to know they were watching." "Then we find Sky." Somewhere in the crowd their enemy was waiting.',
  art:'Pages show: the bandit is spelled "Booyeon" on the note here (a typo in the original story; later chapters correct it to Booyeong). Jade and Chad now dress in matching dark travelling clothes.',
  quote:'"They wanted us to know they were watching." — Chad',
  events:['Jade returns to the cottage','Sky is missing; a ransom note is pinned by a dagger','Jade and Chad go to Vigil Central Market','A disturbance covers a second message handoff','They resolve to find Sky'],
  purpose:['Raise the stakes: Sky\'s kidnapping and the ransom','Start the Sky rescue quest'],
  unlocks:['Rescue quest begins','Investigation (suggested): follow the notes'],
  reward:'Quest: rescue Sky'},
 19:{ title:'Into the Woods', type:'Story Chapter — through the woods', loc:'🛒 Vigil Central Market → 🌲 forest',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:['The black-robed messenger'],
  sum:'At Vigil Central Market Jade paces, wondering what to do. Chad remembers the second note and the mysterious black-robed messenger, and at a quiet shelter outside the market, saying no one else is coming, shows her the note. "You had this all this time?" She slaps him; he says there is no time to argue: the longer they delay, the farther they get. The second note leads them into the woods, which the villagers fear along with Booyeong\'s bandits. Jade refuses to stop even as the path grows darker and rougher. "I\'m fine. Sky matters." Her strength gives out and Chad carries her ("Hey, put me down..." "We have to keep going."). At a large rock in a forest clearing he sets her down; her heel is badly blistered, and he makes a poultice of herbs. In her restless sleep Jade murmurs "No matter what... I won\'t give in..." He checks her pulse, feels a chill of fear and cries "Jade... No!"',
  art:'Pages show: the second note is the one hidden by Chad. Jade\'s sleep murmurs refer to the witch\'s temptation, continued in Chapter 20.',
  quote:'"I\'m fine. Sky matters." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Jade learns Chad kept the second note; she slaps him','They follow the note into the forest','Chad carries Jade when she collapses','Chad tends her blistered heel','Jade slips into a trance and Chad panics'],
  purpose:['Travel and exploration through the forest','Introduce hazards: exhaustion and injury'],
  unlocks:['Forest exploration (suggested)','Herb crafting (suggested)'],
  reward:'Forest route'},
 20:{ title:'The Witch\'s Bargain', type:'Story Chapter — the witch\'s bargain, then separation', loc:'🕳 Large cavern (vision) → 🌲 forest',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:['Her Highness Ximan, the witch (named in the caption)'],
  sum:'Jade opens her eyes in a large cavern before a throned woman. "Who are you?" "Yes, Jade... that\'s I am now, that." The caption names her Her Highness Ximan. Jade says she is not a virgin and so has no use for her lifeforce; the witch asks if she thinks this is about her lifeforce, and whether she realises who she is. She offers to make her stronger, sexier, anything she wishes, and to make "that silly prince" love her forever, if she joins. "I won\'t join forces with a witch!" "You already will, my Jade Gold." The witch says Jade has not heard her out yet. Chad\'s voice cries "Jade! NO! Please, Jade Gold! Wake up!" and an unknown force pulls Jade back to the forest. Chad begs her not to leave him. She says they should keep going, refuses to be carried and slips. She tells him: "Stop this. I don\'t want anything to do with you, Chad. Until we find Sky and defeat Frog Mahan, you\'re just a mercenary that I have no feelings for." Chad ties her to a tree for her own safety, leaves a pouch and says he will go on alone and return to free her so they can continue the quest, and slips into the forest.',
  art:'Pages show: the caption names her Her Highness "Ximan", a short form of Ximanka (Xima is also short for Ximanka). Jade has been bound with rope by Chad in the forest.',
  quote:'"You already will, my Jade Gold." — the witch',
  events:['Jade is pulled into a cavern and meets the witch Ximan','The witch offers power and love in exchange for joining her','Jade is pulled back to the forest','Jade pushes Chad away, calling him just a mercenary','Chad ties her to a tree and goes on alone'],
  purpose:['Introduce the witch as a direct tempter and antagonist','Split the party: Chad goes ahead alone'],
  unlocks:['Vision events (witch encounter)'],
  reward:'Chad on his own; Jade left behind'},
 21:{ title:'At the Bandit\'s Mercy', type:'Story Chapter (Jade\'s first-person narration) — captured', loc:'🌲 Forest → ⛺ Booyeong\'s bandit camp → 🏚 prison',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade (alone)',
  introduced:['Sir Booyeong (first appearance)','Bearded Mouse (named later, ch26)'],
  sum:'Tied to a tree by Chad for her own safety, Jade says this is not true safety. She closes her eyes and a familiar power stirs in her veins; the ropes snap. She notes he bandaged her heel while she slept, but it does not soften her anger. She takes her bundle, changes into a man\'s disguise and continues alone: when she finds Chad again she will make him remember her wrath. A bandit confronts her with a sword ("Who are you?") and she says she wants to join Sir Booyeong\'s bandit army; she wins two rounds against him and orders him to take her to Booyeong. At the camp in the forest he points to the tent. She enters too rashly: Booyeong sees through her disguise at once ("Still wearing a man\'s disguise? How amusing."), cuts her hair tie and slashes open her outer robe. "Jade Gold. Your little powers don\'t work in my territory. I am your nemesis." She says she is just an ordinary person; he says her very existence is the bane of his own. He rings a bell and orders her taken to the prison to "meet her beloved one last time." Led toward a dark prison, Jade knows Sky is somewhere ahead and will not give up.',
  art:'Pages show: the bandit name is now spelled Booyeong. Jade\'s powers are suppressed inside his territory. Jade fights with a sword here.',
  quote:'"Your little powers don\'t work in my territory. I am your nemesis." — Booyeong',
  events:['Jade breaks the ropes and disguises herself as a man','Jade fights her way into the bandit camp','Booyeong sees through the disguise and suppresses her powers','Jade is taken to the prison to find Sky'],
  purpose:['Introduce Booyeong and his suppression field','Story fight: Jade against a bandit (two rounds)'],
  unlocks:['Combat: Jade solo fight','Power suppression zone (suggested mechanic)'],
  reward:'Story: captured by Booyeong'},
 22:{ title:'Between Love and Loyalty', type:'Story Chapter (Chad\'s point of view) — infiltration', loc:'🌲 Forest → ⛺ Bandit camp',
  chars:['chad'], charsNote:'Chad',
  introduced:['Bearded Mouse (the bearded man in black)'],
  sum:'Chad returns to where he left Jade and finds her gone: "I was too late. I made a blunder." He remembers her collapsing, how the jade pendant restored her and how he called her name desperately. Jealousy and regret burn as he follows their tracks. He finds the bandit camp, where Jade has already been taken inside. He distracts two guards with pebbles, takes them down and steals a bandit uniform, then enters the camp disguised as a guard with the ransom money. A bearded man says the master already has what he needs: Sky has been tortured enough and will be released as promised, but the feisty woman is the real target, and soon she will be dead. Jade is held in a cell, bruised and exhausted, her spirit unbroken ("You can kill me... but I won\'t give you what you want."), and she even slapped one of the men. Chad learns she will be thrown into the ravine by the first watch. Sky will be released once the ransom is paid; he has endured the torture but is alive. One is his sworn brother, the other the woman he loves: "How could he choose?" Night deepens and time is running out.',
  art:'Pages show: the jade pendant that restored Jade belongs to Sky; it is shown glowing on her chest. Chad is the one who brought the ransom money.',
  quote:'"Sky... Jade... how can I choose?" — Chad',
  events:['Chad finds Jade gone and follows the tracks','Chad infiltrates the camp in a stolen uniform','He learns Jade will be thrown into the ravine at the first watch','Sky will be released once the ransom is paid','Chad faces a choice between Sky and Jade'],
  purpose:['Infiltration scene: stealth approach (suggested)','Build to the choice between Sky and Jade'],
  unlocks:['Dialogue choice (suggested)'],
  reward:'Chad\'s dilemma'},
 23:{ title:'The Heart\'s Choice', type:'Story Chapter — prison escape', loc:'⛓ Bandit prison',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Sky and Chad',
  introduced:['Aunt Sue (in a vision)'],
  sum:'In the dim prison cell Jade watches over Sky as he sleeps. Injured and shivering, she stays by his side, meditates and heals slowly. In a vision Aunt Sue appears and says "Take care... of my son." When Jade opens her eyes many wounds have healed. She wakes Sky by tickling his foot. He says a girl asked for shelter, then he woke among strangers and fell asleep again. He covers her with his outer robe, says they tortured him but he is fine and wishes the marks were away from her; a soft light eases her wounds. The prison doors open and guards take Jade; Sky tries to resist but his power is suppressed ("I\'m not able to fight!"). A gust of wind drops two guards and Chad appears: "I\'m sorry I am late." Jade tells him to rescue Sky quickly. Chad and Sky help Jade escape, but many bandits block the exit. Jade grabs a dagger and steps forward alone: "I release you from the mission! Go!" She is surrounded, and Chad looks to Sky, facing a terrible choice.',
  art:'Pages show: Aunt Sue is the mother Sky named in Chapter 5 (Yvette Sue), asking Jade to take care of her son. Sky\'s power is suppressed in the camp. Jade fights with a dagger here.',
  quote:'"I release you from the mission! Go!" — Jade Gold',
  events:['Jade heals herself by meditating and sees Aunt Sue','Sky wakes; he shields Jade and heals some wounds','Guards take Jade; Sky\'s power is suppressed','Chad arrives; they break out','Jade stays behind to hold the exit and releases them from the mission'],
  purpose:['Escape sequence from the prison','Establish the suppression field mechanic'],
  unlocks:['Healing / meditation action'],
  reward:'Story: Jade holds the exit'},
 24:{ title:'The Choice He Could Not Make', type:'Story Chapter — the rescue', loc:'🌲 Forest → ⛺ Bandit camp → 🌊 ravine and hidden cavern',
  chars:['chad','jade','sky'], charsNote:'Chad (also Jade and Sky)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In the forest Sky, angry and hurt, confronts Chad: "You left her behind?! Jade trusted us both!" Chad: "...I know. It\'s my fault." Sky tells him to go back and bring her home, giving his approval despite his pain: no matter what, Jade is our sister. Chad promises not to leave her again. That night he returns to the camp in a stolen guard robe. Booyeong celebrates ("Tomorrow, we\'ll make an example of her. No one escapes my mountain.") while Jade is kept in a cage, bruised and exhausted. At dawn the bandits carry the cage to the cliff\'s edge ("Throw her in. Let the ravens finish what we started."). Chad cannot watch her die and leaps after the falling cage. He catches it before it is lost to the ravine, drags it to a hidden cavern and breaks it open. Jade wakes and sees he came back: "Chad...? You came back..." "Yes. I\'m here now. I won\'t leave you again." She thanks him for coming back for her. Banner: Bond Unlocked, Jade and Sky: Sibling Bond.',
  art:'Pages show: a banner announces Bond Unlocked: Jade and Sky, Sibling Bond. Sky calls Jade his sister.',
  quote:'"No matter what, Jade is our sister." — Sky Yale',
  events:['Sky confronts Chad for leaving Jade','Chad returns to the camp in a guard\'s robe','Bandits throw Jade\'s cage into the ravine','Chad leaps after the cage and rescues Jade','Bond unlocked: Jade and Sky, Sibling Bond'],
  purpose:['Rescue scene; reconcile Chad with Sky and Jade','Show the Sibling Bond between Jade and Sky'],
  unlocks:['Bond unlocked: Jade × Sky (Sibling Bond)'],
  reward:'Bond: Jade and Sky, Sibling Bond'},
 25:{ title:'The Truth Behind the Mask', type:'Story Chapter — truth and the bonding art', loc:'🏚 Abandoned hideout near the cave',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:['A mysterious woman (vision)'],
  sum:'In the abandoned hideout near the cave, Jade and Chad study a secret bonding art inscribed by an unknown ancient power. The inscription speaks of a bond that transcended blood, uniting two selves across fate and time. The technique connects their spirits but must be done correctly; at first it does not work. Chad says he has something important to tell her: "I\'m not from Tribute. I\'m from Dragonvale. My true name is Roc Chadwick. I am a prince of Dragonvale." Jade realises the special mission, the stone, the bandits and the prophecy make sense now: "So the prophecy... it was about you." She confides she has memories that do not feel like her own, dreams and feelings she cannot explain, and it scares her. Chad says no matter what memories she carries she is still Jade, and he accepts all of her. (He leaves out parts of who he is.) With their hearts open they try the technique again and the ancient symbols glow with brilliant light. As their spirits synchronise, a vision of a mysterious woman, familiar yet distant, flashes in Jade\'s mind. Banner: Bond Strengthened +1, Jade and Chad: Truth Beyond Duty. Two different worlds, two complicated pasts, to be faced together.',
  art:'Pages show: Chad claims Roc Chadwick is his true name, but this is a deception: his real name is Roc Chadstone (Chapter 1), and he does not tell her everything about his life in Dragonvale. He is a prince of Dragonvale. The inscription carries a dragon sigil.',
  quote:'"Jade… I have something important to tell you. I\'m not from Tribute. I\'m from Dragonvale." — Chad',
  events:['Jade and Chad study the bonding inscription','Chad reveals he is a prince of Dragonvale','Jade shares memories that do not feel like her own','The bonding technique works; a vision of a mysterious woman','Bond Strengthened: Jade and Chad, Truth Beyond Duty'],
  purpose:['Reveal Chad\'s origin and the prophecy link (with deceptions about his name and past)','Introduce the bonding technique (pair skills)'],
  unlocks:['Bond Strengthened +1: Jade × Chad','Bonding technique (pair skills)'],
  reward:'Bond: Truth Beyond Duty'},
 26:{ title:'Return to Faepool', type:'Story Chapter — return to the camp', loc:'🏘 Vigil → ⛺ Booyeong\'s camp',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad and Sky',
  introduced:['Bearded Mouse (named)'],
  sum:'Several months have passed since the escape. At Vigil, Jade has regained her strength, and their hearts are steadier. She trains daily, clearer and more determined ("I will protect what matters now."). Sky recovered slowly in Vigil with herbs and care; outside Booyeong\'s suppression field his abilities are returning ("It\'s still not complete, but it\'s much stronger now."). They discuss what happened: the entire area is under a suppression field, but it is not absolute, so Sky could still form a small healing pact for Jade; there must be dead spots. Chad doesn\'t use magic and relies on pure martial arts. Jade says her full power is still not awakened and there is more she needs to unlock. "We fight together. That is enough." They decide to attack Booyeong: "Tonight, we end this." They move through the camp together: Chad leads with martial skill, Sky supports with precise strikes, Jade keeps their flank. Bearded Mouse recognises Jade, terrified ("Y-you! It\'s you! Please... I didn\'t know...!"); Jade tells him to run and never return. They rush the central tent, where Booyeong waits: "You finally returned."',
  art:'Pages show: the fighting roles are stated outright: Chad leads, Sky supports and Jade keeps the flank. Chad uses no magic. Sky has a healing pact for Jade. The bearded man in black is called Bearded Mouse.',
  quote:'"We fight together. That is enough." — Chad',
  events:['Months of recovery at Vigil','Sky regains power outside the suppression field','The trio plans the assault on Booyeong','They fight through the camp','Bearded Mouse flees; Booyeong waits in the central tent'],
  purpose:['Time skip and training montage','Start of the boss assault: team roles (Chad lead, Sky support, Jade flank)'],
  unlocks:['Training (Vigil)','Party formation roles'],
  reward:'Prepare for Booyeong'},
 27:{ title:'The Bane of Two Souls', type:'Story Chapter — the boss fight', loc:'⛺ Booyeong\'s camp → 🌲 forest',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad and Sky',
  introduced:['Booyeong (confronted)'],
  sum:'Months later, Jade, Chad and Sky launch a surprise assault on Booyeong\'s camp ("Stay close to me!" "I\'ll cover the left side!"). Bearded Mouse is defeated, and Jade chooses mercy: "Go. Live, and remember what happens to those who betray others." Chad tells her she can be merciful with them but not with Booyeong. In the tent Booyeong taunts: "Did you really think he could protect you? You begged for more in the end, didn\'t you?" Jade: "You lie!" Booyeong laughs: "Do you still believe everything she tells you?" A sinister voice from Xima reaches Jade\'s mind: "Kill him." A jewelled dagger manifests in her hand. Sensing something wrong ("This isn\'t real! He\'s trying to manipulate you!"), she says "I... can\'t..." but in the end Jade finishes him. They free the prisoners in the dungeons; Chad notices something strange about one of them. The prisoner runs out and launches a signal ("Ha! Fools!"); bright signal fires rise and reinforcements approach: "We have to go! Now!" Later under a tree Chad is cold and silent: "My dear employer, no words until we return to Vigil." Banner: Bond weakened -1.',
  art:'Pages show: Xima\'s voice drives Jade to kill Booyeong, with a jewelled dagger manifesting in her hand. Booyeong\'s taunts about Chad\'s loyalty turn him cold afterwards. The dagger here is Xima\'s, not Greyson\'s.',
  quote:'"Kill him." — Xima, speaking into Jade\'s mind',
  events:['The trio storms the camp','Jade spares Bearded Mouse','Booyeong taunts them; Xima\'s voice commands Jade','Jade kills Booyeong','A prisoner signals reinforcements; the party flees','Chad goes cold; Bond weakened -1 (Jade × Chad)'],
  purpose:['Boss fight: Booyeong (major battle)','Choice of mercy versus vengeance','Introduce Xima\'s direct influence on Jade'],
  unlocks:['Boss battle: Booyeong','Bond weakened -1: Jade × Chad'],
  reward:'Booyeong defeated'},
 28:{ title:'The Woman Behind the Smile', type:'Story Chapter (Sally\'s introduction) — the brothel', loc:'🏮 Lantern-lit brothel at the edge of the city',
  chars:['chad'], charsNote:'Chad and Sally (Jade absent)',
  introduced:['Sally Sin (new character introduced)'],
  sum:'After the battle at Booyeong, Chad walks away with a cold heart. Jade\'s trust is shaken, and the words she spoke still echo in his mind; he has lost something precious and does not know how to fix it. In a lantern-lit brothel at the edge of the city, a woman named Sally welcomes guests. Behind the smile lies the story of a fallen princess and a heart that never forgot its wounds. Once she was a princess of a noble house; she believed in love and trusted the man at her side, but it was a lie: he used her, betrayed her and brought down her family for power. Her home fell, her family was gone and she became a fugitive with no name and no land. Now she lives as Sally in a brothel, not as a prostitute but as a woman who waits: she endures, she listens, she gathers information, all for the day she can take her revenge. That night a broken man comes to her: "You look as if the world has betrayed you too." "...Maybe it has." "You don\'t have to pretend here. Everyone who comes to me carries a wound." She understands him because she too lost everything once. For that night Chad sets aside his pain and finds warmth in her presence; she does not ask about his past. Banners: New Character Introduced: Sally Sin. Sally + Chad Bond: Forming.',
  art:'Pages show: Sally\'s full name is Sally Sin, a fallen princess working in a brothel to gather information for revenge. She is introduced here; the author says she is recruited in Chapter 28 or 29. This is the first time Sally\'s backstory is told.',
  quote:'"Everyone who comes to me carries a wound." — Sally',
  events:['Chad leaves the camp, cold toward Jade','Sally\'s backstory is told: a fallen princess seeking revenge','Chad meets Sally and finds comfort','New Character Introduced: Sally Sin','Sally + Chad Bond: Forming'],
  purpose:['Introduce Sally with her backstory and motive','Seed the Chad × Sally bond'],
  unlocks:['Sally profile unlocked','Bond: Sally × Chad (forming)'],
  reward:'Sally introduced'},
 29:{ title:'Shadows Between Hearts', type:'Story Chapter — shadows and a return', loc:'🏮 Brothel → 🏘 Vigil',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky'], charsNote:'Chad, Jade, Sky, Sally',
  introduced:['Levi Stanson (alive, appears at the end)'],
  sum:'Chad wakes in Sally\'s embrace: "No matter what happens, you don\'t have to face it alone. You always have a place with me." "Don\'t say that. I know what I am. And I can\'t stay." Outside in Vigil, Jade and Sky spend time together after his recovery ("I\'m so glad you\'re feeling better now, Sky." "I\'m fine! Thanks to you, Jade. You were so brave."). Chad sees them from a distance and his heart tightens: "Of course. I was a fool to think otherwise." Later, in front of others, Sally kisses Chad\'s cheek ("Only you understand me, Chad." "...Do as you like."). Jade sees it from afar: "...I see. So that\'s what I am to you now." Banner: Bond Update, Jade + Sky +1. That night the men from the prison\'s signal attack the village: "Bandits! Get them!" Jade draws her dagger ("Stay back!"), Sky fights bravely though still recovering ("I can still fight!"), and Chad takes down attackers with powerful swordsmanship. A familiar figure steps out of the shadows. Levi Stanson has arrived. "The shadows were far from over... and so was their story."',
  art:'Pages show: Levi Stanson is alive after Greyson\'s pigeon said he was dead. Sally and Chad are both in Vigil. The Jade and Sky bond rises again. Jade fights with a dagger.',
  quote:'"So that\'s what I am to you now." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Chad leaves Sally, torn','Sally kisses Chad in front of Jade; Jade sees','Jade and Sky grow closer (Bond +1)','Bandits attack Vigil at night','Levi Stanson appears'],
  purpose:['Defend Vigil: story fight with all three','Reveal that Levi lives'],
  unlocks:['Combat: Jade, Chad and Sky versus bandits','Bond Update: Jade × Sky +1'],
  reward:'Levi Stanson returns'},
 30:{ title:'The Creek of Promises', type:'Story Chapter — the benefactor and the promise', loc:'🏘 Vigil (ambush) → 🏞 road to Trinity → 🌌 creek under the moon',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky and Levi (the benefactor)',
  introduced:['Levi Stanson (full introduction)'],
  sum:'As night falls over Vigil, the enemy launches a sudden ambush. The mysterious benefactor (Levi) fights beside Jade: "Watch your back. Blades don\'t have eyes." He hands her a crossbow: "Jade, take this." "Thank you! I can use this." With his weapon Jade fights with new confidence ("One down!"), Chad cuts through the enemy with flawless skill, and Sky helps too. The benefactor moves like a shadow, striking from afar. Soon the ambush is over. Sky\'s condition improves day by day. Chad watches from a distance, clearly unsettled, as Sally sits close to him. Jade invites the benefactor to stay with their party: "Please... let us thank you properly, and travel with us to Trinity." "...I\'ll consider it." For the next few days they travel toward Trinity. That evening at an inn along the road, someone remarks: "It seems you are very concerned about your mercenary." "Not at all." Later that night the benefactor leads Jade to a quiet forest path, to a secluded creek under the moon. "Just who are you, Mr Stanson?" "Levi Stanson." "...!" "Our fathers made a promise. Will you still honor it?" In the soft sound of the creek, Jade gives her answer: "...I will." Beneath the moonlit trees a new promise is made, and their journey continues toward Trinity.',
  art:'Pages show: Levi gives Jade a crossbow during the ambush (the crossbow Jade later uses). Jade tells Levi she will honour the engagement, which stands against the Chapter 17 choice of Chad. Their next destination is Trinity.',
  quote:'"Our fathers made a promise. Will you still honor it?" — Levi Stanson',
  events:['Ambush on Vigil; Levi fights beside Jade','Levi gives Jade a crossbow','Jade invites Levi to travel with them to Trinity','At the creek Levi reveals his name and asks about the engagement','Jade answers: "I will."'],
  purpose:['Introduce Levi as an ally and give Jade the crossbow','Set up the journey to Trinity'],
  unlocks:['Crossbow (given to Jade)','Levi joins the party'],
  reward:'Levi joins; Jade receives a crossbow'},
 31:{ title:'Fractured Hearts', type:'Story Chapter (Jade\'s first-person narration) — the break', loc:'🏮 Inn in Vigil',
  chars:['jade','chad'], charsNote:'Jade and Chad',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a cold bath Jade tries to clear her mind, but her thoughts are in turmoil. She had been so close to Levi, yet sounds from the next room disturbed her sleep night after night, and the image of Chad and Sally together keeps appearing: it hurt more than she expected. Late that night the door opens. Chad, who has been drinking, says they need to talk: he saw her with Levi at the creek and asks if they were kissing and what exactly her relationship with him is. Jade says Levi was only removing a twig from her hair: it was not a kiss. Chad says "Forget him. Right now, it\'s just you and me..." and she slaps him. She tells him he is not in the right mind, he made it very clear she is just his employer, and he chose Sally, not her; and as long as Levi is alive she still has a family duty and an engagement promise to consider. She thinks that if Chad could hurt her like this now, nothing would stop him from hurting her worse in the future: he is a prince, and princes often have many wives. "This ends here. We cannot continue like this. I will remain your employer. But there will be no more false hopes, no more closeness, and no more crossing the line. Please respect my decision." Chad says nothing and stands wounded and silent. Banner: Bond Status, Jade + Chad -2.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade now assumes Chad, as a prince, may have many wives. Levi\'s engagement is again considered binding because he is alive.',
  quote:'"This ends here. We cannot continue like this." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Jade cannot sleep; she keeps picturing Chad and Sally','Chad, drunk, confronts her about Levi at the creek','Jade slaps him and ends their closeness','Jade stays as his employer only','Bond: Jade + Chad -2'],
  purpose:['Break the Jade and Chad bond; set up the Levi route','Relationship milestone (bond drop)'],
  unlocks:['Bond change: Jade × Chad -2'],
  reward:'Bond: Jade and Chad fractured'},
 32:{ title:'The Lost Years', type:'Story Chapter — Levi\'s explanation', loc:'🏚 Quiet inn in a small village',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade (narrator), Levi, Sky and Chad',
  introduced:['Ryn (Levi\'s fellow soldier, in a flashback)'],
  sum:'That night, after the turmoil, the three rest at a small inn in a quiet village. Jade had long believed Levi abandoned her or was dead. Levi says he owes her the truth about why he disappeared and why everyone thought he was dead. Years ago he was on a covert mission beyond the northern mountains with a comrade, Ryn, more than a fellow soldier: a brother to him, brave, loyal and always putting others first. During the mission they were ambushed by a larger force. Ryn saved his life and took the fatal blow meant for him, giving Levi the chance to escape; the enemy believed they both died in the chaos. Badly injured, Levi let them think he was dead: it was the only way to protect everyone else and to survive. Greyson later revoked the engagement, not out of cruelty but to protect Levi\'s status: in the eyes of the court Levi Stanson had to remain dead, and only then could he live freely under a new identity. He continued to work in the shadows, gathering information and completing missions that could not be traced back to the Stanson name, because there were still threats to the realm. Jade says: "You didn\'t abandon me. You were protecting everything." Sky says Ryn must have been an extraordinary person. Levi says he still carries guilt every day, but meeting them again makes him believe the lost years were not in vain. Jade is glad he is alive and with them. Banners: Jade + Levi Bond +1, Sky + Levi Bond +1.',
  art:'Pages show: this explains why Greyson\'s pigeon reported Stanson dead in Chapter 14: it was a cover. Levi has been living under another name. Chad is present but silent.',
  quote:'"You didn\'t abandon me. You were protecting everything." — Jade Gold',
  events:['The party rests at an inn in a quiet village','Levi tells the truth of his disappearance: Ryn saved him on a mission beyond the northern mountains','Greyson revoked the engagement to protect Levi\'s status; Levi stayed dead to the court','Levi worked in the shadows under another name','Bonds: Jade + Levi +1, Sky + Levi +1'],
  purpose:['Resolve the mystery of Levi\'s death','Deepen the party\'s bonds with Levi'],
  unlocks:['Bond: Jade × Levi +1','Bond: Sky × Levi +1'],
  reward:'Levi\'s past revealed'},
 33:{ title:'Duty and Distance', type:'Story Chapter — rest and a break-up', loc:'🏘 First post near Vigil',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party arrives at the first post near Vigil, a quiet village where they can rest and lie low. A courier brings a coded message from King Greyson: rest for a week, lie low and learn the villagers\' ways while his spies track Xima\'s evil minions. Jade catches a cold draught and falls ill. Sky and Levi take turns brewing medicine for her with local herbs and care for her patiently ("It\'s bitter... but I\'ll take it."). Chad watches with rising jealousy, but instead of confronting Jade he showers his attention on Sally ("Here, have some tea. Keep warm. You look beautiful in this shawl."). That night Chad comes quietly into Jade\'s room. "Are you still sick?" "Are you here for satisfaction?" "No. I just wanted to check up on you." Jade asks if it disappoints him that she is alive and kicking, or if he seeks an excuse to loaf on the job. He starts "What if after this mission —" and she answers: are you willing to give up everything for me, your life of luxury, your women in Dragonvale, your claim to the throne, Sally...? He is silent. Even if he could, she cannot give up her duty as an Imperial Guard: to King Greyson, to Tribute, to her family. He asks if she is willing to marry Levi Stanson: "Yes, I am." She tells him: "I\'ve made it clear, Roc Chadwick, it\'s not about me and you. This is about more than two families. It\'s a promise spanning several generations." "I said, it\'s over between us. Leave please, Chad." Banners: Jade + Levi +1, Chad + Sally +1, Jade + Chad -1.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade now knows of Chad\'s women in Dragonvale and his claim to the throne, and still calls him Roc Chadwick. The promise to marry Levi is described as spanning several generations.',
  quote:'"It\'s not about me and you. This is about more than two families. It\'s a promise spanning several generations." — Jade Gold',
  events:['The party arrives near Vigil; Greyson orders a week of lying low','Jade falls ill; Sky and Levi nurse her','Chad pays attention to Sally in front of her','Chad visits Jade at night; she refuses to give up her duty','Jade confirms she will marry Levi','Bonds: Jade + Levi +1, Chad + Sally +1, Jade + Chad -1'],
  purpose:['A week of downtime: rest, learn the village, gather information (suggested)','Relationship milestone: Jade commits to Levi'],
  unlocks:['Rest mechanic (suggested)','Bonds changed'],
  reward:'Jade chooses duty'},
 34:{ title:'A Week of Silence', type:'Story Chapter — a week in the village', loc:'🏘 Village near Vigil',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:['Haren (village local)'],
  sum:'A week has passed since they arrived near Vigil. The village is peaceful, almost too peaceful. For the first time in many days the group is not travelling: Greyson\'s orders are to lay low and become part of the village, living quietly among the people and avoiding attention. Sky adapts fastest, treating villagers and earning their trust; the blue-haired healer quickly becomes beloved, and Jade smiles seeing him in his element ("He brings light wherever he goes..."). Levi surprises everyone by fitting in, helping quietly and teaching the young how to use a bow; Jade notices he is not someone who belonged in darkness but someone forced to survive there. Sky notices Jade watching Levi ("You don\'t need to feel guilty for being happy, Jade."). Chad, still hurt, draws closer to Sally, who proves smart and capable, gathering information from villagers and merchants; Chad finds in her a welcome distraction. One evening the group gathers at a village house with Haren, a local who has long lived there. He shares the truth about the northern forest: it has been abandoned for years; people who enter it disappear, and those who go to investigate never return. Jade becomes alert: this is more than rumours. Sky\'s bright expression darkens; Levi listens carefully: "Something is out there." Later Jade stands outside looking over the village. It appears peaceful but something feels unsettling: empty houses, paths that are avoided, a hidden fear in the villagers\' eyes. Levi joins her: "You feel it too, don\'t you?" "Yes. Something is wrong." A cold wind passes and Jade feels a faint pulse in her chest, as if something in the forest recognised her: "...It knows I\'m here." Levi: "Whatever is in the forest... knows you are here, Jade." Progression banners: Jade + Levi Bond +1, Sky + Levi Bond +1, Chad + Sally Bond +1, Jade + Chad distance increases.',
  art:'Pages show: the village is only a cover, since Greyson ordered them to blend in. The northern forest has been abandoned for years and people who enter it vanish. Jade\'s chest pulses in answer to the forest.',
  quote:'"Whatever is in the forest... knows you are here, Jade." — Levi Stanson',
  events:['The party settles into village life','Sky becomes a beloved healer; Levi teaches the village youth archery','Chad grows closer to Sally','Haren tells of the abandoned northern forest where people vanish','Jade and Levi feel something wrong and sense the forest recognising her','Bonds: Jade + Levi +1, Sky + Levi +1, Chad + Sally +1, Jade + Chad distance'],
  purpose:['Downtime chapter: village life and bonding scenes (suggested)','Introduce the northern forest mystery'],
  unlocks:['Village life events (suggested)','Bond: Jade × Levi +1'],
  reward:'A week of silence'},
 35:{ title:'Whispers Before the Storm', type:'Story Chapter — scouting attack', loc:'🏘 Village near Vigil → 🏚 Abandoned shrine in the forest',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi (Sally in the village)',
  introduced:['Xima\'s minions (demonic scouts)'],
  sum:'A week has passed since their last mission. The party stays near the first post outside Vigil, lying low on Greyson\'s orders, blending into the village and watching for signs of Xima. Jade helps with light tasks and regains her strength, Sky treats the villagers, and Levi notices strange traces around the village: markings the same as Xima\'s minions. Chad keeps watch from a distance, his gaze never leaving Jade ("Stay close, Jade."). That night they investigate an abandoned shrine near the forest: "This place... has been corrupted." The same markings are there, with signs of recent activity: "They are close. Much closer than we thought." Shadowy demonic minions emerge from the trees. Chad takes the front, Levi has the rear, and Sky supports with healing magic. As Jade fights she feels an unfamiliar power respond to the danger: a faint crimson light rises within her. The minions retreat after a brief clash: it was only a scouting attack, just to test them. The party regroups, knowing Xima\'s main force is still moving and that next time there won\'t be a warning. Deeper in the forest, unseen, more figures observe: "The awakened one. Just as expected. Inform Lord Xima. They are here."',
  art:'Pages show: Jade\'s crimson power begins to awaken. Xima is called Lord Xima by his minions here (the earlier pages used the witch).',
  quote:'"The awakened one. Just as expected. Inform Lord Xima." — a watcher in the forest',
  events:['Levi finds Xima\'s markings in the village','The party investigates an abandoned shrine','Xima\'s minions attack; a scouting fight','Jade feels a crimson power stir','The watchers report that the awakened one is here'],
  purpose:['Story fight: party versus Xima\'s minions (scouting attack)','Foreshadow Jade\'s awakening'],
  unlocks:['Combat: first minion fight','Jade\'s crimson power (foreshadow)'],
  reward:'Xima\'s scouts engaged'},
 36:{ title:'The People Who Were Taken', type:'Story Chapter — the hidden village', loc:'🌲 Forest → 🏚 Abandoned hidden village',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the strange figure\'s appearance the party follows the clues deeper into the forest and finds a hidden village, bigger than expected, abandoned as if the villagers vanished in an instant, with no sign of a struggle and everything left behind. The atmosphere is heavy; Jade says it feels as if they did not leave willingly. Sky finds untouched medicine, unfinished meals and personal items: "They were taken." The same mark appears on walls throughout the village. They find the missing villagers, alive but changed, with empty eyes and voices no longer their own ("Sister... come with us... The Master will take care of you..."). Jade feels a painful pull in her chest and reaches out instinctively ("Shh... It\'s okay..."), but at her touch dark energy surges and the villager screams: the corruption rejected her. Levi says this is no longer ordinary possession: Xima is using people as vessels. Sky says there must be a way to bring them back since they are still alive. Chad says if they hesitate, more people will be taken. They discover a larger gathering place deeper in the village. "This is not random. They are preparing for something. And we\'re right in the middle of it." Jade realises the villagers were drawn here for a reason: "They were waiting... for me." Xima\'s influence runs deeper than they imagined, and the true ritual has not yet begun.',
  art:'Pages show: the corruption turns people into vessels without killing them, and Jade\'s touch is rejected by it, which she takes as a sign they are connected to her. Sally stays in the group.',
  quote:'"They were waiting... for me." — Jade Gold',
  events:['The party finds an abandoned hidden village','Sky finds untouched belongings: the villagers were taken','They meet the changed villagers; Jade\'s touch makes the corruption surge','Levi explains Xima is using people as vessels','Jade realises the villagers were drawn here for her'],
  purpose:['Investigation: exploring the hidden village','Introduce the vessel corruption and the ritual'],
  unlocks:['Investigation events','Corrupted villagers (enemy type, suggested non-lethal)'],
  reward:'The villagers were bait'},
 37:{ title:'The Shaman', type:'Story Chapter — the shaman', loc:'🏚 Shaman\'s hut in the forest',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:['The Shaman (elder with white hair and a staff)'],
  sum:'After discovering the abandoned village, the party continues deeper into the forest, following the traces left by the taken villagers, to a hut. "This must be the place. Be careful. We don\'t know who is inside." An old shaman says "You are not Xima\'s people. Then you must be the ones King Greyson sent." Jade asks if he knows the king, and who he is. He says the villagers are not mere monsters: they were once people, villagers, neighbours, family. Xima corrupts them, feeds on their fears and turns them into vessels for his power. Sky asks if they can be saved: not easily, since once the corruption takes root their minds are no longer their own; they remain alive but are no longer the people you knew. Chad asks what Xima is trying to achieve: a larger ritual; he is gathering people, not just to create an army, but for something greater. "The girl born under the lunar eclipse... Xima believes her blood can complete the ritual and open the way to something far worse." Jade realises the village was used as bait to draw her here and blames herself: "I caused this... The corruption rejected her. They were not just sick. They had been changed. Because of me..." Chad says it\'s not her fault, she didn\'t know. Sky says there must be a way to help at least some of them. "We will stop Xima\'s ritual." "Whatever it takes." "...Yes. I won\'t let any more people suffer because of me."',
  art:'Pages show: the shaman works with Greyson and calls Xima "he" here. The Prologue\'s lunar eclipse birth is now tied to Xima\'s ritual. Jade takes guilt for the taken villagers. This shaman is not obviously the one from Chapter 16 (who told her of the test of love).',
  quote:'"The girl born under the lunar eclipse... Xima believes her blood can complete the ritual and open the way to something far worse." — the Shaman',
  events:['The party finds the shaman\'s hut','The shaman explains how Xima corrupts villagers as vessels','He reveals Xima\'s larger ritual needs Jade\'s blood','Jade blames herself','The party vows to stop the ritual'],
  purpose:['Lore chapter: the ritual and Jade\'s role','Set the next objective: stop Xima\'s ritual'],
  unlocks:['Main quest: stop Xima\'s ritual','Codex: the ritual, the Shaman'],
  reward:'Objective: stop the ritual'},
 38:{ title:'The Village Beneath the Mask', type:'Story Chapter — investigation and a warning', loc:'🏘 Village near Vigil → 🌲 Forest edge',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally; Xima (final scene)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the incident in the forest the party keeps investigating; the more they learn, the more unnatural the village becomes. Everything feels too deliberate, as if someone has been watching them and waiting. Levi examines the markings they found near the forest: "These are not just warnings. They are tracking marks." Someone has been watching the village. Jade asks why they haven\'t attacked; "Because they don\'t need to." They are observing, not hunting: studying. Soon after, a merchant brings a package from King Greyson with a book, medicine ingredients and a piece of cloth. A parchment reads "Do not pursue the enemy\'s nest. They want you here", written in code. Jade realises Greyson is warning them that the enemy wants them to find the nest; Sky says then this is a trap. Levi becomes even more suspicious: every clue points in one direction, someone is guiding us. Jade: "You think it\'s a trap?" Levi: "I think they wanted us here from the beginning." Meanwhile Chad spends more time with Sally, who asks: "Are you really protecting me... or are you hiding from her?" Sky discovers several villagers suffering the same strange illness: "This is not natural. They aren\'t Xima\'s soldiers. They are victims." That night Jade tries to help one of the infected villagers; the moment she touches them her power reacts and the corruption inside them disappears, even if only slightly. Sky says: "Your power isn\'t meant to destroy. It\'s meant to restore." The realisation frightens her: "So this is... my bloodline\'s true purpose..." Levi says whatever this is, it\'s bigger than they imagined and they must be careful from now on. That night the village looks peaceful, but many truths are hidden. Deep in the forest a demon kneels before Xima, who is shown as a woman in red under a blood-red moon: "The girl has awakened." "So the Gold child has finally returned." "Bring them to me." In her dreams a red light appears.',
  art:'Pages show: Xima is drawn as a woman in a red gown here, and the corruption in the villagers partly clears at Jade\'s touch, which is the first sign her power restores. Sally also asks Chad whether he is hiding from Jade.',
  quote:'"Your power isn\'t meant to destroy. It\'s meant to restore." — Sky Yale',
  events:['Levi decodes the markings: they are tracking marks','Greyson\'s coded package: "Do not pursue the enemy\'s nest. They want you here"','The party concludes it is a trap and someone is guiding them','Sally asks Chad whether he is hiding from Jade','Sky finds villagers with a slow corruption: victims, not soldiers','Jade\'s touch partly cleanses an infected villager','Xima: "The girl has awakened. Bring them to me."'],
  purpose:['Establish the trap: the player is being herded toward the enemy\'s nest','Show Jade\'s power as restorative (a healing and cleansing theme)','Set up the ambush in the next chapter'],
  unlocks:['Coded messages from Greyson','Cleansing touch (Jade, suggested skill)','Investigation events'],
  reward:'The trap is revealed'},
 39:{ title:'Beneath the Quiet Village', type:'Story Chapter — descent into the hidden chamber', loc:'🏘 Village → 🕯 Hidden chamber beneath the village',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The village still looks peaceful on the surface, but now they know the peace is only a mask. Jade and Levi notice strange villagers moving secretly at night toward an old abandoned building: they aren\'t just going home, they are heading somewhere. Sky finds that several villagers have gone missing and the herbs around the area are tainted with something unnatural. Sally gathers information from frightened villagers: "After midnight... people are taken beneath the village. No one who goes down ever returns." Chad: "We investigate now. We can\'t wait any longer. This ends tonight." Following the clues they find a hidden route beneath the village and, below it, a hidden chamber: a place of worship for Xima and her followers. Jade feels a strange pulse; her dormant power reacts to Xima\'s presence: "It feels... familiar." Levi takes position at the rear with his bow, Chad stands at the front and Sky prepares to support and heal. Sally finds records and offerings: "The village has been providing information and sacrifices to Xima\'s followers for years. They traded people... for power." A spectral image of Xima appears above the altar: "Jade... You have finally arrived. This village has always been part of my network. You were expected to come here. Everything leads to me, as it always does." Jade realises the village is part of a larger network serving Xima and that the villagers were never innocent. Xima\'s voice echoes: "The ritual will begin tomorrow night. By then, a new offering will be made. Will you be the final one, Jade?" Jade: "We end this. No more sacrifices. Tomorrow night, we destroy it." They must destroy the hidden altar before the ritual begins tomorrow night. Banners: Jade + Levi Bond +1, Sky + Sally Bond +1, Jade + Chad Tension +1.',
  art:'Pages show: the village has been supplying sacrifices and information to Xima\'s followers for years, which makes the villagers complicit (unlike the taken villagers in Chapters 36-38). Xima appears as a spectral woman in red and says the ritual starts tomorrow night. Positions are stated: Levi at the rear, Chad at the front, Sky supporting.',
  quote:'"Will you be the final one, Jade?" — Xima',
  events:['Villagers are seen moving secretly to an abandoned building at night','Sky finds missing villagers and tainted herbs','Sally learns people are taken beneath the village after midnight','The party finds a hidden route and a chamber of worship for Xima','Sally finds records of years of sacrifices','Xima\'s spectral image speaks: the ritual begins tomorrow night','Jade vows to destroy the altar'],
  purpose:['Exploration and investigation: the descent into the chamber','Reveal that the village is part of Xima\'s network','Start the countdown to the ritual (tomorrow night)'],
  unlocks:['Hidden chamber dungeon (suggested)','Countdown objective: destroy the altar before the ritual'],
  reward:'Objective: destroy the altar'},
 40:{ title:'The Night Before the Offering', type:'Story Chapter — preparation and a dream', loc:'🏘 Vigil Village (lodging) → 🌲 road to the hidden altar',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After leaving the hidden chamber the party returns to the village. The truth is clearer now: the villagers were not willingly serving Xima but living in fear. The village seems peaceful, but the silence feels different. Everyone knows that tomorrow night something will happen. Back at their lodging Jade decodes Greyson\'s message: "Do not chase Xima. The altar is a trap. She wants the Gold child to come to her. Prepare, do not pursue. — G". The hidden altar was not a place to attack, but a trap. Xima had been waiting; tomorrow night she expects Jade to come to her. That night Jade sits alone, unable to sleep: "Every time my power appears, someone gets hurt." Levi tells her: "No. People get hurt because someone chooses to harm them. Your power is not the problem, Jade. It is a part of you. And you are not a curse. You are still you, the same Jade who saves people." In another room Chad prepares their weapons: "No matter what happens tomorrow, I won\'t let anyone else get hurt." Sally watches him quietly: "Are you afraid?" "Of course. I just don\'t have the luxury to show it." Sally: "You\'ve already proven yourself, Chad. You don\'t need to carry everything alone anymore." Sky examines more villagers and finds the same corruption: the markings react strongly to Jade\'s presence, the corruption is tied to Xima\'s ritual and resonates with Jade\'s blood, so tomorrow night Jade may become the target. That night Jade falls into a troubled sleep. In her dream a familiar figure appears: "You finally returned. You don\'t remember, but your blood does. The world forgot what you are... but I never did. Tonight... the Gold child awakens." Jade wakes with a start: "...It felt so real..." At dawn the party sets out for the hidden altar. They would walk into Xima\'s trap, but this time they would be ready. Beneath the village, at the hidden altar, Xima waits with her followers. Progression: Jade + Levi Bond +1, Sky + Jade Bond +1, Chad + Sally Bond +1, Jade + Chad remains distant.',
  art:'Pages show: Greyson\'s decoded message is a direct warning, so walking in is a deliberate choice. The dream repeats Xima\'s "the Gold child awakens". Levi becomes Jade\'s emotional support, while Chad (with Sally) stays apart from her.',
  quote:'"Do not chase Xima. The altar is a trap. She wants the Gold child to come to her. Prepare, do not pursue." — Greyson',
  events:['The party returns to the village, knowing the villagers act out of fear','Jade decodes Greyson\'s message: the altar is a trap','Levi reassures Jade that her power is not a curse','Chad prepares the weapons; Sally tells him he doesn\'t have to carry everything alone','Sky finds the corruption reacting to Jade\'s blood','Jade dreams of Xima: the Gold child awakens','The party sets out at dawn, prepared','Bonds: Jade + Levi +1, Sky + Jade +1, Chad + Sally +1'],
  purpose:['Preparation night: last chance to shop, rest and talk to the party','Build tension before the major battle'],
  unlocks:['Bond events (Levi, Sky)','Preparation: shop, rest and tonics before the battle'],
  reward:'Prepared for the trap'},
 41:{ title:'The Offering at Moonrise', type:'Story Chapter — the major battle', loc:'🏘 Vigil → 🌲 northern forest → 🏛 ancient ruin and altar in a hidden clearing',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky and Levi fight; Sally guides the rescued woman to safety',
  introduced:['Cultists in black robes and masked villagers','A young woman chosen as the offering','Xima (appears above the altar)'],
  sum:'At moonrise the village of Vigil is no longer peaceful. In silence the villagers leave their homes carrying lanterns toward the northern forest. The party follows from the shadows, realising the villagers have been living in fear and serving a darker purpose ("This village was never truly at peace." "We move quietly. Stay together."). Levi scouts ahead and spots masked villagers and black-robed cultists heading toward an ancient ruin hidden deep in the forest. In a hidden clearing the villagers prepare an offering: a young woman is brought before the ancient altar, where the symbols of Xima glow in crimson light. Sally: "The villagers have been living in fear. They obey Xima\'s followers, believing these offerings keep them safe. They had no choice." Chad: "This ends now. I\'ll strike and take them all down. Levi, cover us." "Understood." Sky: "I\'ll keep healing and provide protection." Jade: "You will not take her. Stay behind me." She rushes forward and cuts the offering free: "You\'re safe. Come with us!" The battle begins: cultists and shadow creatures emerge from the forest. Levi\'s arrows strike from the shadows, Sky shields the group and heals the injured, and Sally guides the rescued woman to safety. As the altar pulses with crimson light, Jade feels a strange call stir within her, deeper and stronger than before: "...What is this...? It feels like her... calling to me..." Above the ruined altar a feminine figure appears: Xima. Her voice echoes, soft yet unmistakably powerful: "Little Gold Child... you have stepped onto the true path at last. This was only the beginning."',
  art:'Pages show: this is the first full fight at the altar; Jade cuts the offering free with a dagger glowing red, which fits Greyson\'s gift becoming usable at the major battle. Xima appears as a spectral woman and the fight does not end with her defeat.',
  quote:'"Little Gold Child... you have stepped onto the true path at last. This was only the beginning." — Xima',
  events:['The villagers leave with lanterns at moonrise; the party follows','Levi finds the ruin with cultists and masked villagers','A young woman is chosen as the offering at the altar','Jade cuts the offering free','Battle: cultists and shadow creatures','Sally leads the rescued woman away','The altar\'s call awakens something in Jade','Xima appears above the altar'],
  purpose:['Major battle: protect the offering and fight through the altar guardians','Unseal Greyson\'s dagger and flail (Jade)','Xima\'s first direct appearance'],
  unlocks:['Boss battle: the Offering Warden','Greyson\'s dagger and flail unlocked (Jade)'],
  reward:'Major battle won; Greyson\'s dagger and flail unsealed'},
 42:{ title:'After the Fall', type:'Story Chapter — the cost of the battle', loc:'🌲 Hidden altar → wise healer\'s hut',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky, Levi and Sally',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After Xima\'s appearance the forest altar erupts with crimson energy and shadow creatures surge forward. Xima\'s presence presses down on the battlefield: "At last... the Gold Child awakens. This is only the beginning." Chad steps forward to defend the party ("No one else will die today."), Levi takes high ground and looses arrows, Sky raises a barrier of healing light around the villagers, and Sally pulls rescued villagers to safety. The altar\'s power resonates with Jade\'s blood and a crimson-gold light stirs in her ("It feels familiar... like it\'s calling to me..."). A cursed strike rushes toward Jade and the villagers; Sky throws himself in the way and is struck. In grief and fury Jade\'s hidden power partially awakens: a wave of crimson light tears through the shadows and forces the enemies back. Xima watches with satisfaction: "Yes... the Gold Child has awakened. But this is only the beginning." The cultists retreat, the altar cracks and the crimson storm subsides: the battle is won, but at a terrible cost. Jade holds Sky in her arms ("Stay with me. Please, don\'t go... You always do..."); Chad says "You\'re stronger than this. Don\'t leave us." Sky\'s wound is grave; even his healing light cannot fully close it ("I\'m sorry... I couldn\'t do more... It\'s not your fault..."). They carry him through the night to a wise healer\'s hut, where the elder shaman examines him: "Ordinary medicine will not save him. Only the Pearl of Dragonvale can heal this wound now." Jade: "The Pearl of Dragonvale...? Then... we have to go." Progression: Jade\'s Power Awakened (Partial); Sky Condition: Critical; Next Destination: Dragonvale.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade\'s power awakens partially in this chapter. Sky is gravely cursed by the strike, which sets up his being in the party but unable to fight.',
  quote:'"Only the Pearl of Dragonvale can heal this wound now." — the elder shaman',
  events:['The altar erupts; the party defends the villagers','A cursed strike hits Sky as he shields Jade','Jade\'s power partially awakens and drives back the shadows','The cultists retreat; the battle is won at a terrible cost','The elder shaman says only the Pearl of Dragonvale can save Sky','Next destination: Dragonvale'],
  purpose:['Aftermath of the major battle; Sky is critically wounded and cannot fight (disabled in the party)','Open the Dragonvale arc'],
  unlocks:['Sky: Critical (stays in the party but cannot fight)','Next destination: Dragonvale'],
  reward:'Jade partially awakened; Sky critical'},
 43:{ title:'The Price of Awakening', type:'Story Chapter — the deadline', loc:'🏘 First post near Vigil → road to Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Levi and Sally (Sky unconscious)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party brings Sky back to the first post. The village bears the scars of war, but there is no time to rest. Sky lies in deep unconsciousness and no matter how hard he fought, his body cannot heal (Chad: "I\'m not leaving his side."). The elder shaman examines him with ancient spiritual arts: "This is no ordinary injury. A dark curse has entered too deeply into his body." The only cure is the Dragonvale Pearl, which contains the pure essence of ancient dragons and can purify the curse, but time is short: Sky has only forty-nine days left to live. On the way back Jade feels her awakened power stirring restlessly and has her first direct vision from Xima: "Little Gold Child... the path to Dragonvale leads you deeper to me. Your awakening is only the beginning." She wakes shaken: "Xima... She knows. She\'s calling to me..." Despite the pain and uncertainty their resolve is clear: "We leave immediately for Dragonvale. We have forty-nine days. We can\'t waste any more time." "We save Sky. No matter what it takes." With heavy hearts they set out to find the Pearl, save Sky and face whatever truth awaits them, with Dragonvale\'s white palace shown on a waterfall cliff.',
  art:'Pages show: a forty-nine day deadline (a story countdown). Xima speaks to Jade directly for the first time and wants her to go to Dragonvale.',
  quote:'"We save Sky. No matter what it takes." — the party',
  events:['The party returns to the first post with Sky','The shaman: a dark curse; only the Dragonvale Pearl can cure it','Sky has forty-nine days to live','Jade\'s first direct vision from Xima','The party sets out for Dragonvale'],
  purpose:['Introduce the forty-nine day countdown (story only; the in-game day counter is separate)','Hand off to the Dragonvale arc'],
  unlocks:['Dragonvale quest: find the Pearl'],
  reward:'Journey to Dragonvale begins'},
 44:{ title:'The King\'s Hidden Gift', type:'Story Chapter — Greyson\'s gift and arrival', loc:'🏯 Imperial Capital → 🚗 road → 🏰 Dragonvale palace gate and inner palace',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Sky (carried), Levi, Sally, King Greyson',
  introduced:['Delilah (Dragonvale Royal Consort)','A Dragonvale envoy','Dima (in Jade\'s dream)'],
  sum:'After a gruelling journey the party returns to Tribute with Sky, gravely weakened, hoping for the Dragonvale Pearl; time is short and the road ahead more perilous. King Greyson tells Jade: "The Dragonvale Pearl is the only known cure for Sky\'s condition. But time is limited. You must go to Dragonvale at once." He gives her a sealed box: "It is a gift from me for the Dragonvale King. And one more thing: this bracelet allows us to communicate privately. Do not open the box until you stand before the Dragonvale King. You will know when the time is right. Trust me. Until then, say nothing of this box to anyone." The party leaves with urgency: Levi stays close to Sky, and Chad and Sally ready the arrangements and secure an escort. Before leaving, Chad speaks quietly with a Dragonvale envoy: "Remember, Jade is only an Imperial Guard. No special title, no closer connection. Keep her introduction simple." On the road Jade falls into a restless sleep and meets Dima in a realm of light: "Jade... We have finally met. The path ahead is more than you know. The box you carry holds a truth that will change everything. You will face trials, but you are not alone. The light remembers you. Listen to your heart. For what sleeps in Dragonvale will awaken not only a king... but a greater fate." At last they arrive, but Jade is not brought before the king: she is received only as an Imperial Guard and told to stay within the inner palace grounds until further notice. Delilah, the Dragonvale Royal Consort, meets her: "So this is the Imperial Guard from Tribute... Hmph. You\'re nothing more than a guard, are you? Know your place while you are in Dragonvale."',
  art:'Pages show: Greyson\'s bracelet replaces the pigeon post. Chad deliberately hides Jade\'s status, and Delilah is named on the page as the Dragonvale Royal Consort. Dima appears for the first time (golden light).',
  quote:'"Do not open the box until you stand before the Dragonvale King." — King Greyson',
  events:['Greyson gives Jade a sealed gift for the Dragonvale King and a private communication bracelet','Chad tells a Dragonvale envoy to present Jade as only an Imperial Guard','Jade dreams of Dima, who warns of trials','The party arrives in Dragonvale; Jade is confined to the inner palace','Delilah puts Jade in her place'],
  purpose:['Introduce Dragonvale and its court politics','Replace pigeon post with the communication bracelet'],
  unlocks:['Communication bracelet (instant letters from Greyson)','Sealed box (quest item)','Dragonvale unlocked'],
  reward:'Bracelet and sealed box received; arrival in Dragonvale'},
 45:{ title:'The Guest Without a Name', type:'Story Chapter — a test in the palace', loc:'🏰 Dragonvale inner palace',
  chars:['jade','chad','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Levi, Sally, Delilah (Sky resting)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Within Dragonvale\'s inner palace Jade is treated as a guest without a name, confined to the palace grounds while Sky remains weak and the party waits for an audience with the king. Chad makes his position clear: "She is only an Imperial Guard from Tribute. Do not announce her further, and let no rumours place her in a higher position." Jade soon realises she cannot move freely; eyes follow her everywhere. Delilah approaches with a measured smile: "You must be tired from your journey. The palace can be overwhelming for a guest. Please, let me show you around." Without warning Delilah loses her balance and falls near Jade: "Please... do not blame Lady Jade. I\'m sure she didn\'t mean it..." The palace women whisper ("Did the foreign guard push her?"). Jade stays composed: "I did not touch her. She fell on her own." Chad hesitates: to challenge this now would only complicate things for Jade. Later Levi tells Jade: "She staged it. I saw it. Her step was deliberate." "I know. This is not the first time, and it will not be the last." Sally tells Chad that Delilah is not trying to steal anyone: she is deciding whether Jade deserves a place in Dragonvale, and if Jade cannot withstand this, meeting the king will bring far greater dangers. Sky, weak, tells her "Jade... you can\'t fight this openly. For now, we endure it." Delilah, recovered, smiles at Jade: "Such a shame. Accidents do happen in the palace." In Dragonvale blades were useless against silk and smiles; Jade holds the box that could change everything.',
  art:'Pages show: Delilah stages a fall to discredit Jade. Sally explains it as a test of Jade\'s worth, not romance.',
  quote:'"In Dragonvale, blades were useless against silk and smiles." — narration',
  events:['Chad keeps Jade\'s identity low','Delilah befriends Jade, then stages a fall','The palace women blame Jade','Levi confirms Delilah staged it','Sally explains it is a test of Jade\'s worth','The party chooses to endure for now'],
  purpose:['Court intrigue chapter: no combat; the player must stay calm (suggested dialogue choice)','Establish Delilah as Jade\'s rival'],
  unlocks:['Court reputation (suggested)'],
  reward:'Delilah tests Jade'},
 46:{ title:'The Walls Between Us', type:'Story Chapter — separated', loc:'🏰 Separate wing of the Dragonvale palace → 🌙 Royal Healing Pavilion',
  chars:['jade','chad','levi','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Levi, Sky, Jenika Moon, Ripley, Delilah',
  introduced:['Ripley (Jade\'s assigned handmaiden)','Jenika Moon (Royal Healer)'],
  sum:'Fourteen days have passed. Jade has waited for Chad to return with news of the Pearl, but he has been occupied with Delilah and has not come to see her. She continues to wait in a separate wing of the royal palace, separated from Levi, attended by loyal handmaidens. Ripley introduces herself: "I am Ripley, assigned to attend to Lady Jade\'s needs from now on." Levi remains in a different wing with limited contact: they can only send occasional messages through trusted attendants. Sky is recovering at the Royal Healing Pavilion under the care of Jenika Moon, the royal healer; his condition remains fragile, but he is slowly regaining his strength. The Royal Healing Pavilion is unlocked and Sky can now be visited. During these fourteen days Chad has been with Delilah: they have grown closer, reconciling their differences. After many days Chad finally comes to see Jade and presses her with his influence: "If you become my woman, I might request an audience with the king right away." "I cannot." "Think carefully. My position can give you what you want." "I have my duty. I must stay focused on saving Sky. There are many matters I must still handle. I will not become yours." Chad leaves in frustration. Delilah comes to Jade: "You should know your place, Jade. Chad and I have grown closer than ever. It would be wise for you to stay away from him," resting a hand on her stomach with a smile full of warning. Jade thinks: "It hurts... to see them together. But I cannot let emotions cloud my purpose. The sealed box holds an important duty... I have to save Sky."',
  art:'Pages show: Ripley appears here as Jade\'s handmaiden. Jenika Moon is named as the royal healer, and her Royal Healing Pavilion unlocks. Delilah\'s hand on her stomach hints at pregnancy.',
  quote:'"I will not become yours." — Jade Gold',
  events:['Ripley is assigned to attend Jade','Jade and Levi are kept in separate wings','Sky recovers at the Royal Healing Pavilion under Jenika Moon','Chad has been with Delilah for fourteen days','Chad pressures Jade for an exclusive relationship; she refuses','Delilah warns Jade away'],
  purpose:['Introduce Ripley and Jenika','Unlock the Royal Healing Pavilion (rest, cures, tonics)'],
  unlocks:['Royal Healing Pavilion unlocked (Jenika Moon)','Ripley introduced'],
  reward:'Royal Healing Pavilion unlocked'},
 47:{ title:'The Prince with a Condition', type:'Story Chapter — a wrong turn', loc:'🏰 Dragonvale corridors → Prince Devon\'s chamber',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade (alone)',
  introduced:['Prince Devon (first appearance)','An elderly man (secluded meeting)'],
  sum:'Tired of waiting and worried for Sky, Jade can no longer remain confined. That night she escapes from the guest wing. She sees Chad and Delilah heading to a secluded chamber to meet an elderly man ("The pearl... it has to be with them.") and listens in hiding: "As we discussed, the preparations must be complete before the next moon." "Leave the rest to me. Once the time is right, everything will fall into place." She cannot learn the full truth. Delilah turns as if sensing someone and Jade withdraws. She flees through the palace and takes a wrong turn into a different wing, then enters a chamber to hide. A man looks up from a scroll: strikingly handsome and unmistakably the twin of Chad, yet different: colder, more regal. It is Prince Devon. When guards arrive ("Prince Devon, forgive us. A trespasser was seen nearby. We will search the surrounding corridors") Devon has already pulled Jade onto his bed, hiding her beneath the covers. "Then look elsewhere. No one is here." The guards bow deeply and retreat at once. Jade notices a faint, mysterious blue glow in the room, which must be the pearl, but cannot see it clearly. After the guards leave she kneels before him: "Please... I beg you. I need the pearl to save Sky\'s life." Devon: "Stand up. If you want my help... I have a condition."',
  art:'Pages show: Devon is explicitly Chad\'s twin. Guards fear him. A blue glowing object in his room seems to be the pearl (the Black Pearl of Chapter 48).',
  quote:'"If you want my help... I have a condition." — Prince Devon',
  events:['Jade escapes the guest wing and overhears Chad and Delilah meeting an elderly man','Preparations must be complete before the next moon','Jade hides in Prince Devon\'s chamber; he shields her from the guards','Jade notices a glowing object that must be the pearl','Devon will help on a condition'],
  purpose:['Stealth sequence through the palace (suggested)','Introduce Prince Devon'],
  unlocks:['Prince Devon introduced (not recruitable yet)'],
  reward:'Devon offers help for a price'},
 48:{ title:'The Trial of Love', type:'Story Chapter — the Trial of Love', loc:'🏰 Jade\'s chamber → Royal Healing Pavilion',
  chars:['jade','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Sky, Jenika Moon (Chad and Delilah seen)',
  introduced:['Dima (in a vision)','Xima (in a vision)','Jenika Moon (full introduction)'],
  sum:'After her escape Jade returns to her chambers with more questions than answers. Devon had only said: "I will send someone for you in a few days." Sleep does not come easily; her heart remains with Sky and with the strange prince who helped her. A yellow radiance envelops Jade: Dima says "Jade... I have come to restore your vitality, purity, and your fate. Dear girl, there is a reason your memory of the past was wiped. You must not give in to your deepest desires... nor to Xima\'s dark offers. You have no destiny with him. Your destiny lies with the owner of the Black Pearl. Only through him can your cousin have a chance of living. This is the Trial of Love." Jade wonders if the Sage\'s test was what she felt for Chad. A red voice follows: "Gold child, you know what you want most. I can help you achieve it... if you pledge yourself to me, and not to my sister Dima." Jade: "Begone." Elsewhere Jenika Moon discovers that several vials of a potent material have gone missing. The next day a letter summons Jade to the Royal Healing Pavilion. "I am Jenika Moon, Prince Devon and Roc Chad\'s cousin, and Dragonvale\'s imperial physician. Please, have a seat." She marks Jade\'s arm ("Only a small examination mark. Please relax."). Sky, better now, thanks Jade; his eyes keep drifting toward Jenika, and Jade notices, smiling knowingly. Jade then sees Chad with Delilah: "Be careful, my love. Our child." "I will always protect you and our child." The sight stings, but Sky\'s life and the duty in her hands matter more. Now she knows she is tied to both Dima and Xima, and the Trial of Love has only just begun.',
  art:'Pages show: Dima and Xima are sisters (Xima: "my sister Dima"). Sky is Jade\'s cousin per Dima, and the Black Pearl belongs to Devon. Delilah is carrying Chad\'s child. Jenika is the cousin of both princes.',
  quote:'"Your destiny lies with the owner of the Black Pearl." — Dima',
  events:['Dima restores Jade and warns her about Xima\'s offers','Dima says Jade\'s destiny lies with the owner of the Black Pearl','Xima offers power if Jade pledges herself to her instead of Dima','Jenika Moon introduces herself as the princes\' cousin and the imperial physician','Sky shows interest in Jenika','Jade sees Chad promise to protect Delilah and their child'],
  purpose:['Lore chapter: Dima, Xima, the Black Pearl and the Trial of Love','Establish Jenika and Sky'],
  unlocks:['Royal Healing Pavilion (Jenika) available'],
  reward:'Jade learns her destiny is tied to both sisters'},
 49:{ title:'The Prince\'s Silent Test', type:'Story Chapter — the boat trip', loc:'🏰 Royal Healing Pavilion → 🌙 moonlit royal boat',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade, Ripley, Devon, Jenika',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'At last a long-awaited invitation arrives from Prince Devon: "Prince Devon invites you to a private moonlit sightseeing boat trip. I hope you will grace me with your presence." With the Black Pearl secured and Sky having a cure, Jade accepts: "I give you my word, Prince Devon." On the same day the Black Pearl is delivered to the Royal Healing Pavilion, and Jenika holds it: "It\'s even more beautiful than I expected. With this, Sky\'s recovery will continue smoothly." One week later Jade heads to the venue with Ripley, carrying an access pass and the invitation. Prince Devon waits alone on the royal boat and only Jade is permitted to board. Inside they enjoy wine, a game of Go and conversation: "What kinds of things do you like, Jade?" "I enjoy beautiful scenery, good tea, interesting people... and nights like this. And you, Prince Devon?" "Quiet moments like this... are more precious than I expected." They kiss. The next morning Jade wakes to find that Devon stayed on the deck, keeping his distance so she could rest: "He truly let me rest. He is so gentle and respectful... His kiss was gentle... so different from Chad\'s forceful passion." A messenger arrives: "Lady Jade, His Majesty summons you."',
  art:'Pages show: the Black Pearl is delivered and used for Sky\'s care. Devon is Jade\'s calm, gentle contrast to Chad.',
  quote:'"Quiet moments like this... are more precious than I expected." — Prince Devon',
  events:['Devon invites Jade to a moonlit boat trip','The Black Pearl is delivered to the Royal Healing Pavilion for Sky','Jade and Devon share wine, Go and a kiss on the boat','Devon lets her rest and keeps his distance','The king summons Jade'],
  purpose:['Romance scene: Jade and Devon (no combat)','Black Pearl secured; Sky\'s cure begins'],
  unlocks:['Bond (planned): Jade × Devon (Devon not yet recruitable)','Black Pearl delivered'],
  reward:'Black Pearl delivered; the king\'s summons'},
 50:{ title:'The Princess and the Decree', type:'Story Chapter — the royal court', loc:'👑 Dragonvale royal court → Levi\'s quarters',
  chars:['jade','chad','levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Chad, Devon, Levi, King Chadstone',
  introduced:['King Chadstone (ruler of Dragonvale; father of Roc and Devon)'],
  sum:'Jade is summoned to the royal court and prostrates before King Chadstone, ruler of Dragonvale and father of Princes Roc and Devon. She presents the sealed box: "This is a gift from King Greyson of Tribute, Your Majesty." Inside is a precious tribute and a formal scroll detailing Jade\'s noble identity, her lifelong contributions and her elevation to Princess of Tribute. The king reads in silence and keeps its contents to himself; Jade is surprised, having not known what was inside. "From this day forth, I officially bestow upon you the title of Princess of Tribute, in honor of your noble identity and your many contributions. You have been a true friend to Dragonvale, and your dedication to saving Sky shall be remembered." The court is stunned. The king demands to know why such an esteemed guest was never announced, and his expression hardens when he learns Prince Roc kept Jade\'s presence a secret. He then issues a royal decree: "To strengthen the ties between Tribute and Dragonvale, Princess Jade may choose one of my unmarried princes for marriage. The chosen prince may cast aside any consorts or concubines, for you are now a princess, and this marriage shall unite our kingdoms." Jade respectfully asks for one day to give her answer. As she speaks she glances toward Prince Devon, and Prince Roc notices, his anger burning more fiercely. The king ends court with a polite smile and orders Roc to stay behind. Jade goes to Levi\'s quarters and finds him pale and weak, preparing to leave: "I only see you as a sister, Jade. The one in my heart is still the princess I am searching for." "I feel the same, Levi. Our alliance was always a matter of duty, not romantic love." "You\'re free now. I will be leaving the party. I must continue my search alone." Levi gives Jade his blessing and departs alone, without revealing where he is going. With Levi gone, Jade resolves to seek Prince Devon\'s help, both to save Sky and to uncover the hidden schemes within Dragonvale.',
  art:'Pages show: the King reads the same scroll and keeps it secret. Jade is made Princess of Tribute and chooses one of the unmarried princes. Levi, pale and weak, leaves the party as planned, ending his engagement with Jade by mutual agreement.',
  quote:'"Princess Jade may choose one of my unmarried princes for marriage." — King Chadstone',
  events:['Jade presents Greyson\'s sealed box to King Chadstone','The scroll makes Jade Princess of Tribute','The court learns Roc hid her presence','The king decrees Jade may choose an unmarried prince','Jade asks for a day to answer','Levi and Jade mutually end their engagement; Levi leaves the party alone','Jade resolves to ask Devon for help'],
  purpose:['Levi leaves the party','The sealed box is delivered and removed from the pack','Major political turning point: marriage decree'],
  unlocks:['Levi leaves the party','Princess of Tribute title','Marriage choice (decree)'],
  reward:'Princess of Tribute; Levi departs'},
 51:{ title:'The Prince She Chose', type:'Story Chapter — the proposal', loc:'🏰 Jade\'s chamber → Prince Devon\'s residence',
  chars:['jade','chad','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Roc, Delilah, Sally',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Delilah does not fear Jade choosing Prince Roc. What she truly fears is that whoever Jade allies with could threaten Roc\'s future as crown prince. Each move Jade makes could shift the balance of power, which is why Delilah watches her closely with jealousy and unease. Prince Roc storms into Jade\'s chamber, demanding that she reject the marriage decree: "Reject it! You cannot marry him!" "My lord, I wish to rest tonight. Please leave." Delilah watches Jade turn Roc away with a satisfied smile, though deep down she is still jealous of Roc\'s affection for Jade. Sally has now been granted a noble title as compensation for her past companionship with Roc; she remains part of the wider party but no longer as his lover. Later Jade receives a letter left behind by Levi, and after much thought walks through the quiet palace corridors toward Prince Devon\'s residence with her access pass and the marriage decree. Devon is alone, reading a scroll; his eyes light up for a brief moment before returning to his usual cold composure. Jade kneels and makes her proposal: "I wish to become your wife in name only. We do not need to be true husband and wife. We only need to play the part, and after one year, you may write me a letter of divorce. I will be your most powerful ally in your ambition. I come from a lineage of advisors, and I will do my utmost to support you. I will protect you with my life." Devon: "What\'s in it for me?" Jade: "If you want more, then I will give you more. Whatever you want." Devon steps closer, his gaze intent yet controlled: "What if I want more? What if I want more than a pretend couple?" He kisses her. Jade is dumbstruck, her heart fluttering, not expecting his answer.',
  art:'Pages show: Sally receives a noble title and is no longer Roc\'s lover. Jade proposes a one-year marriage of convenience to Devon, which he turns into something real. The chapter ends here for now.',
  quote:'"What if I want more than a pretend couple?" — Prince Devon',
  events:['Roc demands Jade reject the decree; she sends him away','Delilah fears for Roc\'s future as crown prince','Sally receives a noble title and stays with the party','Jade reads Levi\'s letter','Jade proposes a one-year marriage in name to Devon','Devon: "What if I want more?" and kisses her'],
  purpose:['Resolve Jade\'s choice of prince','Sally gains a noble skill (Noble Grace)'],
  unlocks:['Sally: noble title and new skill','Jade\'s choice: Prince Devon (the wedding is in a later chapter)'],
  reward:'Jade chooses Devon; Sally ennobled'},
 52:{ title:'The Princess\'s Choice', type:'Story Chapter — the choice', loc:'👑 Dragonvale royal court → Jade\'s chambers → Dragonvale market district',
  chars:['jade','chad','sky','sally','ripley'], charsNote:'Jade, Ripley and Sally (King Chadstone; Roc, Devon mentioned)',
  introduced:['Ripley (full introduction)','Sally, Noblewoman (at the market)'],
  sum:'Jade seeks an audience with King Chadstone to declare her choice. The court listens in silence as she speaks with a clear and unwavering heart: "Your Majesty, I have made my decision. I choose Prince Devon as my husband." The king is pleased: "I am not surprised by your choice. Prince Devon is a worthy partner. You have made a wise decision, Jade." He announces the wedding date: in less than two weeks, a most auspicious date. Though surprised by the quick arrangement, Jade remains composed. Back in her chambers Ripley greets her cheerfully ("I\'m so happy you chose Prince Devon! I\'ll do my best to help with the preparations!"). Ripley is a kind and loyal young woman who serves in the palace: the daughter of an officer who committed treason. Her family fell from grace and she was destined for a harsh fate, but Prince Devon secretly arranged for her to be spared and placed in palace service, giving her a new life. "Prince Roc gave me this opportunity, but my true gratitude is to Prince Devon. He saved me and gave me a future. I will always be loyal to him." Jade and Ripley go shopping in the Dragonvale market, dressed as noblewomen, for fabrics and hair ornaments for the wedding ceremony. They meet Sally in the market district: "Lady Jade! It\'s a pleasure to see you." Sally tells her Prince Roc has been punished by the king for keeping Jade hidden and treating her badly, ordered to reflect on his actions, his influence greatly limited, and offers to share court news: "If you ever wish to know what is happening in court, I can share what I hear. I have many sources." Banners: Ripley joins the party (Loyal Companion); Sally, Source of Gossip unlocked (may provide valuable information about the royal court). Back in her chambers Jade\'s communication bracelet glows with a message from Greyson: "You have a new message."',
  art:'Pages show: Ripley\'s loyalty is to Devon (as planned), and the banner lists her as a Loyal Companion. Roc has been punished and sidelined. Sally appears as a Noblewoman and becomes a source of court gossip.',
  quote:'"Your Majesty, I have made my decision. I choose Prince Devon as my husband." — Jade',
  events:['Jade declares her choice: Prince Devon','The king sets the wedding in less than two weeks','Ripley\'s backstory: a traitor\'s daughter spared by Devon','Shopping for the wedding with Ripley','Sally reveals Roc has been punished and offers court gossip','Greyson sends a message'],
  purpose:['Ripley joins the party','Unlock Sally\'s court gossip (information source)'],
  unlocks:['Ripley joins the party','Sally: Source of Gossip (court information)'],
  reward:'Ripley joins; Sally becomes an informant'},
 53:{ title:'Greyson\'s Hidden Mission', type:'Story Chapter — the sealed archive', loc:'🏰 Jade\'s chambers → Royal Archives and the Hall of Records',
  chars:['jade','ripley','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Ripley, Sally and Greyson (by bracelet)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While preparations for Jade\'s wedding quietly begin, her duty to Tribute has not ended. Greyson calls through her bracelet: "Lady Jade, I congratulate you on your upcoming wedding to Prince Devon. I have a special mission for you. Dragonvale may hold answers about the Black Pearl, the Gold Child, Dima, and Xima. I want you to quietly investigate the sealed records of the late empress and the old royal archives. Not everyone should know about this search." "I understand, Your Majesty. I accept this mission. I will uncover the truth, no matter how long it takes." Jade privately meets Prince Devon ("Chad\'s Twin"): "There is indeed a sealed archive beneath the Hall of Records. Very few people are allowed near it. I can help you access it." Ripley offers to guide her through the outer corridor and keep watch, and Sally shares information from her sources: the late empress\'s records were sealed shortly after her death and few know what is inside. That night Jade and Devon enter the royal archives, which have remained unchanged for many years, and discover a hidden chamber with an ancient mural. It shows Dima, Sister of Light, and Xima, Sister of Darkness, reaching toward the Black Pearl. The inscription reads: "The Gold Child\'s Trial of Love is bound to the Black Pearl. When the pearl returns to its true owner, the two sisters shall rise again. Through love, the worlds may be united or destroyed." Jade realises: "So Dima and Xima... the Black Pearl... and the Trial of Love... It\'s all connected." Devon: "Someone deliberately concealed this truth. These records rewrite everything we thought we knew." "This is only the beginning. If you want the truth, you must continue this mission with me, Jade." "I will. No matter what challenges await, I will stand with you and see this through to the end." Mission Unlocked: The Late Empress\'s Archive (investigate the sealed records, uncover the truth about the Black Pearl, learn the connection between Dima, Xima and the Gold Child).',
  art:'Pages show: Dima and Xima are sisters (Light and Darkness) and the mural ties both to the Black Pearl and the Gold Child. Devon is labelled "Chad\'s Twin". Greyson knows Dragonvale holds answers.',
  quote:'"When the pearl returns to its true owner, the two sisters shall rise again. Through love, the worlds may be united or destroyed." — the mural',
  events:['Greyson sends Jade a secret mission through the bracelet','Devon offers access to the sealed archive beneath the Hall of Records','Ripley and Sally help with guidance and information','Jade and Devon find a mural of Dima and Xima with the Black Pearl','The inscription ties the Trial of Love to the Black Pearl','Mission unlocked: The Late Empress\'s Archive'],
  purpose:['Mission: The Late Empress\'s Archive','Lore chapter: the mural'],
  unlocks:['Mission: The Late Empress\'s Archive','Royal Archives location'],
  reward:'The truth behind the sisters begins to emerge'},
 54:{ title:'The Sealed Truth', type:'Story Chapter — the hidden shrine', loc:'🏰 Royal archives → hidden archive shrine',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade and Devon (Devon joins)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Beyond the mural Jade and Devon discover an even deeper secret within the royal archives of Dragonvale. The truth about the late empress, the Black Pearl and the Trial of Love is not yet complete: a final chamber lies ahead, sealed for generations. Jade notices a hidden symbol among the intricate carvings that feels connected to the mural; as she places her hand near it, the ancient lock responds with a faint light and the sealed door slowly opens, revealing a hidden archive shrine filled with precious records, ceremonial objects and the memories of the late empress. Jade finds documents that were deliberately sealed after the late empress\'s death ("Someone wanted this truth erased."). Devon finds a record that reveals a deeper connection: "The Black Pearl is not only tied to Dragonvale... but also to the Gold Child and the Trial of Love." An ancient ward activates and the chamber\'s defences come to life: "I\'ll protect the records!" "We face this together." Jade and Devon work together to disable the ward, using the knowledge in the archives to calm its ancient mechanisms. They rescue the most important records. Devon: "You were right to come here. These records would have been lost forever otherwise. If you still wish to uncover the truth, let me continue this mission with you." Jade: "Then let us see it through together." Two paths, once separate, are now united: the truth still lies ahead, but Jade no longer walks it alone. Banners: Companion Unlocked, Prince Devon (a new ally joins your journey; he will accompany you in your investigation); Mission Updated: The Late Empress\'s Archive (search the sealed records in the hidden archive, trace the Black Pearl\'s origin, learn the truth behind the Trial of Love).',
  art:'Pages show: the shrine\'s ward is a puzzle-and-defence scene; Jade holds a sword in the ward panel (the art drifts, as noted before). The banner officially unlocks Prince Devon as a companion.',
  quote:'"Two paths, once separate, are now united." — narration',
  events:['The party opens the hidden archive shrine','Jade finds records deliberately sealed after the late empress died','Devon reads that the Black Pearl is tied to the Gold Child and the Trial of Love','An ancient ward activates; Jade and Devon calm it together','Devon asks to continue the mission with Jade','Companion unlocked: Prince Devon'],
  purpose:['Prince Devon joins the party','Puzzle and ward sequence (suggested non-lethal fight with ancient guardians)'],
  unlocks:['Companion unlocked: Prince Devon','Mission updated: The Late Empress\'s Archive'],
  reward:'Prince Devon joins'},
 55:{ title:'The Memory Within the Ink (Part 1)', type:'Story Chapter — the letter', loc:'🏰 Royal archives → Jade\'s chambers',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade and Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After opening the sealed chamber Jade and Devon examine the recovered records of the late empress. Among the ancient scrolls are letters, notes and research about the Gold Child, the Black Pearl and a truth that someone had tried very hard to erase. Devon studies a letter: "This handwriting... It feels familiar." For a brief moment memories from his childhood flash through his mind, a gentle voice, a familiar touch and the scent of flowers, but they disappear as quickly as they came. "You recognize it?" "No... But it feels familiar. Strange. I have no reason to remember this." The records reveal that the late empress had studied the Gold Child prophecy and the Black Pearl, but many important pages were deliberately removed: someone inside the palace hid the truth, and whoever did feared what she knew. Later that night in her chambers Jade takes out the letter Levi left behind, which she has carried all this time, hesitant to read. "I should have read it sooner..." She brings it to Devon and reads it with him. Levi writes: "Jade, if you are reading this, then I have already left Dragonvale. I did not leave because I lost faith in you. I discovered something was wrong with my body. At first I thought it was exhaustion. But the symptoms became clearer. Someone poisoned me. The poison is unusual, slow acting. It was designed not to kill immediately, but to weaken. Whoever did this wanted me alive long enough to suffer. I cannot prove who it was. But I know one thing. It happened inside the palace. Do not follow me. Find the truth. — Levi" Jade: "He was poisoned... Why didn\'t he tell me..." Devon: "Because he knew you would chase after him. Then someone in this palace has been moving unseen. We will find the truth."',
  art:'Pages show: Devon has a faint childhood memory tied to the late empress\'s handwriting, a hint about his parentage (the late empress may be his mother). Levi\'s letter confirms the poisoning happened inside the palace and that he left to protect Jade from chasing him.',
  quote:'"Someone poisoned me... It happened inside the palace. Do not follow me. Find the truth." — Levi',
  events:['Devon feels a flicker of childhood memory at the empress\'s handwriting','The records show important pages were removed on purpose','Jade finally reads Levi\'s letter','Levi was poisoned inside the palace and left to protect her','Jade and Devon resolve to find the truth'],
  purpose:['Investigation: the empress\'s records and Levi\'s letter','Introduce the poisoning mystery'],
  unlocks:['Mission: find who poisoned Levi'],
  reward:'Levi was poisoned'},
 56:{ title:'The Memory Within the Ink (Part 2)', type:'Story Chapter — the missing vials', loc:'🌙 Royal Healing Pavilion → palace → Jade\'s chambers',
  chars:['jade','devon','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika, Sally (Roc and Delilah seen)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade and Devon begin investigating the source of the poison. The clues lead them to the Royal Healing Pavilion, where a restricted material has gone missing. Jenika examines the symptoms described in Levi\'s letter: "This matches a restricted preparation. Several vials of a rare material went missing weeks ago. It was not medicine. In the wrong hands, it could be used to harm someone." Jade: "Someone in the palace did this. They had royal-level access." Devon: "Which means the culprit wanted Levi alive long enough to suffer. This was not an ordinary theft. Only someone with royal-level access could have done it." Sally uses her information network: "Someone entered the Healing Pavilion after hours. They used authorization from a royal-level seal. I wasn\'t able to identify who, but it was definitely someone important." Prince Roc learns that Devon has been accompanying Jade ("So you\'ve been by her side this whole time? You\'re more involved in her investigation than I expected.") and Delilah understands the danger: "If Devon remains by Jade\'s side, every truth she uncovers will only strengthen him. That is unacceptable." That night Jade asks Devon: "Do you ever regret this? Since meeting me, you\'ve been dragged into dangerous matters." Devon: "Our marriage may have begun as an arrangement... But my decision to walk beside you did not. When you entered my chambers while being chased by guards, I knew you were dangerous from the beginning." "Then let\'s find Levi together." "No matter what we uncover, we face it side by side." The wedding preparations continue ("Your Highness only needs to appear. The seamstresses will handle everything. This design combines Dragonvale and Tribute. It will suit you perfectly."). Jade thinks of Levi: "I promised I would find the truth. And now... I am also about to become Devon\'s wife." A missing friend, a hidden poison, a palace full of secrets, and a wedding that could change everything. Three days until the royal wedding.',
  art:'Pages show: the poison used a restricted material stolen from the Healing Pavilion (the vials Jenika noticed missing in Chapter 48) with a royal-level seal. Delilah sees Devon\'s alliance with Jade as a threat. The wedding is three days away. The page titles Chapters 55 and 56 as Parts 1 and 2.',
  quote:'"Our marriage may have begun as an arrangement... But my decision to walk beside you did not." — Prince Devon',
  events:['Jenika identifies the poison as a restricted preparation from missing vials','Sally learns someone with a royal seal entered the pavilion after hours','Roc and Delilah see Devon\'s involvement as a danger','Jade and Devon commit to finding Levi together','Wedding preparations continue; three days remain'],
  purpose:['Investigation: the poison trail leads to the royal court','Countdown to the wedding'],
  unlocks:['Clue: royal-seal access to the Healing Pavilion'],
  reward:'Three days until the wedding'},
 57:{ title:'The Vow We Keep', type:'Story Chapter — the wedding', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal palace (grand hall)',
  chars:['jade','devon','ripley','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Ripley, Sally, King Chadstone and Prince Roc Chadwick',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The day of Jade and Devon\'s wedding has arrived. Dragonvale is adorned with red lanterns and flowers as the royal palace celebrates a new beginning. With Ripley\'s help Jade prepares in her bridal attire ("Your hair ornaments are perfect, Lady Jade. You look absolutely radiant." "Today marks a new chapter. I will face it with a calm heart."). Devon prepares in matching red attire: "Today, I take another step in my duty. I will be a worthy husband, and a steady partner to Jade." The court assembles in the grand hall with King Chadstone presiding: "Today, we witness the union of Princess Jade of Tribute and Prince Devon." Prince Roc Chadwick watches the ceremony in silence. Jade enters the hall ("With gratitude in my heart, I take this step today."); Devon: "You look beautiful, Jade." The king formally blesses their union: "I, King Chadstone, bless the union of Princess Jade of Tribute and Prince Devon Chadstone. May you walk together in trust, in duty, and in a bright future." Together they perform the wedding ceremony, bowing before the king and the court. Roc\'s expression remains unreadable, but a storm lingers in his eyes. Sally and Ripley watch with warm and sincere wishes ("They make a graceful pair." "I\'m so happy for Lady Jade."). Later, alone together for the first time after the wedding, Jade: "We did not begin with love. But today, I choose this path with a clear and peaceful heart." Devon: "No. But we began with truth. We have both been through much. I can give you a lifelong partnership. And I will walk beside you." "Then let us promise this much... a lifelong partnership." "I can give you that. And I will walk beside you." The marriage was not the end of their individual journeys, but the beginning of a new path built on truth, duty and a choice to walk together.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade is called Princess Jade of Tribute at the ceremony; Roc watches in silence with a storm in his eyes. Devon says the marriage began with truth, not love. No mission or banner on this page.',
  quote:'"We did not begin with love." — Jade   "No. But we began with truth." — Devon',
  events:['Jade and Devon prepare for the wedding with Ripley\'s help','King Chadstone presides over the ceremony and blesses the union','Roc watches in silence, a storm in his eyes','Sally and Ripley watch with sincere wishes','Jade and Devon promise each other a lifelong partnership'],
  purpose:['Story beat: the wedding','Emotional turning point: Jade and Devon begin a partnership'],
  unlocks:[],
  reward:'Jade weds Prince Devon'},
 58:{ title:'The Princess Beyond the Guard', type:'Story Chapter — the new princess', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal palace → Jade\'s chambers → Sky\'s sickroom',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, a lady-in-waiting, Greyson (by bracelet) and Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The morning after the royal wedding a new day rises over Dragonvale. Jade is no longer just an Imperial Guard: she is now Princess of Dragonvale. A schedule of royal duties (court reception, review reports, meet with ministers, visit the Healing Pavilion, royal banquet in the evening) waits beside a note: "Rest today. You have carried too much alone. — Devon." Jade is surprised: she had expected distance, but found a quiet care ("He... actually thought of me."). A lady-in-waiting presents her official attires as the wife of Prince Devon: her Imperial Guard uniform can no longer represent her position. Looking at her reflection Jade thinks: "I am still me... but now, I must be more than just a guard." Two outfits appear: Daily Royal Attire (Chapter 58 onwards) and Mission / Battle Attire (Phoenix Guard). At the royal court many nobles welcome her while some whisper in doubt ("An outsider becoming a royal princess?" "She was once only a guard..."). Devon speaks before Jade can: "She stood before danger when many nobles hid behind walls. She is my wife, and Princess of Dragonvale." Jade: "I cannot change everyone\'s opinion in a day... But I will fulfill my responsibilities." That night Jade and Devon finally have a real conversation as husband and wife. "Do you regret choosing me?" "No. Many marriages begin with duty. Few become choices." Jade\'s communication bracelet vibrates: Greyson — "Congratulations, Princess Jade. A new chapter begins. Greater challenges await, but you are not alone." Jade: "How does he know everything?" Devon: "Perhaps Tribute\'s king has spies. Or perhaps he really is psychic." Later Jade visits Sky, who is still recovering: "You look different." "I suppose I am." "No... you look like yourself." A new title, a new responsibility, and a future filled with unknowns. But Jade is ready. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: Daily Royal Attire from Chapter 58 and a separate Mission / Battle Attire (Phoenix Guard). Sky is still recovering (the author says he returns after Chapter 61). Greyson seems to know everything (spies or psychic).',
  quote:'"Many marriages begin with duty. Few become choices." — Prince Devon',
  events:['Jade wakes as Princess of Dragonvale; Devon leaves her a note to rest','Her Imperial Guard uniform is replaced: Daily Royal Attire and Phoenix Guard battle attire','Some nobles whisper in doubt; Devon defends her publicly','Husband and wife finally talk honestly','Greyson congratulates Jade by bracelet','Jade visits the recovering Sky'],
  purpose:['Jade\'s new attires (art note: Daily Royal Attire; Phoenix Guard for missions and battle)','Sky\'s recovery beat'],
  unlocks:['Daily Royal Attire (Chapter 58 onwards)','Mission / Battle Attire (Phoenix Guard)'],
  reward:'Jade becomes Princess of Dragonvale'},
 59:{ title:'The Bond Severed', type:'Story Chapter — the bond severed', loc:'🌙 Dragonvale night lake → boat → Cavern of Fireflies (entrance)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and Dima (Ancient Spirit)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a busy week of royal duties Devon takes Jade on another secret boat outing at night. The boat glides smoothly ("He must be using his power to move us through an arcane-support field..."). Devon: "Before I met you, I knew about your past with Prince Roc Chadwick. At first, I intended to claim you as a political prize, a way to strengthen an alliance. But after meeting you, my view changed. You are not a prize... You are Jade. And I chose you because of who you are, not for politics." Jade is silent, wondering whether Devon ever wanted to know more about her past after Jenika examined her, but decides not to ask: "What\'s done is in the past." Inside the boat cabin Jade is alone when a golden light appears before her: Dima, Ancient Spirit. "Let go, Jade Gold. You were born for a purpose. Your destiny lies with the owner of the Pearl... the saviour of Tribute. As long as you sever the bond with Roc Chadwick completely, your fate with him will no longer exist." Jade solemnly vows: "I solemnly sever the bond with Roc Chadwick forever. I pledge my heart to Devon Chadstone, my destiny, and the cause of saving Tribute." Dima: "You are free now, Jade. Your heart is clear, and your path ahead is brighter than ever." Jade wonders: "Then... is Devon the one in the prophecy?" Devon notices the change: "Jade... Are you alright? You seem different." "I have let go of something I should have released long ago. I am alright. Thank you for being here with me." Soon they arrive at the hidden entrance to the Cavern of Fireflies: "It\'s here... The Cavern of Fireflies." "Few people know about this place." Countless fireflies fill the cavern, illuminating a hidden world of beauty and healing. "A place to rest, to heal... and to discover more together." New Area Unlocked: Cavern of Fireflies.',
  art:'Pages show: Dima appears as an Ancient Spirit and frees Jade from her fate with Roc (the destined bond is cut; Jade pledges to Devon). Devon admits he first meant to claim her as a political prize. The Cavern of Fireflies is a new area.',
  quote:'"I solemnly sever the bond with Roc Chadwick forever. I pledge my heart to Devon Chadstone, my destiny, and the cause of saving Tribute." — Jade',
  events:['Devon takes Jade on a secret night boat outing','Devon admits he first intended to claim her as a political prize, then chose her for herself','Dima, Ancient Spirit, appears to Jade in the boat cabin','Jade severs her bond with Roc Chadwick and pledges herself to Devon','They reach the hidden entrance of the Cavern of Fireflies','New area unlocked: Cavern of Fireflies'],
  purpose:['New area: Cavern of Fireflies','Chad\'s bond with Jade is severed (reset to 0)'],
  unlocks:['New Area Unlocked: Cavern of Fireflies'],
  reward:'The bond with Roc is severed; the Cavern of Fireflies opens'},
 60:{ title:'The Cavern of Fireflies', type:'Story Chapter — the poison', loc:'🏞️ Cavern of Fireflies (inner cavern)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade and Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The couple continues deeper into the secret Cavern of Fireflies, a hidden healing place known to very few, where spirit fireflies fill the darkness with eternal light. Devon has set up an arcane support field to reach the inner chambers more quickly and safely. They dock: the inner cavern is partially submerged, the waters deep and the terrain dangerous, so they must go on foot and through the water. Devon ties a cord between them: "I will tie this cord to you. No matter what happens, we will stay together." "I trust you, Devon." At the centre of the cavern countless spirit fireflies illuminate the darkness like a sunrise inside the earth: "It\'s... breathtaking..." Devon closes his eyes and draws in the spirit fireflies\' energy, and the air glows with pure power. Suddenly the fireflies scatter and Devon loses his footing on the slick slope; the cord yanks Jade off balance and they both fall into deeper water. Jade struggles to stay afloat as her strength fades ("I can\'t... breathe...") but Devon finds her, wraps his arms around her and pulls her to the surface, refusing to let go. On a sheltered ledge he uses his internal energy to warm her and restore her strength: "Stay with me, Jade. Breathe slowly." "...I\'m here..." Then his expression changes: he senses something in her body. "There is poison in your system. It\'s a slow-acting poison, one that has been building in your body for some time. That is why the symptoms have been hidden." "Poison...? But how...?" "It has been there for a while. Someone intended it to be hidden. We do not yet know the exact source, but it is real. For now, rest. I will help your body resist it, and we will find the truth." They remain in the cavern overnight in a sheltered place beside the luminous water, Devon keeping watch. "Thank you... for saving me..." Beneath the beauty of the Cavern of Fireflies a darker truth has surfaced: the healing light revealed not only hope but also a hidden danger within Jade\'s own body. The journey ahead would not be easy, but she would face it with Devon by her side.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade is poisoned with the same kind of slow-acting poison as Levi. Devon can resist it with his energy for now. Devon uses the spirit fireflies\' energy (a Dragonvale/pearl-linked power).',
  quote:'"The healing light revealed not only hope... but also a hidden danger within my own body." — Jade',
  events:['Devon and Jade go on foot into the submerged inner cavern, tied by a cord','The spirit fireflies scatter; both fall into deep water','Devon rescues Jade and restores her strength with his internal energy','Devon detects a slow-acting poison in Jade\'s body','They stay overnight in the cavern while Devon keeps watch'],
  purpose:['Mystery: who poisoned Jade (and Levi)?','The Cavern of Fireflies as a healing place'],
  unlocks:['Lore: Jade is poisoned (slow-acting)','Cavern of Fireflies: restoring rest'],
  reward:'Jade is found to be poisoned'},
 61:{ title:'The Moon\'s Lonely Child', type:'Story Chapter — the healer\'s loneliness', loc:'🌙 Royal Healing Pavilion (Dragonvale, by moonlight)',
  chars:['sky'], charsNote:'Jenika Moon and Sky (Jade and Devon are away)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While Jade and Devon are away, the palace returns to a quieter rhythm. Under the moonlight the Royal Healing Pavilion remains a place of light, care and secrets, where Jenika Moon continues her duty as healer of the palace. Jenika is the daughter of a princess and a cousin to the royal princes, entrusted with the care of the palace as a healer blessed with rare moon-aligned magic. "There are still many herbs to prepare before tomorrow... The health of the royal family must always come first." She remembers being a little girl and overhearing adults whisper about a secret concerning Devon and Roc: "They must never know... It is better if the truth remains hidden from the princes." (In Dragonvale it is the custom for royal princes to be raised away from their birth mothers, placed under the care of royal guardians to ensure the future of the kingdom. "There are many reasons, some spoken, and many left unspoken...") She thinks about Jade\'s recent checkup: the mark she placed on Jade was part of the inner-palace medical protocol for women who stay within the palace grounds, a routine procedure to ensure their health and safety. Devon only asked about Jade\'s health and never asked to see the result of the mark. "I was surprised that he showed such concern for her at all. What does it mean?" Her healing magic comes from devotion to the Moon Goddess: through her light she eases pain, mends wounds and brings hope. "The moon has always been my constant companion, even when I am alone. But there is also a curse within me. I am destined for loneliness. If I allow myself to love, it will only bring pain — to me, and to those I care about." Now that Sky has recovered he comes to see her: "Jenika... Thank you. You saved my life. I truly would not be here without you. I have something else to tell you. I care for you... more than I can put into words. I want to be by your side. Please, let me stay." Jenika refuses: "No... you must not come any closer. I am cursed. I cannot return your feelings. If you stay, you will only suffer. Please, do not bind your heart to mine." Sky: "I understand it may be difficult for you to believe, but I do not regret my feelings. Even if you cannot return them, I still want to stay by your side. I will not turn away." "Sky... You are kind, but you do not know what it means to love someone like me. It is safer for you to keep your distance." So Jenika chooses distance, as the only way she can protect him. The moon understands her loneliness: perhaps this is her fate, to heal the wounds of others but never have a love of her own. But even in this distance there is someone who remains. Someone who still chooses to stay.',
  art:'Pages show: Sky has recovered and confesses to Jenika, who refuses because of a curse she believes she carries. Jenika overheard a childhood secret about Devon and Roc (the royal princes are raised away from their birth mothers). The page says the mark she placed on Jade was routine palace medical protocol; Devon only asked about Jade\'s health.',
  quote:'"I do not regret my feelings. Even if you cannot return them, I still want to stay by your side." — Sky',
  events:['Jenika prepares herbs and recalls a secret she overheard as a child','The custom of raising Dragonvale princes away from their birth mothers','Jenika\'s moon-aligned healing and her belief that she is cursed with loneliness','Sky, recovered, thanks Jenika and confesses his feelings','Jenika refuses him for his own safety; Sky says he will stay anyway'],
  purpose:['Jenika / Sky relationship beat','Sky is recovered and returns to active duty'],
  unlocks:['Sky returns to the party (recovered)'],
  reward:'Sky has recovered'},
 62:{ title:'The Shadow Behind the Poison', type:'Story Chapter — the poison trail', loc:'🏮 Jade\'s chambers → Royal Healing Pavilion → old royal archives',
  chars:['jade','devon','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika, Sally, Roc and Delilah',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the wedding Princess Jade returns to her chamber and re-reads Levi\'s letter once more: "Levi... What exactly did you discover... and who was you afraid of?" Devon finds her still working late: "You are not alone in this, Jade. We will find the truth together." Now that the wedding is over they return to the investigation and review what they know: Levi\'s letter (discovered something dangerous, feared for Jade\'s safety, was silenced), the missing material from the Royal Healing Pavilion (a rare, potent material, could be used to create a slow-acting poison) and the royal-level access required (only those with royal authority could enter; security records show legitimate access). "These clues are connected. Someone is working carefully and with power inside the palace. This was not a random theft. Someone with royal authority took it." At the Royal Healing Pavilion they consult Jenika Moon, Royal Healer: "The missing material is extremely potent. It can be used to create a slow-acting poison that leaves few traces. And it could only be taken by someone with legitimate royal access. The records show no signs of forced entry. Such a poison can slowly weaken a person over time. It affects the body\'s internal systems and is very difficult to detect. Whoever took it knows medical knowledge and has access to royal resources. This is a deliberate and calculated act." Later noblewoman Sally shares what she discovered: "I saw someone enter the Healing Pavilion after dark a few weeks ago. They had royal authority. The guards did not stop them. I could not see their face clearly, but it was a man, and he was escorted inside." Meanwhile in a private chamber Prince Roc Chadwick rubs his head: "Why do I feel so exhausted lately...? This makes no sense. I should be stronger..." Delilah watches closely, her thoughts filled with ambition: "Perhaps you have been working too hard, my prince. Leave the unpleasant matter to me. Focus on what truly matters." Putting everything together, Jade: "Levi may have been targeted because he was protecting me, or because he stood in someone\'s way." Devon: "Someone with royal access took a poison-capable material. Levi discovered it, and in time, he was silenced. This is bigger than we thought. It may involve a faction within the royal family. We need to find out who had access at that time... and why." Following the clues they arrive at the old royal archives and find an old Royal Healing Pavilion Access Authorization from that period: "Look at this... An old authorization record from that period. The name has been erased, but the royal seal is real." "Someone deliberately erased the name. Who were they trying to hide? And what other secrets are buried in these archives?" The truth goes deeper than they imagined...',
  art:'Pages show: the poison trail points to a man with royal-level access and a deliberately erased authorization record. Roc is tired and unsure why: per the author this is the effect of Dima removing his bond with Jade (ch59), not poison and not yet any dark-magic backlash. Delilah steers him. Sally is a witness.',
  quote:'"The name has been erased, but the royal seal is real." — Jade',
  events:['Jade and Devon review the clues: Levi\'s letter, the missing material, royal-level access','Jenika confirms the missing material makes a hard-to-detect slow poison','Sally saw a man escorted into the Pavilion after dark','Roc is unusually exhausted (the aftermath of his severed bond with Jade) while Delilah reassures him','In the old royal archives they find an access record with the name erased'],
  purpose:['Investigation: who had royal access to the Healing Pavilion','Mission: The Erased Name'],
  unlocks:['Mission: The Erased Name','Location: Old Royal Archives'],
  reward:'The trail leads to an erased name'},
 63:{ title:'Court of Suspicions', type:'Story Chapter — the court', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal court / Royal Healing Pavilion',
  chars:['jade','devon','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika, Roc, Delilah, King Chadstone and Sky (briefly)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After their wedding Jade and Devon continue the investigation into Levi\'s poisoning. Though Levi has already left Dragonvale, his letter and the remaining clues still raise many questions. "Levi\'s letter suggests he may have discovered something dangerous before he became ill." "The pieces are connected. This was not a random incident. Someone inside the palace did this. Someone with access, knowledge... and a reason." At the Royal Healing Pavilion Jenika Moon shares an important clue: several restricted vials and rare materials were found missing from the Pavilion\'s secured storage earlier this month. "These are potent materials, tightly controlled and only accessible to authorized royal personnel. The timing matches when Levi\'s condition began to worsen. This cannot be a coincidence." Jade: "So the person responsible had access to the Healing Pavilion, knew what they were taking, and had the means to use it." Devon: "And someone within the palace could move these materials without immediate suspicion. We need to look closer at who had access during that time." At the Dragonvale court Prince Roc deliberately provokes Devon, trying to undermine him in front of the nobles: "Prince Devon, you were always nothing more than a guard! And now you dare to sit beside the princess as an equal?" Devon: "Mind your words, Prince Roc." Delilah: "This court is not the place for personal attacks." Roc continues to speak out of turn, his jealousy clear to everyone: "Devon is favored only because of luck and the princess\'s sentiment! He has no true royal standing! Dragonvale deserves stronger leadership than this pretense!" The court falls into an uneasy silence and many nobles show their disapproval ("This is inappropriate." "He has gone too far." "Such disrespect to the crown... Unacceptable."). Later Roc is seen weakened by dark-magic backlash, the effects of the severed bond and his own unraveling emotions: "This... curse... Why am I feeling weaker? I should be stronger.." Delilah: "You have done enough today, my prince. Rest. Do not let them see you like this." King Chadstone finally addresses Roc\'s behavior and places him under house arrest: "Prince Roc Chadstone! You have repeatedly displayed improper conduct in this court, spoken out of turn, and brought disgrace to the royal family. Effective immediately, you are to remain under house arrest in your residence until further notice. Reflect on your actions and regain your composure. This is my command." Later Jade and Devon continue their investigation, now more aware than ever that the palace is full of dangerous secrets. "Roc\'s behavior only confirms that something is deeply wrong. He is hiding something... or afraid of what we might uncover." "The missing materials, Levi\'s letter, and Roc\'s sudden instability... Everything is connected." There are still answers to find... and the palace holds more secrets than we imagined.',
  art:'Pages show: the page itself names Roc\'s weakness as dark-magic backlash and the effects of the severed bond. Roc is put under house arrest. Sky appears briefly beside Jenika.',
  quote:'"There are still answers to find... and the palace holds more secrets than we imagined."',
  events:['Jenika reports restricted vials missing from the Pavilion','Roc provokes Devon in open court','Roc is seen weakened by backlash and the severed bond','King Chadstone places Roc under house arrest','Jade and Devon sense the palace is hiding something'],
  purpose:['Investigation: access to the Healing Pavilion','Roc\'s instability introduced'],
  unlocks:['Roc under house arrest (story)'],
  reward:'Roc is placed under house arrest'},
 64:{ title:'The Marriage Proposal', type:'Story Chapter — the alliance', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal court and Roc\'s residence',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, King Chadstone, Roc, Delilah',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the unrest in court Dragonvale\'s nobles remain uneasy; questions about Prince Roc\'s conduct linger in every corridor. King Chadstone is deeply disappointed but remains a thoughtful ruler, not a tyrant: "Roc possesses talent... His military merit and ambition are undeniable. But his emotions have begun to control him." That same day a letter arrives from the Kingdom of Altan proposing a marriage alliance with Dragonvale. When it is read in the royal council the ministers are surprised: the proposed candidate is Prince Roc Chadstone. The king reasons: "Roc remains a prince of great ability. He has martial reputation, influence, and the bearing of a future crown prince. Perhaps a wife will give him stability. If this marriage can help him find balance... then it is a path worth trying." In his residence Roc reads the proposal with a complicated expression: "A foreign princess... So even now, my worth is measured by my place in the line of succession." Delilah sees the opportunity within the proposal ("But this could bring you closer to the throne. A political marriage with Altan is no small advantage, my prince."), yet ambition does not quiet the unrest in his heart: "Power may be gained... ...but some things cannot be erased so easily." Jade and Devon receive the news: "So His Majesty chose Prince Roc..." "He is trying to save him through duty." "But no one can be changed by another person alone." "...You\'re right. A person must choose to change for himself. All we can do is hope he finds his own answer." Before any answer is sent a second letter follows: Princess Altan will personally travel to Dragonvale. Before accepting the man chosen for her, the princess of Altan would first see Dragonvale with her own eyes. A new alliance was approaching... and with it, a new storm.',
  art:'Pages show: the Kingdom of Altan proposes the alliance and names Roc as the candidate; the king hopes marriage will steady him. Delilah encourages it for the throne\'s sake.',
  quote:'"A person must choose to change for himself." — Devon',
  events:['King Chadstone weighs Roc\'s talent against his unstable emotions','A letter arrives from the Kingdom of Altan proposing a marriage alliance','Altan names Prince Roc as the candidate','Roc reflects bitterly; Delilah sees political advantage','A second letter: the princess of Altan will come in person'],
  purpose:['Introduce the Altan alliance'],
  unlocks:['Kingdom of Altan introduced'],
  reward:'The Altan alliance is proposed'},
 65:{ title:'The Trader Princess', type:'Story Chapter — the disguised princess', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale market district',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Princess Altan (disguised), Jade, Devon, Roc, Delilah',
  introduced:['Seraphina Altan (disguised as a trader)'],
  sum:'Princess Altan arrives in Dragonvale, but not as a royal guest. She comes in disguise as a travelling trader, eager to see the city and to judge Prince Roc for herself before accepting the proposed marriage alliance. "This is my first time in Dragonvale. I must observe with an open mind. First impressions often reveal a person\'s true character." Later Prince Roc Chadstone and Delilah arrive at the market. Roc scorns her stall: "What is all this clutter? These goods are cheap and worthless. Do you really think anyone of importance would buy such things?" Delilah: "Such a mediocre stall. It\'s hardly worthy of Dragonvale. Look at this. Such poor quality. How embarrassing to sell this in our city." Roc steps on her goods: "These trinkets are beneath us. Know your place, commoner." Jade and Devon step in: "That\'s enough! These are someone\'s livelihood. No one has the right to treat others with such contempt." They help the trader pick up her goods ("You\'ve worked hard to prepare these goods. Let me help you pick them up." "Th-Thank you... You don\'t have to..." "A person\'s worth is not determined by their status, but by their character and hard work. Everyone deserves respect."). The trader looks at them with surprise: she had expected arrogance from royalty, but saw kindness, dignity and fairness. "They treat me with respect... even though they do not know who I am. So this is what true nobility looks like..." Roc: "How tiresome. Always playing the righteous couple. Tch. Must you interfere in everything? It\'s only a worthless trader." Delilah: "Do you really care so much about a commoner?" Devon: "Kindness is never a waste of time. A just kingdom values all its people." Jade and Devon leave after helping, but their words linger in Altan\'s heart. Her first impression of Roc was not the talented prince she had heard about, but an arrogant man who looked down on others; Jade and Devon had unknowingly earned her respect. She would continue to observe, for the truth behind the alliance mattered more than ever.',
  art:'Pages show: Princess Altan is the trader (the court does not know yet). The chapter makes Roc and Delilah look cruel and Jade and Devon look just. Chapter 66 is the official reveal.',
  quote:'"A person\'s worth is not determined by their status, but by their character and hard work." — Jade',
  events:['Princess Altan arrives in Dragonvale in disguise as a trader','Roc and Delilah mock and trample her stall','Jade and Devon defend her and help gather her goods','Altan judges Roc as arrogant and Jade and Devon as truly noble'],
  purpose:['Seraphina arrives (disguised); first impressions','Set up the reveal in chapter 66'],
  unlocks:['Seraphina Altan appears'],
  reward:'Seraphina meets Jade and Devon in disguise'},
 66:{ title:'Princess Altan Revealed', type:'Story Chapter — the reveal', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal hall',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Seraphina Altan, King Chadstone, Roc, Delilah, Jade, Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Dragonvale palace gathers in full to welcome the envoy from Altan and formally confirm the proposed marriage alliance. Nobles from both kingdoms fill the hall, anticipating the arrival of the foreign princess who would become Prince Roc\'s bride. Jade: "Today, the princess of Altan will finally arrive. I feel that something important is about to be revealed..." Soon the Altan procession enters the royal hall; at its head is the princess herself, not a merchant but the true Princess Altan, resplendent in her royal attire. A wave of surprise sweeps through the court: the travelling merchant they had once seen in the market was none other than Princess Altan ("That merchant... was the princess of Altan?!" "She came to Dragonvale in disguise?!"). Roc recognizes her immediately: "...! It was you... You were the trader?" Delilah understands the significance: "Her majesty was the merchant... all this time? This changes everything... If she already knows Prince Roc\'s true character, our plans may be in danger..." Princess Altan addresses the court with poise: "I came to Dragonvale not only as a princess, but also as a traveler, so I could see the city and its people for myself. What one does when they believe they are unknown often reveals more than any formal meeting. A true alliance should be built on understanding, not on empty titles." Jade understands: "Altan had already seen who Prince Roc truly was before knowing his title. She chose to deserve him as a commoner first... and what she saw must have been disappointing." Devon: "First impressions often reveal a person\'s true nature. Rank and titles can be a mask, but behavior cannot be hidden forever." The proposed marriage alliance was no longer simple: now that Princess Altan knew Prince Roc\'s true nature, the path ahead would be far more complicated than anyone had expected.',
  art:'Pages show: the trader is revealed as Princess Altan. Roc is exposed in front of the court. The page calls her Princess Altan; her full name Seraphina Altan appears on later pages.',
  quote:'"A true alliance should be built on understanding, not on empty titles." — Princess Altan',
  events:['The court assembles to welcome the Altan envoy','Princess Altan enters in royal attire: she was the trader','Roc and Delilah realise the market insult was to the princess','Altan explains why she came in disguise','Jade and Devon read what she saw in Roc'],
  purpose:['Seraphina\'s official arrival reveal'],
  unlocks:['Princess Seraphina Altan officially revealed'],
  reward:'Princess Altan is revealed'},
 67:{ title:'The Princess and the Fallen Prince', type:'Story Chapter — the engagement', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale palace',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Seraphina Altan, Roc, Jade, Devon, King Chadstone',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After Princess Altan\'s official arrival, preparations for a royal marriage begin at once. But behind the ceremony neither bride nor groom welcomes the union with warmth. A lady-in-waiting asks the princess: "Your Highness, are you satisfied with Prince Roc?" "I did not expect perfection. But I expected respect." She had already seen his true character before his title. Jade comes to apologize for what happened in the market: "I wished to apologize for what happened in the market." "You defended me before you knew who I was." The princess asks: "Is Prince Devon always like that?" Jade: "No. He learned." Roc, asked whether he regrets this, says: "No." A princess, a throne, everything he thought he wanted, yet nothing felt settled within him. Devon: "Do you pity him?" Jade: "No. But I understand him." Roc: "I once believed power could fill what was missing inside." The alliance of Dragonvale and Altan is celebrated before the royal court, King Chadstone presiding over the marriage. Roc: "I will fulfill my duty as your husband." Seraphina: "And I will fulfill mine as your wife." The court welcomes the union, seeing a strong alliance for the future ("They look like a perfect match.") but Jade: "A perfect appearance is not the same as a perfect bond." The marriage had begun. But duty could not force two hearts to unite. What mirrored Jade and Devon on the surface carried an entirely different meaning beneath. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: Seraphina and Jade speak warmly; the engagement ceremony before King Chadstone. The chapter title card names Roc as "the fallen prince".',
  quote:'"A perfect appearance is not the same as a perfect bond." — Jade',
  events:['Seraphina tells her attendant she expected respect, not perfection','Jade apologizes for the market incident; Seraphina thanks her','Roc admits he once believed power could fill what was missing','The engagement is celebrated before the court','Jade notes a perfect appearance is not a perfect bond'],
  purpose:['Marriage preparations','Seraphina and Jade connection'],
  unlocks:[],
  reward:'Roc and Seraphina are engaged'},
 68:{ title:'The Marriage Without Love', type:'Story Chapter — the marriage', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal hall → Roc and Seraphina\'s chamber',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Seraphina, Roc, Delilah, Jade, Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The marriage is sealed before the court, but no warmth follows it into the night. Princess Seraphina Altan and Prince Roc Chadstone are now husband and wife: a union of duty, power and alliance. They stand together perfect in appearance before the kingdom, but behind their composed faces lies a distance neither could deny. In their private chamber Prince Roc makes his intentions clear: "I will not consummate this marriage. This marriage will remain political. Nothing more." Seraphina: "That suits me well, Prince Roc." He turns away, leaving a space between them. To Seraphina his refusal is not an insult but a relief ("I can breathe at last..."). They reach a mutual understanding: "We will maintain the appearance of a united couple before the court. For the sake of our kingdoms. But nothing more." "I understand. I, too, will fulfill my duties as your wife. A political alliance is enough." Delilah soon learns of Prince Roc\'s refusal. Even without intimacy Seraphina\'s presence as his wife still unsettles her: "Why does this still unsettle me...? He does not love her, yet she has what I wanted." Alone, Prince Roc is consumed by frustration rather than love: "So this is all that remains... frustration. Jade... You chose him. And now all I feel is bitterness." Where respect had shaped Jade and Devon\'s bond, resentment now defines Roc and Seraphina\'s. In Dragonvale two marriages now stand side by side: one built on trust, the other on emptiness. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: the marriage is political only and unconsummated by agreement; both are relieved. Delilah is unsettled. Roc is still bitter over Jade.',
  quote:'"We will maintain the appearance of a united couple before the court. For the sake of our kingdoms. But nothing more." — Roc',
  events:['Seraphina and Roc are married before the court','Roc declares the marriage will stay political','They agree to keep up appearances','Delilah is unsettled by Seraphina\'s presence','Roc is consumed by bitterness over Jade'],
  purpose:['The loveless alliance','Roc\'s decline begins in earnest'],
  unlocks:[],
  reward:'Roc and Seraphina marry'},
 69:{ title:'The Price of Ambition', type:'Story Chapter — the source of the darkness', loc:'🏮 Roc\'s chamber / ravine cave (recalled) / Jade\'s study',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Roc, Seraphina, Delilah, Jade, Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Dragonvale palace stands under an uneasy sky. Though the torches still shine, a sense of darkness lingers: a reminder that some ambitions always come at a price. In his chamber Prince Roc feels the power within him growing wilder. The same darkness that gave him strength is now slowly consuming his body: "This power... It still gives me strength. But why does it also feel like poison?" The source of Roc\'s dark arts traces back to the ravine cave where Jade\'s cage once fell, a place filled with ancient markings and a long-forgotten power. While Jade lay injured in the cave, Roc explored deeper and discovered ancient markings and a forbidden power that should have remained undisturbed: "Such power... It could make me stronger than anyone." Roc accepted the power, knowing it was dangerous, but the temptation was too great: "With this power, I will never be weak again. I will take what is mine." Now Princess Seraphina witnesses the price of that decision. The man she married is no longer the same: "This power is destroying you." "Without power, everything is taken from me." "No. You are the one pushing everything away." Delilah watches Roc\'s decline with growing unease: "This is worse than I expected. His ambition was never meant to destroy him." Elsewhere Jade and Devon continue their investigation, comparing the clues from Levi\'s poisoning and Roc\'s strange condition: "Levi\'s poisoning, the restricted vials, and Roc\'s sudden change... The pieces are connected. We need to look at the ravine cave again. It may be the key to both incidents." Jade recognizes the place immediately: the ravine cave was not just where her cage fell, it was the beginning of it all. "These markings... This is the same cave. The power Roc found here must be what is affecting him now." "Then we need to find out more about this power, and how to stop it before it consumes him completely." Back in the palace the dark magic continues to consume Roc: "It hurts... But I cannot let go. I cannot be weak again..." Roc had taken the darkness for strength, believing it would secure his ambitions. But now he realized the truth: the power he desired so much was no longer a weapon he controlled. It was consuming him.',
  art:'Pages show: the origin of Roc\'s dark arts is the ravine cave (from the cage fall earlier in the story). Jade recognizes the markings. Seraphina and Delilah both see the cost.',
  quote:'"The power he desired so much was no longer a weapon he controlled. It was consuming him."',
  events:['Roc\'s dark power grows wilder and starts to poison him','The source: ancient markings in the ravine cave where Jade\'s cage fell','Seraphina warns him the power is destroying him','Jade recognizes the cave\'s markings','Jade and Devon plan to return to the ravine cave'],
  purpose:['Dark magic origin revealed','Investigation: link Levi\'s poison and Roc\'s condition'],
  unlocks:['Clue: the ravine cave markings'],
  reward:'The source of Roc\'s power is revealed'},
 70:{ title:'The Fading Blade', type:'Story Chapter — the decline', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale training yard → Roc\'s residence',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Roc, Delilah, Seraphina',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the political marriage unrest has not fully left the palace. Though an alliance has been formed many still watch, doubt and wait for change. Amid lingering tensions Prince Roc continues to chase strength, believing greater power is the only way to protect what he has gained. He pushes himself harder than ever, refusing to show any sign of weakness. His swordsmanship remains formidable but the strain begins to show. Then, in the middle of a drill, his arm trembles and his sword slips from his grasp. Roc refuses to stop: "Again." "My prince, you should rest. You have trained enough for today." "I said again." Delilah watches from a distance, her heart heavy, beginning to realize the power Roc clings to is consuming him. Seraphina observes silently: "No alliance can heal a heart that worships its own ambition more than life itself." He continues to train but his movements are slower and his control less stable; the courtiers cannot ignore the change ("The prince seems weaker than before... What is happening to him? Has the marriage taken a greater toll than we thought?"). Later Roc is alone, hiding his weakness from the eyes of others: "...Ha... I will not... I cannot be weak..." The dark marks, once dormant, begin to spread again: "No... Not now... Not again..." Delilah finally approaches him in private, unable to stay silent any longer: "Roc... Please, let me help you. You do not have to bear this alone." "Do not pity me. I am still the same. I need no help. Stay out of this." That night Seraphina reflects in her chamber. She no longer expects this marriage to change him; now she only feels sorrow for a man being destroyed by his own ambition: "He was never truly lost because of me. He is lost because he cannot stop chasing a strength that will eventually consume him." "I cannot lose my strength." The blade that once made him feared has begun to fail him.',
  art:'Pages show: Roc\'s strength is visibly failing; the dark marks spread across his arm. Delilah and Seraphina both see it. This is the chapter the author marked as the start of his permanent decline.',
  quote:'"The blade that once made him feared had begun to fail him."',
  events:['Roc drills past his limits and drops his sword','Delilah and Seraphina see the power consuming him','The dark marks spread across his arm','Delilah offers help; Roc refuses','Seraphina no longer expects the marriage to change him'],
  purpose:['Roc\'s dark-magic backlash (first permanent stat change)'],
  unlocks:['Roc\'s stats begin to be permanently altered'],
  reward:'Roc\'s strength begins to fail'},
 71:{ title:'The Truth Beneath the Darkness', type:'Story Chapter — the access logs', loc:'🏮 Royal Healing Pavilion → palace records',
  chars:['jade','devon','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the wedding Jade and Devon return to the investigation into Levi\'s poisoning. Beneath the peace of the palace the search for the truth continues; the secrets hidden beneath the palace begin to surface and the clues lead deeper than they had ever imagined. Jade and Devon review Levi\'s letter looking for more clues: "Levi suspected someone powerful before he left. He wrote that he had discovered something, but could not reveal it directly." "He was afraid. This was more than a personal conflict. Someone in a high position was involved." At the Royal Healing Pavilion Jenika Moon studies the traces left in Levi\'s body and the missing restricted materials: "This energy is not ordinary poison. It is connected to forbidden spiritual arts. The materials used in this poisoning match the restricted supplies from the pavilion\'s sealed storage. These traces contain spiritual energy that should not exist in common medicine. And several key materials are missing from our restricted inventory." As Jade pieces the clues together she remembers the ravine cave from the past, the place where her cage fell and Roc saved her: "That cave... I never forgot it. There was a strange feeling there, as if something dark was hidden beneath the surface. In that ravine cave, Roc found me when my cage fell... Roc found something there." Devon: "The cave did not create this darkness. It only revealed what he was willing to do. What happened in that cave was not the beginning. It was a glimpse of what already existed within him." The investigation leads to palace records: the Restricted Archive Access Log shows someone with royal authority entered restricted areas and obtained forbidden materials, on the 3rd Moon (Restricted Storage), 5th Moon (Alchemy Archives), 8th Moon (Forbidden Materials) and 11th Moon (Sealed Vault), each signed Prince Roc Chadstone. "These records show that Prince Roc had access to the sealed areas multiple times. The same rare materials used in Levi\'s poisoning were taken from restricted storage. And the information was later concealed from the royal council." Jade: "Everything leads back to the palace... and to Roc. Could he have been the one behind Levi\'s poisoning?" Devon: "We cannot jump to conclusions yet. But the evidence is too clear to ignore." Someone within the palace is using forbidden power, and the clues now point closer to Roc. "There is still more to uncover. But now I understand. The darkness we are facing is not outside the palace. It has always been closer than we thought."',
  art:'Pages show: the access log names Prince Roc Chadstone on four Moons (3rd, 5th, 8th, 11th) and records the information was concealed from the royal council. Jenika links the poison to forbidden spiritual arts. This resolves the Levi poisoning investigation (the logs point to Roc); still not a direct confession.',
  quote:'"The darkness we are facing is not outside the palace. It has always been closer than we thought." — Jade',
  events:['Jenika ties the poison to forbidden spiritual arts and the missing restricted materials','Jade recalls the ravine cave where Roc found something','Devon: the cave only revealed what already existed within Roc','The Restricted Archive Access Log names Prince Roc on four separate Moons','Jade and Devon accept the clues now point at Roc'],
  purpose:['Investigation: the Restricted Archive Access Log','Resolve who took the restricted materials (evidence points to Roc)'],
  unlocks:['Mission: The Access Log (investigation)','Roc\'s stats alter further'],
  reward:'The clues point to Roc'},
 72:{ title:'The Choice of Delilah', type:'Story Chapter — the judgment', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal court',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'King Chadstone, Roc, Delilah, Seraphina, Jade, Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the growing investigation tensions envelop Dragonvale. The truth has begun to surface and the royal family now faces consequences that cannot be ignored. Love, power, means and sorrow chose paths that could not be undone. King Chadstone summons Roc. He is not angry: he is devastated, because he sees his son destroying himself. "Why? You already had everything." Roc: "No. I had everything... Except what I wanted. Power, a title, wealth... None of it mattered if she was not mine." Jade and Devon watch from the court, understanding the seriousness of the moment. The evidence can no longer be denied: dark magic traces, misuse of royal authority, restricted materials, and an undeniable connection to Levi\'s poisoning (the restricted archive records list misuse of royal authority, forbidden materials, dark magic traces, connection to Levi\'s poisoning and access to restricted areas). Seraphina Altan observes silently: this marriage could not save a man who refused to confront himself. The king urges Delilah: "You can still save yourself. Leave him. Your family can protect you. You have a child to think about. You do not have to fall with him." Delilah: "Everyone believes I chose him because of his position. They are wrong. I chose him before he had the crown. Title or not... Roc has always been the same man to me. I am not innocent. I made my choice. If he falls... I fall with him." A king must judge a prince, but a father struggles to judge his own son. King Chadstone: "Tomorrow... You will answer for everything you have done." The choices he made... have finally caught up to him.',
  art:'Pages show: the Levi poisoning is tied to Roc by the records. Delilah (who is pregnant) refuses to leave him. The king will pass judgment tomorrow. Roc\'s motive is stated openly: Jade.',
  quote:'"If he falls... I fall with him." — Delilah',
  events:['The king asks Roc why he did it; Roc says nothing mattered if she was not his','The archive records confirm dark magic, misused authority and the link to Levi\'s poisoning','King Chadstone urges Delilah to leave Roc and save herself and her child','Delilah refuses: if Roc falls she falls with him','The king sets judgment for tomorrow'],
  purpose:['Resolve the poisoning investigation','Roc\'s final backlash stage'],
  unlocks:['Roc\'s dark-magic backlash reaches its final stage'],
  reward:'The evidence condemns Roc'},
 73:{ title:'The Exiled Prince', type:'Story Chapter — the exile', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal court → Royal Healing Pavilion → one year later',
  chars:['jade','devon','seraphina'], charsNote:'King Chadstone, Roc, Delilah, Jade, Devon, Jenika, baby Liora',
  introduced:['Liora (infant)'],
  sum:'After the truth comes to light Dragonvale passes judgment on Prince Roc. For his abuse of power, use of dark arts and crimes against the palace, his princely status is stripped and he is banished from Dragonvale. King Chadstone: "Prince Roc... For your use of dark arts, your abuse of royal authority, and your crimes within the palace... I strip you of your princely status and exile you from Dragonvale. You are no longer a son of this royal house. From this day forward, you shall live in exile." He speaks not with anger but with a broken heart. Roc stands before the throne exhausted and hollow: he has lost the crown, lost Jade and lost his place in Dragonvale. "So this is the end... No crown... No Jade... I have nothing left but myself." Delilah chose Roc: even when warned that she could still save herself she refused to leave him: "I know what you have done. I am not innocent either. But I choose you. I will go with you into exile." Roc leaves Dragonvale in exile with Delilah by his side. Not Jade. Not the throne. Only Delilah. Before they depart Liora is born. For the child\'s safety and future Delilah entrusts her daughter to Jade and Devon: "My daughter... Please forgive me. I cannot give you the life you deserve. Live on, little Liora. Be happy... and know that I do love you." Jade and Devon accept baby Liora, becoming her temporary guardians: "We will protect you, little one. You are still family. And you are loved." Jenika Moon helps care for Liora at the Royal Healing Pavilion. One year later: a year has passed. Jade and Devon protected Dragonvale, completed royal missions, subdued demons, and raised the only royal grandchild. They faced demons and threats to the realm... and found joy in the quiet moments in between ("You are so brave, Liora. You bring light to our lives."). One year later Dragonvale stands in fragile peace. The past cannot be forgotten, but for now Jade, Devon and little Liora move forward, protecting the realm, honoring those they love, and preparing for the next mission.',
  art:'Pages show: Roc is exiled and stripped of his title; Delilah goes with him and entrusts baby Liora to Jade and Devon. The page then jumps one year ahead, to the quests: Jade and Devon protect Dragonvale, subdue demons and raise Liora. (Seraphina is not shown on the exile pages; the author has her taking Roc\'s place in the party.)',
  quote:'"No crown... No Jade... I have nothing left but myself." — Roc',
  events:['King Chadstone strips Roc of his title and exiles him','Delilah chooses to follow Roc into exile','Liora is born and entrusted to Jade and Devon','Jenika helps care for Liora at the Pavilion','One year later: Jade and Devon protect Dragonvale, subdue demons and raise Liora'],
  purpose:['Roc leaves the party permanently','Seraphina fights in Roc\'s place inside Dragonvale (temporary guest; permanent at 87)','One-year time skip: begins the Dragonvale quest period (74 onward)'],
  unlocks:['Roc leaves the party','Seraphina Altan joins the party','Liora in Jade and Devon\'s care'],
  reward:'Roc leaves; the year of quests begins'},
 75:{ title:'Whispers at the Border', type:'Story Chapter — the border unrest (start of the quest period)', loc:'🏔️ Dragonvale palace → border village → ancient border ruins',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, a border guard, a village child and elder',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After Greyson\'s message Jade and Devon turn their attention beyond the palace. Strange unrest has begun along the Dragonvale border, and it is time to uncover the truth: missing caravans, frightened villagers and eerie shadows near the ancient ruins suggest a new threat is stirring at the edges of Dragonvale. Jade and Devon review reports from the border looking for a pattern. "Several caravans have gone missing, and entire villages have lost contact. The travelers who returned speak of strange shadows near the old mountain road." A border guard arrives with new reports: "My Highnesses, three more villages have lost contact. The people are afraid to travel the old mountain road. They claim to have seen eerie lights and beastlike shadows near the ruins." "We should investigate in person." "I agree. The border ruins are ancient places tied to Dragonvale\'s forgotten power. If something is awakening, we need to see it for ourselves." With a small and discreet escort Jade and Devon leave the palace and head toward the troubled region. At a border village they find a community living in fear ("People have disappeared at night... We don\'t dare go near the mountain road anymore..."). Jade comforts a frightened child: "You are safe here. Tell me what you saw. We will protect you." "There were lights in the ruins... and shadows... like giant beasts... They took my brother..." Devon examines the traces near the village perimeter: "These are not ordinary beast tracks. There is a strong dark spiritual residue here. This disturbance is not natural." The village elder explains: "At night, strange lights rise from the ancient ruins. Beastlike shadows emerge, and people vanish. This has been happening for weeks. Those ruins were once part of Dragonvale. But we were always warned to stay away... as if something was sealed there." Jade: "This is connected to Greyson\'s message. The unrest is spreading." "This is only the beginning. We must continue the investigation." That night they make their way to the ancient border ruins ("The energy here feels different... as if something has awakened." "Stay close. We don\'t know what we\'ll face."). Shadowy spirit beasts emerge from the ruins: "These are spirit beings... corrupted by something beneath the ruins!" Jade and Devon fight together, using their combined strength to drive the creatures back: "They are drawn to something... This place is a source of dark energy, not just a random attack." After the battle Devon examines the ruins more closely: "These ruins have been reactivated. The seals are weakening, and the dark spiritual energy is coming from deeper beneath Dragonvale. Someone is trying to break what was once sealed here." Jade: "This is larger than we expected. The unrest at the border is only a sign of something greater. We need to continue our investigation and find the source before more villages are put in danger." Main Story Quest: Whispers at the Border. Objectives: investigate the missing villages; search the ancient border ruins; uncover the source of the spirit disturbance.',
  art:'Pages show: this is the first chapter of the quest period (one year after the exile). A "Main Story Quest" box lists three objectives. The author calls it the baseline for how the later quests are set up: report, investigate in person, fight at the site, then a larger source remains.',
  quote:'"The unrest at the border is only a sign of something greater." — Jade',
  events:['Greyson\'s message sends Jade and Devon to the border','Villages lose contact; caravans go missing; shadows near the old ruins','A village child and elder describe lights and beastlike shadows at night','Devon finds dark spiritual residue, not ordinary beast tracks','Spirit beasts attack at the ruins and are driven back','The ruins\' seals are weakening; the dark energy comes from deeper beneath Dragonvale'],
  purpose:['Start of the quest period and the main-story quest format','Greyson\'s mission 2: spirit and demon disturbances'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Whispers at the Border (3 objectives)','Location: Dragonvale Border'],
  reward:'Main Story Quest: Whispers at the Border'},
 74:{ title:'The King\'s Message', type:'Story Chapter — Greyson\'s message (start of the quest period)', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale palace',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Greyson (by bracelet)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After Roc\'s exile Jade and Devon remain in Dragonvale, balancing their royal duties, the lingering investigations and the protection of the realm. Though they are now husband and wife, their work has not ended: there are still questions to be answered, and Dragonvale\'s peace depends on what they uncover next. Jade and Devon continue to review reports and new information, determined to find the truth behind the recent events. "There are still inconsistencies in these records..." "We will find the answers. Together." Suddenly Jade\'s communication bracelet glows with a familiar royal blue light. "A message... from His Majesty Greyson?" Greyson: "Congratulations, Princess Jade. I assume married life has not stopped you from investigating trouble." "You already know?" "I am a king. I hear things. This is not a command. Consider it a trust. Continue your investigation. If unrest stirs in Dragonvale, I believe you will find its source. The poison, the forbidden materials, the unrest within the palace — these may be threads of the same knot. Watch the borders, the ruins, and the court." Jade: "I understand. I will continue the investigation." Devon: "Dragonvale\'s burdens are mine as well. We will not ignore this." With Greyson\'s message in mind Jade and Devon begin to make new plans: an aide brings the latest reports ("I\'ve compiled the latest reports, Your Highnesses.") "We will look into every lead. Nothing will be overlooked." "Let\'s focus on the palace, the border movements, and the ruins. There must be a connection." With their love, their shared purpose and the king\'s trust, Jade and Devon move forward, ready to uncover the next truth hidden within Dragonvale. Main Story Quest: The King\'s Message. Objectives: continue the Dragonvale investigation; watch for unrest in the palace and at the borders; follow Greyson\'s trust and uncover the next threat.',
  art:'Pages show: the quest period begins with the page\'s own "Main Story Quest" box with three objectives. Greyson repeats the "I am a king. I hear things." joke from the bracelet scene.',
  quote:'"This is not a command. Consider it a trust." — King Greyson',
  events:['Jade and Devon keep reviewing the records after Roc\'s exile','Greyson calls through the bracelet: poison, forbidden materials and unrest may be threads of one knot','Greyson tells them to watch the borders, the ruins and the court','Jade and Devon plan to focus on the palace, the border movements and the ruins'],
  purpose:['Start of the quest period','Greyson\'s trust mission'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The King\'s Message (3 objectives)'],
  reward:'The quest period begins'},
 76:{ title:'The Ruins Awaken', type:'Story Chapter — the awakened ruins', loc:'🏔️ Border village → ancient Dragonvale ruins',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, border villagers and a child',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a year in Dragonvale reports of strange disturbances reach the court, and Jade and Devon journey to the border to investigate the unrest near the ancient ruins. In the misty mountains beyond the border an old ruin has stirred: strange lights are seen at night and travelers have gone missing, and the people live in fear as darkness gathers once more. At the border village frightened villagers share what they have seen ("Strange lights appear at night... then the livestock vanishes." "Several travelers have gone missing. We hear screams from the mountains." "It feels like something evil has awakened near the ruins."). Jade comforts a child: "You are not alone. We will protect you. Stay within the village, and do not go out at night. We will find the cause and end this danger." Devon examines old records and the markings left at the site: "These symbols are from ancient Dragonvale. The energy here is very old. This is not a random disturbance. The ruins have been awakened by something with purpose." That night they make their way toward the ancient ruins, which have stood in silence for ages; now faint lights glow once more and the air is heavy with a strange presence. Ancient runes at the ruins have begun to glow again. Jade: "I can feel it... This power is real. It\'s dangerous, and it\'s calling to something in the depths." Devon: "These are true Dragonvale runes. They should have remained sealed. Something has deliberately awakened this site. This is only the surface. There is a deeper force behind it." Suddenly corrupted spirit beasts emerge from the darkness. Jade fights to protect the villagers, her sword shining like a flame ("Stay behind me! I will not let anyone be harmed!"). Devon unleashes his royal magic, holding back the corrupted creatures: "Return to the shadows! This land is not yours to claim!" After a fierce battle the spirit beasts are suppressed and the villagers are safe ("You are safe now. We will strengthen the village\'s defenses and keep watch." "Thank you... You saved us."). Devon: "We have only sealed the surface. Something deeper lies within these ruins. This was a deliberate awakening, tied to an older power." Jade: "Then we will go deeper. We must discover the truth, no matter how dangerous it is. The people of the border deserve to be safe, and this evil must be stopped." The truth behind the border disturbances lies deeper within the ancient ruins; their investigation has just begun. Main Story Quest: The Ruins Awaken. Objectives: investigate the ancient border ruins; protect the border villagers; uncover the source of the spirit disturbance.',
  art:'Pages show: the same border incident as chapter 75 told from the village and the ruins, with a new quest box. Jade\'s sword glows like a flame in combat; Devon uses royal magic to hold the corrupted beasts back. Note: the author\'s gameplay plan calls this chapter "The Awakening Ruins"; the page title card reads "The Ruins Awaken" (the comic is canon).',
  quote:'"We have only sealed the surface. Something deeper lies within these ruins." — Devon',
  events:['Villagers describe lights, vanishing livestock and screams','Devon reads the symbols: ancient Dragonvale, awakened with purpose','Ancient runes glow; Jade feels a dangerous power calling from the depths','Corrupted spirit beasts attack and are driven back','Devon and Jade resolve to go deeper into the ruins'],
  purpose:['Dungeon: the ancient Dragonvale ruins','Introduce corrupted spirit beasts and purification'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Ruins Awaken (3 objectives)','Location: Ancient Dragonvale Ruins'],
  reward:'The ruins are awake'},
 77:{ title:'The Heart of the Ruins', type:'Story Chapter — the seal core', loc:'🏛️ Ancient Dragonvale ruins (central chamber)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, border scouts and villagers',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the events in the border ruins Jade and Devon follow the source of the disturbance deeper into Dragonvale. At last they reach the heart of the ancient ruins, where the true cause lies hidden. Here, in the depths of the mountains, an ancient seal core has slumbered for ages. Now it has been forcibly awakened, and the unrest across Dragonvale all leads to this place. Jade and Devon enter the inner ruins, following the growing spiritual disturbance toward the central chamber ("The deeper we go, the stronger the unrest becomes."). They meet border scouts and villagers who fled from the awakened spirits: "Your Highnesses, the spirits came from the sealed chamber below! When the inner seal broke, they attacked!" Jade studies the ancient markings: "These markings... they are older than the palace records. The energy here feels ancient and unstable." Devon carefully observes the disrupted spiritual patterns: "This awakening is not natural. Someone forced the old wards to respond." At the center of the ruins they find an ancient altar with its seal core glowing with overwhelming power: "This is the source... The ancient seal core of Dragonvale." Suddenly corrupted spirit beasts emerge from the awakened seal. Jade: "Then we end it here! I will clear the path!" Devon: "Stay behind us. I will stabilize the seal." Jade and Devon work together to stabilize the ancient seal and suppress the corruption. Gradually the corrupted spirits are quelled and the seal\'s light grows steady once more ("The spirits are calming..."). Jade: "This was not an accident. Someone deliberately awakened this place. So the unrest at the border was only the beginning." Devon: "For now. But the ruins were awakened deliberately. Yes. Someone is testing Dragonvale\'s ancient foundations." With the seal stabilized Jade and Devon know this is not the end: a hidden hand has stirred Dragonvale\'s ancient seals, and greater dangers still lie ahead. "We have uncovered a part of the truth. But someone is moving in the shadows, and we must continue the investigation." Main Story Quest: The Heart of the Ruins. Objectives: calm the awakened ruins; protect the border settlements; investigate who stirred Dragonvale\'s ancient seals.',
  art:'Pages show: the awakened seal core is a protective ward of Dragonvale, corrupted by someone who forced it to respond; Jade clears the path and Devon stabilizes the seal. The author\'s gameplay plan adds a corrupted ancient protector as the boss and a couple skill called Twin Dragon Harmony.',
  quote:'"Someone is testing Dragonvale\'s ancient foundations." — Devon',
  events:['Jade and Devon descend to the heart of the ruins','Scouts report spirits pouring from the sealed chamber when the inner seal broke','They find the ancient seal core of Dragonvale','Corrupted spirit beasts burst from the seal; Jade clears the path while Devon stabilizes it','The seal steadies: someone deliberately awakened it'],
  purpose:['Boss: the awakened seal core','Introduce the unseen hand behind the unrest'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Heart of the Ruins (3 objectives)','(Couple skill moved to chapter 103 as Jade Dragon Harmony)','Dragonvale reputation and exploration areas'],
  reward:'The seal is stabilized'},
 78:{ title:'Echoes of the Forgotten Temple', type:'Story Chapter — the Moonveil Temple', loc:'🏮 Royal Archives → Moonveil Temple (eastern mountains)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Greyson (by bracelet)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the disturbances at the ruins new clues have emerged, pointing toward an older secret that has been hidden in Dragonvale for generations. Beyond the palace, amidst misty mountains and forgotten legends, the trail now leads to a place long buried by time. In the archives Jade studies an ancient symbol: "This ancient symbol appeared at the ruins... and these records mention a temple in the eastern mountains of Dragonvale." Devon: "It seems to predate the current royal line. Whatever happened there, it\'s connected to the Black Pearl." Her bracelet glows: a message from His Majesty Greyson, Young King of Tribute: "Jade, congratulations on your recent discovery. The symbol you found also appears in Tribute\'s oldest records, dating back even further than we expected. There may be answers in Dragonvale, Jade. An ancient mountain sanctuary called the Moonveil Temple is mentioned in our records. I believe it may hold important clues. I trust your judgment. Could you investigate it for me?" Jade: "I will investigate the Moonveil Temple. Thank you for sharing this information with me, Your Majesty." Devon: "I will accompany you. If this temple is connected to ancient Dragonvale royalty, we need to see it with our own eyes." Soon Jade and Devon set out for the hidden mountain sanctuary. At last they arrive at the forgotten temple, overwhelmed by a sense of ancient power, yet untouched by time. As Jade touches an ancient relic fragments of a forgotten memory flash before her eyes: a radiant woman, a black pearl, and the faint silhouette of a child. Devon: "These crests... they match the symbols of the old Dragonvale royalty. Our ancestors knew of this place. It wasn\'t just a legend." Deeper within the temple they discover a sealed inner chamber and an ancient stone tablet. The inscription reads: "When the Gold Child awakens, the pearl shall return." The past had not been erased: it had only been waiting. Mission Unlocked: Moonveil Temple. Objectives: investigate the hidden sanctuary of the Moonveil Temple; uncover the meaning of the ancient symbol; search for clues about the Black Pearl.',
  art:'Pages show: the mission box titled "Moonveil Temple" has three objectives (hidden sanctuary, ancient symbol, clues about the Black Pearl). The author\'s note said the sealed objective \'Investigate who stirred Dragonvale\'s ancient seals\' stays locked after this chapter; it is not in this box, so it remains on The Heart of the Ruins.',
  quote:'"When the Gold Child awakens, the pearl shall return." — the stone tablet',
  events:['The ancient symbol from the ruins points to a temple in the eastern mountains','Greyson: the symbol also appears in Tribute\'s oldest records; he asks Jade to investigate the Moonveil Temple','Jade touches a relic and sees a radiant woman, a black pearl and a child','The crests match old Dragonvale royalty','A sealed inner chamber holds a stone tablet: the Gold Child inscription'],
  purpose:['Investigation: the Moonveil Temple','Introduce the Gold Child inscription'],
  unlocks:['Mission: Moonveil Temple (3 objectives)','Location: Moonveil Temple'],
  reward:'The Moonveil Temple is found'},
 79:{ title:'The Black Pearl Records', type:'Story Chapter — the tablet and the three records', loc:'🏮 Royal Healing Pavilion and Royal Archives',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the discovery at the Moonveil Temple Jade and Devon bring the stone tablet back to Dragonvale for further study. The truth is revealed piece by piece, as the records of the past begin to speak once more within the palace. In the Royal Healing Pavilion and the Royal Archives the stone tablet is examined in greater detail, together with the ancient records of the Black Pearl. Jenika: "This is not Dragonvale writing alone. The markings contain influences from Dragonvale, Tribute, and ancient spiritual orders. It seems to be a record created across different eras, by those who knew the Black Pearl." They find three connected records. Record 1, The Pearl chooses: "The Black Pearl is not simply an object. It chooses. It responds." Record 2, The Gold Child carries the balance: "This record points toward the Gold Child... It speaks of one who carries the balance between light and darkness." Record 3, The guardian walks beside the chosen: "It suggests that the chosen one is not alone on this path... but it does not name the guardian directly." Jade: "Was I chosen because of my ability... or because of my bloodline? Or because of the pearl itself? I do not know if I should feel honored... or afraid." Devon: "Whatever destiny chose... your choices are still your own. You are more than a prophecy, Jade. No matter what the records say, I will always be by your side." Jade: "Even if the past has already written a path... I still want to choose how I walk it. The Black Pearl may have chosen me... but I will decide who I become." As the investigation continues the stone tablet suddenly begins to respond: the markings change and new writing emerges from the stone, as if a hidden record has finally awakened. Within the light a single name appears: Dima. The name brings new questions, and the truth remains deeper than they ever imagined.',
  art:'Pages show: three records (The Pearl chooses; The Gold Child carries the balance; The guardian walks beside the chosen) and the tablet revealing the name Dima. Jenika joins the study in the Pavilion and Archives.',
  quote:'"The Black Pearl may have chosen me... but I will decide who I become." — Jade',
  events:['The tablet is studied with Jenika: its writing mixes Dragonvale, Tribute and ancient spiritual orders','Three records: the Pearl chooses; the Gold Child carries the balance; the guardian walks beside the chosen','Jade doubts why she was chosen; Devon says her choices are her own','The tablet reacts and the name Dima appears'],
  purpose:['Lore: the three Black Pearl records','Reveal the name Dima on the tablet'],
  unlocks:['Lore: the three Black Pearl records','Clue: Dima'],
  reward:'The name Dima is revealed'},
 80:{ title:'The Shadow Behind the Pearl', type:'Story Chapter — the Pearl Chamber', loc:'🌙 Moonveil Temple (Pearl Chamber)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika, Greyson (by bracelet)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In the Moonveil Temple of Dragonvale the search continues. Knowing a name does not mean knowing the truth: some answers only lead to deeper questions. The records of the past are like a shadow: they reveal what was, but not always why. Jade, Devon and Jenika continue to examine the records of Dima, searching for the truth behind her past. Devon: "These records show that Dima was not simply a spirit... She was once a guardian. A protector. And she was deeply connected to the pearl." The ancient records speak of a being chosen to guard the balance: Dima appears in many forms, a protector, a guide, and a bridge between light and darkness. "But the details are incomplete. So many pages are missing..." Jade cannot stop thinking about the day Dima severed the bond with Roc: "Was my choice truly mine? Did she protect me... or take something from me?" Devon: "A person who protects you does not remove your ability to choose. Roc wanted possession. Dima wanted your destiny. And she will always allow you to choose." Jenika: "This record suggests that Dima served a purpose greater than the palace. She was tied to the pearl... and to a child of light. But the rest is hidden. It seems someone deliberately removed the most important parts." Following the hidden clues they discover a sealed chamber deep within the temple: the Pearl Chamber. "This place... it feels different from the others." "The air itself holds memories." At the center of the chamber rests a fragment of the Black Pearl. Jade reaches out and touches it, and the moment her fingers touch the pearl visions flood her mind: fragmented images of Dima, a woman of light, a weeping mother, a battlefield, and a promise. Then a message appears in ancient script, clear and undeniable: "The child of gold shall return when darkness rises." Suddenly Jade\'s communication bracelet glows. King Greyson: "Jade... I believe we are no longer searching for the truth. The truth has started searching for you." The past is no longer a distant story: it is moving closer, and its shadow has found them once again. Jade: "Whatever comes next... I will face it."',
  art:'Pages show: the Pearl Chamber holds a fragment of the Black Pearl; Jade\'s vision (Dima, a woman of light, a weeping mother, a battlefield, a promise); the message "The child of gold shall return when darkness rises." Records say someone deliberately removed the most important pages.',
  quote:'"The truth has started searching for you." — King Greyson',
  events:['Records show Dima as a guardian tied to the pearl and a child of light','Jade wonders if Dima\'s severing of the bond took her choice away; Devon says Dima always allows her to choose','Important pages were deliberately removed','The sealed Pearl Chamber holds a fragment of the Black Pearl','Jade\'s vision: Dima, a woman of light, a weeping mother, a battlefield, a promise','Message: "The child of gold shall return when darkness rises."'],
  purpose:['Reveal: Dima as guardian','Pearl fragment and the prophecy line'],
  unlocks:['Location: Pearl Chamber (Moonveil Temple)','Lore: Dima, guardian of the balance'],
  reward:'The pearl shows its shadow'},
 81:{ title:'A Year of Peace', type:'Story Chapter — quiet life', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale palace',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, King Chadstone',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the turmoil of recent months a quieter rhythm settles over Dragonvale. Jade and Devon remain at the palace, balancing royal duty, peacekeeping, and the life they were slowly building together. Princess Jade adapts quickly to court and public duty ("She was once only a guard." "And yet she serves Dragonvale well."). King Chadstone: "You have carried your new responsibilities with grace, Princess Jade." "Thank you, Your Majesty. I will continue to do my duty." "She has already earned the respect of this court." Their days are filled with royal matters, quiet investigations, and the steady protection of the realm. "The borders remain calm for now." "You make this all feel less unfamiliar." "Then I will keep doing so." Jade: "You never asked." "About what?" "About us... about when I would be ready." "Because I already know. When you are ready, you will tell me." "You would wait?" "I wait." Their marriage has not yet become a union of bodies, but it has already become a bond of trust, patience, and choice. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: the marriage is still unconsummated by Jade\'s own pace; Devon says he will wait. No mission or banner.',
  quote:'"When you are ready, you will tell me." — Devon',
  events:['Jade adapts to court and public duty; the court respects her','King Chadstone praises her','Jade and Devon talk about when she will be ready; Devon says he will wait'],
  purpose:['Peace interlude','Jade and Devon\'s relationship beat'],
  unlocks:[],
  reward:'A year of peace'},
 82:{ title:'The Crown Prince', type:'Story Chapter — the succession', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale royal court',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'King Chadstone, Devon, Jade, Prince Aster Chadstone',
  introduced:['Prince Aster Chadstone'],
  sum:'After Roc\'s exile the royal court of Dragonvale gathers once more: the kingdom now needs a clear successor. A crown chooses responsibility, not ambition. The nobles debate ("The next crown prince must have strong military ability." "The royal bloodline and political connections are also important." "He must be able to unite the nobles and maintain stability."). King Chadstone thinks of Roc, his ambitious firstborn son: "...Ambition alone is not enough to carry a crown." The court naturally expects Prince Devon to be named the next crown prince; he has proven his loyalty, wisdom, and unwavering dedication to Dragonvale. Devon: "Father. There is someone more suitable." Jade: "Someone else...?" King Chadstone: "You recommend another... instead of yourself?" Devon: "A kingdom deserves the best ruler." Prince Aster Chadstone, the younger prince, has long focused on study and martial arts, staying away from politics. He is calm in temperament, bright in mind, and understands the weight of responsibility; a brilliant star of Dragonvale, respected for his knowledge, martial skill, and integrity. King Chadstone: "You looked farther than ambition. You observed your brothers well, judged with foresight, and chose what is best for Dragonvale. That is the heart of a true ruler and the maturity of a prince. By my decree, Prince Aster Chadstone is named Crown Prince of Dragonvale. May he lead with wisdom, strength, and a heart for our people." Aster: "I will carry this responsibility faithfully and strive to be worthy of your trust, Father." The nobles of Dragonvale acknowledge the royal decree: "Long live Crown Prince Aster Chadstone!" Jade: "You could have been king." Devon: "I already have everything I wanted."',
  art:'Pages show: Devon recommends his younger brother Prince Aster Chadstone and declines the crown himself. Aster is a new character (not shown as a party member).',
  quote:'"A kingdom deserves the best ruler." — Prince Devon',
  events:['The court debates who should be the next crown prince','The court expects Devon; Devon recommends Prince Aster instead','King Chadstone names Aster Crown Prince of Dragonvale','Jade tells Devon he could have been king; Devon says he already has everything he wanted'],
  purpose:['Succession resolved (Aster is Crown Prince)'],
  unlocks:['Prince Aster Chadstone introduced'],
  reward:'Aster becomes Crown Prince'},
 83:{ title:'The Life We Build', type:'Story Chapter — daily life in Dragonvale', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale palace, villages and Royal Healing Pavilion',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika, Liora, Greyson (by bracelet)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After many trials and difficult choices life in Dragonvale finds a calmer rhythm. The palace and its people continue to grow stronger together. Not every important moment is a battle: sometimes the greatest strength is found in the days we build together. Jade trains the palace guards ("Stay focused. Protection is a responsibility to our people. A strong Dragonvale depends on all of you.") and visits the villages, listening to the needs of the people and offering her support ("Your voices matter. A strong kingdom is built with its people."). Devon teaches young nobles and retainers, sharing his knowledge and experience ("Leadership is not about power, but about knowing when to listen and when to act."), and handles royal affairs, reviewing reports and magical research to strengthen Dragonvale\'s future ("These new magical archives will help us prepare for what comes next. Knowledge today prevents crises tomorrow."). At the Royal Healing Pavilion Jenika teaches Liora about herbs and basic healing ("This is a calming herb. It helps the body heal and feel at peace." "It\'s so pretty! Can it help people feel better?"). The palace seamstresses teach Liora simple embroidery ("I did it! It\'s a flower like yours!"). Jenika: "Dragonvale\'s energy flows differently. That is why Liora has grown so quickly. Her potential is remarkable." Later Jade and Devon enjoy a quiet moment with Liora, reflecting on the past and the future. "Do you think people can change?" "Some can. But only when they choose to. Roc chose his path. Delilah chose hers. In the end, everyone must live with the choices they make." Later Jade\'s bracelet vibrates with a message from Greyson: "Enjoy your time in Dragonvale. Soon, Tribute will need you again." "Another mission?" "Eventually. For now, we continue building the life we have here." There will always be new challenges, new responsibilities, and roads we must take. But today, we have something precious: a kingdom that we protect, a family that we cherish, and a life we build together. And whatever comes next, we will face it, side by side. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: a daily-life chapter with Liora (now a small child who grows fast because of Dragonvale\'s energy). Greyson hints that Tribute will need Jade again soon.',
  quote:'"Not every important moment is a battle." — narration',
  events:['Jade trains the palace guards and visits villages','Devon teaches young nobles and reviews magical research','Jenika and the seamstresses teach Liora','Jade and Devon talk about Roc\'s and Delilah\'s choices','Greyson: soon Tribute will need you again'],
  purpose:['Peaceful life in Dragonvale (daily activities)','Foreshadow the return to Tribute'],
  unlocks:['Dragonvale daily life activities'],
  reward:'A calm year'},
 85:{ title:'The Last Duty Before Departure', type:'Story Chapter — the final Dragonvale mission', loc:'🏔️ Dragonvale palace → border village (eastern border) → mountain shrine',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Greyson (by bracelet), border villagers',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a year of protecting Dragonvale, countless challenges and many truths uncovered, one final duty remains before Jade and Devon return to Tribute. The kingdom is at peace, but old wounds still linger; before departure there is one more matter they have to resolve. In the palace Jade and Devon review the latest reports from the border regions: "The disturbances have grown more frequent near the eastern border." "This will be our final mission in Dragonvale. Let\'s see it through to the end." Jade\'s bracelet glows. King Greyson: "Before you return to Tribute... there is one matter only you can resolve. The border disturbances, the awakened creatures, and the weakened ancient barriers in Dragonvale are connected. I need you to finish this last duty." Jade: "I understand. I will complete this final duty for Dragonvale." Devon: "I am with you until the end. We\'ll resolve this together." They journey to a remote border village where the people have been plagued by corrupted spirits and restless creatures: "The village has been living in fear... The barrier near the mountain shrine has weakened." Jade protects the villagers with her sword, driving back the corrupted spirits ("Stay behind me! I will keep you safe!") while Devon channels royal magic to stabilize the ancient seal ("Hold steady... The barrier is responding!"). The ancient barrier has been disturbed by lingering consequences of past forbidden events; with their combined strength they restore what had been weakened ("The seal is healing... Dragonvale\'s spirit still endures."). As the final seal is restored a message appears: "The path continues beyond this kingdom." With their last duty complete Jade and Devon look upon the healed borderland: their year in Dragonvale is nearly at an end, but the path ahead will lead to new lands, new responsibilities, and deeper truths. "This is the end of our time in Dragonvale... ...but only the beginning of what lies ahead." "No matter where we go, we face it together." Main Story Quest: The Last Duty Before Departure. Objectives (all checked): investigate the border disturbances; defeat the corrupted spirits; restore Dragonvale\'s ancient barrier.',
  art:'Pages show: the author\'s planned \'Before returning to Tribute\' mission: Greyson says the border disturbances, awakened creatures and weakened barriers are connected. The ending message \'The path continues beyond this kingdom\' points beyond Dragonvale (Altan?). Chapter 84 is not provided yet.',
  quote:'"The path continues beyond this kingdom." — the restored seal',
  events:['Greyson: one matter only Jade can resolve before she returns to Tribute','A remote border village lives in fear; the barrier near the mountain shrine has weakened','Jade drives back corrupted spirits while Devon stabilizes the seal','The barrier is restored; a message says the path continues beyond the kingdom'],
  purpose:['Greyson\'s mission 4: the final Dragonvale mission','Close the Dragonvale arc'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Last Duty Before Departure (3 objectives)'],
  reward:'The last duty is done'},
 84:{ title:'The Princess and the Child', type:'Story Chapter — Liora grows up', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale palace and Royal Healing Pavilion',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Jenika, Liora and the palace seamstresses',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a year in Dragonvale life is peaceful, and Liora has grown surrounded by love, knowledge, and the kingdom\'s powerful magic. The magical energy of Dragonvale helped her grow more quickly than an ordinary child: now, at three years old, Liora is bright, curious, and full of life. At the Royal Healing Pavilion Jenika teaches Liora the basics of healing: the names of herbs, how to prepare simple tonics, and the importance of caring for others ("This is snowbloom. It helps the body heal gently." "I want to help people too!"). The palace seamstresses also teach Liora embroidery and stitching; she quickly learns, her small hands already skilled and careful ("Look! I made a flower like the ones in the palace garden!" "It\'s beautiful, Liora. You have a very good eye."). Jade teaches Liora discipline and focus: that a princess must be both kind and strong, with a calm heart and a steady mind ("Keep your posture straight, Liora. A true strength comes from within." "Yes! I will be brave like you!"). Devon teaches Liora patience: to observe, to think, and to stay calm even when things are difficult ("Sometimes the best choice is to wait and understand first." "I will try to be patient like you, Father."). As the days pass Liora continues to grow, learning from everyone around her, cherished by the people of Dragonvale; her laughter brings warmth to the palace. Jade: "She smiles like Delilah." Devon: "And she has Roc\'s stubbornness. Both are precious parts of her." Liora faces each new day with curiosity and kindness: she discovers the beauty in small things ("Look! A butterfly! It\'s so pretty!"), and her joy reminds everyone why they continue to build a brighter future. "I want to help many people... just like everyone here has helped me!" This is the life they chose: a family built not only from blood, but from love, protection, and all the tomorrows they will face together. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: Liora is three years old on the page and calls Jade and Devon Mother/Father in the dialogue (Devon is called Father). Jenika, the seamstresses, Jade and Devon each teach her something different.',
  quote:'"I want to help many people... just like everyone here has helped me!" — Liora',
  events:['Jenika teaches Liora herbs and tonics','The seamstresses teach her embroidery','Jade teaches discipline and focus; Devon teaches patience','Liora smiles like Delilah and has Roc\'s stubbornness','Liora wants to help many people, as everyone has helped her'],
  purpose:['Liora\'s childhood (supports the letters and the later pouch)'],
  unlocks:['Liora (age 3) in Dragonvale'],
  reward:'Liora grows up surrounded by love'},
 86:{ title:'Farewell to Dragonvale', type:'Story Chapter — the farewell', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale throne hall → palace gate',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'King Chadstone, Jade, Devon, Jenika, Liora',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With the final duty complete peace returns to Dragonvale. At last Jade and Devon prepare to leave for Tribute. King Chadstone: "You restored what had been weakened and protected this kingdom in its hour of need. You came here as an outsider. You leave as someone Dragonvale will never forget." Jade: "Your Majesty, Dragonvale has become precious to me as well." Devon: "We only did what duty required. But this kingdom will always remain in our hearts." Liora: "You\'re really leaving?" Jenika: "Duty is calling them home." Jade: "Even if we travel far, you are still family, Liora." Devon: "Grow well, little one. We will return whenever we can." Jenika: "Leave her without worry. I will watch over her here." King Chadstone to Devon: "You looked beyond ambition, Devon. Your foresight, restraint, and understanding of your brothers brought wisdom to this house. That is the mind of a true prince." "Thank you, Father." Liora: "Come back soon!" "We will." Jade: "Our year here changed so much." Devon: "And it gave us something worth protecting." They leave Dragonvale not as strangers, but as names the kingdom would remember. To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: Jenika keeps Liora in Dragonvale. Jade and Devon leave for Tribute by horse carriage. The return to Tribute is the next chapter.',
  quote:'"You came here as an outsider. You leave as someone Dragonvale will never forget." — King Chadstone',
  events:['King Chadstone honours Jade and Devon','Jade tells Liora she is still family','Jenika promises to watch over Liora','King Chadstone praises Devon\'s wisdom','Jade and Devon leave for Tribute'],
  purpose:['Close the Dragonvale year','Hand off to the return to Tribute'],
  unlocks:['Liora stays in Dragonvale with Jenika','Departure for Tribute'],
  reward:'The farewell'},
 87:{ title:'The Shadow at Dragonvale\'s Gate', type:'Story Chapter — the departure and reunion', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale gate → the road to the jetty',
  chars:['jade','devon','seraphina','levi','sky','sally'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Seraphina, Levi, Sky, Sally (and Jenika, Liora in the distance)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'At Dragonvale\'s gate a new departure begins. Some farewells mark an ending; others mark the return of what was lost. Seraphina Altan approaches Jade and Devon: "Princess Jade. Prince Devon. I ask to travel with you." She holds up a scroll: "His Majesty has granted my divorce. I would rather choose my own road now." Though they are leaving, part of their hearts remains with the life they built in Dragonvale: the Royal Healing Pavilion stands in the distance, where Jenika and Liora are, the people who brought so much light into their lives. Sally, in her noble purple, says: "Take care of yourselves. Dragonvale will always welcome you back." Sky, too, says goodbye after spending so much time with Jenika during the year: "Safe travels." On the way to the jetty their journey is interrupted by an unexpected shadow on the road: a lone figure stands before them, blocking the way. Levi: "I suppose I took longer than expected to return. A spirit healer found me between life and death. I survived... and I recovered." Jade: "Levi... you\'re alive." Devon: "Then come with us. Your place is still beside us." Jade embraces him: "I\'m so happy to see you again. Welcome back, Levi." "We\'re stronger now, together once more. A new journey awaits us." Banners: Permanent Party Member Joined: Seraphina Altan. Party Member Rejoined: Levi.',
  art:'Pages show: no battle (the road is blocked by Levi, not an ambush). The banners list only Seraphina (permanent) and Levi (rejoined). Sky is shown saying goodbye to Jenika with new blue-and-white attire and says \'Safe travels\'; he stays with the party (confirmed by the author): he is sad to leave Jenika. Sally waves them off and stays in Dragonvale. Levi\'s attire is dark green with a long cloak; he was healed by a spirit healer.',
  quote:'"A spirit healer found me between life and death. I survived... and I recovered." — Levi',
  events:['Seraphina asks to travel with Jade and Devon, holding the Divorce Scroll','Sally and Sky say goodbye','A lone figure blocks the road: Levi, alive and recovered','Levi rejoins the party','Banners: Seraphina Altan joins permanently; Levi rejoins'],
  purpose:['Seraphina becomes a permanent party member','Levi returns (reborn)','Departure toward Tribute'],
  unlocks:['Permanent Party Member Joined: Seraphina Altan','Party Member Rejoined: Levi','Sky\'s recovery gear'],
  reward:'Seraphina joins; Levi returns'},
 88:{ title:'The Ghost Healer', type:'Story Chapter — how Levi survived (no battle)', loc:'🏔️ Mountain road → a village on the edge of the mountains',
  chars:['jade','devon','seraphina','levi','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Seraphina, Levi, Sky and the Ghost Healer',
  introduced:['The Ghost Healer'],
  sum:'After leaving Dragonvale Levi returns to the group. The journey continues as they travel through the mountains, giving them time to rest and talk. Though safe for now, many questions remain, especially how Levi survived after his defeat. Jade: "Levi... How did you survive? You were gravely wounded." Levi: "I was dying after my defeat. I thought it was the end... But then... a healer found me." "A healer? Who are they?" "Are they from a sect? A kingdom?" "You don\'t know who they are?" "No. Even now... I still do not know their true identity." Levi: "I awoke in a small village on the edge of the mountains. A mysterious healer had found me and brought me there. The villagers called them the Ghost Healer. They appear suddenly, heal the impossible, and always disappear before dawn. I was badly wounded, my body tainted by corrupted magic. They used ancient techniques and rare herbs to cleanse the darkness within me. I would not have survived without them." Today the party has the chance to meet them. They agree to help for a short time, but remain as enigmatic as the rumors say. Ghost Healer: "I have only one condition. I do not stay in any city, and I do not reveal my name." The Ghost Healer notices Sky\'s healing ability immediately and studies his technique with great interest: "That power... Where did you learn this?" Sky: "I don\'t remember." "Your power is unusual. It is like no healing art I have seen. There are traces of something very old within you... something long forgotten." Sky: "I really... don\'t remember anything about my past." Jade: "Sky... Your past may be connected deeper than we imagined." Levi: "The Ghost Healer\'s reaction was not normal. Whatever you are, Sky, it is important. And someone has hidden it from you." Jade: "Perhaps this is the beginning of a greater truth, about Sky... and about the world itself." Levi has returned, but new mysteries have now emerged. The identity of the Ghost Healer remains unknown, and Sky\'s origin may be tied to a forgotten past and a power that could change everything. For now the Ghost Healer travels with us, but only for a while. A new journey has begun, and the truth is still hidden in the shadows.',
  art:'Pages show: no battle. The Ghost Healer is veiled, long-haired, and unnamed. They agree to travel with the party for a while on one condition: they do not stay in any city and do not reveal their name. They recognise something very old and forgotten in Sky\'s healing. The comic writes the Ghost Healer as \'they\'.',
  quote:'"There are traces of something very old within you... something long forgotten." — the Ghost Healer',
  events:['Levi explains a healer found him dying and took him to a mountain village','The villagers call them the Ghost Healer: they appear suddenly, heal the impossible and vanish before dawn','The party meets the Ghost Healer; they agree to help for a short time','Their one condition: no staying in any city, and no name','They sense something old and forgotten in Sky\'s healing','The Ghost Healer travels with the party, but only for a while'],
  purpose:['Explain how Levi survived','Introduce the Ghost Healer (slotless companion)','Seed the mystery of Sky\'s past'],
  unlocks:['The Ghost Healer joins (does not use a party slot)','Quest: A Gift for the Ghost Healer'],
  reward:'The Ghost Healer joins; a mystery about Sky'},
 89:{ title:'Return to Tribute', type:'Story Chapter — the homecoming', loc:'🏯 Tribute capital (palace gates)',
  chars:['jade','devon','seraphina','levi','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Seraphina, Levi, Sky and King Greyson',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a year in Dragonvale the traveling party returns to Tribute. The familiar spires rise before them once more. The road has been long, the journey dangerous, and many mysteries still remain, but for now they are home. The travelers return weary but safe, carrying new experiences, new allies, and new questions. King Greyson: "Welcome back. It has been too long." "I leave you in Dragonvale for one year... and you return with more mysteries than answers." Jade: "You expected less?" Greyson: "No. That is why I sent you. You have all endured much. For your efforts, I grant you one week of rest. Even heroes need a home." Levi: "A whole week? I\'m looking forward to real food and a real bed." Sky: "It\'s been too long." Jade: "One week to rest, to see my family again, and to be back in Tribute..." Greyson: "...then we prepare for what comes next. For now, we are home." For one week the travelers can rest, reunite with loved ones, and regain their strength. But the mysteries of Dragonvale, and the shadows ahead, still await.',
  art:'Pages show: the court (Greyson) welcomes the party in the capital; Seraphina stands among them (a permanent party member). The page\'s own caption calls Greyson \'the young king of Tribute\'.',
  quote:'"Even heroes need a home." — King Greyson',
  events:['The party returns to the Tribute capital','Greyson welcomes them and grants one week of rest','Jade looks forward to seeing her family'],
  purpose:['Return to Tribute','One week of rest'],
  unlocks:['One week of rest (party fully restored)'],
  reward:'The party is home and rests a week'},
 90:{ title:'The Gold Reunion', type:'Story Chapter — the Gold residence', loc:'🏡 Gold residence, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Unique Gold, Elara Valor, Adrian Gold',
  introduced:['Unique Gold (father)','Elara Valor (mother)','Adrian Gold (older brother)'],
  sum:'With their rest period granted Jade and Devon arrive at the Gold residence, the place she once called home but could barely remember. The gates, the familiar scent, the golden trees: everything feels both strange and warm. She has returned, but this time she is no longer a child. Jade: "I\'m more nervous now than when facing a demon..." Devon: "You have faced far greater dangers without hesitation. This is just a family dinner. Demons don\'t ask embarrassing questions." Her father Unique Gold, Imperial Advisor: "Welcome home, my daughter." Her mother Elara Valor, of a psychic lineage: "It\'s been too long." Unique Gold: "Prince Devon, thank you for accompanying my daughter back. I have heard much about you. A prince who refuses a crown is a rare sight in this world." Her older brother Adrian Gold, a government official: "So... this is my little sister. It has been a long time, Jade." Jade: "I\'m sorry... I don\'t remember you." Adrian: "Then I suppose I have to reintroduce myself again. Even if you have forgotten, I have not." He holds out a small flower charm: "You refused to let go of this when you were little. You said it protected you." Jade: "...I did?" Devon: "It seems... you were very loved." Though many things have changed, Jade realises some feelings remain the same. She may have lost her memories, but she has not lost her place. This was home.',
  art:'Pages show: the Gold family are introduced with name plates: Unique Gold (father, Imperial Advisor), Elara Valor (mother, psychic lineage), Adrian Gold (older brother, government official). Adrian gives Jade back her childhood flower charm. Jade does not remember them.',
  quote:'"She may have lost her memories, but she had not lost her place. This was home."',
  events:['Jade and Devon arrive at the Gold residence','Unique Gold, Elara Valor and Adrian Gold are introduced','Jade does not remember them','Adrian returns the flower charm she would not let go of as a child'],
  purpose:['Introduce Jade\'s family','Return Jade\'s childhood charm'],
  unlocks:['Location: Gold residence','Item: Childhood Flower Charm'],
  reward:'Jade is home'},
 91:{ title:'The Mother\'s Question', type:'Story Chapter — a mother\'s questions', loc:'🏡 Gold residence',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Elara Valor, Unique Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the events of the Gold Reunion Jade returns to the Gold residence in Tribute, where she is finally home with her family again. Amidst the warmth and laughter her mother soon pulls her aside for a private conversation. Jade: "It feels so good to be home again." Elara: "Jade, my dear. Come with me for a moment?" "Of course, Mother." In a quieter corner of the residence Elara has the unmistakable look of a mother who has questions. "Are you happy?" "Yes." "Is he kind?" "Yes." "Does he respect you?" "Yes." "Good. Then why haven\'t you consummated?" Jade: "Mother!" Elara: "Oh? Did I say something wrong? A mother simply has a very strong intuition." Jade: "Devon has been so patient with me. He has never pressured me... I just... I wasn\'t ready yet..." Elara: "Mm. A considerate husband is a treasure. But being ready doesn\'t happen by accident, dear. Shall I give you some advice? There are many things a mother can teach you. ♥" Even a princess cannot escape her mother\'s questions. Some things never change... and perhaps that is a kind of love too.',
  art:'Pages show: a comic family beat. Elara\'s intuition picks up that the marriage has not been consummated (matches chapter 81). Devon is not in this scene.',
  quote:'"A considerate husband is a treasure. But being ready doesn\'t happen by accident, dear." — Elara',
  events:['Elara pulls Jade aside','Jade says she is happy, Devon is kind and respectful','Elara guesses the marriage is unconsummated; Jade is embarrassed','Elara offers advice'],
  purpose:['Family comedy beat','Jade and Devon\'s relationship'],
  unlocks:[],
  reward:'Mother knows best'},
 92:{ title:'The Missing Sister', type:'Story Chapter — Yvette Sue Valen', loc:'🏡 Gold residence (family dinner)',
  chars:['jade','devon','levi','sky'], charsNote:'The Gold family, Jade, Devon, Levi, Sky',
  introduced:['Yvette Sue Valen (missing)'],
  sum:'During their rest in Tribute the Gold family spend time together, sharing stories and old memories. But amid the familiar warmth a long-hidden pain surfaces. In the safety of Tribute, surrounded by family, they speak of the past, and in that conversation a name emerges once more. Jade, holding a framed portrait: "Who is that?" Elara: "My sister. My half-sister was Yvette Sue Valen. We had the same mother, but different gifts. I inherited the psychic abilities... Yvette did not have visions, but she possessed another gift... healing. She left one day... and never returned. We do not know why. She simply disappeared..." Jade: "You never searched?" Elara: "We did. But even my visions could not find her. No trace. It was as if she vanished from this world." Devon: "For a family with visions... that is almost unthinkable." Adrian: "Yet we could not find her..." Unique Gold: "Some wounds never truly heal." Sky sits silently, looking at the portrait. A family blessed with psychic sight could not find one of their own. Some memories disappear. Some people disappear. And the question still remains. (Portrait plate: Yvette Sue Valen, Elara\'s half-sister, Healer.)',
  art:'Pages show: Sky, Levi and Devon at the family table; Sky stays quiet and looks at the portrait. Elara\'s visions could not find Yvette. Yvette is called \'Sue\' in later chapters.',
  quote:'"It was as if she vanished from this world." — Elara',
  events:['Jade finds a portrait of Elara and her half-sister','Elara tells of Yvette Sue Valen, a healer who disappeared','Even Elara\'s visions could not find her','Sky says nothing, looking at the portrait'],
  purpose:['Introduce the missing sister','Seed Sky\'s connection'],
  unlocks:['Lore: Yvette Sue Valen'],
  reward:'The missing sister'},
 93:{ title:'The Boy Who Looks Like Sue', type:'Story Chapter — Sky\'s resemblance', loc:'🏡 Gold residence training court',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Gold family, Jade, Devon, Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'During their week of rest in Tribute the Gold family spend more time together. On one quiet day, in the residence\'s training court, Sky demonstrates his healing ability during practice: he gently mends a training injury, his light soft, warm and filled with life, amazing everyone who watches. From nearby Elara watches and suddenly freezes. A familiar feeling stirs in her heart, one she has not felt for many years. Jade: "Mother?" Elara: "What is your name?" "Sky." "Who taught you healing?" "I don\'t know." Everyone falls silent: Jade, Devon, Unique Gold and Adrian look at Sky with concern and curiosity; there is something deeply puzzling about his answer. Elara: "He looks like her." Jade: "Who?" Elara: "My sister. Yvette Sue." Sky: "Your sister?" Yvette Sue Valen, Elara\'s younger sister: a kind and gentle woman with rare psychic abilities, she disappeared many years ago, leaving behind unanswered questions and a family that never stopped wondering. Sky: "The past sometimes returns wearing a different face." An old disappearance, a beloved sister, and a boy who looks just like her.',
  art:'Pages show: Sky heals a training injury in front of the Gold family; Elara sees Yvette Sue in him. The page calls Yvette Elara\'s \'younger sister\' (chapter 92 called her half-sister).',
  quote:'"The past sometimes returns wearing a different face." — Sky',
  events:['Sky heals an injury at the training court','Elara freezes: his light is familiar','Sky does not know who taught him healing','Elara: he looks like her sister, Yvette Sue'],
  purpose:['Link Sky to Yvette Sue Valen'],
  unlocks:['Lore: Sky resembles Yvette'],
  reward:'Sky looks like Yvette Sue'},
 94:{ title:'The Unanswered Bloodline', type:'Story Chapter — the family gathers', loc:'🏡 Gold residence',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Gold family, Jade, Devon, Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'During their week of rest in Tribute the Gold family continue to search for answers about Sky\'s past. The recent revelation raises new questions that cannot be easily resolved. The family gathers to share what they know and to consider the possibilities, even if the truth is still out of reach. Elara: "Sky\'s healing ability resembles Yvette\'s technique. The way he channels light and restores others is very similar. It is a rare and unique gift that carried through our family line." Yvette Sue was known for her gentle healing, her deep empathy, and her ability to bring comfort to those in pain; Sky\'s mannerisms also remind them of her: his kindness, his quiet nature, and the way he looks at people with such compassion. Sky: "I don\'t know... I remember so little. I can\'t say whether it means anything. My memories are still incomplete." Unique Gold: "It\'s possible his memories were sealed. Or that he was separated from Yvette at a young age. There could be many reasons..." Adrian: "We cannot jump to conclusions. There are still too many unknowns." Devon: "Whether or not he is blood, Sky is family now. But if there is a truth to discover, we should be prepared for whatever it may be." Jade suddenly remembers something: the light green jade pendant that Sky once showed her. "Sky... the jade pendant you once showed me, the light green one... It\'s no longer with you? Do you know what happened to it?" Sky: "I don\'t know. It\'s gone... I don\'t remember when or how I lost it." Jade: "If Sky is connected to your family... then he deserves to know the truth. Whatever the answer is, he has the right to his past, and to the people who are part of it." Devon: "Another person searching for where they belong. Just like Jade... Just like so many of us. The past does not always give clear answers, but it still matters." Elara: "After all these years... Did fate finally bring you back?"',
  art:'Pages show: the lost light green jade pendant is a new clue (Sky once showed it to Jade; he does not remember losing it). Nothing is confirmed: Sky may or may not be Yvette\'s son. This chapter ends the week of rest.',
  quote:'"Whether or not he is blood, Sky is family now." — Devon',
  events:['Elara compares Sky\'s healing to Yvette\'s technique','Sky remembers little; his memories are incomplete','Unique Gold: his memories may have been sealed, or he was separated young','Jade remembers Sky\'s light green jade pendant; he has lost it','Devon and Jade say Sky has the right to his past'],
  purpose:['Sky\'s origin mystery deepens','Plant the lost jade pendant quest'],
  unlocks:['Clue: Sky\'s lost jade pendant','Future quest: Sky\'s origin'],
  reward:'Sky\'s past is an open question'},
 95:{ title:'The Imperial Guardian Returns', type:'Story Chapter — back at court', loc:'🏯 King Greyson\'s court, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, King Greyson, Adrian Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a week of rest in Tribute Jade and Devon return to King Greyson\'s court. The time to recover has ended and now Jade is home again. The same palace, the same people, but everything feels different now: she is no longer just a guest of Dragonvale. This is her home. Greyson: "Welcome back, Jade. Welcome back, Devon. A week was enough?" Devon: "For eating and sleeping. Perhaps not enough for peace." Greyson: "I expected nothing less." In Tribute Jade stands not only as Devon\'s wife but also as a trusted guardian and ally of the young king: this is her place, and her responsibility. Adrian Gold (Jade\'s older brother, government official): "The last time I saw you, you were still small enough to hold my hand." Jade: "I\'m sorry. I still don\'t remember everything." Adrian: "Then I will remember enough for both of us." Some nobles still question Lady Jade\'s position: "She returned from Dragonvale, but what is her role in Tribute now?" Greyson: "Jade Gold was not chosen because of blood alone. She proved herself by protecting this kingdom when others hesitated. She remains a valued guardian of Tribute. That is enough." Adrian: "Prince Devon, my sister has carried much alone." Devon: "Then I will stand beside her, not behind her." Greyson: "Dragonvale needed you. Now Tribute needs you again. There are new challenges ahead, and I want you by my side." Jade once thought she had to choose where she belonged, but now she sees she does not have to choose. She can belong to more than one home. As family, as a protector, and as a part of both Dragonvale and Tribute, her journey continues. Main Story Quest: The Imperial Guardian Returns. Objectives: return to Greyson\'s court; reunite with Adrian Gold; prepare for Tribute\'s next mission.',
  art:'Pages show: the Main Story Quest box has three objectives. Nobles question Jade\'s role; Greyson defends her. The boxed quote: she can belong to more than one home.',
  quote:'"She does not have to choose. She can belong to more than one home."',
  events:['Greyson welcomes Jade and Devon back','Adrian Gold stands at court and tells Jade he will remember enough for both of them','Nobles question Jade\'s role; Greyson names her a valued guardian of Tribute','Devon: he will stand beside her, not behind her','Greyson: Tribute needs you again'],
  purpose:['Return to Tribute\'s court','Settle Jade\'s place at court'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Imperial Guardian Returns (3 objectives)'],
  reward:'Jade is Tribute\'s guardian again'},
 96:{ title:'The Brother Who Remembers', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian and the accident', loc:'🏯 King Greyson\'s court, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Adrian Gold, Unique Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a week of rest in Tribute Jade returns to court; this time she sees her brother not as a distant memory but as one of King Greyson\'s trusted officials. Jade was no longer just a guest from Dragonvale: she had returned as family, and her brother stood beside the king. Unique Gold: "Your analysis is thorough, Adrian. These policies will strengthen Tribute\'s borders and our alliances." While away from home Adrian studied at the Imperial Academy and served in government training: he learned statecraft, law, history, diplomacy, calligraphy, music and refined arts, while also maintaining martial discipline. He became a calm and observant official who helps Greyson manage the court, with wisdom, integrity, and a deep sense of duty to the people of Tribute. Jade: "He has grown so much... This is the life he built while I was gone. You\'ve become such an important part of the court, Adrian." Adrian: "I only did what I should. I\'m glad you have returned, Jade." Memories: "We once played together beneath the golden trees at the Gold residence. You were always so full of life." "I taught you calligraphy, history, and discipline. I wanted to protect you and help you grow stronger." "Years ago, I left home to study at the Imperial Academy and to serve the realm. Our family saw me off with pride, knowing it was my duty to learn and to return stronger one day." "But then, the accident changed everything. After I nearly drowned, many of my memories were lost. The girl who returned felt different, as if a part of her had changed forever. Some in the family called the blessing that remained "Luck."" Jade: "I still don\'t remember everything clearly, Adrian... But I am still Jade Gold. Now I carry both myself and Luck\'s power, permanently. It is part of who I am." Adrian: "It doesn\'t matter what you remember or what you have forgotten. I remember enough for both of us, Jade. You are still my sister." Devon watches the reunion with a quiet smile: even after so much change, family endures. Main Story Quest: The Brother Who Remembers. Objectives: learn Adrian Gold\'s role in court; revisit Jade\'s childhood memories; understand how "Luck" became part of Jade\'s life.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade nearly drowned as a child (an accident), her childhood memories blurred together afterwards, and \'Luck\' remained as a blessing (a power she carries permanently, along with herself). Adrian was away at the Imperial Academy when it happened. AUTHOR NOTE: the comic says memories were \'lost\'; the author clarifies they were never meant to be lost, only fuzzy and merged (the drowning is the transmigration; spoiler, kept out of game text). Dragonvale tonics (given after her marriage, and sometimes sent as royal tribute) help her recover them.',
  quote:'"It doesn\'t matter what you remember or what you have forgotten. You are still my sister." — Adrian',
  events:['Adrian\'s role: Imperial Academy, statecraft, now Greyson\'s trusted official','Jade remembers playing beneath the golden trees','The accident: Jade nearly drowned, memories blurred, \'Luck\' remained','Jade carries both herself and Luck\'s power, permanently','Adrian: I remember enough for both of us'],
  purpose:['Introduce Luck (a lasting power from the accident)','Adrian\'s role at court'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Brother Who Remembers (3 objectives)','Lore: Luck'],
  reward:'Jade\'s brother remembers'},
 97:{ title:'The Advisor\'s Daughter', type:'Story Chapter — the house of Gold and the Valor lineage', loc:'🏡 Gold residence, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Unique Gold, Elara Valor',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After returning to court Jade spends part of her week of rest with her family, listening to the stories that shaped the house of Gold. For the first time she is not only a daughter returning home but a woman deciding what her place in Tribute will be. Unique Gold: "Our family has served Tribute for generations. An Imperial Advisor does not chase glory. We preserve balance." The house of Gold stood beside the throne not as rulers, but as guides, offering judgment, strategy, and loyalty to the crown. Elara: "And the Valor bloodline carries a different duty. We listen to what others cannot hear." Elara came from a psychic lineage, a family touched by visions, intuition, and strange fragments of fate. Jade: "Then what am I meant to be?" Unique Gold: "Not a copy of either of us." Elara: "You were born between two legacies. Wisdom from one side. Sight from the other." As a child Jade had been taught history, discipline, and compassion beneath the golden trees of home. After the accident many memories faded, yet something within her endured: something the family once called Luck. Jade: "I still do not understand all of it. But I know I am Jade Gold." Unique Gold: "That is enough. A name gains meaning through the life it chooses. Titles may come later. But your role is already clear. In Dragonvale, you protected a kingdom. In Tribute, you may serve as guardian, envoy, and witness to the truth." Devon: "You do not need to choose only one home." Jade: "Then I will protect both, Tribute and Dragonvale." The daughter of an advisor and a psychic lineage did not need to become what others expected. She only needed to become herself. Main Story Quest: The Advisor\'s Daughter. Objectives: learn the duty of the house of Gold; understand the Valor psychic lineage; define Jade\'s place in Tribute.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade\'s role is defined as guardian, envoy and witness to the truth in Tribute. \'Luck\' is named again as what endured after the accident.',
  quote:'"A name gains meaning through the life it chooses." — Unique Gold',
  events:['Unique Gold explains the house of Gold: guides who preserve balance','Elara explains the Valor lineage: they listen to what others cannot hear','Jade is born between two legacies: wisdom from one side, sight from the other','Her role: guardian, envoy and witness to the truth','Jade resolves to protect both Tribute and Dragonvale'],
  purpose:['Define Jade\'s place in Tribute'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Advisor\'s Daughter (3 objectives)','Title in Tribute: guardian, envoy and witness'],
  reward:'Jade chooses to be herself'},
 98:{ title:'The Missing Documents', type:'Story Chapter — the royal archives', loc:'📚 Royal archives, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky','seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Elara, Adrian, Unique Gold, Greyson (reports to court)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The quiet week in Tribute has ended. Now the search for the past resumes in the royal archives. Several old files have gone missing: the names within them may matter more than anyone realized. Greyson reports to the court. Adrian: "These shelves once held border logs, healer registries, and restricted family records. Some pages were removed by hand. Look at this. Entire sections are gone. They were deliberately taken, not lost over time." Jade: "Someone wanted these records hidden." Devon: "Then the truth was known by someone long before us." Sky: "Yvette Sue Valen... Why does that name feel familiar? I still remember nothing... but I know this matters." Healer Registry: Yvette Sue Valen, Healer, Travel Permit Approved. Year 812: Healer, Imperial Service. Year 814: Departure, West Border. Year 815: [Missing]. Jade: "Because your mystery may have started long before we met." Sky: "Yvette Sue Valen... a healer? She traveled? Why does this feel like a part of me... even though I cannot remember?" Elara: "My sister\'s name appears again... but never in full. It is always followed by a gap, as if someone erased the rest." Travel Permit: Name Yvette Sue Valen; Purpose: Medical Service; Destination: Western Regions; Companions: none; Approved by: Imperial Court; Year 814, 3rd Month [next entry missing]. Adrian: "Here, this ledger mentions her departure. But the next entry is gone. It should contain where she went, who she met, and what happened after." Devon: "Not lost. Taken. Someone did not want us to know what came next." Sky: "I feel a strange pull when I see her name. It is like a missing piece inside me, but I still cannot remember." Jade: "Then we keep searching. No matter how many records are missing, we will find the truth. You are not alone in this, Sky." The file Family Records, Valen Lineage is empty: the documents have been removed; even the seal was broken and resealed. Devon: "This is larger than a single disappearance. Someone has been hiding the connection between your past and Yvette Sue for many years." Sky: "So my past... my existence... and Yvette Sue\'s disappearance are connected. I may not remember yet, but I will find out. I need to know who I am, and what happened to her." Some truths are hidden by time. Others are hidden by choice. Main Story Quest: The Missing Documents. Objectives: search the royal archives for missing files; find the records on Yvette Sue Valen; trace the missing files tied to Sky\'s past.',
  art:'Pages show: Yvette left in Year 814 (Imperial Service, destination West Border / Western Regions) and the next entry is missing. The Valen lineage file is empty and its seal was broken and resealed. The third objective (trace the missing files tied to Sky\'s past) is open: it stays sealed until the story reaches it.',
  quote:'"Some truths are hidden by time. Others are hidden by choice."',
  events:['Entire sections of the royal archives were deliberately removed','Healer Registry: Yvette Sue Valen, Imperial Service 812, departure to the West Border in 814, then missing','The Valen lineage file is empty; the seal was broken and resealed','Sky feels a strange pull at her name','Devon: someone has been hiding Sky\'s connection to Yvette for years'],
  purpose:['Investigation: the missing documents','Set up the western regions'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Missing Documents (3 objectives)','Lead: Yvette Sue Valen went to the Western Regions in 814'],
  reward:'Yvette\'s trail goes cold in the west'},
 99:{ title:'The King and His Sister', type:'Story Chapter — Jade named Princess of Tribute', loc:'🏯 Greyson\'s court, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, King Greyson, Adrian, Unique Gold, Elara and the court',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the discovery of the missing documents King Greyson summons Jade before the court of Tribute. Nobles, officials, and the royal family gather to witness an important announcement, one that will change the future of Tribute. Jade, accompanied by Devon, enters the royal court; Adrian, Unique, Elara and many lords are present. Whispers: "Why has Jade been called before the king?" "Is it about the missing documents?" "What could he be planning?" Greyson: "Before you were an Imperial Guard... you were the first person who stood beside me. In my earliest days, you stood beside me. When others saw only the throne, you saw me, not as a king, but as a person. You guarded my path long before you carried a blade." Devon: "She has always been there... I could not be prouder of her." Unique Gold: "Jade has always been a pillar of Tribute." Elara: "She has given so much to this kingdom. This is well deserved." Greyson: "Jade Gold, from this day, I acknowledge you as my sworn sister, Princess of Tribute, and guardian of this crown." The court: "Princess of Tribute? The king acknowledges her as his sister? How extraordinary! Truly deserved." Jade: "Your Majesty... I will remain worthy of your trust." Greyson: "Rise, Jade. Family does not kneel alone." Jade: "Thank you... for believing in me." Greyson: "You have always been my sister. And you always will be." Some bonds are forged not only by blood, but by loyalty, trust, and the choice to stand beside one another. Main Story Quest: The King and His Sister. Objectives: attend Greyson\'s court; receive Jade\'s formal acknowledgment; prepare for Tribute\'s next mission.',
  art:'Pages show: Greyson names Jade his sworn sister, Princess of Tribute and guardian of the crown. A flashback shows them as children together. The quest box has three objectives.',
  quote:'"Family does not kneel alone." — King Greyson',
  events:['Greyson summons Jade before the court','He recalls she was the first to stand beside him','He names her his sworn sister, Princess of Tribute, and guardian of this crown','The court accepts the title','Greyson: you have always been my sister'],
  purpose:['Jade becomes Princess of Tribute (and of Dragonvale)'],
  unlocks:['Title: Princess of Tribute','Main Story Quest: The King and His Sister (3 objectives)'],
  reward:'Jade is Princess of Tribute'},
 100:{ title:'The Visions She Hid', type:'Story Chapter — the visions', loc:'🏯 Gold residence / the palace, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Elara, Unique Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After returning to Tribute and reuniting with her family Jade finally speaks of the visions she kept hidden during Dragonvale. Some connections are not destiny; some are wounds waiting to be healed. Devon: "You have been thinking about Dragonvale." Jade: "There is something I never told anyone. During our journey... I saw things." Elara: "You never told anyone?" Jade: "When Roc kept me confined, I felt a strange connection... a bond I could not break. I saw Lady Delilah with child. I thought they were dreams. Two weeks later, my vision came true. Later, I saw Roc leaving with Delilah, but I did not understand what it meant. I had unknowingly seen his exile. Dima came to me. She severed the bond, the dark connection to Roc. She was shielding me from a corrupted connection. But there were other visions too... Visions from Xima. They felt different: older, darker, and far more dangerous." Elara: "Not every vision comes from the same source. The visions of Roc came from the cave\'s dark magic, a bond that connected you to him." Unique Gold: "Your other visions came from your own psychic lineage. And Xima\'s visions were warnings... of a larger evil that still exists." Devon: "You feared what you saw... but you never let it decide who you became." Jade: "...Thank you, Devon." Jade once believed visions were chains binding her to a fate Jade could not escape. But now she understood: the future was not something she had to obey. It was something she could choose to face. And with her family by her side, she would protect not only her own heart, but the island, and those she loves, from what was still to come.',
  art:'Pages show: the visions of Roc came from the cave\'s dark magic and a bond to him (cut by Dima); Jade\'s other visions are her psychic lineage; Xima\'s visions are warnings of a larger evil that still exists. No quest box.',
  quote:'"The future was not something she had to obey. It was something she could choose to face."',
  events:['Jade tells Devon and her family about the visions she hid','The visions of Roc came from the cave\'s dark magic and the bond with him','Dima severed that bond to shield her','Other visions are her psychic lineage; Xima\'s visions are warnings of a larger evil','Devon: you never let the visions decide who you became'],
  purpose:['Explain Jade\'s visions','Reveal that Xima\'s evil still exists'],
  unlocks:['Lore: the three sources of Jade\'s visions'],
  reward:'Jade shares her visions'},
 101:{ title:'The King\'s Request', type:'Story Chapter — the mission beyond Tribute', loc:'🏯 Greyson\'s court, Tribute',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, King Greyson, Adrian, Unique Gold, Elara',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the ceremony the royal court slowly empties. But for Jade, King Greyson\'s summons has not yet ended. A new duty is about to begin, one that will lead beyond Tribute. Greyson: "Jade. Stay behind. What I gave you today was a title the world can see. But there is also a duty only you can fulfill. Beyond Tribute\'s shores, an allied territory has sent word. Envoys have gone missing. Old records have surfaced. And near forgotten ruins, people have begun to disappear. This matter touches Tribute, but it does not belong to Tribute alone." The hidden records may concern an old alliance, one someone wanted erased. Greyson: "I need you to go there, investigate the truth, and represent Tribute beyond this island. Before you were my Imperial Guard... you were the first person who stood beside me." Jade: "If this is your command, I will go." Devon: "Then I will go with her. Where Jade walks, I will stand beside her." Adrian: "It is a distant land, with many uncertainties." Unique Gold: "Then this mission carries both political and personal weight." Elara: "And perhaps answers waiting beyond our sight." Greyson: "Good. Go as Jade Gold: Princess of Tribute, guardian of this crown, and the woman I trust." A week of rest has ended. Now another journey is beginning. Main Story Quest: The King\'s Request. Objectives: travel beyond Tribute; investigate the missing envoys; uncover the hidden records; represent Tribute abroad.',
  art:'Pages show: the allied territory beyond Tribute\'s shores is not named on these pages (the author\'s plan points to Altan). The quest box lists four objectives. The party sets out after this chapter.',
  quote:'"Go as Jade Gold: Princess of Tribute, guardian of this crown, and the woman I trust." — King Greyson',
  events:['Greyson asks Jade to stay behind after the court','Envoys have gone missing in an allied territory beyond Tribute; old records resurfaced; people vanish near forgotten ruins','Greyson sends Jade to investigate and represent Tribute abroad','Devon goes with her','A week of rest has ended: another journey begins'],
  purpose:['Start the journey beyond Tribute','Link the hidden records to an old alliance'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The King\'s Request (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'A journey beyond Tribute begins'},
 102:{ title:'The Road Beyond Tribute', type:'Story Chapter — the departure', loc:'🏯 Tribute harbour',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon (the party is gathering)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The king\'s order has already been given. Now Jade Gold will carry Tribute\'s will beyond its shores. Jade, holding the sealed letter: "So this is where the next road begins." Devon: "And this time, we leave prepared." This is no ceremonial journey: if danger comes, they have to be ready from the first step. Jade: "No fur this time?" Devon: "I prefer surviving ambushes." The missing envoys. Hidden records. A forgotten alliance beyond Tribute. Jade: "The mission begins beyond Tribute\'s borders." Devon: "Then our guard begins now." Jade: "You don\'t have to come." Devon: "I know. I am coming anyway." Jade: "Then I will rely on you again." Devon: "You always can." Behind them is Tribute\'s safety. Ahead of them wait distance, uncertainty, and truth someone has tried to erase. A sealed order in her hands. A new road before her. And beside her, the companion who will walk it with her. Main Story Quest: The Road Beyond Tribute. Objectives: leave Tribute; protect the sealed order; investigate the missing envoys.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade carries Greyson\'s sealed order; Jade and Devon are in travelling armour. The Main Story Quest box has three objectives. The fixed party travels from here.',
  quote:'"Behind them was Tribute\'s safety. Ahead of them waited distance, uncertainty, and truth someone had tried to erase."',
  events:['Jade and Devon set out with the sealed order','Devon: this time we leave prepared','Jade: the mission begins beyond Tribute\'s borders','Devon comes anyway: you always can rely on me'],
  purpose:['Start the journey','Fix the travelling party'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Road Beyond Tribute (3 objectives)','The travelling party is now fixed'],
  reward:'The party leaves Tribute'},
 103:{ title:'The Choice He Made', type:'Story Chapter — husband and wife in truth', loc:'🏯 Jade and Devon\'s chamber, Tribute (the night before departure)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon (Dima in a vision)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The night before departure one final private moment remains for Jade and Devon. Before they step onto the road beyond Tribute they become husband and wife in truth. Jade: "I have something I must tell you. About the palace examination... and the mark it left on my body. I am afraid... how you will see me now." Devon: "Tell me. Whatever it is, you can always tell me. I never cared whether you were \'pure\' or not. I knew my brother\'s tendencies with women. You were a victim, not someone at fault." Jade: "Why did the examination happen? Did you... request it?" Devon: "No, I never requested it. I only wanted to know if you were healthy. If you had needed it, I would have asked Jenika to prescribe something to restore your vitality. Your health came back fine. The only thing that mattered to me... was that you chose me." Jade: "...I chose you, Devon. And I still choose you. Always. I also need to tell you about Dima\'s restoration... and the Tribute prophecy. She has regained her power, and the prophecy speaks of a great change that will affect us all..." Devon: "Fate does not frighten me. If a prophecy exists, then I will face it with you. Whatever comes... I choose you, Jade." Jade: "Then let us face everything together. As husband and wife." That night they give themselves to each other completely: two souls, once wounded, now whole, bound by love, trust, and a future they will face together. They are no longer alone in this world. Whatever road awaits them beyond Tribute, they will walk it together. Their bond awakens a new power: a harmony of dragon and phoenix, born from love, healing, and an unwavering choice. Couple Skill Unlocked: Jade Dragon Harmony (synchronized spiritual power between partners; stronger combat coordination and combined techniques; shared protective resonance that shields both minds and hearts). From this night forward Jade and Devon are not only allies on the road beyond Tribute: they are husband and wife in truth, and their journey will never be the same again.',
  art:'Pages show: the marriage becomes a true one (the scene closes on the couple at night). The comic names the couple skill Jade Dragon Harmony. Earlier plans called a couple skill Twin Dragon Harmony at chapter 77; the comic is canon, so it is one skill, Jade Dragon Harmony, from chapter 103. Dima has regained her power and a Tribute prophecy is mentioned (not explained).',
  quote:'"Whatever comes... I choose you, Jade." — Devon',
  events:['Jade tells Devon about the palace examination and the mark it left','Devon: he never cared, and she was a victim, not at fault','Jade also mentions Dima\'s restoration and the Tribute prophecy','They become husband and wife in truth','Couple Skill Unlocked: Jade Dragon Harmony'],
  purpose:['Jade and Devon\'s marriage becomes complete','Unlock Jade Dragon Harmony (couple skill)'],
  unlocks:['Couple Skill: Jade Dragon Harmony','Lore: Dima has regained her power; the Tribute prophecy'],
  reward:'Jade Dragon Harmony unlocked'},
 104:{ title:'The Forgotten Western Territory', type:'Story Chapter — the Valen Borderlands', loc:'🌄 Tribute → the Valen Borderlands (Forgotten Western Territory)',
  chars:['jade','devon','seraphina','levi','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon (and the party), a border guide and an old archivist',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'By dawn Jade Gold and Devon have already left Tribute behind. The king\'s sealed order leads them west, toward a land the capital no longer truly knows. The Valen Borderlands, once a frontier of healers, envoys, and old alliances, are now known by another name: the Forgotten Western Territory. Jade: "So this is where the next road leads." Devon: "And this time, we travel prepared." "The Valen Borderlands... Missing envoys. Erased records. And a name that keeps returning." The west once linked Tribute to distant allied lands, but its roads have broken, its outposts emptied, and its history begun to vanish. Jade: "Do you think the missing envoys reached the west?" Devon: "If they did, something stopped them from returning." A guide at the old outpost: "Travelers from Tribute? Then you have come to a place people prefer to forget. Messengers vanish on the western road. Old files disappear. And some ruins are better left untouched." Jade, at a crest on the wall: "That crest... Yvette Sue Valen." Devon: "You have seen it before." Even here the past has been disturbed. An archivist: "Sections were removed by hand. Not lost. Taken." Jade: "Someone erased more than names." Devon: "Then the truth is still here. Hidden." The old archivist: "If you seek the old Valen records... pray the dead stayed buried." Beyond Tribute\'s safety lie dust, silence, and truths no one has wanted found. And in the forgotten west, the road toward Yvette Sue\'s mystery has finally begun. Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Western Territory. Objectives: travel to the Valen Borderlands; deliver the sealed order; investigate the missing envoys; search for traces of the erased records.',
  art:'Pages show: the Valen Borderlands (the Forgotten Western Territory) is where Yvette Sue Valen\'s mystery leads (the registry said she went west in Year 814). The caduceus-style crest is Yvette\'s. The map of the Valen Borderlands was provided separately.',
  quote:'"Pray the dead stayed buried." — the old archivist',
  events:['Jade and Devon leave Tribute at dawn with the sealed order','The Valen Borderlands are now called the Forgotten Western Territory','Messengers vanish, files disappear, ruins are better left untouched','Jade finds a crest linked to Yvette Sue Valen','An archivist confirms sections were removed by hand'],
  purpose:['Arrive in the Valen Borderlands','Start Yvette Sue\'s trail in the west'],
  unlocks:['New area: Valen Borderlands (Forgotten Western Territory)','Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Western Territory (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The western road begins'},
 105:{ title:'The Borderland That Was Forgotten', type:'Story Chapter — the Valen records hall', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: border outpost and the old Valen records hall',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Captain Rowan Mirel, Mira Valen, Master Teren',
  introduced:['Captain Rowan Mirel','Mira Valen','Master Teren'],
  sum:'In the forgotten western territory ruins still stand, people still live, and memories still linger. Jade and Devon step deeper into the Valen Borderlands, seeking the truth behind the missing envoys and the erased records. Captain Rowan Mirel, Border Warden: "Tribute finally remembers the west." Jade: "We didn\'t come empty-handed. We came because people disappeared." Devon: "This is King Greyson\'s sealed order." Rowan: "The king sent a princess?" Devon: "No. He sent someone he trusts." The old Valen records hall still stands, but many sections are empty: the damage is too deliberate to be time alone. Jade: "The records were not destroyed." Devon: "Then where are they?" Rowan: "That is a question everyone stopped asking." Devon: "This place does not look abandoned." Rowan: "Someone is still maintaining it. Someone wants the truth to stay hidden." Mira Valen, Valen Descendant: "That symbol... my family used to carry it." Jade: "You are from the Valen family?" Mira: "A distant branch... but the name still remains, even if the world has forgotten us." Jade: "Why were the Valen records removed?" Mira: "Because some truths were not meant to be remembered." Master Teren, Retired Archive Keeper: "Sections were taken by hand. Important names. Routes. Alliances. All removed." Jade: "Look at this... this seal matches the crest we saw at the border." Devon: "It\'s the Valen healer crest." And within the dust of a forgotten archive, a name appears once more: Yvette Sue Valen.',
  art:'Pages show: Captain Rowan Mirel (Border Warden), Mira Valen (Valen descendant, a distant branch) and Master Teren (retired archive keeper) are introduced. No quest box on this chapter. Someone is still maintaining the empty records hall.',
  quote:'"Someone wants the truth to stay hidden." — Captain Rowan Mirel',
  events:['Captain Rowan Mirel greets Jade and Devon and reads Greyson\'s sealed order','The old Valen records hall stands but sections are deliberately empty','Rowan: someone is still maintaining the place','Mira Valen, of a distant Valen branch, recognises the symbol','Master Teren confirms sections were taken by hand','The seal matches the Valen healer crest: Yvette Sue Valen'],
  purpose:['Introduce Rowan, Mira and Teren','Confirm someone maintains the silence'],
  unlocks:['Contacts: Captain Rowan Mirel, Mira Valen, Master Teren'],
  reward:'The west remembers Tribute'},
 106:{ title:'The People Left Behind', type:'Story Chapter — resentment in the west', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: border outpost and market',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Mira Valen (local healer), Lio (border runner)',
  introduced:['Lio (Border Runner)'],
  sum:'Beyond the border roads Jade and Devon find not only missing records, but the people left behind. The west still remembers Tribute, but memory has hardened into grief, fatigue, and resentment. Mira Valen, Local Healer: "You came from Tribute?" Jade: "We did. I am Jade Gold." Mira: "Then you have arrived later than most promises." Lio, Border Runner: "Tribute remembers us only when it needs something." The region is not merely poor: it is tired, of waiting, of loss, and of being forgotten. Mira: "The roads broke. The envoys stopped returning. The healers thinned. But the people remained." Lio: "We buried the missing, fed the living, and learned not to expect the capital to look back." Jade: "Then let us begin by listening." Devon: "A land does not grow this resentful without reason." Mira: "My family kept what records we could. Not enough to save the past, but perhaps enough to start finding it." Lio: "If you want truth, don\'t ask the polished halls. Ask the people who stayed." In the Forgotten Western Territory the mission gains new faces, and a truth harder than missing documents: the west had not been empty. It had been abandoned. Main Story Quest: The People Left Behind. Objectives: meet Mira Valen; gain Lio\'s trust; learn why the west resents Tribute; search for the people behind the missing records.',
  art:'Pages show: Mira Valen is a local healer; Lio is a border runner who resents Tribute. The quest box has four objectives. The west was abandoned, not empty.',
  quote:'"It was not empty. It had been abandoned."',
  events:['Mira Valen meets Jade: Tribute arrived later than most promises','Lio: Tribute remembers the west only when it needs something','The roads broke, envoys stopped returning, healers thinned','Jade chooses to listen first','Mira\'s family kept what records they could; Lio: ask the people who stayed'],
  purpose:['Build the west\'s resentment and its contacts','Gain Lio\'s trust'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The People Left Behind (4 objectives)','Contacts: Mira Valen, Lio'],
  reward:'The west was abandoned'},
 107:{ title:'The Healer\'s Legacy', type:'Story Chapter — the healer village', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: a secluded healer village',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sister Anwen (local healer)',
  introduced:['Sister Anwen'],
  sum:'In the Valen Borderlands remnants of the old healer tradition still remain. Though the records were erased, the knowledge has not completely disappeared. Jade and Devon visit a secluded healer village, where a few still carry on the methods of Yvette Sue Valen quietly, away from the eyes of the world. Sister Anwen, Local Healer: "Welcome to our village. We are few in number, but we still practice the Valen healing methods." Jade: "These herbs... I haven\'t seen these before. They are part of the Valen tradition, yes?" Anwen: "Yes. These methods were developed by the Valen family generations ago. They focus not just on treating the body, but also calming the spirit and restoring the inner balance." Devon: "This technique is different from Tribute\'s healing practices. It works with spiritual energy, not against it." Anwen: "The founder of this tradition... Yvette Sue Valen... She believed healing should never be used as a weapon. She helped many people across the western lands, regardless of their kingdom or status. That is why the Valen name was respected... until it was no longer allowed to be remembered." Jade: "Even now, people still follow her teachings in secret. Someone must have wanted her to be forgotten." Of a symbol in the healer texts: "It is the Valen crest, a combination of the healing flower and the dragon spine. It represents life and balance." Devon: "This is more than a family crest. It looks like a key... to something much larger?" Anwen: "There are still people who watch this village. We do not keep these teachings openly. If the wrong people find out, even this place may be taken from us." Devon: "The Valen healers helped the western lands for generations. Yet their name was erased from all official records." Jade: "Who would go to such lengths... to erase healers who only wanted to save lives? And what truth are they trying to hide?" In the forgotten west the healing light of Yvette Sue Valen still lives on, in people, in memories, and in a truth that refused to die. Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Western Territory. Objectives: learn about the Valen healer tradition; find more traces of Yvette Sue Valen; investigate why the records were erased; uncover the connection to the prophecy.',
  art:'Pages show: Yvette Sue Valen is the founder of the Valen healing tradition. The Valen crest joins the healing flower and the dragon spine (life and balance) and looks like a key to something larger. The quest box reuses the title The Forgotten Western Territory with four new objectives. The healer village is watched.',
  quote:'"She believed healing should never be used as a weapon." — Sister Anwen',
  events:['Sister Anwen shows the Valen healing methods','Yvette Sue Valen founded the tradition: healing should never be a weapon','The Valen crest: the healing flower and the dragon spine, life and balance','The village is watched; the teachings are kept secret','Devon: the crest looks like a key to something larger'],
  purpose:['Learn the Valen healer tradition','Tie the crest to something larger (the prophecy)'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest objectives for The Forgotten Western Territory (4)','Lore: the Valen crest','Location: the secluded healer village'],
  reward:'The healing light still lives'},
 108:{ title:'The Empty Records', type:'Story Chapter — the hidden archive', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: abandoned registry hall and the hidden second archive',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Master Teren',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The deeper Jade and Devon go into the Forgotten Western Territory, the more the past feels deliberately buried. Some names survive in whispers; others have been erased from ink. Devon: "This place guards its silence too carefully." Master Teren, Retired Archive Keeper: "So the court finally sent someone willing to read what remains." Jade: "You are Master Teren?" Teren: "Keeper of what they forgot. Or what they wished forgotten." Behind the abandoned registry hall lies a second archive, one never listed in the official records. Jade: "These shelves are incomplete... entire sections are gone." Devon: "Not only missing. Some were rewritten." Teren: "Travel permits. Healer registries. Border reports. Lineage records. Many were removed. Others were corrected until they became lies." Jade: "Then someone wanted the west to lose its own memory." Teren: "And someone feared what those memories might reveal." Jade: "Her name again... Yvette Sue Valen." Devon: "What are you not telling us?" Teren: "Only this: if you seek the truth, begin with the records no one was meant to open." In the hidden archive the silence of the west finally speaks, and what it reveals is not absence but tampering. Main Story Quest: The Empty Records. Objectives: meet Master Teren; search the hidden archive; trace the altered records; investigate the file on Yvette Sue Valen.',
  art:'Pages show: a second, unlisted archive. Records were not only removed but rewritten until they became lies. Teren hints that the records no one was meant to open hold the answer; the last objective (the file on Yvette Sue Valen) is left open.',
  quote:'"Begin with the records no one was meant to open." — Master Teren',
  events:['Master Teren welcomes Jade and Devon to the abandoned registry hall','A second archive behind it, never listed in the official records','Records were removed or rewritten until they became lies','Yvette Sue Valen\'s name appears again','Teren: begin with the records no one was meant to open'],
  purpose:['Reveal the tampering','Point to Yvette\'s file'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Empty Records (4 objectives)','Location: the hidden second archive'],
  reward:'The silence of the west speaks'},
 109:{ title:'The Man Who Knows Too Much', type:'Story Chapter — the provincial magistrate', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: provincial administration',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Magistrate Corvin Hale, Mira Valen',
  introduced:['Magistrate Corvin Hale'],
  sum:'After uncovering parts of the erased records Jade and Devon bring their findings to the provincial administration in the Valen Borderlands, only to find that someone stands in their way. The deeper they look the clearer it becomes: the missing records are no accident, and the person in charge of this region seems determined to keep certain truths buried. Magistrate Corvin Hale, Provincial Magistrate of the Valen Borderlands: "Lady Jade Gold, Prince Devon. I trust your journey here was uneventful. Unfortunately, the matters you seek to investigate are beyond your authority." Jade: "These records belong to Tribute. We have the right to see them." Devon: "With respect, Magistrate Hale, these are not matters of personal curiosity. They concern the people who were erased from official records." Hale: "The west has always been a difficult region to govern. Old records are often lost, damaged, or removed for the sake of stability. Some truths are best left in the past. By royal decree, access to restricted archives requires imperial approval. Until such approvals are granted, I must deny your request." Jade: "But these were not simply lost. Someone removed them. Deliberately." Devon: "Who gave the order?" Hale: "Careful, Your Highness. Asking the wrong questions can create dangerous rumours. There are many forces at work in the west: forces you may not fully understand. My duty is to maintain order. That is all you need to know." Jade: "He is hiding something. Those reactions were too practiced. He knows exactly what we are looking for." Mira Valen, Local Healer: "Magistrate Hale has been here for years. He is closely connected to several noble families. People say he knows more than he says, and that many of the missing records were sealed under his watch. If he is involved, we will need to be more careful from now on." The magistrate\'s refusal confirms their suspicions: the erased records were not the result of time but of deliberate hands. And somewhere behind Magistrate Corvin Hale stands a power determined to keep the truth hidden. Main Story Quest: The People Left Behind (box continued). Objectives: confront Magistrate Corvin Hale; learn about his connections; find another way to access the sealed records; investigate who ordered the erasures; prepare for the next move.',
  art:'Pages show: Magistrate Corvin Hale (Provincial Magistrate, a man with a moustache and a ring) blocks them with a decree. The quest box still carries the title The People Left Behind with five new objectives.',
  quote:'"Some truths are best left in the past." — Magistrate Hale',
  events:['Hale denies access: restricted archives need imperial approval','Jade: the records were removed deliberately; Hale warns about dangerous rumours','Devon and Jade read his practised answers as a sign he is hiding something','Mira: Hale is tied to noble families and the records were sealed under his watch'],
  purpose:['Introduce the antagonistic official','Open the investigation of Hale'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest objectives (5)','Contact: Magistrate Corvin Hale'],
  reward:'Hale blocks the way'},
 110:{ title:'The Magistrate\'s Shadow', type:'Story Chapter — the forbidden page', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the magistrate\'s office',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Magistrate Corvin Hale',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade and Devon return to Valen to confront Magistrate Corvin Hale. The missing records, the vanished officials, and the unanswered questions all lead back to his office. But when they meet him they find more than a man blocking the truth: someone carrying a burden of his own. Hale: "Princess of Tribute, you came searching for answers. But some answers are buried because people died protecting them." Jade: "I am not here for half-truths, Magistrate Hale. These are Tribute\'s people. They deserve to be remembered." Devon: "You refuse access to the western records. On what authority?" Hale: "The western archives are not provincial matters. They are sealed under imperial directive. Those records are not for public eyes." Jade: "Several officials connected to the old alliance have disappeared. You expect me to open records that do not exist, or that have been removed for a reason? Yet people continue to vanish. And you expect us to believe this is merely coincidence?" Devon: "He\'s afraid. This is not the face of a man who is hiding for power. He\'s hiding because he knows something." Hale: "You think I do this willingly, Your Highness? I inherited this position after the previous magistrate disappeared. Since then, three more officials have been reassigned, and none of them have been seen again. The cover-up extends beyond Valen. There are things in those records that connect to other kingdoms. If I speak openly, more people will die." Jade: "And yet you chose to tell us this." Hale: "Because someone must remember. Because I cannot let their names be erased completely. Take this. It is only one page. A page that was never supposed to exist." Jade: "This... it\'s a western lineage registry. But this name..." Magistrate Corvin Hale was not simply a villain. He was guarding a truth that had already claimed many lives, and the danger was far from over. The single page in Jade\'s hands opens a new question: if this record was never meant to exist, how many others are still hidden? And who else would try to stop them from finding it? Main Story Quest: The Magistrate\'s Shadow. Objectives: confront Magistrate Corvin Hale; learn why he is blocking the western records; discover the fate of the previous magistrate; obtain the forbidden page; investigate the wider cover-up.',
  art:'Pages show: Hale is not the villain: he is afraid. He gives Jade one forbidden page, a western lineage registry. The page\'s name is cut off in the panel. Three officials were reassigned and vanished after the previous magistrate disappeared.',
  quote:'"Because someone must remember." — Magistrate Hale',
  events:['Hale: some answers are buried because people died protecting them','He inherited the post after the previous magistrate disappeared; three more officials have vanished since','He warns the cover-up reaches other kingdoms','He gives Jade a single forbidden page: a western lineage registry','Jade and Devon see he was a guard of the truth, not its enemy'],
  purpose:['Turn Hale from obstacle to reluctant ally','Hand over the forbidden page'],
  unlocks:['Item: the Forbidden Page','Main Story Quest: The Magistrate\'s Shadow (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'Hale gives them a page'},
 111:{ title:'The Valen Family Name', type:'Story Chapter — the Valen portrait', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the hidden archive',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Mira Valen',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Within the hidden archive Mira finally speaks of her family, the Valens. Their name has been reduced to a single healer in the official records, but the truth is much deeper. The Valen family preserved knowledge that went beyond healing: knowledge that connected kingdoms, history, and the hidden threads of the world. And that is why they were targeted. Mira: "My family was more than a line of healers. We served as royal medical advisors, historians, and guardians of knowledge that should not be in the hands of the wrong people." Jade: "So the Valens recorded more than medicine?" Mira: "Yes. We recorded history, ancient rituals, bloodlines, and knowledge that linked different kingdoms. Some of it should have remained hidden, but someone wanted to control it instead." Jade: "That\'s why Yvette Sue Valen was erased? She wasn\'t insignificant..." Mira: "Because she knew something. She recorded what she saw: connections between Tribute and the west, and truths that threatened certain people." A portrait is found: Yvette Sue Valen with a member of Tribute\'s royal family (c. ??? years ago). Mira: "These are copies my family saved in secret. Not all of the originals survived." Jade: "She was close to Tribute\'s royal family... Then her records must contain things they didn\'t want remembered." Mira: "After her, the Valen name was gradually removed from the official archives. Our family continued in secret, passing down what remained in fragments." Devon: "This explains why the western records were sealed. It\'s not just local politics. Yvette recorded meetings, alliances, and names. People who wanted those connections forgotten would ensure her name disappeared too." Jade: "This portrait... it changes everything. Yvette Sue Valen was not a footnote. She was part of a much larger story." Main Story Quest: The Valen Family Name. Objectives: learn about the Valen family\'s history; examine Yvette Sue Valen\'s portrait and records; identify the royal connection to Tribute; search for other hidden Valen archives; decide who to trust with this knowledge.',
  art:'Pages show: a portrait of Yvette Sue Valen with a member of Tribute\'s royal family (the caption leaves the age blank). The royal figure wears a crown. The page cuts off the fifth objective after \'Decide who to trust with\'. The author may know who the royal figure is: it is not named.',
  quote:'"Yvette Sue Valen was not a footnote. She was part of a much larger story." — Jade',
  events:['Mira: the Valens were royal medical advisors, historians and guardians of knowledge','Yvette Sue Valen recorded connections between Tribute and the west','A portrait: Yvette Sue Valen with a crowned member of Tribute\'s royal family','The Valen name was removed from the archives after her; the family kept fragments in secret','Devon: the western records were sealed for the same reason'],
  purpose:['Reveal the Valen family\'s role','Show Yvette\'s tie to Tribute\'s royal house'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Valen Family Name (5 objectives)','Lore: the Valens as advisors and historians','Item: Yvette\'s portrait'],
  reward:'Yvette was close to Tribute\'s royal family'},
 112:{ title:'The Forgotten Alliance', type:'Story Chapter — the pact', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the western archives',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Mira Valen, Master Teren',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep within the western archives Jade and Devon find traces of a past that has been deliberately buried: an alliance between Tribute and the Valen family. It was not a war pact, but a bond built on protection and knowledge. Yet somewhere along the way the alliance was broken and history was rewritten. Jade: "Here it is... Tribute and Valen signed a mutual protection pact twenty years ago." Devon: "Tribute secured the western borders, and the Valen family provided healers, medical knowledge, and historical records. It was a partnership of equals." (The pact\'s heading reads: For the Safety of the People, For the Preservation of Knowledge, For Generations to Come.) Yvette Sue Valen worked closely with Tribute\'s royal family: she was not just a healer, she was a historian and advisor. Mira: "The Valen family recorded border conditions, disease outbreaks, and political negotiations. They preserved knowledge that affected both nations. But these later records claim the Valen family betrayed Tribute. They were accused of leaking military information and endangering the kingdom." Jade: "It doesn\'t make sense. Look at this. The handwriting is different. This section was added later." Devon: "The original record never mentioned betrayal. It spoke of renewing the alliance. Someone altered these documents and blamed the Valen family after the fact. Several officials who supported the alliance disappeared. And the ones who survived suddenly changed their accounts." Master Teren: "This was not a simple disagreement. It was a deliberate erasure. Someone benefited from making both sides see the other as a traitor." Mira: "If the alliance had continued, the western territory would have remained stable. The Valen knowledge would have protected more lives." Jade: "So this was never about treason. It was about controlling knowledge. And removing the people who could keep the truth alive." Devon: "Someone wanted both sides to believe they betrayed each other. Divide the alliance. Erase the truth. And ensure no one could ever put it back together." The break between Tribute and the Valen family was not a consequence of failure, but a carefully orchestrated act of deceit. Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Alliance. Objectives: uncover the truth behind the broken alliance; investigate the missing officials; trace who altered the records; find evidence of who benefited from the division.',
  art:'Pages show: a twenty-year-old mutual protection pact between Tribute and the Valen family; the later betrayal accusations were added in a different hand. Master Teren and Mira are in the scene. (Sky is not shown: left out of the cast list.)',
  quote:'"Divide the alliance. Erase the truth. And ensure no one could ever put it back together." — Devon',
  events:['Tribute and Valen signed a mutual protection pact twenty years ago','Later records accuse the Valen family of betrayal, in a different handwriting','Officials who backed the alliance vanished; survivors changed their accounts','Teren: someone profited by making both sides see the other as a traitor','The break was an orchestrated deceit, not a failure'],
  purpose:['Reveal the broken alliance','Frame the conspiracy'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Alliance (4 objectives)','Item: the Pact Record','Lore: the Tribute-Valen pact'],
  reward:'The break was deliberate'},
 113:{ title:'The Price of Silence', type:'Story Chapter — the village testimonies', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: a Valen village',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Valen villagers',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade and Devon travel to a Valen village where the memories of the past still live in the hearts of the people. The records could be manipulated, but the pain in people\'s eyes could not. To uncover the truth they have to listen to those who lived through it. An old man: "You came with a royal seal. Do you know how many times that seal came before... and never returned?" A woman: "My grandmother tended Tribute soldiers too. When the alliance ended, those same soldiers were ordered to burn our stores of medicine. How are we supposed to forget that?" A man: "My brother was taken for questioning. He never came back. They said he was a traitor... but he was only a healer." Devon: "The anger here is not baseless. People lost family, homes, and the knowledge they lived by. The silence lasted too long." Villagers: "They left us with nothing but rumors. Are we supposed to trust another royal promise? Words do not heal wounds." Jade: "I do not wish to defend what was done in the past. I will not ask you to forget, and I will not make promises I cannot keep. But I am here now, not to demand loyalty... Then let me be the one who finally listens. Tell me everything. The pain, the anger, the truth. Even if it hurts to hear. Because your voices matter. And I will carry them with me, not as a royal decree, but as a bridge to a different future." The old man: "You speak differently from the others. Perhaps... just perhaps... this time we can be heard." The people do not give their trust easily. But in their tears, in their stories, and in their willingness to speak, a small crack in the wall of silence begins to open. Every story adds a piece to the missing years and a deeper understanding of what has truly been lost. Main Story Quest: The Price of Silence. Objectives: listen to the people of Valen; learn about the human cost of the alliance\'s collapse; gain the villagers\' testimonies; understand the truth behind the lasting resentment; build a new path forward.',
  art:'Pages show: villagers give testimony of burned medicine stores, a brother taken for questioning, and a royal seal that came and never returned. Jade promises only to listen. A prop: Devon wears a fur-collared coat in these pages.',
  quote:'"Then let me be the one who finally listens." — Jade',
  events:['A village elder: the royal seal came before and never returned','A woman: Tribute soldiers burned the village\'s stores of medicine','A man\'s brother was taken for questioning and never came back','Jade promises to listen, not to demand loyalty or make false promises','The elder: perhaps this time we can be heard'],
  purpose:['Show the human cost of the broken alliance','Begin to rebuild trust with the west'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Price of Silence (5 objectives)','Lore: the villagers\' testimonies'],
  reward:'A crack opens in the wall of silence'},
 114:{ title:'The Hidden Enemy', type:'Story Chapter — the third faction', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the hidden archive',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Master Teren',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The more they learn, the clearer it becomes: the missing records are not caused by a misunderstanding between Tribute and Valen. Someone else has been working in the shadows: a third party that benefited from breaking the alliance and erasing the truth. Jade: "This record was removed from the Valen archive after the alliance collapsed... but a copy survived in a private collection. It mentions a third faction, one that operated in both realms." Devon: "They were neither Tribute nor Valen. They moved through the borderlands, trading information, powers and people. They created tensions, spread false information, and ensured both sides lost trust. A divided region made it easier for them to operate." Jade: "Look at this name and symbol. These records mention agents who used illusions, disease and spiritual manipulation. This is the same symbol we found in the forbidden healer records." Master Teren: "This symbol is linked to Xima\'s remaining influence. But it is also used by other factions who follow her teachings. They do not always act openly. They prefer to weaken kingdoms from within: through fear, division and forgotten truths." Jade: "It appears again and again... whenever knowledge is erased. So the missing records... the vanished officials... the blame placed on Valen... it was all part of a larger plan." Devon: "Someone wanted both sides to believe they betrayed each other. As long as we remained suspicious, they could continue their work." A sealed document hidden behind a false panel in the archive carries the same symbol on its seal. Jade: "Xima\'s influence may be weaker now, but she is not gone. Her remaining followers, and those who seek her power, still move in the shadows." Devon: "Some are old factions from the western lands. Some are nobles who lost influence. And some... may already be closer to Tribute than we expected." Jade: "Then we are not just looking for lost records any more. We are dealing with a threat that is still alive." Main Story Quest: The Hidden Enemy. Objectives: investigate the third faction; learn more about Xima\'s remaining influence; trace the use of the symbol across regions; identify who benefits from the division; prepare for what comes next.',
  art:'Pages show: the sun-and-eye symbol is tied to Xima\'s remaining influence and appears whenever knowledge is erased. Some followers may already be close to Tribute. The sealed document with the same symbol was hidden behind a false panel.',
  quote:'"Xima\'s influence may be weaker now, but she is not gone." — Jade',
  events:['A surviving copy names a third faction that worked in both realms','The faction used illusions, disease and spiritual manipulation to divide the region','Its symbol links to Xima\'s remaining influence and recurs whenever knowledge is erased','A sealed document behind a false panel bears the same symbol','Some followers may already be closer to Tribute than expected'],
  purpose:['Identify the real enemy','Tie the conspiracy to Xima'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Hidden Enemy (5 objectives)','Clue: the sun-and-eye symbol','Lore: the third faction'],
  reward:'The hidden enemy has a name'},
 115:{ title:'The Healer\'s Secret', type:'Story Chapter — Dima and the Gold Child', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the hidden archive',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Mira Valen',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In a quieter corner of the hidden archive Mira finally shares the truth her family has kept: a secret passed down for generations. Her ancestors protected someone, a person who carried knowledge too important to be lost: knowledge that connected the past, the present, and the future of the world. Mira: "My ancestors were not just healers. They were tasked with protecting someone. A person who carried knowledge about Dima, the Gold Child prophecy, and the ancient methods of restoration. She was a scholar, a healer, and a seer. She travelled between kingdoms, recording what she learned. My family hid her and her records when it became dangerous." Jade: "Protected... for generations?" Mira: "She sought the truth about Dima, not as a weapon, but as a way to heal what was broken. She also recorded the signs of the Gold Child, and knowledge of ancient restoration that could save lives across the world. But the records were incomplete. Part of them were taken. Some were deliberately destroyed. And some were written in a way only certain people could understand. This page was copied from her personal notes. It speaks of the balance between life, death and restoration, a knowledge tied to Dima\'s lineage. She wrote that the power was never meant for one kingdom. It belonged to the world." Devon: "So the prophecy... was not only about Tribute?" Mira: "No. It was connected to the entire world. The Gold Child is not a ruler. The prophecy speaks of a child who can bridge kingdoms, restore what was lost, and heal the rift between worlds. If restoration becomes possible, it would change the balance of power in the world." Jade: "No wonder Yvette Sue Valen was targeted. She knew too much. And what she recorded could not be allowed to fall into the wrong hands." Mira: "My family chose to protect the knowledge instead of seeking power. But in doing so, we lost many of our people. And we were made to look like traitors. This symbol appears in her notes, just like the one you found in the forbidden records. It represents the ancient restoration methods and the responsibility to use them wisely." Jade: "The prophecy... it was never about one kingdom, one family, or one bloodline. It is about all of us. About healing a world that has been divided for far too long." Main Story Quest: The Healer\'s Secret. Objectives: learn about Dima and the Gold Child prophecy; understand the Valen family\'s role as protectors of knowledge; discover the ancient restoration methods; trace why the records were targeted; prepare for the next step in the search for the truth.',
  art:'Pages show: the Valen family protected a scholar, healer and seer who studied Dima, the Gold Child and restoration. The prophecy concerns the whole world. The Valen healer crest shows a sun-and-moon token. The protected person is not named; the context makes it plausible it is Yvette, but the author reveals this in 117.',
  quote:'"It is about all of us. About healing a world that has been divided for far too long." — Jade',
  events:['Mira: the Valens protected a scholar, healer and seer who carried knowledge about Dima and the Gold Child','Her notes speak of the balance between life, death and restoration, tied to Dima\'s lineage','The Gold Child is not a ruler: a child who can bridge kingdoms and heal the rift between worlds','The Valens chose to protect the knowledge instead of seeking power, and were made to look like traitors','The prophecy is about the whole world'],
  purpose:['Reveal the prophecy\'s scope','Explain why the records were targeted'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Healer\'s Secret (5 objectives)','Lore: the Valen guardianship and the ancient restoration methods'],
  reward:'The prophecy belongs to the world'},
 116:{ title:'The Borderland Trial', type:'Story Chapter — the archive attack', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the western archive (burning)',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and the archive raiders',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The truth does not stay hidden for long. As Jade and Devon continue to investigate the missing records, someone moves to destroy what remains in the western archive. It is a deliberate attack: a coordinated effort to erase the past before they can uncover the truth. But this time Jade and Devon are ready. Jade: "They\'re destroying the archive! We can\'t let them take any more records!" Devon: "Then we stop them. Stay close. I\'ll match your movement." Jade senses danger before it strikes; Devon amplifies her movement with magic. Their powers complement each other: Jade\'s instincts and precision, Devon\'s magic and control. Together they fight as one. Jade: "Left side! Three more coming!" Devon: "I see them. Follow my lead." Jade Dragon Harmony: not a romantic bond, but a combat synchronization. Different strengths. The same purpose. Two paths. One rhythm. Jade moves like the rising dragon. Devon\'s magic becomes her wings. In the chaos of battle their rhythm is natural, honed through trust, training and a shared understanding. The attackers eventually retreat, leaving behind a message carved into the wall: the same symbol found in the forbidden records. Jade: "They\'re still here... And they\'re watching."',
  art:'Pages show: a battle chapter. Only Jade and Devon fight. Jade Dragon Harmony is named on the page as a combat synchronisation. The attackers leave the sun-and-eye symbol carved into the wall. No quest box.',
  quote:'"Two paths. One rhythm." — on Jade Dragon Harmony',
  events:['Raiders attack and burn the western archive','Jade and Devon fight as one: she senses danger, he amplifies her movement','Jade Dragon Harmony: a combat synchronisation, not a romantic bond','The attackers retreat and carve the sun-and-eye symbol into the wall','Jade: they\'re still here, and watching'],
  purpose:['Battle: defend the western archive (Jade and Devon only)','Show Jade Dragon Harmony in action'],
  unlocks:['Story battle (Jade and Devon)'],
  reward:'The raiders retreat'},
 117:{ title:'The Truth Behind Yvette Sue Valen', type:'Story Chapter — Yvette\'s own writings', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the western archives',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep within the western archives Jade, Devon and Sky finally uncover the truth about Yvette Sue Valen: a truth that has been deliberately buried, rewritten, and erased for generations. The records were not lost by accident. They have been altered on purpose, and Yvette\'s name was removed from history so completely that she became little more than a story: a forgotten sister. Jade: "These are Yvette\'s own writings... She did not disappear. She left willingly." Devon: "She discovered the truth about the alliance. Someone was using both Tribute and Valen, turning them against each other for their own gain. To protect her family, her people, and the knowledge she carried... she erased herself from the records." Sky: "She understood how dangerous the truth was. So she chose to remove her own name, to make it seem as though she had never existed, rather than risk the knowledge falling into the wrong hands." Yvette carried the burden alone, accepting that history would remember her as a disappearance rather than the truth, because the truth was too dangerous for her time. Jade: "She was a healer, a scholar, and a protector. She cared for the world beyond just one kingdom." The alliance was manipulated from within by a third party, a faction that benefited from division. Yvette discovered this, and her remaining research connected Dima, the Gold Child prophecy, and the ancient restoration methods to a much larger truth. Devon: "They did not just erase a name. They erased a truth that could have changed everything." Sky, holding a green pendant: "Her knowledge... lives on. I carry part of it through the pendant my mother gave me... even though it was lost to save my life. She still protected me, even in her absence." Jade: "She wasn\'t forgotten." Devon: "Someone made the world forget her." Sky: "But we remember her. And we will make sure the truth she protected is no longer buried." Yvette Sue Valen disappeared from the world, but she was not lost. She chose silence so that others could live. And now her story will be told at last. Main Story Quest: The Truth Behind Yvette Sue Valen. Objectives: read Yvette\'s personal records; learn why she erased her name from history; understand the true purpose of the alliance\'s manipulation; discover the link to Dima, the Gold Child prophecy and the ancient restoration methods; recover Yvette\'s remaining items; honor her memory and prepare for what comes next.',
  art:'Pages show (revised version): Sky is present with blue hair. Sky says he carries part of Yvette\'s knowledge through a pendant his mother gave him, and that it was lost to save his life: \'She still protected me, even in her absence.\' Per the author, this is Sky\'s MOTHER\'S pendant (Yvette\'s), a second pendant: Sky\'s own jade pendant from chapters 1 and 94 is the one that was lost. Chapter 119 has Sky call Yvette "Mother" outright.',
  quote:'"She still protected me, even in her absence." — Sky',
  events:['Yvette\'s own writings: she left willingly','Someone used both Tribute and Valen against each other; she erased herself from the records to protect her people and the knowledge she carried','Sky: she chose to remove her name rather than risk the knowledge reaching the wrong hands','A third party manipulated the alliance; her research ties Dima, the Gold Child and restoration to a larger truth','Sky: the pendant his mother gave him carried part of her knowledge, and was lost to save his life'],
  purpose:['Resolve Yvette\'s motive','Tie Sky to Yvette (implied)'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Truth Behind Yvette Sue Valen (6 objectives)','Lore: Yvette\'s sacrifice','Item: Yvette\'s Hair Ornament'],
  reward:'Yvette\'s story is told'},
 118:{ title:'Return of the Western Territory', type:'Story Chapter — the restoration', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the restored west',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Magistrate Corvin Hale, Mira Valen and Lio',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Valen Arc does not end with conquest, but with restoration. Jade returns to the western territory not as an invader, but as a bridge, carrying the truth, memories, and a new beginning. With the truth about Yvette Sue Valen finally revealed, the western territory begins to heal. Old wounds cannot be erased, but broken connections can be restored, and this time they chose a better path forward. Jade: "We are not here to take Valen. We are here to restore what was broken, and make sure the truth is never lost again." Corvin steps forward publicly, supporting the restoration. His involvement signals Valen\'s commitment to a new alliance built on truth, not manipulation. Devon: "This is not the end, but a new beginning. Valen is once again part of the world, not as an enemy, but as an ally." Mira is appointed as the new representative of Valen. As a healer and a scholar she will lead the reopening of the archives and coordinate the restoration of the healer routes across the regions. The archives are reopened: lost records are recovered and restored, including knowledge about ancient healing methods, Dima, the Gold Child prophecy, and the true history of Yvette Sue Valen. Lio becomes a messenger between regions, carrying letters, information, and people\'s hopes. He will help maintain communication and ensure that the alliance remains open and honest. Jade: "We exposed the corruption that hurt Valen." Devon: "And we gave them the chance to choose a different future." The corrupt officials who manipulated the alliance are brought to light. Their actions are exposed, and Valen\'s leadership begins the process of reforms. Jade: "This is what Yvette wanted. Not silence. Not erasure. But a world where knowledge and compassion could live on." Healer routes are restored, allowing healers, researchers and travellers to move freely again between regions. The western territory is no longer isolated, but reconnected to the world. The alliance between Tribute and Valen is rebuilt: not through fear or control, but through truth, respect, and shared purpose. Main Story Quest: Return of the Western Territory. Objectives: reopen the Valen archives; restore healer routes across the regions; rebuild the diplomatic relationship with Valen; expose the corrupt officials; support Corvin\'s public role; confirm Mira as Valen\'s representative; appoint Lio as a messenger between regions; complete the Valen Arc and prepare for the next journey.',
  art:'Pages show: the closing chapter of the Valen arc. Hale (Corvin) publicly supports the restoration; Mira becomes Valen\'s representative; Lio becomes a messenger between regions; the corrupt officials are exposed. The quest box has eight objectives, the last of which completes the Valen Arc. The page shows Lio with brown hair (the messenger).',
  quote:'"This is what Yvette wanted. Not silence. Not erasure." — Jade',
  events:['Jade tells the west they come to restore, not to take','Corvin Hale publicly supports the restoration','Mira is appointed Valen\'s representative and leads the reopening of the archives','Lost records are recovered, including Dima, the Gold Child and the true history of Yvette','Lio becomes a messenger between regions','The corrupt officials are exposed; healer routes are restored; the alliance is rebuilt'],
  purpose:['Complete the Valen arc','Reconnect the western territory'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Return of the Western Territory (8 objectives)','Valen is restored: Mira (representative), Lio (messenger), healer routes','Valen Borderlands become an ally'],
  reward:'The Valen Arc ends in restoration'},
 119:{ title:'The Letter Left Behind', type:'Story Chapter — Yvette\'s final message', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the restored archives',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Among the restored archives Jade receives a sealed letter: Yvette\'s final message. It had not been lost, only hidden, waiting for the right time. Yvette\'s words finally explain the choices she made, the secrets she kept and the reason she disappeared. It was not abandonment, but protection. She explains why she trusted certain people, writes about the dangers within the alliance, and why some truths had to be hidden until the time was right. She disappeared because she discovered the truth about the alliance: she erased herself to keep others safe, and to keep the prophecy from falling into the wrong hands. Sky: "Mother, you went through so much alone. But you protected all of us, even like this." Jade: "She knew what would happen... and she still chose to leave." Devon: "She trusted us with the truth because she believed we would use it wisely." Jade realises: "This... this is about me." Devon reads aloud what Yvette believed: "The one beside the Gold Child will not be chosen by fate, but by choice." The letter is a final reminder that the future is not written by prophecy alone. It will be shaped by the choices we make, and the people we choose to stand beside. The three look out over the restored city at sunset.',
  art:'Pages show: Sky calls Yvette "Mother" outright for the first time (the earlier pages only implied it). The letter\'s line is about "the one beside the Gold Child", and Jade says it is about her. Quest box has six objectives.',
  quote:'"The one beside the Gold Child will not be chosen by fate, but by choice." — Yvette\'s letter',
  events:['Jade receives a sealed letter hidden in the restored archives: Yvette\'s final message','Yvette explains why she trusted certain people and warns of the dangers within the alliance','She disappeared to protect others and to keep the prophecy from the wrong hands','Sky calls her "Mother"','The letter: "The one beside the Gold Child will not be chosen by fate, but by choice"','Jade: "This is about me"'],
  purpose:['Close Yvette\'s story','Introduce the theme of choice over fate'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Letter Left Behind (6 objectives)','Lore: The one beside the Gold Child'],
  reward:'Yvette\'s final message is read'},
 120:{ title:'Beyond the Forgotten West', type:'Story Chapter — farewell to the west', loc:'🌄 Valen Borderlands: the restored west',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Mira Valen (Local Healer) and Lio (Messenger)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Valen Arc comes to an end, not with conquest, but with restoration. Jade and Devon prepare to return to Tribute, carrying new bonds, renewed trust and a future reborn from the past. Mira: "You have done more than restore our records, Princess Jade. You gave our people a voice when no one was listening." Jade: "It was you who kept the truth alive, Mira. I only had the chance to listen." Devon: "The Valen family protected far more than healer knowledge. They protected people, and the right to remember." Lio promises to keep sending news between the regions. The western people no longer see Jade as a distant royal but as the princess who listened. The archives are reopened, the lost records recovered and the healer routes re-established; the connection between Tribute and Valen is rebuilt not by fear or control but by truth, respect and shared purpose. Then a new message arrives from beyond the western borders: there are missing records, and a symbol similar to the ones found in Valen. Devon: "We have restored what was lost here. But there are still many places like this." Jade: "Then we will go. There are still people waiting for the truth." Together: "Then let\'s go."',
  art:'Pages show: Mira Valen is labelled "Local Healer" and Lio "Messenger". The new message came from beyond the western borders and carries a symbol like the Valen ones. The last quest box line is "Prepare for the next journey". Sky is not shown in this chapter.',
  quote:'"You are not just the princess from the capital anymore..." — a western villager',
  events:['Mira and the people of the west thank Jade','Lio will keep carrying news between regions','The archives, records and healer routes are restored','A message arrives from beyond the western borders with a symbol like the Valen ones','Jade and Devon decide to go on'],
  purpose:['Close the Valen Arc','Point the story at the next forgotten place'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beyond the Forgotten West (6 objectives)'],
  reward:'Jade is known in the west as the princess who listened'},
 121:{ title:'Return to Tribute', type:'Story Chapter — the royal court', loc:'🏰 Imperial Capital: the royal court',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and King Greyson',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After weeks on the road Jade and Devon return to Tribute. This time Jade is not simply coming home: she brings answers. Together they step once more into the royal court, not as travellers but as bearers of a truth that would shake the kingdom. Jade: "I have brought Corvin\'s testimony, the Valen records, and the evidence of the altered history." Devon: "No matter what comes next, I am at your side." Greyson: "You have returned. Tell me everything you have found." Jade: "We found altered records in Valen. Corvin testified to what really happened." The Valen records, the original accounts before they were changed, prove that key events, people and alliances were deliberately erased from history. Jade: "Yvette Sue Valen was erased for what she knew. She discovered the truth about the alliance, and she had to disappear." Greyson: "This was not a single act of cover-up. It was a coordinated effort, reaching beyond Valen. Then the truth reaches beyond the western borderlands. This is larger than I expected. There are forces at work even within our own kingdom." He tells them: "You have given Tribute a great gift, no, a great responsibility. The truth will not be easy to face, but we will face it together."',
  art:'Pages show: the king is Greyson. Jade presents Corvin\'s testimony and the Valen records. The quest box has five objectives. The ending line suggests forces inside Tribute itself, which is new.',
  quote:'"There are forces at work even within our own kingdom." — Greyson',
  events:['Jade and Devon return to the royal court','Jade presents Corvin\'s testimony, the Valen records and the proof of the altered history','Yvette was erased for what she knew about the alliance','Greyson: this was a coordinated effort reaching beyond Valen, and into Tribute','Greyson: a great gift, and a great responsibility'],
  purpose:['Report the Valen findings to the crown','Raise the stakes: forces within Tribute'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Return to Tribute (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'The court knows the truth'},
 122:{ title:'The First Omen', type:'Story Chapter — the demons are fleeing', loc:'🏰 Imperial Capital: the royal court',
  chars:['jade','devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, King Greyson and a frontier scout',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'They return carrying truths many wished had remained buried, but before the court can settle, another sign appears. Jade: "We have returned, Your Majesty, with what we found in Valen. But our investigation is not over. What we uncovered points to something far greater." Greyson: "Reports have already arrived from our borders. There have been strange sightings in the west and north. It seems the next part of your journey has already found us." A scout from the western frontier reports many demon sightings, but the demons are not attacking. They appear near forgotten shrines, ancient battlefields and the old seal sites of the fifteen evils. The sightings match locations whose seals have recently weakened. Jade: "The timing is too precise. This is connected to what we found in Valen. The remaining fifteen evils... their seals are weakening." Greyson: "These are not the movements of an army preparing to invade Tribute. They are moving in the opposite direction." Jade: "Then what are they fleeing from?" Greyson: "Demons do not fear our borders. If they are running, it means something even worse is behind them." The scout: "We saw them with our own eyes! Whole groups of demons, retreating in panic, heading away from the west! They were wounded, terrified... as if something behind them was far more dreadful than any human army." At ancient ruins demons were seen fleeing, not advancing. Near long-forgotten seal sites they ran in fear, avoiding places they once guarded, as if something has awakened in those places. They abandoned territories they had held for generations. Jade: "The first omen was not invasion, but warning." Greyson: "If even demons fled, then something older has begun to wake."',
  art:'Pages show: the Arc V chapter. The map names four areas: Forgotten Shrines, Ancient Seals, Sealed Ruins and Western Frontier. The opening caption repeats chapter 121\'s ("They left Tribute searching for missing records"). No quest box on this page. The Arc V cover is still being made.',
  quote:'"The first omen was not invasion, but warning." — Jade',
  events:['Greyson: reports of strange sightings in the west and north','A frontier scout: many demon sightings, but they are not attacking','The sightings match locations whose seals recently weakened','The demons are fleeing from the west, wounded and terrified','Jade: the remaining fifteen evils\' seals are weakening','Greyson: if even demons fled, something older has begun to wake'],
  purpose:['Begin Arc V: the omen','Set the next destination: the forgotten west'],
  unlocks:['Arc V begins (cover pending)','Map: the Ancient Battlefield opens','Reports: demon sightings, weakening seals'],
  reward:'The first omen is understood as a warning'},
 123:{ title:'The Sleeping Enemy', type:'Story Chapter — the ancient battlefield', loc:'🏛️ The Forgotten Battlefield',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Cael Ardyn (the last Seal Keeper)',
  introduced:['Cael Ardyn: the last Seal Keeper, golden-haired and strikingly like Dima; a guardian of a vanished order'],
  sum:'The omen leads them not to a demon\'s nest, but to a place far older than Xima\'s war. After the first omen Jade, Devon and Sky follow the signs, tracing them to an ancient battlefield long forgotten by time. Jade, kneeling at a carved stone: "This symbol... it isn\'t Xima\'s." Dima, golden-haired, approaches in a dream and answers: "Xima\'s curse was only the wound. Something older is awakening." They find no bodies, no broken weapons, no sign of battle. Only silence. All around them stand statues: ancient warriors, mages and creatures standing together against some greater enemy. Sky: "This energy... it feels like mine. No... older. But related." Devon: "This place is tied to an older force..." Jade: "It\'s not just Xima\'s war. Something far older than the Fifteen Evils is connected to this place." A golden-haired man appears, holding a teal-green pendant: "You should not have come here. These ruins are not relics. They are warnings." Jade: "Who are you? You know this place." He answers: "I am Cael Ardyn... the last Seal Keeper. The Fifteen Evils are only symptoms." He sees the pendant Jade wears: "That pendant... where did you get it?" Jade: "It belonged to my family." Cael: "Then the Gold lineage has returned... and the sleeping enemy will not remain asleep for long." The battlefield still stands. The warriors still watch. And now, the sleeping enemy begins to stir.',
  art:'Pages show: Cael Ardyn introduces himself as the last Seal Keeper. Jade shows a teal-green pendant that "belonged to my family"; Cael calls it the Gold lineage. The page does not say whether it is the same as Yvette\'s or Sky\'s pendant. Sky says the energy feels like his own but older. Per the author, the golden-haired figure in the vision panel is Dima, approaching in a dream. Cael Ardyn looks like Dima; no relation is stated on the pages. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"Xima\'s curse was only the wound. Something older is awakening."',
  events:['The party traces the omen to an ancient battlefield','The carved symbol is not Xima\'s','No bodies, no weapons: only silent statues of warriors, mages and creatures','Sky: the energy feels like his, but older and related','Cael Ardyn, the last Seal Keeper: the Fifteen Evils are only symptoms','Jade\'s pendant belonged to her family: Cael names it the Gold lineage','"The sleeping enemy will not remain asleep for long"'],
  purpose:['Introduce Cael Ardyn and the Seal Keepers','Expose a force older than Xima'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Sleeping Enemy (5 objectives)','Location: The Forgotten Battlefield','Lore: Cael Ardyn, the Gold lineage pendant'],
  reward:'The sleeping enemy is named'},
 124:{ title:'The First Broken Seal', type:'Story Chapter — the cracked seal', loc:'🏛️ The Forgotten Battlefield: the heart of the field',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Cael Ardyn',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following the omen and the ancient statues, Jade, Devon and Sky are led to a truth buried deeper than the wars of this age: a damaged ancient seal. In the heart of the forgotten battlefield they find the first of the seals, cracked, but not destroyed. Jade: "It\'s cracked... but not destroyed." Cael: "Do not mistake a crack for safety. A broken seal is not a door opening. It is a prison remembering it has a prisoner." Devon: "Someone is trying to release it." Jade: "Or... someone is trying to escape it." Sky: "This energy... it feels ancient. Like the same source as the omen we saw." Cael: "The seal system predates the wars of this age. Long before the kingdoms, there were forces the world could not contain. The fifteen evils are only symptoms. Not the source. My order was built to watch, to maintain these seals. And when kingdoms began to use them for their own power, they were the first to fall. That is why we no longer exist. Because humans always forget. And always repeat the same mistakes." He sees the pendant on Jade: "But this... This pendant. The Gold lineage... I did not expect it to still exist." Jade: "Then what was it made for?" Cael: "This seal was not made to keep evil away. To keep something inside... that even the ancient world feared." The first seal has awakened a truth far older than the wars of men. And somewhere beneath this battlefield, something still remains.',
  art:'Pages show: Cael explains the seal system and why his order disappeared (kingdoms used the seals for power, and the Seal Keepers were the first to fall). The seal was made to keep something in, not evil out. Jade wears the teal pendant on her chest. Quest box has four objectives.',
  quote:'"A broken seal is not a door opening. It is a prison remembering it has a prisoner." — Cael Ardyn',
  events:['The first seal is found: cracked, but not destroyed','Cael: a broken seal is a prison remembering it has a prisoner','Devon: someone is trying to release it. Jade: or someone is trying to escape it','The seal system predates the wars of this age; the fifteen evils are symptoms, not the source','Cael\'s order was built to maintain the seals; kingdoms used them for power and the Keepers were the first to fall','The seal was made to keep something inside that even the ancient world feared','Something still remains beneath the battlefield'],
  purpose:['Reveal the seal system','Explain the Seal Keepers\' fall'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The First Broken Seal (4 objectives)','Lore: the seal system, the Seal Keepers'],
  reward:'The first broken seal is found'},
 125:{ title:'The Forgotten Light', type:'Story Chapter — the sanctuary', loc:'🏛️ The Forgotten West: the ancient sanctuary',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Cael Ardyn',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The cracked seal was not an isolated wound. Guided by Cael Ardyn, the party follows the traces of ancient light deeper into the forgotten west. If the barriers were failing, then somewhere beyond the ruins, a power older than Xima\'s curse still remained. Cael: "The fifteen evils are not the source. They are what escapes when the seals weaken." Jade: "Then the omen was only the beginning." Devon: "Who created these barriers?" Cael: "Those who understood balance. Dima knew of them. Xima only worsened an older wound." Sky, touching the stone: "This light... it feels like the energy left in the battlefield." Cael: "Because it is part of the same path. Old healing. Old guardianship." Beyond the battlefield they find the remains of a sanctuary history had nearly erased. Cael: "That pendant... the Gold lineage." Jade: "You recognize it?" Cael: "I recognize what it means. Kingdoms forget. They bury what they fear." Devon: "Then help us uncover it before more seals break." The west had not only hidden broken records. It had hidden a forgotten light, and a truth that connected the past, the seals, and the fate still approaching.',
  art:'Pages show: Cael says Dima knew of the barriers and that Xima only worsened an older wound. Sky feels the light is the same as the battlefield\'s ("Old healing. Old guardianship."). The party finds the remains of a sanctuary. Cael recognizes the Gold lineage pendant but says only "I recognize what it means". Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"Kingdoms forget. They bury what they fear." — Cael Ardyn',
  events:['Cael: the fifteen evils are what escapes when the seals weaken','The barriers were made by those who understood balance; Dima knew of them, Xima only worsened an older wound','Sky: the light feels like the battlefield\'s: old healing, old guardianship','The remains of a forgotten sanctuary','Cael recognizes what the Gold lineage pendant means','Devon asks Cael to help them uncover the truth before more seals break'],
  purpose:['Connect the seals to old healing and Dima','Open the sanctuary thread'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Light (5 objectives)','Lore: the sanctuary, the forgotten light'],
  reward:'A forgotten light is found'},
 126:{ title:'The Saint of Forgotten Light', type:'Story Chapter — the sanctuary', loc:'🏛️ The Forgotten Sanctuary',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Cael Ardyn and Seris Valen (Saint of Forgotten Light)',
  introduced:['Seris Valen: the Saint of Forgotten Light, keeper of a sanctuary few still remember'],
  sum:'Beyond the broken seal, the western road leads them to a sanctuary few still remember. There, among the fading light, another keeper of forgotten knowledge remains. Jade: "So this is the sanctuary Cael spoke of..." Devon: "The light here feels old. Untouched." Seris Valen, Saint of Forgotten Light: "Few come here seeking truth. Fewer still arrive carrying both sorrow and resolve." A wounded man lies near them: "He was caught in the corrupted mists on the western road... His wounds won\'t close." Sky: "Let me help." His healing light works where nothing else did. Seris: "I know of it. It belongs to a healing path the world believed extinct." Jade: "You know this power?" Devon: "Then Sky\'s power is tied to something older than Valen\'s erased records." Seris: "The old healing arts were connected to knowledge older than the recent kingdoms: a light that healed not only bodies, but the very wounds of this world." Devon asks if that is the whole of it. Seris: "Perhaps. Or perhaps the past is beginning to return through those who survived it." Sky, quietly: "There are things I still do not fully understand about this power either." The forgotten light had not vanished completely. And in Seris Valen\'s gaze, Sky saw the first sign that his mystery was part of something far older than memory.',
  art:'Pages show: Seris Valen is named on the page "Saint of Forgotten Light" (the Valen surname is new here; her relation to Mira, Yvette or Sky is not stated). She recognises Sky\'s healing as "a healing path the world believed extinct". The wounded man was caught in corrupted mists on the western road. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"A light that healed not only bodies, but the very wounds of this world." — Seris Valen',
  events:['The party reaches the sanctuary Cael spoke of','Seris Valen, Saint of Forgotten Light, welcomes them','Sky heals a man caught in the corrupted mists','Seris recognises the power: a healing path the world believed extinct','Devon: Sky\'s power is tied to something older than Valen\'s erased records','Seris: the past may be returning through those who survived it'],
  purpose:['Introduce Seris Valen','Tie Sky\'s power to the ancient healing'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Saint of Forgotten Light (5 objectives)','Location: The Forgotten Sanctuary','Lore: Seris Valen and the old healing'],
  reward:'The forgotten light is found'},
 127:{ title:'The Light That Remains', type:'Story Chapter — the inner sanctuary', loc:'🕊️ The Forgotten Sanctuary: the oldest chambers',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Seris Valen (Saint of Forgotten Light)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Seris guides them beyond the sanctuary gate, where the oldest chambers of Forgotten Light have remained untouched by time. There, memory was not preserved in stone alone, but in healing paths, records, and the light that still endured. Jade: "This place feels older than the kingdoms themselves." Seris: "Because it is. Forgotten Light existed before borders, before courts, and before many of the names history now remembers. It was knowledge. Healing, preservation, and balance." Devon: "Then what survived here was more than faith." The records speak of a forgotten art: one meant not only to heal flesh, but to mend the wounds left between lands, peoples, and ages. Sky, touching the surviving records: "This energy... it answers the same way my power does." Seris: "That technique should have disappeared centuries ago." Jade: "You recognize it." Seris: "I recognize its lineage, not its bearer." Devon: "Then Sky\'s power is tied to this sanctuary." Seris: "To this sanctuary... and perhaps to a history that was never meant to survive." Jade: "So the Forgotten Light was protecting something." Sky: "Why does it feel like I have been here before?" Seris: "Not something. Someone... and a path the world abandoned. Because some truths do not vanish. They wait." The sanctuary had not given them answers alone. It had given them direction. And as the old light stirred, Sky\'s mystery drew one step closer to the past that had been waiting for him.',
  art:'Pages show: Seris leads the party into the oldest chambers. The records describe a forgotten art that heals wounds between lands, peoples and ages. Sky\'s power answers the records "the same way"; Seris recognises the technique\'s lineage "not its bearer". Seris says the Forgotten Light was protecting "Someone... and a path the world abandoned". Sky says it feels like he has been here before. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"Some truths do not vanish. They wait." — Seris Valen',
  events:['Seris guides the party into the oldest chambers of Forgotten Light','Forgotten Light predates borders and courts: healing, preservation and balance','The records describe an art that mends the wounds between lands, peoples and ages','Sky\'s power answers the records the same way; Seris recognises the lineage, not the bearer','The sanctuary was protecting "someone" and a path the world abandoned','Sky feels he has been here before'],
  purpose:['Tie Sky to the sanctuary','Set up the next step: a path left for someone'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Light That Remains (5 objectives)','Lore: Forgotten Light, the forgotten art'],
  reward:'The old light stirs'},
 128:{ title:'The Path Remembered', type:'Story Chapter — the guiding map', loc:'🕊️ The Forgotten Sanctuary: the oldest halls',
  chars:['jade','devon','sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Seris Valen',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Within the oldest halls of Forgotten Light, memory still lives in paths no kingdom had fully erased. The sanctuary had guarded more than relics: it had guarded direction. Jade: "So Forgotten Light preserved a road as well as a truth." Devon: "Then the next seal was never meant to be found by chance." Sky: "This light... it\'s guiding us somewhere." Seris: "When knowledge is hunted, it must learn to travel. This sanctuary preserved not only the healing arts, but also routes, records, and memories for times of crisis. What had survived here was not only healing, but a way forward." Sky: "This energy feels the same as my power... As if it has been waiting for me." A star-map of lights opens over the floor. Seris: "Not somewhere. Someone once prepared this path for those who would come after. Beyond this sanctuary, the forgotten paths lead toward the next fracture in the old world." Jade: "Then we follow it." Devon: "Together, as we have this far." Sky: "I will go. This light... it feels like a part of my own history." Seris: "The sanctuary cannot walk the road for you, but it can show where the next truth lies." The map reveals the next destination: a forgotten region beyond the old seals, where another truth still waits. Forgotten Light had not ended. It had only shown the way forward.',
  art:'Pages show: a glowing star-map opens in the sanctuary floor; Seris says someone prepared this path for those who would come after. The next destination is "a forgotten region beyond the old seals" (unnamed). Sky says the light feels like part of his own history. The last quest-box line is "Prepare to leave for the forgotten road".',
  quote:'"When knowledge is hunted, it must learn to travel." — Seris Valen',
  events:['The sanctuary preserved routes, records and memories for times of crisis','Sky\'s resonance wakes a star-map in the floor','Seris: someone once prepared this path for those who would come after','The map shows the way to the next broken seal','Jade, Devon and Sky agree to follow it','The next destination: a forgotten region beyond the old seals'],
  purpose:['Point the story at the next seal','Reinforce that Sky\'s past is the thread'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Path Remembered (5 objectives)','Lore: the sanctuary\'s guiding map'],
  reward:'The way forward is shown'},
 129:{ title:'Eira Solenne', type:'Story Chapter — the scholar of the sanctuary', loc:'🕊️ The Forgotten Sanctuary: a hidden sanctuary within the ruins',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Seris Valen and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:['Eira Solenne: a scholar who inherited the knowledge of a time the world had long forgotten'],
  sum:'The path leads the party to a hidden sanctuary within the ruins, a place preserved not by force, but by memory. Here they meet Eira Solenne, a scholar who inherited the knowledge of a time the world had long forgotten. Jade: "You\'re Eira Solenne? I\'ve heard your name in Seris\'s records." Eira: "Yes. I am Eira. I only inherited a small part of what remains. Most of the knowledge was already lost long before I was born." Devon: "You are not a guard like Cael, but you still protected this place?" Eira: "In a way... Knowledge also needs someone to protect it. This sanctuary preserves the writings, memories, and maps left behind by the Forgotten Light. Not to hide them... but to wait for the day someone would understand them again." The sanctuary holds fragments of history, healing techniques, and routes to places that no longer existed: evidence of a world that had once been whole. Sky: "These tests... they match the energy I felt at the seals. It\'s the same resonance." Eira: "Yes. The Forgotten Light created the seals not only to contain something... but to maintain the balance between life, death, memory, and the world itself." Devon: "So the seals, the ruins, and these paths... are all connected?" Eira: "Yes. They are pieces of the same truth. The world was once united, and these paths linked it all. But someone changed it, deliberately. And now, the old connections are waking up again." Sky: "Then we need to learn more. These paths might lead us to the next broken seal... and to the one behind all of this." Jade: "We\'ve found a piece of the past." Devon: "And now, we follow where it leads."',
  art:'Pages show: Eira has long white-silver hair and carries a book; her surname Solenne is new. She says the Forgotten Light made the seals to keep balance between life, death, memory and the world, and that "someone changed it, deliberately". A gold-haired figure (Seris) stands with the party on the cover. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"Knowledge also needs someone to protect it." — Eira Solenne',
  events:['The party reaches a hidden sanctuary preserved by memory','Eira Solenne: she inherited only a small part of the old knowledge','The sanctuary keeps the writings, memories and maps of the Forgotten Light','Sky: the tests match the energy he felt at the seals','Eira: the seals keep the balance between life, death, memory and the world','The world was once united by these paths; someone changed it on purpose, and the connections are waking'],
  purpose:['Introduce Eira Solenne','Connect the seals, ruins and paths'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Eira Solenne (5 objectives)','Lore: Eira Solenne, the purpose of the seals'],
  reward:'Eira joins as the party\'s guide'},
 130:{ title:'The Forgotten Path', type:'Story Chapter — the first section of the path', loc:'🕊️ The Forgotten Sanctuary: the Forgotten Path',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne and Seris Valen',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With Eira as the guide, the party sets out toward the Forgotten Path, a trail that once connected the old worlds but had long been sealed from sight. It is not a road on any modern map, but a path that can only be reached through fragments of memory, symbols, and places that still held traces of Forgotten Light. Jade: "So this is the Forgotten Path... It feels different from any route we\'ve taken before." Eira: "This path does not rely on distance, but on resonance. It reveals itself only to those who still carry a part of the old world\'s truth." Devon: "Meaning... it is not just a physical path. The path chooses us as much as we choose to follow it." Sky: "The air here feels familiar... It\'s like a memory that doesn\'t belong to me, but somehow I remember." Eira: "These ruins once served as a bridge between realms. Knowledge, people, and even time could travel through here. But when the balance broke, the path was fragmented on purpose. Pieces were hidden across the world so that its power would not be misused again. Each fragment acts like a key. Only when they are correct and in harmony will the next part of the path appear." Jade: "So the path is testing us... Not our strength, but whether we understand what the old world was trying to protect." Sky: "This energy feels the same as my power... As if it has been waiting for me all this time." Devon: "Then we follow it. Together, as we have this far." Eira: "This path is more than a route. It is a reflection of the choices the old world left behind. There are still many fragments left, and the path ahead will not be an easy one. But this is only the beginning." The path did not lead to a destination, but to a deeper understanding of the old world, of their own pasts, and of the choices they would have to make next.',
  art:'Pages show: the Forgotten Path reveals itself through resonance and memory, not distance. Three glowing crystals (red, blue, white) are the "fragments" that act as keys. Sky says again the energy feels like his own. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"The path chooses us as much as we choose to follow it." — Devon',
  events:['The party sets out on the Forgotten Path, sealed from sight','The path reveals itself by resonance, not distance','It once bridged realms; when the balance broke it was fragmented on purpose','Each fragment is a key; only fragments in harmony open the next part','Jade: the path tests whether they understand what the old world protected','Sky: the energy has been waiting for him'],
  purpose:['Start the journey along the path','Explain the fragment keys'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Path (5 objectives)','Lore: the Forgotten Path'],
  reward:'The first true section of the path'},
 131:{ title:'The Forgotten Road', type:'Story Chapter — the region beyond the known lands', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the forgotten road',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Beyond the known lands the party enters a region untouched for centuries: a forgotten world preserved in time, where ruins still stand and the air holds the memory of a different age. Mountains float above valleys, rivers flow between the heavens and earth, and an ancient city rests in silence. It is a place that time has not abandoned, but preserved. Eira: "These places were not built for war. They were created to preserve a balance between people, nature, and the spiritual realms." The murals show a time when humans, beasts, mages and spiritual beings lived together, sharing knowledge, protecting the land and honouring the flow between all worlds. Sky: "These symbols... I can feel healing energy within them. They are connected to my ability, though I still don\'t know why." Devon: "Eira, do we know why a place like this was left behind?" Eira: "History never truly disappears, Devon. Only people do. The ruins remain because they still have something to tell us." Jade: "Even if the people are gone, their choices, hopes, and truths still remain here. These ruins are not just broken stones: they are the record of a world that once believed in a better future." Levi: "And it\'s our job to listen." Sky: "The more I feel these symbols, the more it seems this place is still alive, in a way, waiting for us to understand." As the party follows the forgotten road they reach a vast city marked everywhere with a glowing broken-seal symbol: towering spires, suspended bridges and silent halls, a place of great knowledge and deeper mysteries. The broken seal is carved on every gate, tower and bridge, a sign of a world that had fallen silent, and a truth that still waited beyond.',
  art:'Pages show: Levi (green cloak, bow) appears on the page; per the author he has been in the party since the group left Dragonvale, and the comic only draws the characters relevant to each arc. The first mention of floating mountains and rivers between heaven and earth: this is the Celestial Ruins from the author\'s Arc V notes (the page itself does not name it). Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"History never truly disappears, Devon. Only people do." — Eira Solenne',
  events:['The party enters a forgotten region preserved in time','Eira: these places were made to preserve balance, not for war','Murals show humans, beasts, mages and spiritual beings living together','Sky feels healing energy in the symbols, linked to his ability','Jade: the ruins are the record of a world that believed in a better future','A vast city marked everywhere with the broken-seal symbol'],
  purpose:['Reach the Celestial Ruins','Tie the healing symbols to Sky'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Road (5 objectives)','Location: The Celestial Ruins'],
  reward:'The silent city is in sight'},
 132:{ title:'The City That Forgot', type:'Story Chapter — the abandoned city', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the silent city',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Eira Solenne and a surviving guardian',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party arrives at a city that should have been lost to time. Yet it stands beautiful, intact and undamaged, as if no time had passed at all. The streets are filled with homes, markets, libraries and flowers. Everything remains exactly as it once was. But there is no one here. Jade: "It\'s all still here... The houses, the markets, the people\'s belongings. Nothing is damaged... It\'s as if everyone just disappeared in an instant." Meals remain untouched on dining tables. Books are still open in libraries. Conversations left unfinished. Eira: "When a seal weakens, it can cause memory loss in an area. People, places, and even events can disappear from history... The land remains, but it is removed from the world\'s memory." Jade: "Just like what happened to Yvette Valen... She wasn\'t dead because of war or disaster. She was erased from the world\'s memory." Devon: "This is deliberate. This is not simple destruction. Someone is breaking the seals on purpose." Levi: "Not to destroy... but to erase. They are removing people and entire histories from existence." In a quiet temple at the heart of the city the party finds a single surviving guardian. He is frail, but his mind remains clear. Guardian: "We were not attacked. We were erased. The one breaking the seals is not trying to destroy the world. They are trying to bring something back." This was not the end of a lost world. It was the beginning of something far greater.',
  art:'Pages show: a perfectly preserved city with nobody in it. Jade links it to Yvette ("Yvette Valen", the page\'s spelling of Yvette Sue Valen): erased from memory, not killed. The surviving guardian is an old white-haired man; he is unnamed. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"We were not attacked. We were erased." — the guardian',
  events:['An intact, empty city: meals on tables, books left open','Eira: a weakening seal can erase people, places and events from memory','Jade: like Yvette, erased from the world\'s memory','Devon and Levi: someone is breaking the seals on purpose, to erase','A single surviving guardian: "We were erased"','He says the seal breaker is trying to bring something back'],
  purpose:['Show the seal-decay memory loss','Link the seal breaker to a goal of bringing something back'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The City That Forgot (5 objectives)','Lore: seal decay and erased memory'],
  reward:'The seal breaker\'s aim is hinted'},
 133:{ title:'The Broken Seal Chamber', type:'Story Chapter — the weakened seal', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the seal chamber beneath the city',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following the forgotten path, the party descends beneath the ruins and arrives at an ancient seal chamber hidden deep within the silent city. Unlike the other seals, this one was not destroyed but deliberately weakened. In the heart of the old world\'s deepest sanctum a seal still stands: not in broken pieces, but in careful balance, weakened yet alive, as if waiting for someone to return. Jade: "This is the seal we came for. It feels intact... but something about it is wrong." Devon: "The structure itself is intact. But the core has been deliberately weakened. This was no accident." Sky: "I can feel the same energy as my healing ability. But this is not a healing seal. It is something much older... of a different nature entirely." Eira: "This is not the work of a demon. Someone with deep knowledge of seals did this, with precision and purpose." Levi: "Whoever did this knows exactly how much damage to cause... and how much to keep. They wanted this seal to remain, not to be destroyed. This was done with intention." Ancient murals line the chamber walls, showing humans, beasts, mages and spiritual beings standing together: not the records of war, but of a forgotten time of harmony. A world united. A world that once lived as one. Then words appear across the ancient seal, a message carved not only in stone, but in light itself: "The world forgot the truth once. I will make it remember." Jade: "This is more than a seal... It\'s a message. A declaration that someone will return." This seal is not just a barrier. It is a message. A declaration. A promise of return.',
  art:'Pages show: the seal is intact but its core deliberately weakened, "done with intention". Murals of a united world. The glowing message "The world forgot the truth once. I will make it remember." Levi is part of the party and speaks. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"The world forgot the truth once. I will make it remember." — the message on the seal',
  events:['The party descends to a seal chamber beneath the silent city','The seal was deliberately weakened, not destroyed','Sky: the energy is older than his healing and of a different nature','Eira: not the work of a demon, but of someone who knows seals deeply','Murals show a united world of humans, beasts, mages and spiritual beings','The seal carries a message: "The world forgot the truth once. I will make it remember."'],
  purpose:['Show the seal breaker acts with intent','Plant the promise of return'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Broken Seal Chamber (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'The message is witnessed'},
 134:{ title:'The Name Behind the Ruins', type:'Story Chapter — the records of the seal breaker', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the archive of past incidents',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Eira Solenne and a watcher in the shadows',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following the traces left in Dima, the party turns its gaze to earlier incidents across the forgotten ruins, seeking the truth behind the seals and the one who left them. Different lands. Different eras. But the same symbol, the same method, and the same handwriting. Records: Dima, Year 1023; Eastern Ruins, Year 986; Stormreach, Year 954; Valmere, Year 1001; Celes Kingdom, Year 978. Jade: "This symbol... It\'s the same one we saw at Dima. Identical. Even the smaller markings match." Devon: "The method is the same. The order of the seals, the structure, even the handwriting. This was not a single incident, but the work of the same person across many years. Deliberate. Systematic." Sky: "I can still feel the residual energy in these ruins... It belongs to someone who understands both life and death. This is not the work of a normal human." Eira: "The technique is identical down to the order of the seals. These records span at least several decades... across different kingdoms and ruins that should have no connection. Same handwriting. Same measurements. Same structure. Whoever did this left a consistent record over generations." Jade: "Dima\'s restoration... Was it truly meant to heal the world? Or was it also part of something larger, preparation for what is coming?" Eira: "People who leave such consistent records do not act without purpose. This spans generations. Every incident, every seal, every ruin... It was part of a long-term plan. Someone with a clear vision of the future." Devon: "A single person active across decades, even kingdoms... They must have understood the world far beyond what most people see." Sky: "They knew how to bind, how to preserve... and how to awaken. They aren\'t just protecting the past. They are preparing the next stage." Piece by piece the party begins to understand: the seals, the ruins, the records, and Dima\'s restoration were not separate events but connected parts of a single, vast plan. And at the center of it all was a name, hidden behind the ruins until now. From the shadows of the forgotten ruins, someone watched: "So... the Gold Child finally walks the forgotten path. Just as foretold."',
  art:'Pages show: five dated incident records (Dima 1023, Eastern Ruins 986, Stormreach 954, Valmere 1001, Celes Kingdom 978) with the same symbol and handwriting. The last panel is a dark-haired man with ravens watching from the shadows; he is not named on this page (ch135 names him). The page raises whether Dima\'s restoration was also part of the plan. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"So... the Gold Child finally walks the forgotten path. Just as foretold." — the watcher',
  events:['The party studies earlier seal incidents across the ruins','Dima 1023, Eastern Ruins 986, Stormreach 954, Valmere 1001, Celes Kingdom 978: same symbol, method and handwriting','Sky: the energy belongs to someone who understands life and death','The work spans generations: a long-term plan by one person','Jade asks whether Dima\'s restoration was part of the plan','A watcher in the dark: "the Gold Child finally walks the forgotten path"'],
  purpose:['Reveal one hand behind many seals','Introduce the watcher'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Name Behind the Ruins (5 objectives)','Lore: the incident records'],
  reward:'The watcher appears'},
 135:{ title:'The Seal Breaker', type:'Story Chapter — Varyn Noctis', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: before another broken seal',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Eira Solenne and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:['Varyn Noctis: the Seal Breaker, Ruin Warden (title from the cast sheet)'],
  sum:'Following the traces left behind in Dima and across the forgotten ruins, the party finally reaches another broken seal and finds the one responsible standing before it. In a place where history itself has been forgotten, the one who breaks the seals waits, calmly, as if he has been expecting them all along. Jade: "You are the one weakening the seals." Varyn: "Weakening? No. I am opening what was imprisoned. The royal families always believed they were protecting the world. But they were only protecting the lies they inherited." Jade: "What are you trying to release?" Varyn: "The truth." For centuries, the world feared what was sealed away. But nobody asked... why it was sealed.',
  art:'Pages show: Varyn Noctis is named only in the quest box ("Confront Varyn Noctis, the Seal Breaker"), as the dark-haired man with ravens; the cast sheet calls him "Ruin Warden". He directs "royal families" accusations at Devon. Quest box has four objectives. Chapter 136 repeats this exchange almost word for word.',
  quote:'"I am opening what was imprisoned." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['The party finds the seal breaker waiting before another broken seal','Varyn Noctis: not weakening the seals, opening what was imprisoned','"The royal families were only protecting the lies they inherited"','He wants to release the truth','For centuries nobody asked why it was sealed'],
  purpose:['Confront the seal breaker','Reframe the seals as hiding a truth'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Seal Breaker (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Varyn is named'},
 136:{ title:'The Truth He Refuses to Bury', type:'Story Chapter — the memory fragment', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the pulse in the seal',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Eira Solenne and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following the trail left behind in the ruins, the party reaches another broken seal. Unlike the others, this place still holds a faint pulse, as if it had been waiting for someone to return. There he stands. Calm. As if he had been expecting us. Jade: "You are the one weakening the seals." Varyn: "Weakening? No. I am opening what was imprisoned. The royal families always believed they were protecting the world. But they were only protecting the lies they inherited." Eira: "You believe history itself is corrupted." Varyn: "Corrupted? No. It was rewritten." Jade: "What are you trying to release?" Varyn: "The truth." Sky: "This energy... it doesn\'t feel demonic. It\'s neither dark nor hostile. It feels... ancient." Eira: "The records we\'ve studied never mentioned this seal. Or the place behind it. This matches the original Seal Keepers\' notations... But this seal should not exist in known records." Varyn: "Your kind fear what you do not understand. So you call it evil, write it as a monster, and seal it away. But fear is a poor guardian of the truth. Your family inherited a crown. Mine inherited questions no crown wanted answered. That is the difference between us, Prince Devon." Devon is silent. Varyn: "Look. I will show you a fragment of what was buried. Before the seals, the world was different. Humans, mages, beasts, and others stood together in the same lands. This is only a fragment. But it is enough to show you a truth that someone did not want you to remember."',
  art:'Pages show: Varyn calls Devon "Prince Devon" and says his family inherited a crown while Varyn\'s inherited unanswered questions. Sky says the seal energy is ancient, not demonic. Varyn offers a memory fragment of the world before the seals. Quest box has five objectives. Page repeats the ch135 exchange; the two pages overlap.',
  quote:'"Fear is a poor guardian of the truth." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['Another broken seal with a faint pulse; Varyn waits, calm','Varyn: history was rewritten, not corrupted','Sky: the energy is ancient, neither dark nor hostile','The seal matches the original Seal Keepers\' notations but is in no known record','Varyn to Devon: your family inherited a crown, mine inherited questions','Varyn shows a memory fragment of the world before the seals'],
  purpose:['Deepen Varyn\'s argument','Show the world before the seals'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Truth He Refuses to Bury (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'A fragment of the buried truth is shown'},
 137:{ title:'What the Seals Were Made For', type:'Story Chapter — the kinds of seals', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the old seal',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Eira Solenne and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the memory fragment reveals a hidden past, the truth about the seals becomes far more complicated than anyone had imagined. The seals were not simply prisons for evil. They had been created for different purposes. And the world had forgotten. Eira: "Ancient seal texts distinguish between containment, preservation, and separation. They are not all the same. Not every seal was made to imprison evil. Some were never meant to be prisons at all." Jade: "Then history reduced all of them to the same fear. The seals keep monsters out... and nothing more." Varyn: "That was the point. A simpler story is easier to control. So the truth was buried, and the seals became nothing more than a warning in children\'s tales." Levi: "If some seals protected people, how can you justify weakening them? Innocent lives could still be at risk." Sky: "This energy still doesn\'t feel demonic... only ancient. It\'s layered... like many things are sealed together." Eira: "Some seals preserved dangerous forces, keeping them contained. Others separated lands, peoples, memories, or forms of magic after the great catastrophe." Devon: "Then you\'ve been following a design, not a whim. You didn\'t start breaking the seals blindly. Someone left instructions for you." Varyn: "Exactly. Because I am not breaking them blindly. Someone before me left instructions. And it all leads back to the Dima-era records." For generations, the world believed the seals existed only to keep monsters out. But the records, the memory, and Varyn\'s revelation suggest a different truth: the seals were made for many purposes, and that truth was deliberately forgotten.',
  art:'Pages show: three kinds of seals (containment, preservation, separation). Varyn says someone before him left instructions that lead back to the Dima-era records, tying him to the earlier handwriting. Quest box has five objectives (numbered 1-5 on the page).',
  quote:'"A simpler story is easier to control." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['Ancient seal texts: containment, preservation and separation','Not every seal was made to imprison evil','Levi challenges Varyn: innocent lives could still be at risk','Sky: the energy is layered, like many things sealed together','Devon: Varyn follows instructions left by someone before him','The trail leads back to the Dima-era records'],
  purpose:['Explain the three kinds of seal','Show Varyn follows a design'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: What the Seals Were Made For (5 objectives)','Lore: containment, preservation, separation'],
  reward:'The original purposes of the seals are learned'},
 138:{ title:'The First Choice', type:'Story Chapter — the battle at the seal', loc:'🌌 The Celestial Ruins: the weakening seal',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Eira Solenne and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The seal begins to destabilize faster than expected. Fragments of a forgotten world stir beyond the seal, and the choice before the party is no longer a story. It is real. Jade: "No. You do not get to choose this for everyone." Varyn: "Then stop me." Devon: "Step away from the seal." Jade and Devon fight together in Jade Dragon Harmony: their battle rhythm moves as one. Varyn: "You still think you can stop what must be opened?" Neither side seeks to kill. This is a battle of conviction. Sky: "I can stabilize the life-energy, but only for a moment!" Eira: "The mechanism is responding. We can open only a narrow passage! Hold it steady!" Levi: "That\'s not a prison..." Jade: "What is that place?" Varyn: "Now tell me again that nothing was stolen from the world." Beyond the seal lies a world untouched by modern maps: a civilization that had simply vanished from history. Not a prison. Not a cage. A forgotten world.',
  art:'Pages show (two versions of the page were sent; the wider one is used): Jade Dragon Harmony is named on the page. "Neither side sought to kill. This was a battle of conviction." Sky stabilises the life-energy, Eira opens a narrow passage, Levi draws his bow. The title card on both versions prints "Jade Dragon Harmony" with a garbled J. Beyond the seal is a floating-ruin world, not a prison. Quest box has five objectives.',
  quote:'"Now tell me again that nothing was stolen from the world." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['The seal destabilises faster than expected','Jade: "You do not get to choose this for everyone"; Varyn: "Then stop me"','Jade Dragon Harmony: Jade and Devon fight as one, neither side seeking to kill','Sky stabilises the life-energy; Eira opens a controlled, narrow passage','Beyond the seal: a forgotten world, not a prison','Varyn: "tell me again that nothing was stolen from the world"'],
  purpose:['Battle: stop Varyn from forcing the seal open (Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi)','Reveal the forgotten world behind the seal'],
  unlocks:['Story battle (Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi)','Main Story Quest: The First Choice (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'A forgotten world is revealed'},
 139:{ title:'The People Behind the Barrier', type:'Story Chapter — the civilization behind the seal', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: the cut-off civilization',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Through the temporary opening the party steps beyond the seal. What they find is not a realm of monsters, but the remains of a civilization cut away from the world: a people who once lived, created and hoped, just like any other. Jade: "They were not imprisoned for a crime... They had homes, schools, temples, people... Why would anyone seal an entire land of innocent people?" Eira: "These records match what we saw. Their history, their language, their arts... They were a living civilization, not demons or a threat." Sky: "I can still feel their presence... It\'s not dark. They\'re gone, but it feels like they were waiting to be remembered." Cael: "The original Seal Keeper texts mention a review period. The separation was meant to be temporary. But the review never happened." They farmed. They studied. They built. They lived. And then they were simply forgotten. Devon: "So the world chose to erase them instead of finding a way to live together. How many other truths have been buried in the name of protection?" Varyn: "My ancestors came from here. We were not monsters. We were people who were judged, separated, and left behind. That is why I have spent my life tracing the seals. The royal families called it protection. But it was abandonment. History remembers the victors. Not the people who were silenced." Jade: "If this is true... then everything we were taught about the seals... We might have been fighting to preserve a lie. How many other lives were sacrificed so the world could remain comfortable in ignorance?" Among the restored fragments Eira uncovers a name that connects to Cael\'s past: Ardyn. The same name appears in both the ancient records and the Seal Keeper archives that Cael once studied. Cael: "...Ardyn? This name... It should not be here. But it matches a record from my family\'s own archives."',
  art:'Pages show: Varyn walks with the party for the first time (his speech: his ancestors came from the sealed land). The seal was meant to be temporary, with a review period that never happened. The name Ardyn appears among the restored fragments. Levi is not drawn (art focus per arc). No quest box on this page.',
  quote:'"The royal families called it protection. But it was abandonment." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['The party steps through the opening into a cut-off civilization','The people were not imprisoned for a crime: they had homes, schools and temples','Cael: the original texts mention a review period that never happened','Varyn: his ancestors came from here; the seal was abandonment, not protection','Jade: they may have been fighting to preserve a lie','Eira finds the name Ardyn, tying the ruins to Cael\'s family'],
  purpose:['Reveal who was sealed away','Link Cael\'s family to the ruins'],
  unlocks:['Lore: the people behind the barrier'],
  reward:'The sealed people are seen'},
 140:{ title:'The Keeper\'s Oath', type:'Story Chapter — the two oaths', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: the Keepers\' records',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In the ruins beyond the seal the party finds the truth hidden in the Keepers\' records: not just what was sealed, but why. Two versions of the same oath: one written in hope, the other in fear. Cael: "The Seal Keepers were not just guardians. We were tasked with judging when each seal should remain closed, weaken, or eventually reopen. The seals were never meant to be permanent." The Original Oath (Founding Era): "Guard the seals to be balance returns. When the world is ready, reopen what can be reopened, and allow what has been separated to return." The Altered Oath (Later Era): "Guard the seals forever. Let none be reopened. Let none be questioned." Varyn: "At some point, someone changed the oath. From a promise of balance... to a command of permanent obedience. Your line chose obedience over truth." Jade: "Who changed the oath? And why?" Cael: "It happened during the final years of the Dima/Xima conflict. The chaos gave someone the power to overwrite the original oath. After that, no review was ever allowed again. I cannot defend it." Sky: "I can feel it... This is the same resonance as my healing power. And the bloodline from Yvette\'s side. This document... it\'s connected to me." Eira: "The original and altered versions use the same seal notation and ink style. Which means this was not a new document. It was deliberately changed." Devon: "If the seals were meant to be reviewed... then our ancestors inherited a world built on an unfinished decision. We have been living with only half of the truth." Varyn: "I have said what I came to say. Find out why the oath was changed. Then decide whether I am your enemy. Until then... we are not done." Cael stares at the two versions of the Keeper\'s oath. One written in hope. One rewritten in fear. Between them lay a truth the world had been denied for centuries.',
  art:'Pages show: the two oaths side by side (a tree-of-life crest for the original, a compass star for the altered). The oath changed during the final Dima/Xima conflict. Sky feels the oath\'s resonance is the same as his healing power "and the bloodline from Yvette\'s side". No quest box. The first panel typo "to be balance returns" is on the page itself.',
  quote:'"Your line chose obedience over truth." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['The Keepers judged when each seal should stay closed, weaken or reopen','The original oath promised to reopen what the world was ready for','The altered oath commands that none be reopened or questioned','It was changed during the final years of the Dima/Xima conflict','Sky feels the oath resonates with his healing power and the bloodline from Yvette\'s side','Varyn: find out why the oath was changed, then decide whether he is your enemy'],
  purpose:['Show the oath was rewritten','Tie Sky to the oath'],
  unlocks:['Lore: the original and altered oaths'],
  reward:'The oath\'s two versions are known'},
 141:{ title:'The Oath Before the War', type:'Story Chapter — the first Keeper council', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: the oldest records',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Within the ruins the party finds records older than the crowns, older than the wars: records from a time when the Seal Keepers were not jailers but mediators. Long before the world was divided there were those who worked to keep it whole. Cael: "The original Seal Keeper oath was not written by a single kingdom. It was a joint accord between several royal houses, the spiritual orders, and the first Keeper council." The record: "To maintain the balance between realms, to mediate when separation is necessary, and to reopen when the world is ready, so that peoples may live together again." Devon: "This is very different from the later version. The original oath gives the Keepers the authority to decide when to close... weaken... or eventually reopen a seal." Jade: "Dima is here... and Xima too. They were working together in the early days?" Records show Dima and Xima standing alongside the first Keeper council, before the world was divided. Eira: "At this time, their methods were different... but they shared the same goal. To protect the world and its people. To maintain balance. To heal what could be healed." Sky: "This feels true. They weren\'t enemies then." The first Keeper council included mages, healers, royal representatives and appointed guardians from different lands. Cael: "My family archives did not include this period. We were taught only the later history... after the conflict. Someone deliberately removed these records from the Ardyn line." Jade: "So the conflict between Dima and Xima didn\'t begin as simple good against evil... Something changed. And we still don\'t know what or why." Devon: "This means the present world may exist because someone decided that separation was safer... and later generations simply accepted it without question." Cael: "Look here. One of the first Seal Keepers... Ardyn. This is an ancestor of my family."',
  art:'Pages show: the first Keeper council (mages, healers, royal representatives, guardians). Dima and Xima stand beside it before the world was divided. "Ardyn" is named among the first Keepers; the last bubbles ("This is an ancestor of my family") are unattributed over the book cover and read as Cael\'s. A note on the page: in some areas within the broken seals Jade\'s hair may look red from the ancient seal energy; her natural hair is black. No quest box.',
  quote:'"They weren\'t enemies then." — Sky',
  events:['The original oath was a joint accord of royal houses, spiritual orders and the first Keeper council','Keepers were mediators, with authority to close, weaken or reopen a seal','Dima and Xima stood beside the first council, working together','Cael\'s family archives omitted this period: someone removed the records from the Ardyn line','Ardyn is named as one of the first Seal Keepers','Author note: inside the broken seals Jade\'s hair may look red; her natural colour is black'],
  purpose:['Show Dima and Xima as allies','Reveal the first council'],
  unlocks:['Lore: the first Keeper council'],
  reward:'The oath before the war is read'},
 142:{ title:'Before Dima and Xima Became Enemies', type:'Story Chapter — the restored memory', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: a restored memory record',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Through a restored memory record the party witnesses a time before the war, when Dima and Xima still worked together. Their methods were different, but their goal was the same: to protect the world. They were not always enemies. There was a time when balance required both light and shadow, and both sisters stood on the same side. Eira: "Look at this record. Dima and Xima were working together. Restoration, containment, research... They shared knowledge and resources." Dima specialised in restoration and balance. Xima understood dangerous forces, corruption and containment. Their methods were different, but they complemented one another. Sky: "They respected each other. This was not a simple story of good and evil. Something happened later that changed everything." Devon: "Many histories removed this period completely. Later generations only recorded the conflict, not what came before it." Cael: "My family archives deliberately omitted this period. We were taught to focus only on the conflict and its outcome... Not on what led to it." The records show the sisters disagreed over one central question: "Should damaged regions be healed and reunited, or permanently isolated before corruption spreads?" Jade: "So the war wasn\'t inevitable. There was a time when they still believed they could solve the problem together. What caused them to become enemies?" The restored memory ends abruptly, just before the event that divided them. Varyn: "Do not turn Dima into another flawless legend. Both sisters made choices. And those choices had consequences for many people." Among the documents they find a reference to a joint project between Dima, Xima and the early Seal Keepers. One of the names listed matches an Ardyn ancestor. Cael: "...This is my ancestor. He stood with them at the beginning. Before the war. Before the oath was changed." Jade: "History is far more complicated than we were taught. We need to know what happened between this moment... and the day they became enemies."',
  art:'Pages show: Dima and Xima called "sisters" (the page says "both sisters"). Dima: restoration and balance; Xima: dangerous forces, corruption and containment. Their central disagreement: heal and reunite damaged regions, or isolate them permanently. The memory cuts off just before the dividing event. Varyn warns against making Dima a flawless legend. Same author note about Jade\'s hair. No quest box. Chapter 141 was regenerated after 142 to fix a design inconsistency, which is why they arrived out of order.',
  quote:'"Do not turn Dima into another flawless legend." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['A restored memory shows Dima and Xima working together before the war','Dima: restoration and balance. Xima: dangerous forces, corruption, containment','They disagreed over healing and reuniting damaged regions or isolating them','The memory ends just before the event that divided them','Varyn: both sisters made choices with consequences for many people','A joint project lists an Ardyn ancestor: he stood with them before the oath was changed'],
  purpose:['Show how Dima and Xima began as allies','Hint at the unseen dividing event'],
  unlocks:['Lore: Dima and Xima, before the war'],
  reward:'The sisters\' early alliance is seen'},
 143:{ title:'The Child Between Two Legacies', type:'Story Chapter — Sky\'s lineage', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: a hidden Dima-era chamber',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In a hidden chamber from the Dima era the party finds a restoration device unlike any they had seen before. It responds to healing, to blood, and to a lineage long thought lost. It was not written for the Seal Keepers. It was a record for those who would carry fragments of restoration beyond the seals. Sky: "It... responds to me. I don\'t have to know how... I just feel it." The chamber recognised Sky\'s bloodline and healing signature, not his identity. Cael: "These records mention a lineage of healers... They were entrusted with fragments of restoration knowledge outside the Keeper order. This connects to Yvette... and the Valens." Devon: "So the Valen line was more than just healers. They were meant to preserve knowledge. No wonder they were targeted." A memory surfaces for Sky: a woman placing a jade pendant around him. "Healing is not the same as undoing death. You must know the difference." Sky: "I don\'t know if this is a memory of Yvette... or something I inherited. But the feelings are real." Jade: "So your healing power... it\'s tied to this lineage. The jade pendant... and Devon\'s black pearl must have awakened something. You\'re not just Devon\'s brother, Sky. You carry a legacy they tried to erase." The restored mural shows the healers passing down fragments of light across generations outside the Keeper authority. Varyn: "If this is true... then you were hunted because of what you are. But you are also the reason these records survived. Your existence proves they failed completely." A title appears on a plaque: "Bearer of the Returning Light". Sky: "...Bearer of the Returning Light? That\'s not my name. It\'s a title... but it feels like it belongs to me." Cael: "This title appears in multiple records. It was given to those who carried restoration beyond borders... to heal, to preserve, and to prepare for a time when the world could be whole again."',
  art:'Pages show: the memory of a woman placing a jade pendant around child Sky (the woman is not named; the page leaves open whether it is Yvette). The jade pendant and Devon\'s black pearl are both named as having "awakened something". The title Bearer of the Returning Light appears on a plaque. Jade calls Sky "Devon\'s brother". Pendant (per the author): there were two identical pendants, Sky\'s own and his mother\'s. The one in this memory is most likely Sky\'s own, which was destroyed and lost; the one he holds now is his mother\'s old pendant. No quest box.',
  quote:'"Healing is not the same as undoing death. You must know the difference."',
  events:['A Dima-era restoration device responds to Sky\'s bloodline and healing signature','Cael: a lineage of healers held restoration knowledge outside the Keeper order, tied to Yvette and the Valens','A memory: a woman places a jade pendant around young Sky','Jade: the jade pendant and Devon\'s black pearl must have awakened something','Varyn: Sky was hunted for what he is, and his existence proves they failed','Sky is named Bearer of the Returning Light'],
  purpose:['Establish Sky\'s lineage and title','Tie the Valens to restoration'],
  unlocks:['Lore: Bearer of the Returning Light'],
  reward:'Sky bears the Returning Light'},
 144:{ title:'Cael Ardyn\'s Inheritance', type:'Story Chapter — the Ardyn confession', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: the Seal Keepers\' ruins',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Ardyn family was not just one of the Seal Keepers. They were among those who changed the original oath after the conflict. What their ancestors believed was necessary became a duty passed down for generations, and a truth that shaped the world as it is today. Cael: "My family did more than guard the seals. One of my ancestors helped rewrite the Keeper oath after the Dima and Xima conflict. For generations, my family believed this was necessary. We were taught that reopening any major seal would bring another catastrophe. It was my duty. It was all I ever knew." The Ardyn line participated in altering the original Keeper oath, changing it from mediation and balance to permanent separation. Varyn: "Your family helped erase entire civilizations. Whether your ancestors believed it or not, the result was the same. People, histories, and lands were cut off and forgotten." Varyn accuses the Ardyns of betraying the original purpose. Cael: "I accept this accusation. Later generations inherited the lie. We did not create it... but we maintained it because we believed it was right." Jade: "Inherited guilt does not remove responsibility. But it also does not make descendants guilty for choices they never made. What matters now... is what we choose to do with the truth." Varyn: "The world suffered because of this oath. You cannot change what your ancestors did... But you can choose not to repeat it." Cael: "I found something in the restricted archives. A sealed confession, written by the ancestor who changed the oath." The sealed document contains a confession from the Ardyn ancestor. Cael: "He wrote this knowing it might never be seen. There were reasons... but also doubts. Even he was no longer certain whether the proof they were shown was real."',
  art:'Pages show: Cael\'s hair is silver-white here and he wears a fur-collared black-and-blue coat. Varyn accuses the Ardyns; Jade answers that inherited guilt does not remove responsibility but does not make descendants guilty. A sealed confession from the Ardyn ancestor (a red-wax tree seal) is found. No quest box (confirmed by the author).',
  quote:'"You cannot change what your ancestors did... But you can choose not to repeat it." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['An Ardyn ancestor helped rewrite the Keeper oath after the Dima/Xima conflict','Cael: the family believed reopening any major seal would bring another catastrophe','Varyn accuses the Ardyns of helping erase civilizations','Cael accepts the accusation: they maintained the lie because they believed it right','Jade: inherited guilt does not remove responsibility, but what matters is what is done with the truth','Cael finds a sealed confession; the ancestor doubted whether the proof was real'],
  purpose:['Resolve Cael\'s inheritance','Set up the sealed confession'],
  unlocks:['Lore: the Ardyn inheritance'],
  reward:'Cael accepts his family\'s part'},
 145:{ title:'The Confession of the First Betrayer', type:'Story Chapter — the unnamed adviser', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: the ruins of the Seal Keepers',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In the ruins of the Seal Keepers the party uncovers a sealed confession, a record that reveals a truth far more complicated than history ever told. The confession left by the first betrayer shatters what they thought they knew: the Keepers did not willingly choose to seal the world forever. Cael: "This is a confession from one of my ancestors... a Keeper who was present during the final Dima and Xima crisis. The council did not willingly choose to seal the world forever. They were convinced that reopening the separated regions would allow an ancient force to return." An unnamed adviser appeared repeatedly during negotiations between Dima, Xima, the royal families and the Keepers. Their instructions always carried the same symbol: a compass star. Varyn: "This adviser appeared in every negotiation... with Dima, Xima, the royal families, and the Keepers. They presented proof that if the regions were reunited, an ancient force would return to this world." Sky: "There are records of this adviser appearing again and again... Always with the same symbol, always with the same warning. But their identity has been erased from the official records." Jade: "So the ancient war... may have been manipulated. Dima and Xima were pushed toward conflict by someone else\'s designs... The suffering of countless lives... might have been orchestrated." Cael: "My ancestor altered the oath because he believed permanent separation was the only way to prevent catastrophe. He could not trust that the adviser\'s proof was false... and so he chose to seal the world, even against the will of many." Varyn: "So... my ancestors may have blamed the wrong people. We pursued Dima and Xima as enemies... when the real culprit was the one who manipulated everything from the shadows." In the ancient mural Dima and Xima stand on opposite sides, but between them a third figure, the adviser, has been almost completely scratched out, as if their existence was meant to be erased from history.',
  art:'Pages show: the unnamed adviser with the compass-star symbol (the same symbol as the altered oath and the seal-breaker records). A mural has a third figure scratched out between Dima and Xima. Cael and Varyn each realise their line blamed the wrong people. Quest Objectives box (four lines, with check boxes).',
  quote:'"We pursued Dima and Xima as enemies... when the real culprit was the one who manipulated everything from the shadows." — Varyn Noctis',
  events:['A sealed confession from an Ardyn Keeper present at the final Dima/Xima crisis','The Keepers were convinced reopening the regions would bring an ancient force back','An unnamed adviser, marked with a compass star, appeared in every negotiation with false proof','The adviser\'s identity has been erased from the official records','Jade: the war may have been manipulated','The mural shows the adviser almost scratched out between Dima and Xima'],
  purpose:['Reveal a hidden third party behind the war','Ties the compass-star symbol to the adviser'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Confession of the First Betrayer (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The first betrayer\'s confession is read'},
 146:{ title:'The Truth Before the Curse', type:'Story Chapter — the end of Arc V', loc:'🌌 The Land Beyond the Seal: a memory of Dima and Xima',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Eira Solenne, Cael Ardyn and Varyn Noctis, with Dima and Xima in the memory',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Long ago the world faced the same threat. Dima and Xima were not enemies at first: they were sisters in purpose, who saw the same darkness but chose different paths. Dima wanted balance. Xima wanted control. Their conflict created the curse, and the world was divided to keep the ancient threat from returning. Dima: "We both saw what was coming. I believed the world must remain whole, even in imperfection. Balance allows people to learn, to choose, and to change." Xima: "I believed control was the only way to stop it. People would only bring ruin if they were free to choose. So I chose to contain, even if it meant sacrificing half the world." Together: "Our conflict was real... but it was also used. There was a third party, working in the shadows. They manipulated our fears, our visions, and the choices we were given." Varyn: "Our ancestors fought each other... but they may have been following a story written for them. We may have blamed the wrong people." The ancient threat did not disappear. It retreated. It waits. And the curse was a barrier, but also a prison, one built from their pain, their fear and a manipulated truth. Cael: "We were shown proof. I no longer know whether that proof was real. But I believed it. So I changed the oath... and sealed the world to prevent its return." Jade: "Then... why was I chosen?" Dima: "Because the Gold bloodline was never meant to defeat darkness. It was meant to choose what comes after." The truth behind the seals has been uncovered. But the curse remains. The fifteen evils still walk the world. Now Jade understands that defeating them is only part of what must be done. Arc V Ending, The Discovery Phase: the origins of the curse, the truth about Dima and Xima, and the hidden manipulation have been revealed. The journey continues. The question is no longer: "Can Jade defeat the curse?" But: "Can Jade create a world that no longer needs heroes?"',
  art:'Pages show: this is the arc\'s ending (the author\'s Arc V notes called it "Chapter 145: The Truth Before the Curse"; on the pages it is chapter 146, and 145 is The Confession of the First Betrayer). Dima and Xima speak together in the memory; the silver-haired Keeper who "changed the oath" is Cael\'s ancestor in the memory, not Cael himself (the bubble is on the memory scene). The last panels show Jade at night looking over a harbour city. Ending card: "Arc V Ending, The Discovery Phase".',
  quote:'"Because the Gold bloodline was never meant to defeat darkness. It was meant to choose what comes after." — Dima',
  events:['Dima wanted balance, Xima wanted control: their conflict created the curse','The conflict was real but also used: a third party manipulated their fears, visions and choices','The ancient threat retreated and waits; the curse is a barrier and a prison','The Keeper who changed the oath did so on proof he could no longer trust','Jade asks why she was chosen; Dima: the Gold bloodline was meant to choose what comes after','The fifteen evils still walk the world; the question is whether Jade can create a world that no longer needs heroes'],
  purpose:['Close Arc V','Reframe the final phase'],
  unlocks:['Arc V complete: The Discovery Phase','Lore: the truth before the curse'],
  reward:'Arc V ends: the Discovery Phase'},
 147:{ title:'The Fifteen Names', type:'Story Chapter — Arc VI begins: the Fifteen Evils', loc:'🏰 Imperial Capital: the royal council chamber',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'seraphina', 'levi', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, King Greyson and Adrian',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the revelations at the Broken Seals, Jade and the others return to Tribute, but the end of one truth is only the beginning of another. In the royal council chamber they gather once more. New reports have arrived from across Tribute: strange disturbances, missing settlements and dangerous entities. Adrian: "Since the Broken Seals, incidents have increased. Fifteen major entities have been identified across the continent. These are the records we\'ve gathered, copied and passed down for centuries. They are known as the Fifteen Evils of Tribute." The register lists: 1. The Thorned Widow, 2. The Mourning Hart, 3. The Hollow King, 4. The Black Tide, 5. The Silent Flame, 6. The Weeping Stone, 7. The Sky Eater, 8. The Bone River, 9. The Sunless Child, 10. The Drowned Crown, 11. The Ashen Serpent, 12. The Mirror Queen, 13. The Endless Winter, 14. ???, 15. ???. Jade: "So our next mission is to find these... and destroy them?" Devon: "No. After everything we learned, I no longer wish for blind destruction. Each of them may have a history, a purpose, or a truth we do not yet understand. These records are incomplete. They were written by people who feared what they did not understand. They may not tell the whole truth. We find them. We understand them. Then we decide what must be done." Sky: "Some of them are undoubtedly corrupted. But others may be victims... or guardians, like what we found near the seals." Levi: "People are already being hurt. Entire settlements have disappeared. We cannot ignore these reports." Seraphina: "Trade routes and foreign merchants may help us. We can trace patterns through their records and news from other kingdoms." Greyson: "Jade. You have faced the truth at the Broken Seals, and you understand how complex this world is. I am entrusting the investigation of the Fifteen Evils to you. Lead this mission. Choose your companions. You will have the full support of Tribute." Jade: "I understand. I will find the truth behind each of the Fifteen Names, and decide what must be done. Not as an end... but as a new beginning for Tribute." Greyson: "Then let us begin. The Fifteen Names are our next journey."',
  art:'Pages show: the first chapter of Arc VI (the arc cover is not supplied yet). Greyson gives Jade command of the investigation and tells her to choose her companions. The register names thirteen Evils; the 14th and 15th are "???". Devon (not Jade) argues against blind destruction. Seraphina is drawn again (blonde, beaded headdress). Quest box has five objectives. Note: the register calls them "the Fifteen Evils of Tribute", while the early chapters speak of fifteen territories and Xima\'s servants; the page does not say how the earlier ones (e.g. Frog Mahan) relate.',
  quote:'"Each of them may have a history, a purpose, or a truth we do not yet understand." — Devon',
  events:['Fifteen major entities are identified across the continent, the Fifteen Evils of Tribute','The register names thirteen of them; two are still unknown','Devon: no blind destruction; find them, understand them, then decide','Sky: some are corrupted, others may be victims or guardians','Greyson entrusts the investigation to Jade and lets her choose her companions','Jade: the Fifteen Names are the next journey, a new beginning for Tribute'],
  purpose:['Begin Arc VI','Introduce the Fifteen Evils register'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Fifteen Names (5 objectives)','Fifteen Evils Register (Imperial Network)'],
  reward:'Jade leads the Fifteen Names'},
 148:{ title:'Rumours of the First Evil', type:'Story Chapter — Sally\'s letters', loc:'🏰 Imperial Capital: the royal council chamber',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'seraphina', 'levi', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, King Greyson (Young King of Tribute) and Adrian (Royal Scholar)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the revelations at the Broken Seals Jade\'s group begin their first step in charting a path into the Fifteen Evils. They gather at Tribute to receive new information. Somewhere beyond Tribute\'s borders rumours are spreading of a forest that has fallen silent, and now, through letters from Dragonvale, the truth draws them north. Greyson: "We have received new letters from Sally in Dragonvale. She has been investigating the unusual disturbances near the northern forests." Adrian: "Sally\'s reports mention a series of strange attacks and disappearances in the villages beyond our borders. These letters contain first-hand accounts and rumours from the local people in Dragonvale. The signs all point to the influence of one of the Fifteen Evils." Greyson: "The situation is worse than we expected. Sally believes this may be the first of the Fifteen Evils to have awakened... and it is centred around the northern forest." Several letters have arrived from Sally in Dragonvale, filled with detailed reports and witness accounts, addressed to His Majesty and the Northern Party. Jade: "Sally writes that entire villages near the northern forest have been attacked. There are also reports of people disappearing without a trace, and strange creatures seen in the forest at night." The locals believe it is the first of the Fifteen Evils. Devon: "Sally believes these disturbances are connected. The forest, which was once lively, has fallen strangely silent. Even the beasts have fled." Sky: "Her correspondence suggests a dark presence growing stronger in the northern forest. She urges us to investigate before more lives are lost." Levi: "The reports match other rumours we\'ve heard: travellers vanishing, merchants not returning, and lights seen in the forest at night. This is no mere bandit activity." Seraphina: "Sally also writes that the local people fear the name of the First Evil, though they do not know its true form. Superstition or not, the fear is spreading quickly." Greyson: "We cannot ignore these reports. If this is truly one of the Fifteen Evils, we must learn the truth before it spreads further." Jade: "Then our course is clear. We will travel to the northern forest and see for ourselves." Devon: "We go together. We will follow Sally\'s leads and investigate the source of these rumours. Whatever we find, we face it as a team." With Sally\'s letters guiding their way, the party leaves Tribute behind and heads north. Ahead lies the northern forest, known in whispers as the Black Forest. There, the trail to the first Evil begins.',
  art:'Pages show: Greyson is captioned "Young King of Tribute" and Adrian "Royal Scholar". Sally writes from Dragonvale about villages near "the northern forest" (the letter is addressed "To His Majesty and the Northern Party, From Sally Sin, Dragonvale": the page\'s own spelling). The party rides north on horseback. The forest is named the Black Forest. Quest box has five objectives. Note: Sally\'s letters come from Dragonvale, but the map and the earlier chapters put the Black Forest far from Dragonvale; the page does not explain how her reports reach it.',
  quote:'"Whatever we find, we face it as a team." — Devon',
  events:['New letters from Sally in Dragonvale: attacks and disappearances in the villages near the northern forest','Adrian: first-hand accounts point to one of the Fifteen Evils','Greyson: Sally believes this may be the first Evil to have awakened','Entire villages attacked overnight, people vanishing, strange creatures seen at night','Levi: matching rumours of vanished travellers and lights in the forest','The party leaves Tribute for the Black Forest'],
  purpose:['Start the first hunt','Show the Sally letter network at work'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Rumours of the First Evil (5 objectives)','Location: The Northern Frontier'],
  reward:'The trail to the first Evil is chosen'},
 149:{ title:'The Spirit Ranger', type:'Story Chapter — the Black Forest', loc:'🌲 The Black Forest: the northern forest',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'seraphina', 'levi', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin Kaede (Spirit Ranger, Monster Tracker)',
  introduced:['Rin Kaede: a Spirit Ranger and monster tracker already hunting the first Evil'],
  sum:'Guided by the reports sent from Dragonvale, Jade\'s party travels north into the forest whispered about in Sally\'s letters. There, before they find the First Evil, they find someone already hunting it. The northern forest is ancient, and heavy with a presence that did not belong to this world. And they are not the only ones following its trail. Jade: "This forest feels different from the others." Sky: "The air is thick with both spiritual and corrupted energy..." Levi: "We should be close to where the reports mentioned." A figure watches from the trees. Rin Kaede (Spirit Ranger, Monster Tracker): "They\'re the royal party... So you\'ve come all the way too." Jade: "You were watching us." Rin: "Only because you were trespassing on my trail." Seraphina: "Then perhaps we are hunting the same thing." Rin: "I\'ve been tracking it myself. I don\'t need palace hunters slowing me down." Levi: "You\'re a tracker." Rin: "Spirit Ranger. Monster tracker." Devon: "If you know this forest, then help us understand what we\'re facing." Rin: "Corruption leaves one trail. Spirits leave another. Whatever you\'re hunting leaves both. See here?" Claw marks like a beast\'s, but with spiritual residue, as if a spirit passed through at the same time. Sky: "Both...? That means it isn\'t purely a corrupted creature. It carries a spiritual nature as well." Devon: "That is why your Evil has not behaved like an ordinary monster. It does not fit simple categories. It is something in between." Seraphina: "Then will you allow us to continue alongside you?" Rin: "I still don\'t fully trust royal assistance. But... you may come with me. Stay close, follow my lead, and do not get in my way." Jade: "The trail continues deeper into the forest. The first hunt is only the beginning." The trail leads deeper into a forest where spirits and corruption are entwined. The First Evil was no ordinary monster. It did not fit simple categories, and the truth behind the Fifteen Evils was far more complex than they had imagined.',
  art:'Pages show: Rin Kaede is captioned "Spirit Ranger, Monster Tracker" (teal-green hunter\'s coat, flower hairpiece, bow). She agrees to let the party follow her. The page\'s caption misspells Dragonvale as "Dogayama" and Sally as "Salty"; I used the right names. Per the author\'s Arc V notes, "Spirit Ranger" was planned as Levi\'s new class, but on this page it is Rin\'s title: please confirm. The first Evil\'s name (the Thorned Widow) is not spoken in the chapter. Quest box has four objectives.',
  quote:'"Corruption leaves one trail. Spirits leave another. Whatever you\'re hunting leaves both." — Rin Kaede',
  events:['The party enters the Black Forest: spiritual and corrupted energy together','Rin Kaede, a Spirit Ranger, is already tracking the First Evil','She tells them corruption leaves one trail and spirits another; the Evil leaves both','Claw marks with spiritual residue: it is something in between','Rin agrees, grudgingly, to let them follow her lead','The First Evil does not fit simple categories'],
  purpose:['Introduce Rin Kaede and the spirit/corruption dual trail','Set the theme that the Evils are not all the same'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Spirit Ranger (4 objectives)','Location: The Black Forest','Lore: Rin Kaede'],
  reward:'The First Evil is no ordinary monster'},
 150:{ title:'Forest of Thorns', type:'Story Chapter — the corrupted forest', loc:'🌹 The Forest of Thorns',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin Kaede',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Beyond Tribute\'s northern reach the party enters a region hunters fear by name alone: the Forest of Thorns. Here corruption has spread through root, beast and air alike, turning the forest itself into a hunting ground. Levi: "The thorns are alive..." Devon: "Stay close. This forest wants to divide us." Rin: "These traces are spiritual. Something passed here feeding on both fear and corruption. I follow spirit trails." Levi: "And something heavy moved with it. Broken branches, claw depth, and blood on the bark. I follow the living forest." Sky: "The corruption is spreading through the roots. If it reaches the water, the whole region could change." Jade: "Then lead us together." Devon: "Yes. We move as one. Rin, you take the spirit trails. Levi, track the physical path. Sky, watch for corruption surges. I will keep the party together." Then: "Ambush!" Corrupted beasts burst from the thorns. Rin: "Left flank!" Levi: "Three more above us!" Jade and Sky cut through them. In the Forest of Thorns the path to the First Evil is no longer rumour, but a trail written in claw, spirit and blood. And as Rin and Levi read the forest in different ways, the party realises this hunt will demand more than strength alone.',
  art:'Pages show: the first use of the dual-tracking roles: Rin follows the spiritual trail, Levi the physical one, Sky watches for corruption surges, Devon keeps the party together. A corrupted ambush follows (a battle). Seraphina is a silent member of the party here: per the author she has no big role until Altan, so she is not drawn. Quest box has five objectives. The page typo "Thees traces" was read as "These traces". Which speech bubble belongs to Devon and which to Jade is partly inferred.',
  quote:'"I follow spirit trails." / "I follow the living forest." — Rin and Levi',
  events:['The party enters the Forest of Thorns: corruption in root, beast and air','Rin follows spirit trails; Levi tracks the physical path; Sky watches corruption surges','The corruption is spreading through the roots toward the water','A corrupted ambush','The path to the First Evil is a trail of claw, spirit and blood','The hunt will demand more than strength alone'],
  purpose:['Show dual tracking in action','Reach the First Evil\'s territory'],
  unlocks:['Story battle: the corrupted ambush','Main Story Quest: Forest of Thorns (5 objectives)','Location: The Forest of Thorns'],
  reward:'The trail to the First Evil is found'},
 151:{ title:'The Thorned Widow', type:'Story Chapter — the first Evil', loc:'🌹 The Forest of Thorns: the forgotten shrine',
  chars:['jade', 'devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon (Phoenix Guard Jade fights beside Devon) and the Thorned Widow',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deeper within the Forest of Thorns the party finally reaches the source of the corruption: a forgotten shrine where a once-gentle guardian has fallen into nightmare. The Thorned Widow is a twisted remnant of a once-benign forest spirit; now almost nothing remains but a monstrous shell draped in thorns, grief and corruption. Jade: "This is it... Our first proper Evil. I have to fight it." Devon: "Its original nature may have been to protect this forest. But now... only corruption remains." There are still traces of who it once was, a guardian, a widow of the forest, but the corruption has consumed almost everything. Now it is only hunger, thorns and endless pain. The Widow: "All who trespass... become part of the forest... Blood... Roots... Forever..." Phoenix Guard Jade and Devon move as one once more, their strikes and magic sharper and more perfectly in tune than ever before: different strengths, the same purpose, two paths, one rhythm. Jade: "Left side! I\'ll take the thorns!" Devon: "I\'ll open a path. Follow my lead!" Together: "Now!" The Thorned Widow fights with the forest itself, thorns, roots and corrupted spirit energy, striking from every direction in a battle of relentless ferocity. Even as they wound it, it continues to regenerate. The corruption runs too deep. This is only the beginning. The Widow: "...Still here... Still mine... The forest... never... dies..." At its core something darker still stirs. The Thorned Widow is far from defeated.',
  art:'Pages show: only Jade and Devon fight (the other three are not drawn). Jade is called "Phoenix Guard Jade". The battle ends with the Widow regenerating and "far from defeated", so the chapter\'s fight is the first round, not the kill; the kill is in chapter 152 (which opens with "The Thorned Widow has fallen"). Quest box has four objectives; the first is "Defeat the Thorned Widow".',
  quote:'"All who trespass... become part of the forest..." — the Thorned Widow',
  events:['The party reaches the forgotten shrine at the source of the corruption','The Thorned Widow is a once-benign forest spirit, now thorns, grief and corruption','Jade: our first proper Evil, and I have to fight it','Jade and Devon fight as one: different strengths, the same purpose','The Widow fights with the forest itself and keeps regenerating','At its core something darker still stirs'],
  purpose:['Battle: the first Evil (Jade and Devon)','Hint it was once a guardian'],
  unlocks:['Story battle (Jade and Devon)','Main Story Quest: The Thorned Widow (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The Widow is wounded but not beaten'},
 152:{ title:'What Remained', type:'Story Chapter — the first Evil resolved', loc:'🌹 The Forest of Thorns: the restored shrine',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin Kaede',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Thorned Widow has fallen, and the forest grows quiet. The choking thorns recede, the corruption fades, and the land begins to breathe again. The first Evil was truly dangerous: it brought ruin, suffering and death. But now, among the remains, a different truth begins to emerge. Sky: "There\'s healing energy inside it... It wasn\'t born like this." Rin: "This shrine names it a guardian spirit." The weathered records speak of a spirit that protected this forest, healed the land and guided lost souls. It was a guardian before corruption twisted it into a nightmare. Jade: "So the first Evil was once a protector..." Devon: "Corruption changed it, but something remained." Levi: "Then the Fifteen Evils may not all be what history claims. We need to learn the truth before we face the others." The first Evil was a guardian spirit of this forest. It nurtured life, healed wounds and kept balance between the mortal world and the wild. But the corruption took root, twisting its purpose and consuming its mind. It became a weapon of pain, and while it had to be stopped, it was not originally evil. Now the shrine stands once more. The forest begins to heal, and a lost spirit may finally rest in peace. But fourteen more remain, and many questions are still unanswered. Register: 1/15 Resolved. This was the first. The journey continues.',
  art:'Pages show: the register counter 1/15 RESOLVED. The Widow "has fallen" and the shrine is restored, with a white spirit-creature in blossoms. The page does not say whether it was destroyed, purified or put to rest; the register calls it simply Resolved, and the game records it that way. Levi is drawn differently here (a brown hooded cloak, short auburn hair): per the author this is reborn Levi going through changes. Quest box is the register counter (no objective list).',
  quote:'"It was not originally evil." — on the first Evil',
  events:['The Widow has fallen; the thorns recede and the corruption fades','Sky: healing energy inside; it wasn\'t born like this','The shrine\'s records call it a guardian spirit that healed the land and guided lost souls','Jade: the first Evil was once a protector','Levi: the Fifteen Evils may not all be what history claims','Register: 1/15 Resolved'],
  purpose:['Resolve the first Evil','Establish that the Evils may be victims or guardians'],
  unlocks:['Fifteen Evils Register: 1/15 Resolved','Location: Mourning Valley opens'],
  reward:'The first of the Fifteen is resolved'},
 153:{ title:'The Village That Fears the Deer', type:'Story Chapter — the mountain village', loc:'🏮 Mourning Valley: the mountain village',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin Kaede and the villagers',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'At the edge of the Forest of Thorns the party arrives at a small mountain village where fear hangs heavy in the air after a monstrous stag began attacking anyone who entered the valley. The villagers speak of an enormous spectral stag that attacks anyone who enters the valley. They want it killed, and at first it seems like a straightforward hunt. Elder: "That stag... it is a monster! Anyone who enters the valley does not return! Please, kill it for us! Our friends... our family... they\'re gone..." Jade: "A spectral stag attacking people... We\'ll take this seriously." Devon: "Quickly then. We gather information, track its path, and end this." Sky: "If people are dying, we cannot leave it be." Rin: "These tracks are massive... much larger than a normal deer. The earth is torn deep. Its strength is extraordinary." Levi: "Look at these broken branches. The stag moves with immense force, not just speed. The damage is consistent along this trail. It has a clear territory." Sky: "I can feel its presence... This is not simple corruption. Its spiritual energy feels ancient... sorrowful... as if it is bound here by something unresolved." Deep within the misty valley the spectral stag appears: a majestic yet terrifying presence, its antlers like shards of moonlight, its form neither fully real nor a mere illusion. It watches from the mist, its eyes filled with a sadness that did not belong to an ordinary beast. And yet any who approached never returned. Jade: "The villagers want it killed, and on the surface this is a hunt. But something about this feels different." Devon: "Whatever the truth, we need to see it directly. Let\'s follow the trail and learn why it attacks." Rin: "Agreed. We\'ll investigate the valley. Find the source, and decide what must be done." Levi: "This is more than a monster. There\'s a story here... and we need to find it."',
  art:'Pages show: Rin is the one reading the tracks in the first panels and Levi the damage (matching the dual tracking). The page leaves out Seraphina. The valley is not named on the page (ch154\'s quest and Arc VI design notes give it as Mourning Valley). Quest box has four objectives.',
  quote:'"This is more than a monster. There\'s a story here... and we need to find it." — Levi',
  events:['A mountain village at the edge of the Forest of Thorns fears a spectral stag','The villagers want it killed; at first it seems a straightforward hunt','Rin and Levi read the tracks: huge, with a clear territory','Sky: its energy is ancient and sorrowful, bound by something unresolved','The spectral stag watches from the mist; no one who approached returned','The party decides to learn why it attacks'],
  purpose:['Begin the second Evil','Frame the hunt as an investigation, not a kill'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Village That Fears the Deer (4 objectives)','Location: Mourning Valley'],
  reward:'The second hunt begins'},
 154:{ title:'The Mourning Hart', type:'Story Chapter — the spectral stag', loc:'🏮 Mourning Valley: the shrine of the stag',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin Kaede',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The valley the villagers feared is not silent. It pulses with a restless spirit that strikes down all who enter. At its heart waits the Mourning Hart, a guardian the village now calls a monster. Jade: "There it is!" Devon: "Stay sharp. Its pressure is strong." Levi: "Tracks circle the shrine. It was guarding this place." Rin: "No ordinary beast moves like that." Sky: "Wait... Its energy... this isn\'t corruption. It feels like protection." The hart attacks; Jade and Devon answer, and it roars. Jade: "Protection? Then why attack us?" Devon: "Because we crossed a boundary." Rin: "The shrine behind it..." Sky: "It\'s defending something. This isn\'t a mindless beast." Jade: "Everyone, stop! Do not strike the hart down!" What the villagers feared as a killing spirit may once have been a guardian mourning something it could no longer protect.',
  art:'Pages show: the Mourning Hart is named in the title and caption. The first clash is fought but Jade stops it before the hart is struck down. Quest box has five objectives. Seraphina is a silent member of the party (per the author: no big role until Altan), so she is not drawn.',
  quote:'"Everyone, stop! Do not strike the hart down!" — Jade',
  events:['The party meets the Mourning Hart at the heart of the valley','Levi: tracks circle the shrine; it was guarding this place','Sky: its energy is not corruption: it feels like protection','The first clash: the hart attacks because the party crossed a boundary','Jade calls everyone to stop before the hart is struck down'],
  purpose:['Test Aggression vs. Intent','Hint the hart is a mourning guardian'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Mourning Hart (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'The fight is stopped before the truth is lost'},
 155:{ title:'Beneath the Valley', type:'Story Chapter — the burial ground', loc:'🏮 Mourning Valley: the hidden sanctuary',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin Kaede',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Beneath the valley, hidden from the world, lies an ancient burial ground: a sacred sanctuary long sealed away from the living world. Waterfalls conceal the entrance, and below them rest the graves of countless souls. This place is both a burial ground and a sealed spiritual sanctuary. Jade: "This is what it was protecting..." Levi: "Tracks. More than one group. They kept coming back." Rin: "Not hunters. Looters... and soldiers." Sky: "The energy here is grieving. The sanctuary has been wounded." Devon: "These seals were disturbed repeatedly. Human hands did this. This was not just a burial ground... It is a sanctuary. A place to seal restless spirits and guide them beyond." Jade: "Then the hart attacked because we kept violating this place." Levi: "Treasure seekers come for the relics. And corrupt officials often send soldiers to take them." Rin: "You can see the tool marks, pry bars, ropes... They dug up the graves and stole the offerings. This was deliberate." Sky: "The sanctuary\'s energy is meant to protect and rest the dead. It is not malicious. It is wounded by human greed." The Mourning Hart was not a monster. It was a guardian spirit, standing watch over those who could no longer speak, in a place humans kept desecrating. Now we understood. The hart\'s anger was not toward us alone, but toward all who would disturb the rest of the dead.',
  art:'Pages show: looters and "corrupt officials\' soldiers" disturbed the burial ground repeatedly (the same corrupt-officials thread as Valen). The last quest-box line "Protect the burial ground from further harm" is the chapter\'s end action; nothing in the comic resolves the hart yet (the Register still lists it as not resolved). Seraphina is a silent member of the party (per the author: no big role until Altan), so she is not drawn. Speaker attributions in this chapter are partly inferred.',
  quote:'"The hart\'s anger was not toward us alone, but toward all who would disturb the rest of the dead."',
  events:['A hidden burial ground and sealed spiritual sanctuary lies beneath the valley','Looters and soldiers kept coming back: tool marks, pry bars, ropes','The seals were disturbed repeatedly by human hands; the offerings were stolen','Sky: the sanctuary is wounded by human greed, not malicious','The hart attacked because the burial ground kept being violated','The Mourning Hart is a guardian spirit watching over the dead'],
  purpose:['Reveal the hart\'s motive','Point at corrupt officials behind the looting'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beneath the Valley (5 objectives)','Lore: the burial ground'],
  reward:'The hart\'s motive is understood'},
 156:{ title:'A Different Victory', type:'Story Chapter — the Mourning Hart resolved', loc:'🏮 Mourning Valley, then the royal court',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin Kaede; King Greyson at court',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep in the northern mountains the party reaches the hidden valley, a sanctuary guarded by the Mourning Hart, a spirit of ancient times. What they once believed to be a monster is a guardian protecting this sacred land. The Hart had not attacked out of malice, but to keep intruders from a place of deep importance. Face to face with the truth, the party seeks a different path. Jade: "You are not a monster. You are the guardian of this valley. We understand now. We do not come to harm you." Devon: "Jade is right. This land is precious. We will respect your role and help protect it." The Hart watches them, its sorrowful eyes filled with memories of a long-lost time, and slowly the hostility in its gaze fades. Rin performs a spirit ritual: "Let the valley know that we come in peace, and that its guardians are not alone." The sanctuary\'s energy calms and the Hart lowers its head in acknowledgement. Sky: "I can feel it... The valley is alive with protective spirit energy. It accepts us now." Levi: "The surrounding spirits are no longer on edge. We can lower our weapons." The Hart turns and withdraws deeper into the sanctuary. Back in Tribute the party reports the truth to King Greyson, who issues a formal decree: the northern valley and its surrounding forests are protected land under Tribute. No hunting, logging or settlements are permitted; the spirits who dwell there are to be respected and left undisturbed. The sanctuary is under the direct protection of the crown. Evils Resolved: 2 / 15.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin before the Hart (Seraphina is not drawn, as before). The closing narration: "Not all Evils are defeated through death. Some are resolved through understanding, respect, and protection. The Mourning Hart remains: a guardian, not an enemy." The page does not say who among the party speaks the "weapons" line (inferred as Levi). The decree scene is at the royal court; the build keeps the chapter in Mourning Valley and adds the decree as the chapter\'s end.',
  quote:'"Not all Evils are defeated through death. Some are resolved through understanding, respect, and protection."',
  events:['The party stands before the Mourning Hart and speaks to it as a guardian','The Hart\'s hostility fades; Rin performs a spirit ritual of respect and remembrance','The sanctuary calms; the Hart lowers its head and withdraws deeper into the valley','Greyson formally recognises the valley and its forests as protected land under the crown','The Mourning Hart is resolved without being slain: Evils Resolved 2 / 15'],
  purpose:['Show that resolving an Evil does not mean killing it','Close the Aggression vs. Intent test'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Different Victory (4 objectives)','Register: the Mourning Hart resolved (2/15)'],
  reward:'The Mourning Hart is resolved: the valley is under Tribute\'s protection'},
 157:{ title:'The Walking Ruin', type:'Story Chapter — the third Evil', loc:'🏚️ The abandoned territory beyond the protected valley',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin Kaede',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Beyond the protected valley, new reports lead the party into abandoned territory: ancient settlements still stand, but no life remains within them. A humanoid figure has begun to appear among the ruins. It does not merely wander. It speaks, and remembers names no living person recognises. Jade: "This place feels abandoned... but not empty." Devon: "Someone has walked these streets recently." Levi reads the tracks: "The tracks are human. Or close enough to be." Rin: "It moves from settlement to settlement, always near the oldest remains." Sky, reading the energy: "This isn\'t beast-like. It\'s memory... and sorrow." Among the ruins the figure appears at last, a being neither fully living nor fully dead, clad in the remnants of ancient royalty. It murmurs: "Auren... Sel Veyr... House Merinth..." and, "Nothing to you. Everything to the dead." Jade: "Those names mean nothing to us." Devon: "It speaks as if it remembers this city alive." Sky: "This isn\'t ordinary corruption. It\'s as if the ruins themselves are speaking through him." The figure does not howl like a monster nor strike like a mindless evil; it walks the ruins like a king through the remains of his court. Jade understands that the Third Evil will not be simple to judge.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and a teal-haired figure (Rin) reading the trail. The moon and snow-covered ruins carry red banners. The Hollow King is first seen here as a crowned, cracked-faced figure in black and gold; he is named in the quest box ("the being called the Hollow King").',
  quote:'"Nothing to you. Everything to the dead." — the figure in the ruins',
  events:['New reports lead the party into abandoned territory with ancient settlements and no life','Fresh human tracks and a figure that moves from settlement to settlement near the oldest remains','Sky senses memory and sorrow rather than beast-like corruption','The figure appears: a crowned being, neither living nor dead, murmuring names (Auren, Sel Veyr, House Merinth)','It walks the ruins like a king through his court; the Third Evil will not be simple to judge'],
  purpose:['Introduce the third Evil as someone who remembers','Set up the judgment of the Hollow King'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Walking Ruin (5 objectives)','The abandoned territory'],
  reward:'The third Evil is found: a king among the ruins'},
 158:{ title:'The Third Evil Speaks', type:'Story Chapter — the Hollow King', loc:'🏚️ The abandoned ruins: the ancient throne',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party enters the abandoned ruins deeper within the northern region, where an ancient throne still stands, and there the Third Evil has been waiting. He is not a beast but a king long dead, a remnant of a fallen age wrapped in tattered regalia, with eyes as hollow as the moon. This is the Hollow King, the Third of the Fifteen Evils. Jade: "So this is... the Third Evil." Levi: "He looks like a king..." Sky: "His presence feels ancient... and sorrowful." Devon: "He\'s human... but not alive." The Hollow King turns his eyes toward Jade, as if recognising something in her blood. "Gold." "They are still sending Golds after us." "I remember your name. The blood of the first sunrise... The last heir of Solmir. You bear the same light as she did." "I remember Velran. I remember Elaris. I remember the ones who stood before you. Different faces... same blood. The Golds never stop chasing." Jade: "He knows... my lineage?" Levi: "The Fifteen Evils... They have been hunting the Golds all this time." Devon: "Names from an age long before ours..." Sky: "So the Golds... have always been their target?" The truth now stands before them: the Fifteen Evils are bound to Jade\'s family line, and the hunt has never ended. The conversation that would change everything is only just beginning.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi on the steps before an ancient throne. Speaker attributions for the four reaction lines are inferred from the order of the panels. Several names are new in this chapter: Solmir ("the last heir of Solmir", "the blood of the first sunrise"), Velran and Elaris (earlier Golds who "stood before" Jade). The caption says the Fifteen Evils were bound to Jade\'s family line; the Hollow King himself speaks of Golds being sent "after us".',
  quote:'"They are still sending Golds after us." — the Hollow King',
  events:['The Hollow King waits on an ancient throne among the ruins','He recognises Jade\'s blood: "Gold... the last heir of Solmir"','He remembers earlier Golds: Velran and Elaris, different faces and the same blood','The party realises the Fifteen Evils have long been tied to the Gold lineage','The conversation that would change everything is only beginning'],
  purpose:['Tie the Fifteen Evils to the Gold lineage','Make the Hollow King a speaker, not a monster'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Third Evil Speaks (5 objectives)','Lore: the Gold lineage and the Fifteen'],
  reward:'The Hollow King knows Jade\'s lineage: the Gold name is tied to the Fifteen'},
 159:{ title:'Fifteen Monsters', type:'Story Chapter — the Hollow King\'s account', loc:'🏚️ The ruins before the throne',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Under the cold light of the moon the party stands before the Hollow King. He does not attack and does not retreat; he speaks of names, of history, and of the Fifteen that the world has called Evils. "There were never fifteen Evils." "There were fifteen entities designated as dangerous during the ancient crisis. They were given the name of Evils not because they were all the same, but because they could not be understood, controlled, or easily explained." "Some were corrupted. Some resisted the rulers. Some guarded forbidden places. And some were simply impossible to control." Jade: "A different name does not erase what you have done. Whether you call them Evils or something else, they still caused suffering." Devon: "This sounds like justification. History can have more nuance, but we will not lower our guard." Sky: "So the records were incomplete. There is more to their story than the kingdoms ever told us. The past... is more complicated than we imagined." Levi: "No matter the reason, you are still dangerous. We cannot simply believe you. Tell us the truth. All of it." The Hollow King speaks of a history shaped by fear, politics and power: fifteen entities bound by different fates, branded with the same name, and remembered as monsters. But though his words cast doubt on the old records, he remains an enigma, his intentions uncertain and his truth not yet proven.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi before the throne; four small panels show the four kinds of "designated" entity (corrupted, resisted the rulers, guarded forbidden places, impossible to control). The party does not accept his account yet: the chapter ends with the Hollow King an enigma. The quest box asks the player to "decide whether the Hollow King can be trusted"; nothing in the pages gives a choice, so the build treats it as the story\'s own step.',
  quote:'"There were never fifteen Evils." — the Hollow King',
  events:['The Hollow King neither attacks nor retreats; he speaks','There were never fifteen Evils: fifteen entities were designated dangerous in the ancient crisis','Some were corrupted, some resisted the rulers, some guarded forbidden places, some could not be controlled','The party refuses to take him at his word: a different name does not erase suffering','His account casts doubt on the old records, but his intentions stay uncertain'],
  purpose:['Reframe the Fifteen as designated entities','Keep the Hollow King\'s truth unproven'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Fifteen Monsters (5 objectives)','Lore: designation versus corruption'],
  reward:'The old records are in doubt: the Fifteen were designated, not all born monsters'},
 160:{ title:'The Crownless King', type:'Story Chapter — the sealed kingdom', loc:'🏚️ The ruined throne hall',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep within the northern ruins the party stands before the Hollow King in what was once a royal throne hall; broken pillars and faded banners speak of a lost kingdom, a land cut away from the world. He is still the Hollow King: a ruler without a crown, a king from a forgotten age whose kingdom was buried by the seals and whose people were erased from history. "I was king before these borders existed. The seals did not only imprison monsters. They erased kingdoms." "My people lived in a land of rivers and mountains... a kingdom with a name, a history, and a future. Then the seals cut our world away. Our land was removed from the maps. Our people were buried, and their names died with them." "We were not monsters. We were a people. And yet the world chose to forget us." Jade: "What happened to you was wrong. Your people did not deserve to be erased." Devon: "Injustice in the past does not give you the right to spill innocent blood now." Sky: "I can still feel the grief in you... the loss of a kingdom, and all the lives that were forgotten. Your pain is real." Levi: "But you\'ve killed people in the present. These ruins are not empty. The dead are real." Jade: "But the dead you left behind in the present are real too. Suffering does not absolve cruelty." The Hollow King: "You speak of the dead as if they belonged to your world. I did what I had to do. This world took everything from me. Why should I show mercy in return? A king cannot apologize for surviving. The world forgot us first." He is both a victim of a cruel history and a wielder of present violence: victimhood does not erase responsibility.',
  art:'Pages show: the throne hall, a golden vision of the lost kingdom (a castle among waterfalls and a bridge), and the same land shattered into floating stone by the seals. Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi stand together. The Hollow King does not name his kingdom in this chapter. The chapter title and the register call him the Crownless King; the build uses "The Crownless Marches" (the register\'s name for his region) for the ruins, which is not written on the pages.',
  quote:'"The seals did not only imprison monsters. They erased kingdoms." — the Hollow King',
  events:['The Hollow King, once a king of a land cut away from the world by the seals','The seals erased his kingdom: removed from the maps, its people buried, their names dead with them','Jade and the party grieve with him but refuse to excuse present killing','He answers that the world forgot his people first and he owes it no mercy','Victimhood does not erase responsibility; history may have forgotten him, but the innocent dead will not be forgotten again'],
  purpose:['Make the Hollow King a victim and a wielder of violence','Show that the seals erased a kingdom'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Crownless King (5 objectives)','Lore: the sealed kingdom'],
  reward:'The Hollow King is a victim who became dangerous: justice must be decided'},
 161:{ title:'Judgment', type:'Boss Battle — the Hollow King', loc:'🏚️ The ruined settlement at the heart of the seal-region',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'seraphina', 'levi', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Seraphina, Levi and Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party reaches the ruined settlement at the heart of the seal-region, where the Hollow King still remains: a ruler long dead, whose suffering was real and whose choices brought untold ruin. He had been wronged by a cruel history, and yet he continued to kill, to erase, to bury entire peoples. Today Jade and her companions face him, not to excuse his past, but to determine his judgment. Jade: "You were wronged. Your people were betrayed. You suffered real pain. And yet you still chose to kill. You cannot hide behind the past forever." The Hollow King: "Judgment... from a Gold? You think you understand my pain? I would rather this world burn than kneel again. I will not surrender." Devon: "Then we stop you. Not to erase what you endured, but to prevent more people from suffering." Seraphina: "Your tragedy does not give you the right to take innocent lives. This ends now." Levi: "I\'ll keep him covered from range!" Sky: "I\'ll maintain healing and boost everyone\'s energy! Stay in formation!" Jade and Devon move as one, their strengthened powers in perfect harmony; Seraphina\'s elegant strikes cut through the shadows while Levi\'s arrows rain from afar and Sky\'s healing light keeps the formation alive. Jade: "Your pain is real. But your crimes are real too. We cannot let you go." The Hollow King: "So this is my fate... To be sealed by those who inherit a kinder world... Very well. Bind me, then. But know this: my pain will not be forgotten." The answer is not simple destruction but containment: the Hollow King is sealed, his power restrained, his story remembered as a warning for the future. Chained, he says: "I am still here... Even in chains... Remember... Remember what you saw." Compassion and judgment can exist together.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Seraphina, Levi and Sky in battle formation (this is the first chapter where Seraphina fights openly in Arc VI), Levi with a bow, Sky casting blue light, and the Hollow King bound at the end by a ring of golden chains and sigils. Rin is not drawn. The quest box ("Decide its final judgment") has no visible choice on the pages: the result is containment, and the build treats it as the story\'s own decision.',
  quote:'"Your pain is real. But your crimes are real too. We cannot let you go." — Jade',
  events:['The party faces the Hollow King to determine his judgment, not to excuse his past','Jade and Devon fight as one; Seraphina, Levi and Sky hold the formation','The Hollow King accepts that he will be sealed by those who inherit a kinder world','He is contained in golden chains rather than destroyed: his story is kept as a warning','The Third Evil is resolved by containment: Evils Resolved 3 / 15'],
  purpose:['Resolve the third Evil by containment','Show that compassion and judgment can exist together'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Judgment (5 objectives)','Register: the Hollow King contained (3/15)'],
  reward:'The Third Evil is contained: Evils Resolved 3 / 15'},
 162:{ title:'Three Evils, Three Truths', type:'Story Chapter — the research hall', loc:'📚 Imperial Capital: the imperial research hall',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Master Orin Vale, Adrian Gold and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party returns to Tribute carrying new truths from the northern lands. Within the imperial research hall they gather with Master Orin Vale and Adrian Gold to compare the three recent cases. The three encounters had all been called Evil, yet each had revealed a different truth. Master Orin Vale, Keeper of the Fifteen Register: "For decades, I catalogued them as the Fifteen Evils. That was the understanding passed down through generations. But your findings are forcing the Register itself to change. The truth behind these three cases proves that the records were incomplete... even wrong in some places." Adrian: "Then the title Evil was never the truth. Only a label left by history. A name does not guarantee a single reality." Evil I, the Corrupted Guardian: "Evil I was consumed by corruption. It truly was dangerous, and it had to be destroyed." Evil II, the Misidentified Protector: "Evil II was protecting what humans had violated. It was misidentified, its true nature was never understood." Evil III, the Historical Victim: "And Evil III was a victim of history who still became dangerous. Tragic... but still a threat that had to be contained." "The same name concealed three completely different realities. A corrupted monster. A rightful protector. And a wounded soul shaped by the past." "Then each case must be judged for what it truly is. We cannot rely only on old names or inherited fear." "Not by rumor. Not by old fear. We must look at the truth before us. But by what remains beneath the name. Each place, each history, each suffering... Only then can we understand what we are truly facing." The Register is updated: the Mourning Hart, original classification Hostile cursed beast, revised classification Ancient territorial guardian, corruption uncertain. Orin: "If the records are wrong... then every future entry may change. The Fifteen Evils were never a simple list of monsters. They are histories waiting to be understood." Jade: "The name Evil does not tell us everything. Each one holds its own truth. From now on, we will not assume. We will investigate, listen, and judge with our own eyes."',
  art:'Pages show: seven people around a long table in the research hall (Jade, Sky, Devon, Adrian in green, Master Orin Vale with grey hair and glasses, Levi, and a teal-ornamented figure); the blonde woman who says "Then each case must be judged for what it truly is" is Eira Solenne (an ally and guest, not a party member: the author confirms she is not locked to the Broken Seals area); the lines credited to Sky, Devon, Levi are attributed by panel position. Quest box: Review the three recent cases; Examine the Fifteen Register; Witness the Register update; Understand why the title "Evil" never guaranteed a single truth; Prepare for the next investigation.',
  quote:'"The name Evil does not tell us everything. Each one holds its own truth." — Jade',
  events:['The party compares the three resolved cases with Master Orin Vale and Adrian','Evil I: the Corrupted Guardian, consumed and destroyed; Evil II: the Misidentified Protector; Evil III: the Historical Victim, contained','Orin Vale admits the Register was incomplete and in places wrong','The Register is updated: the Mourning Hart\'s classification is revised','Jade: from now on we will not assume; we will investigate, listen and judge with our own eyes'],
  purpose:['Name the three truths behind the first three Evils','Open the question of the Register itself'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Three Evils, Three Truths (5 objectives)','The Register update'],
  reward:'The Register is revised: three Evils, three truths'},
 163:{ title:'The Fifteen Register', type:'Story Chapter — the royal archive', loc:'📚 Imperial Capital: the royal archive',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Master Orin Vale, Adrian Gold and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Back in Tribute the party returns to the royal archive to compare the truths behind the first three resolved Evils. What they discover reveals a larger mystery: the Fifteen Register itself may be based on rewritten history. Master Orin Vale, Royal Archivist and Researcher: "The official list has been copied for centuries. We know the copyists, the scholars, priests and archivists who reproduced it across generations. But we do not know the original author." Adrian Gold, Royal Scholar: "Then the foundation of the Register is uncertain from the very beginning. It may not be a record of truth, but a record of how truth was later interpreted and rewritten." Eira Solenne, Scholar: "This terminology is not from the oldest Keeper records. It appears only after the Keeper oath was altered. The language, classifications, and even the word Evil reflect a later period." Jade: "So even the name Evil may be part of a rewritten history. What if these were not monsters from the beginning, but people, places, or guardians whose stories were changed?" The Register\'s revised entries show: Evil I, the Thorned Widow, originally classified as an ancient guardian spirit and rampaging corruption entity, revised: a corrupted guardian, destroyed. Evil II, the Mourning Hart, originally a hostile cursed beast, revised: ancient territorial guardian, corruption uncertain. Evil III, the Hollow King, originally a hostile undead ruler and village destroyer, revised: a historical victim who became dangerous, contained. All three are Resolved. Sky: "Three labels. Three entirely different truths. A corrupted guardian, a protector, and a historical victim." Levi: "Meaning the names cannot be judged blindly. Each one may hide a different truth, shaped by the time, the politics, or the people who wrote it." The first three cases show that the Fifteen Evils are not just monsters: they are complex histories, each with a truth that was hidden, altered or lost. The Register may not be a record of what truly was, but a record of what later generations chose to believe. "It is a map of rewritten history. And there are still twelve names left to understand."',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Master Orin Vale, Adrian Gold and Eira Solenne in the royal archive, with three large Register cards (Evil I, II, III) each marked RESOLVED. The attributions of the closing lines are inferred. Eira is in Tribute here as an ally and guest (not a party member). Chapter 162 covers the same comparison of the three cases in the research hall, so this chapter repeats it from the archive side and moves on to the Register itself.',
  quote:'"It is a map of rewritten history. And there are still twelve names left to understand."',
  events:['The party compares the first three resolved cases in the royal archive','The copyists of the official list are known, but not its original author','Eira: the terminology and the word Evil date from after the Keeper oath was altered','The Register shows original and revised classifications for the first three Evils, all Resolved','The Register may be a record of what later generations chose to believe; twelve names remain'],
  purpose:['Raise the question of who wrote the Register','Link the Register to the altered Keeper oath'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Fifteen Register (5 objectives)','Register: original and revised classifications'],
  reward:'The Register may be rewritten history'},
 164:{ title:'The Missing Fourth Entry', type:'Story Chapter — the royal archive', loc:'📚 Imperial Capital: the royal archive',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Master Orin Vale, Adrian Gold and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Back in Tribute the party continues its investigation of the Fifteen Register, comparing the official list with older records to uncover the truth behind the missing entry. "Let\'s compare the official list with the older records and see what we can find. There may be details hidden in the wording, the numbering, or the seals." Master Orin Vale: "The official list has been copied for centuries. It exists in archives across many kingdoms. But no one knows who first created it, or when it was originally written." Adrian: "The numbering is wrong. It jumps directly from III to V. There is no Entry IV in the official list." Eira: "This terminology is later than the oldest Keeper records. It appears only after the Keeper oath was altered. The language and classification style match a later period, not the original eras." The official list shows I The Thorned Widow, II The Mourning Hart, III The Hollow King, IV (blank), V The Silent Tide, VI The Ashen Crown. Jade: "Then Entry IV was removed? It wasn\'t destroyed by time or war? Someone deliberately took it out?" The page was cleanly removed: not the result of fire, water or decay; the binding shows it was carefully extracted. "Not destroyed. Removed. Someone wanted it hidden." The cuts are clean and precise: this was done deliberately, not by accident. Comparing a Keeper-era document with a later archive copy (after the oath alteration), the older records number and word things differently, and Entry IV existed in the earlier documents; in later copies it is missing, and the terminology changes match the period after the Keeper oath was altered. Eira: "Someone did not want future generations hunting Evil IV. They removed it from the official record, from every copy that followed. But they left the other entries intact. Why?" There was once a Fourth Entry in the Fifteen Register. It was real. It was known. And then it was removed, deliberately. "Someone had the power to alter history itself. They hid Evil IV from the world. But what were they trying to protect... and why?"',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon (blue-black robes), Sky, Adrian (green), Eira, Orin Vale around the archive table; the Register\'s Official List with Roman numerals, and a side-by-side of a Keeper-era page (Entry IV, with a black sigil) and a later copy (Entry V). MISMATCH to confirm: the list shown here is I Thorned Widow, II Mourning Hart, III Hollow King, IV [removed], V The Silent Tide, VI The Ashen Crown, but chapter 147 listed 4. The Black Tide, 5. The Silent Flame, 6. The Weeping Stone. The build keeps the 147 names and treats this page\'s names for V and VI as the artist\'s wording until the author decides.',
  quote:'"Not destroyed. Removed. Someone wanted it hidden."',
  events:['The party compares the official Register with older Keeper-era records','The numbering jumps from III to V: Entry IV is missing from the official list','The page was carefully extracted, not lost to fire, water or time','Keeper-era documents carry Entry IV; later copies after the oath alteration do not','Someone removed Evil IV from every copy on purpose and left the other entries intact'],
  purpose:['Establish that Evil IV was deliberately hidden','Tie the removal to the altered Keeper oath'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Missing Fourth Entry (5 objectives)','Lore: the missing Fourth Entry'],
  reward:'Entry IV was real, known, and removed on purpose'},
 165:{ title:'The Nameless Witness', type:'Story Chapter — the archive-shrine', loc:'🏛️ An abandoned archive-shrine',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Eira Solenne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Under the cold light of the moon the party reaches an abandoned archive-shrine, an ancient settlement once connected to the missing Fourth Entry of the Fifteen Evils. Someone is already waiting there: a figure who seems to know the Fifteen not from records, but from a time when the world called them by different names. "The fourth entry was cut out cleanly. Not destroyed. Removed. The other entries are still here... so someone deliberately took this one." "Someone did not want future generations hunting Evil IV." "This is not the work of ordinary raiders. They understood the value of information." "This place was once a proper archive. Not a random ruin." "The removal was intentional." "They did not destroy the truth. They tried to erase it from being found." "Someone who knows the Fifteen... and who fears what people might learn." "This place feels like it has been watched for a long time. Even now, someone is here." A hooded figure speaks: "So the Gold Child has finally started asking what an Evil is." Jade: "Who are you?" "Someone your ancestors were told to forget. You still call them Evils. Names are useful. But they are not the whole story. I have seen the Fifteen before the world gave them that name. I have seen what they were... what they became... and why some of their records had to disappear. There are truths that are kinder when they remain unfound. Our paths will cross again, Gold Child. When you are ready to see beyond the names." The Nameless Witness speaks as someone who had seen the Fifteen in an earlier time. The Fourth Entry was not destroyed but removed, a deliberate act to keep the truth from future generations. The mystery behind Evil IV runs deeper than the party imagined.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina (hair snow white, part of her power: it shifts to white when she fights and golden otherwise) and Eira Solenne (the pale blonde woman) before the archive-shrine; the hooded figure with long silver-grey hair and gold-trimmed black cloak is the Nameless Witness (not Varyn, as the roadmap says). The shrine\'s location is not named on the pages, so the build calls it "The Abandoned Archive-Shrine". The witness dissolves into floating stone at the end. Quest box: Investigate the ruined archive-shrine and the missing Fourth Entry; Analyze the remaining records for clues about Evil IV; Learn more about the Nameless Witness and their connection to the Fifteen; Determine why the Fourth Entry was removed; Prepare for the party\'s next encounter with the Nameless Witness.',
  quote:'"So the Gold Child has finally started asking what an Evil is." — the Nameless Witness',
  events:['The party reaches an abandoned archive-shrine tied to the missing Fourth Entry','The Fourth Entry was cut out cleanly, by someone who understood the value of information','A hooded figure is already there: someone who saw the Fifteen before they were named','"Someone your ancestors were told to forget": names are useful, but not the whole story','"Our paths will cross again, Gold Child. When you are ready to see beyond the names."'],
  purpose:['Introduce the Nameless Witness','Deepen the mystery behind Evil IV'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Nameless Witness (5 objectives)','Dossier: the Nameless Witness'],
  reward:'The Nameless Witness has appeared: the mystery of Evil IV runs deeper'},
 166:{ title:'Fifteen Shadows', type:'Story Chapter — Arc VI finale', loc:'🏰 Imperial Capital: the royal court',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, King Greyson, Adrian Gold and Master Orin Vale',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade and the party return to Tribute, bringing new truths from the northern forest. The trail to the Fifteen Evils is not over, but it can no longer be walked in ignorance. They have seen how easily rumours become monsters, and now they stand before their king with a decision that will change the course of the campaign. King Greyson receives Jade and the party, listening to their reports. Greyson: "You have returned. The northern forest has given us more questions... but also a clearer path." Adrian: "The letters, witness accounts, and local records all confirm the same thing: the truth is more complicated than the old stories." Greyson: "I will not abandon this campaign. But we must no longer hunt them blindly." Jade: "We do not destroy the Fifteen Evils. We resolve them. Each name hides a different wound, a different history. The same label can hold many truths." Greyson: "Then let the mandate be changed. From this day forward, Tribute seeks truth before judgment. We do not fear the Fifteen Evils, but neither shall we reduce them to simple monsters again." Jade: "The same name can belong to a villain, a victim, a guardian, or a warning. Our task is not only to stop what they do... but to resolve what they are." Adrian: "I will formally revise the mission register. The campaign will continue, with a new mandate." Master Orin Vale: "Then the record itself will begin to tell a truer history. We must distinguish rumour from fact, and pain from guilt." Adrian revises the mission register, updating the mandate from destruction to resolution: the mission mandate now reads "Resolve the Fifteen Evils." The record of the Fifteen Evils is rewritten, not to erase the past, but to see it clearly. The first three cases stand as proof that the same label can hide very different truths: Evil I, the Corrupted guardian: Destroyed. Evil II, the Misidentified protector: Reconciled. Evil III, the Historical victim who became dangerous: Contained. THE FIFTEEN EVILS. Resolved: 3 / 15. Remaining: 12. Unknown classifications: ? "Not every monster was born a monster. Not every victim remained innocent. And not every name history gave them was true." The journey to resolve the Fifteen Evils continues. The same name. Different truths. The next path will take them deeper into the shadows, where more stories wait to be uncovered. Because the truth is never simple. And the Fifteen Evils are only the beginning.',
  art:'Pages show: the royal court with King Greyson, Adrian, Master Orin Vale, Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, and two golden-haired women (Eira, and Seraphina, whose hair is golden out of battle and snow white in battle as part of her power). There is no quest box on this page, so the chapter\'s mission is built from the chapter\'s own beats. The Register card shows Evil II as Reconciled, Evil I as Destroyed and Evil III as Contained, matching the Register. The closing line and the arc\'s final card match the roadmap.',
  quote:'"We do not destroy the Fifteen Evils. We resolve them." — Jade',
  events:['Jade and the party report to King Greyson on the truths from the northern forest','Greyson will not abandon the campaign, but will no longer hunt the Fifteen blindly','Jade: we do not destroy the Fifteen Evils, we resolve them','Adrian revises the mission register: the mandate changes from destruction to resolution','The Register: Resolved 3 / 15, Remaining 12, Unknown classifications ?'],
  purpose:['Change the campaign\'s mandate from Destroy to Resolve','Close Arc VI and open the next hunt'],
  unlocks:['The mandate: Resolve the Fifteen Evils','Arc VI complete'],
  reward:'The mandate is changed: Resolve the Fifteen Evils'},
 167:{ title:'The Message from Dragonvale', type:'Story Chapter — Arc VII begins: the Sunken Crown', loc:'📚 Imperial Capital: the royal archive',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Adrian Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'A new report reaches Tribute from Sally\'s intelligence network in Dragonvale. Ships have begun vanishing along an abandoned maritime route. Fishermen speak of black water appearing after sunset, while others swear they have seen the towers of an ancient palace beneath the waves. Sally\'s network sent several reports from coastal villages and fishing towns: "Fishermen report that ships vanish without a trace along an abandoned maritime route. After sunset, the sea turns black. Those who return speak of unnatural waters, unlike anything they have seen." "Several vessels disappeared in this area. No wreckage. No survivors. The water is black as ink, and it spreads only after sunset..." "Others claim they saw the towers of an ancient palace beneath the waves. They say it rises in the black water... just before the ships vanish." Adrian: "One name matches the Register. The Black Tide. The descriptions align: unnatural black water, missing ships, and a submerged palace. The Black Tide is listed in the Fifteen Register." The Register page reads: The Black Tide. A name lost to history. Waters that swallow ships. A palace beneath the waves. Associated with an erased maritime boundary. Status: Unresolved. Caution: Extreme danger. Devon: "These coordinates belong to an ancient Dragonvale maritime boundary... one that officially never existed. It was erased from all modern records. Even the imperial charts do not acknowledge this route." Sky: "The sea itself feels wrong. There is a strong sense of stagnant malice... as if the waters themselves remember something." Seraphina: "A palace beneath the waves... Such structures are not built by ordinary kingdoms. This must be something far older than Dragonvale\'s current rule." Levi: "Then this route was erased for a reason. Someone wanted it forgotten. And if ships are still disappearing... that means the threat remains." Jade: "People are disappearing. That is reason enough. We investigate. We will follow Sally\'s leads, investigate this route, and discover what lies beneath these waters." Devon: "Whatever awaits us... we face it together."',
  art:'Pages show: Devon, Sky, Jade, Adrian (green robe, hair up, glasses in some panels), Levi and a golden-haired woman (Seraphina, golden at rest per the author) around the archive table. The Register card for the Black Tide is headed "Entry 7-3", which does not match the chapter 147 numbering (4. The Black Tide) and sits oddly beside chapter 164\'s missing Entry IV: the build keeps the 147 numbering. The page misprints "Consult the Register" as "Consult th.. about the Fifteen Register" in the quest box.',
  quote:'"One name matches the Register. The Black Tide." — Adrian',
  events:['Sally\'s network reports ships vanishing along an abandoned maritime route in Dragonvale', 'Black water after sunset, and the towers of an ancient palace beneath the waves', 'Adrian: the Fifteen Register lists the Black Tide, Status: Unresolved, Caution: Extreme danger', 'Devon: the coordinates mark an ancient Dragonvale maritime boundary that officially never existed', 'Jade: we investigate; the party prepares for an expedition'],
  purpose:['Open the Black Tide hunt', 'Link the erased maritime boundary to the Register'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Message from Dragonvale (5 objectives)', 'Arc VII: The Sunken Crown begins'],
  reward:'The Black Tide is a threat: the party prepares to investigate Dragonvale'},
 168:{ title:'Letters Beneath the Blossoms', type:'Story Chapter — Jade and Adrian', loc:'🌸 Imperial Capital: the royal gardens',
  chars:['jade', 'devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Adrian Gold and (briefly) Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Before the journey to Dragonvale, the siblings take a rare moment to walk together in Tribute\'s royal gardens. Devon takes his leave: "I think you two should have some time alone. We have much to prepare, so I will attend to the other matters." Adrian: "Shall we take a walk beneath the blossoms? It has been a while since we had time to talk properly." Jade: "It feels just like when we were children. We would sneak into these gardens to escape our studies. Do you remember?" Adrian: "I remember. You were always fearless, Jade. I was never built for the battlefield the way you were. So I learned balance, breath, and how to survive without meeting force with force. I focus on balance, controlled breathing, evasive steps, and redirecting force. I carry smoke bombs, gas bombs, and small grenades or pellets when necessary. When I\'m in dangerous situations, I rely on intelligence, negotiation, and tactical tools rather than direct combat." Jade asks about someone he mentioned, Eve Gray: "This is the first time I\'m hearing her name." Adrian: "I met Eve on an assignment. She had been travelling disguised as a young man. At an inn, some men realized the truth and began to bully and humiliate her. I intervened. Words, not weapons. I persuaded them to back down, and convinced the innkeeper to protect her instead." After that they travelled together for a time, sharing many conversations, and he grew to care for her deeply. But one day Eve disappeared without explanation. He searched for her, but found no trace. Some time later a specially trained pigeon brought him a letter from her, and their correspondence has continued ever since: with each letter she shares a little of her life, and sometimes sends small tokens. Jade: "Adrian... Do you love her?" Adrian: "Yes. I think I have. She is kind, brave, and sees the world in a way that feels like home to me." Jade: "Then be honest with your feelings. But also be careful. Her disappearance is still a mystery. There may be more to this than we know. I hope one day I can meet Eve Gray myself." The pigeon arrives with another letter: "It\'s her... She always finds me. Another letter. I wonder what she wishes to tell me this time." Neither of them yet understood how important Eve would one day become to their journey.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Adrian (green robe, hair tied up) and Devon leaving. This chapter shows Adrian\'s defensive skills (balance, breathing, evasion, smoke bombs, gas bombs, small grenades); the build does not turn him into a party member, but they are the natural kit if he is ever made an ally. Eve Gray is new: her name, her disguise, her disappearance and the pigeon letters are canon from this page, and nothing is said about who she is or where she is.',
  quote:'"Some letters carry more than words. Beneath the blossoms of Tribute, a new thread of fate quietly unfolded."',
  events:['Devon leaves Jade and Adrian to talk in the royal gardens', 'Adrian: he learned balance, breath and evasion, and carries smoke bombs, gas bombs and small grenades', 'Eve Gray: met on an assignment, disguised as a young man; Adrian stood up for her with words', 'She disappeared without explanation; a trained pigeon later brought a letter, and they have written ever since', 'A new letter arrives by pigeon'],
  purpose:['Show Adrian\'s defensive style and his past', 'Introduce Eve Gray as a thread for later'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Letters Beneath the Blossoms (5 objectives)', 'Lore: Adrian and Eve Gray'],
  reward:'Adrian\'s story: the letters of Eve Gray'},
 169:{ title:'The Pearl That Remembers', type:'Story Chapter — the Black Dragon Pearl', loc:'📚 Imperial Capital: the royal archive',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Adrian Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'As the party studies Dragonvale\'s old maritime charts, Devon notices a strange reaction from the Black Dragon Pearl. Ancient charts, faded records and forgotten routes speak of a sea where ships vanish and a palace lies beneath the waves. Jade: "It\'s responding to the maps?" Devon: "Only to certain locations. The closer it gets, the stronger the resonance." Sky: "This energy... I know it. It feels like the same restorative force that saved my life." They remember the day Yvette\'s jade pendant and Devon\'s pearl worked together to restore Sky\'s damaged life force. Adrian: "If this is the same energy, then the pearl may be much older than Dragonvale\'s royal line. It may not belong to Dragonvale at all... but to a civilization that came before it." Devon: "The strongest resonance is here... the region linked to the Black Tide." Jade: "Then the missing ships and the pearl are connected." Devon: "Then this route is more than a shipping lane." Jade: "We investigate Dragonvale. This is our destination." Guided by a pearl that remembers, the party prepares to sail for Dragonvale: a sea of lost ships, forbidden truths, and a palace drowned in time.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Devon (black gloves, fur collar, holding the glowing pearl), Sky and Adrian (with glasses) at the chart table. The pearl\'s resonance is strongest over the Black Tide region on the chart. A flashback panel shows Sky lying with Yvette\'s jade pendant and the pearl glowing together. Note: this makes the Black Dragon Pearl older than Dragonvale\'s royal line, which later chapters (175-176) expand.',
  quote:'"Guided by a pearl that remembers, the party prepares to sail for Dragonvale."',
  events:['Devon notices the pearl reacting to certain locations on the old charts', 'Sky recognises the energy: the restorative force that saved his life', 'Adrian: the pearl may belong to a civilization older than Dragonvale\'s royal line', 'The strongest resonance is the region linked to the Black Tide', 'The expedition\'s destination is Dragonvale'],
  purpose:['Link the pearl to the Black Tide', 'Tie the pearl to Sky\'s recovery'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Pearl That Remembers (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'The pearl and the missing ships are connected'},
 170:{ title:'Return to Dragonvale', type:'Story Chapter — Dragonvale\'s court and harbour', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale: the court',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Adrian, Sally, Roc and Delilah',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade returns to Dragonvale not as the same visitor who once passed through its court, but as someone who has learned how power buries truth. A courtier says: "Lady Jade... your reputation now reaches far beyond our shores. Your insight into foreign courts is most impressive." An older minister adds: "But some worry, Your Highness, that your habit of questioning accepted history may disturb the stability of Dragonvale. There are matters best left in the past." Sally, with her network\'s reports: "The disappearances are real. Fishermen speak of black water after sunset... and towers beneath the waves. Our network has collected reports from coastal villages and fishing towns. Ships vanish along an old route that is no longer used. The sightings have become more frequent lately." Roc sits with Delilah (the caption reads: if Roc was purified, he returns with renewed vitality beside Delilah; otherwise, lingering illness still shadows him). Sailors avoid those waters now: "The old route has been feared for generations. There are currents that make no sense, and places where the sea itself feels wrong." Adrian: "The Register gives one matching name. The Black Tide. These coordinates mark a maritime boundary that Dragonvale officially denies ever existed. The descriptions align with the missing ships and the accounts we\'ve gathered." Records about the Sunken Kingdom have been deliberately suppressed for generations. Some are restricted; others have mysteriously disappeared. Entire sections of maritime records are missing, as if they were removed. Jade: "Why has Dragonvale deliberately avoided discussing the Sunken Kingdom for generations?" The officials: "These are merely sailors\' superstitions. There is no proof of any such kingdom. These records are not relevant to the present. We suggest you focus on matters that concern the living." Jade: "Then the silence is deliberate. The missing ships and the erased records are connected. We investigate the route, the records, and whoever erased this history."',
  art:'Pages show: Dragonvale\'s court with Jade, Devon (fur collar), Sky, Levi, Adrian and a golden-haired woman (Seraphina) among Dragonvale\'s officials; the old minister is grey-haired, the courtier bearded. Sally appears in a purple-blue robe with hair flowers; Roc (long dark hair, beard) sits beside Delilah (purple robe). The Roc caption is conditional on the Register of his fate (purified or not): the build uses the roc_purified flag for the wording. First time the page names the "Sunken Kingdom".',
  quote:'"Then the silence is deliberate." — Jade',
  events:['Jade returns to Dragonvale as someone who has learned how power buries truth', 'Sally\'s network confirms the disappearances and the black water', 'Roc and Delilah are met in Dragonvale', 'Dragonvale\'s officials call the Sunken Kingdom a superstition and ask Jade to leave the past alone', 'The records about the Sunken Kingdom have been suppressed for generations'],
  purpose:['Bring the party to Dragonvale', 'Show Dragonvale suppressing the Sunken Kingdom'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Return to Dragonvale (5 objectives)', 'Lore: the suppressed records'],
  reward:'The silence is deliberate: the missing ships and the erased records are connected'},
 171:{ title:'The Forbidden Sea Route', type:'Story Chapter — the harbour at night', loc:'⚓ Dragonvale: the harbour',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Adrian, Sally and Dragonvale\'s sailors',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'As night falls, Jade and her party return to the harbour of Dragonvale, where whispers of a forbidden sea route have begun to surface once more: a route to a prosperous kingdom that no longer appears on any modern maps. The harbour still thrives, but beneath its lively surface lie forgotten routes, missing ships, and a truth that had been deliberately buried. A sailor: "Aye, I\'ve heard of that route. My grandfather sailed it long ago. It connected Dragonvale to a wealthy kingdom across the Black Water. But the route was abandoned after the sea changed." Jade: "Do any of you remember what that kingdom was called?" "Few still remember. The name has been lost from official records. But some of us have fragments: old charts, stories... enough to know it was real." Devon: "Ships vanished along that route? With no wreckage?" "Aye. Many. They were said to fall into waters that turned black as ink. No trace left behind." Levi: "These claw-like marks aren\'t from ordinary rocks or reefs. The wood has been eroded by something in the water... like the Black Tide. There are traces of the same residue here on the docks. It\'s the same as what we saw near the Black Tide, but older. This place has been affected for a long time." Sky: "I can sense a deep spiritual disturbance beneath the waves. Something still lingers there... as if the sea itself remembers what was lost." Sally: "Several merchants have secretly purchased ancient navigation documents in recent years. They weren\'t ordinary trade maps, but copies of much older charts. Someone is trying to reconstruct this route." Among the documents they recovered, one surviving chart reveals the original name of the drowned territory: Aelyndra. Much of its history has been erased, but the route is clear: it once connected Dragonvale to a kingdom that no longer exists. Adrian: "These records were deliberately removed from official archives. Dragonvale\'s historians hid this route, erased it from maps and sealed any mention of that kingdom. There is a reason they did not want this information to survive." Jade: "So the route is real. A kingdom once flourished there... and now it lies beneath the sea, hidden from the world. We need to see the truth for ourselves." Devon: "This will not be a simple voyage. The Black Tide still lingers, and something remains in those waters. We must be well prepared." With the ship prepared, new maps in hand, and a long-buried truth finally uncovered, Jade and her companions set out to investigate the forbidden sea route.',
  art:'Pages show: the harbour at night with Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Adrian and the sailors; Sally (purple robe, hair flowers) reads the old charts. The chart\'s name is written Aelyndra. The title card says "Forbidden Sea Route"; the build names the sea location after it.',
  quote:'"So the route is real. A kingdom once flourished there... and now it lies beneath the sea, hidden from the world."',
  events:['Old sailors remember a route to a wealthy kingdom across the Black Water, abandoned after the sea changed', 'Claw-like marks and Black Tide residue on the docks; Sky feels a deep spiritual disturbance beneath the waves', 'Merchants have secretly bought ancient navigation documents: someone is reconstructing the route', 'A surviving chart names the drowned territory: Aelyndra', 'The party prepares a ship for the expedition'],
  purpose:['Name the drowned kingdom', 'Set the expedition sailing'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Forbidden Sea Route (5 objectives)', 'The forbidden route to Aelyndra'],
  reward:'The drowned territory has a name: Aelyndra'},
 172:{ title:'The Black Tide', type:'Major Encounter — the Black Tide, first manifestation', loc:'🌊 The forbidden waters',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and the expedition crew',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'As the expedition ship leaves the last known routes of Dragonvale, it enters forbidden waters. The sea is strangely calm, its surface like dark glass, and an unnatural stillness fills the air. But after sunset the sea begins to change. Black water spreads across the surface, like a living corruption, and from its depths something begins to rise. The calm sea turns into a field of darkness; corrupted creatures rise from the black water, attacking the ship from all sides. Jade: "Everyone to your positions! Defend the ship! Do not let them board!" An archer: "On my mark! Focus on the creatures from the left side!" A second archer: "More are approaching! I\'ll take the ones in the water!" Devon: "I\'ll hold the line with royal magic! Protect the ship at all costs!" Sky: "The waters here are deeply corrupted... I can feel an ancient presence beneath the sea. I\'ll try to stabilize the spiritual disturbance!" When the ship is nearly overwhelmed, Devon\'s Black Dragon Pearl responds. A radiant barrier expands from the pearl, encasing the ship in a dome of light that pushes back the Black Tide. The corrupted creatures are forced back, and the Black Tide slowly retreats into the depths. It has not been defeated, only driven away for now. As the darkness fades it disappears beneath the waves, leaving behind an uneasy silence. Something in the deep was calling to it, and the source still remains below. The Black Tide was only the first manifestation. Its source lies deeper still.',
  art:'Pages show: the expedition ship at sunset and night, red-eyed black sea creatures, Jade giving orders, two archers (Levi and a second archer with a green hair ribbon, inferred as the other ranger of the party: not named on the page), Devon casting gold magic, Sky stabilising with blue light, and the pearl\'s dome. The caption "Major Encounter: The Black Tide: First Manifestation" and the quest line "Activate the Dragon Pearl\'s protective ability" make this a battle that ends with the pearl\'s barrier and the Black Tide retreating, not defeated. The build\'s fight uses Tide Horrors and Drowned Shades, not a boss kill.',
  quote:'"It had not been defeated, only driven away for now."',
  events:['The expedition enters forbidden waters: a calm like dark glass, then black water after sunset', 'Corrupted marine creatures attack the ship from all sides; the party defends it', 'Devon\'s Black Dragon Pearl answers with a radiant dome of light', 'The Black Tide retreats into the depths, driven away but not defeated', 'Its source lies deeper still'],
  purpose:['Show the first manifestation of the Black Tide', 'Wake the pearl\'s protective power'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Black Tide (5 objectives)', 'The pearl\'s protective barrier'],
  reward:'The Black Tide is driven back: its source lies deeper'},
 173:{ title:'Beneath the Waves', type:'Story Chapter — the submerged passage', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the underwater passage',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and the expedition',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the Black Tide retreats, Devon\'s Black Dragon Pearl guides the expedition toward a submerged passage beneath the sea, leading them deeper into the drowned territory. The pearl\'s resonance leads them through an ancient underwater route, where massive magical structures maintain breathable spaces beneath the ocean. They discover ancient restoration chambers that connect different parts of the drowned territory. Jade: "The pearl is leading us somewhere." Devon: "This resonance... it\'s pulling us deeper." Sky: "These chambers are restoration anchors. They\'re still trying to preserve this place." Jade: "Then we restore what we can and move forward." "The barriers are old... but still holding." "These corridors connect multiple districts." The restoration chambers form a vast network of passages linking the different districts of the submerged kingdom. Many of the structures are deteriorating, but the magical barriers still hold, creating air-filled spaces while the ocean presses against them. Beyond the first chamber, a greater sight awaits. An entire kingdom lies beneath the sea: roads, towers, marketplaces, temples and royal buildings preserved within enormous magical barriers. Jade: "An entire kingdom..." Devon: "And it has been waiting beneath the sea all this time." The Sunken Kingdom survived in silence, almost untouched by time, yet eerily empty except for the distant movement of the sea. (Underwater dungeon exploration and restoration-anchor puzzles.)',
  art:'Pages show: the party in a submerged glass-and-gold passage and a vast city under a dome. The note "Underwater dungeon exploration and restoration-anchor puzzles" is a design note: the build treats the restoration chambers as an investigation chain; a puzzle mechanic is not built. The second archer (green hair ribbon) is again in the group, unnamed.',
  quote:'"An entire kingdom... And it has been waiting beneath the sea all this time."',
  events:['The pearl guides the ship through a submerged passage into the drowned territory', 'Magical structures keep air-filled spaces beneath the ocean', 'Ancient restoration chambers connect the districts and still try to preserve the place', 'The restoration chambers form a vast network linking the submerged kingdom\'s districts', 'An entire kingdom lies beneath the sea, preserved within enormous barriers'],
  purpose:['Reveal the Sunken Kingdom', 'Introduce the restoration chambers'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beneath the Waves (5 objectives)', 'The Sunken Kingdom'],
  reward:'The Sunken Kingdom is found: an entire kingdom beneath the sea'},
 174:{ title:'The Kingdom That Chose the Sea', type:'Story Chapter — the preserved city', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the preserved city',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and the expedition',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deeper within the Sunken Kingdom, Jade\'s party discovers the remains of a vast and magnificent city, still preserved beneath the waves inside ancient magical barriers. Homes, schools, workshops, markets and temples stretch before them: a thriving civilization frozen in time. This was no cursed wasteland, but a kingdom that had truly lived. They find preserved homes, furnished just as their inhabitants had left them; schools where children once studied, their desks, scrolls and teaching tools still in place; workshops and bustling marketplaces. Jade: "This was a real civilization... People lived here, raised families, studied, created, and built a beautiful kingdom. It doesn\'t look like a place that was destroyed by a natural disaster." "These inscriptions mention the Dima crisis... the Xima invasion. The records say the royal council made a decision to deliberately submerge portions of the kingdom." Sky: "These barriers have kept everything intact. It\'s as if they expected the city to remain hidden beneath the sea for a very long time." "This wasn\'t abandonment. It was a deliberate preservation measure. They chose the sea to protect something of immense importance." Ancient murals depict the royal council invoking powerful magic to lower the city beneath the sea, sealing it away during the Dima/Xima crisis. The inscriptions clearly show it was a planned act, not a collapse, not a natural disaster, but a choice: they submerged parts of their kingdom to protect something vital. Jade: "But what exactly were they trying to protect?" The records end here. They do not say what it was, or why it had to be hidden beneath the sea. "So much history portrayed this kingdom as a tragic ruin, a victim of the sea... but now it seems the truth is far more complex. Maybe this wasn\'t the end of a kingdom... but an emergency measure to preserve something for the future." Jade: "What could have been so important that they were willing to submerge their own homes, their cities, and their way of life? And why are the records incomplete?" "There are still so many unanswered questions. Whatever they protected... it remains a mystery to this day." The Sunken Kingdom was not a waste lost to the sea. It was a civilization that chose to disappear, sacrificing its own lands to protect something greater. But the most important part of the story is still missing.',
  art:'Pages show: preserved homes, a school, a workshop and market, and a mural of the royal council raising a wall of water. The inscriptions name the Dima crisis and the Xima invasion, so the Sunken Kingdom belongs to the same ancient crisis as the Keepers and seals. The speaker of several lines is not shown; the build leaves them unattributed.',
  quote:'"The Sunken Kingdom was not a waste lost to the sea. It was a civilization that chose to disappear."',
  events:['A thriving city frozen in time: homes, schools, workshops, markets and temples', 'Inscriptions mention the Dima crisis and the Xima invasion', 'The royal council deliberately submerged portions of the kingdom: a planned act, not a disaster', 'Murals show the council invoking powerful magic to lower the city beneath the sea', 'They protected something vital; the records end there'],
  purpose:['Show that the Sunken Kingdom chose the sea', 'Tie it to the Dima and Xima crisis'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Kingdom That Chose the Sea (5 objectives)', 'Lore: the deliberate submersion'],
  reward:'The kingdom chose the sea to protect something vital'},
 175:{ title:'Maris of the Deep Archives', type:'Story Chapter — the Tide Archivist', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the Deep Archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Maris Aurel',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deeper within the Sunken Kingdom, Jade\'s party reaches an ancient archive where surviving records have been guarded in secret for generations. There, among the preserved halls of memory, they meet someone who has never stopped searching for the truth of the drowned kingdom. Maris Aurel, Tide Archivist: "Outsiders should not be walking these archives. Dragonvale\'s court erased enough already. I will not let royal hands take what remains." Devon: "What if we came to restore it?" Maris: "That pearl... where did you get it? This is no ornament. It is one of the restoration keys. It was developed before Dragonvale\'s current royal dynasty. The Black Dragon Pearl can activate parts of the Sunken Kingdom\'s preservation network." Sky: "Its energy matches the preservation network." Maris: "Then the old system can still answer." The Black Dragon Pearl serves as a key, resonating with ancient anchors throughout the kingdom, activating the preservation network that maintained the underwater city and its records. Jade: "You know this place. Help us understand what the sea was protecting." Maris: "Very well. I will guide you, but the truth you seek was buried on purpose. My goal is to restore the historical identity of my ancestors." Maris had preserved fragments of the Sunken Kingdom\'s history in secret, determined that her ancestors would not vanish from memory. With the Tide Archivist as their guide, the party gains access to the deeper records of the drowned realm.',
  art:'Pages show: the Deep Archives with floating blue records, jellyfish and statues; Maris Aurel is a teal-haired woman in a white and blue robe with a jewelled headdress, captioned "Maris Aurel, Tide Archivist". She says her goal is to restore the historical identity of her ancestors, so she is a descendant of the Sunken Kingdom\'s people. The build lists her as an ally in the Record (dossier), not a party member or guest: the author decides.',
  quote:'"The truth you seek was buried on purpose." — Maris Aurel',
  events:['The party reaches an ancient archive guarded in secret for generations', 'Maris Aurel, the Tide Archivist, challenges them: Dragonvale\'s court erased enough already', 'She recognises the Black Dragon Pearl as one of the restoration keys, older than Dragonvale\'s dynasty', 'The pearl can activate parts of the Sunken Kingdom\'s preservation network', 'Maris agrees to guide them and opens the deeper records'],
  purpose:['Introduce Maris Aurel', 'Reveal the pearl as a restoration key'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Maris of the Deep Archives (5 objectives)', 'Dossier: Maris Aurel'],
  reward:'Maris Aurel guides the party into the deeper records'},
 176:{ title:'The Dragon Pearl', type:'Story Chapter — the restoration chamber', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the restoration chamber',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Maris Aurel',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep within the Sunken Kingdom, Maris leads the party to a chamber that houses ancient restoration mechanisms: forgotten systems designed to preserve life and mend damaged souls. Here, at the heart of the underwater city, the truth about the Black Dragon Pearl is finally revealed: an ancient purpose that has been hidden for generations. Maris: "This chamber contains ancient restoration mechanisms. The Black Dragon Pearl is not a weapon or a mere royal jewel. It is a restoration anchor." Devon: "A restoration anchor... I never knew this was its true purpose." Jade: "So it preserves life... but it cannot bring back someone who is truly dead." Sky: "I can feel the same restorative energy here... the same kind that saved me." The Black Dragon Pearl serves as a restoration anchor, preserving damaged life force long enough for spiritual recovery to occur. Its effectiveness depends on the condition of the individual and the presence of compatible restoration magic. Sky\'s survival was not an arbitrary miracle. Yvette\'s jade pendant began restoring his damaged spiritual system, while the Black Dragon Pearl stabilized and completed the process. Two ancient restoration traditions worked together. Maris: "The pearl preserves damaged life force, buying time for the soul to recover. It cannot resurrect someone whose life force has completely disappeared." Devon: "My family inherited an artifact of immense significance... yet its true purpose was forgotten. We carried it for generations without fully understanding what it was." Sky: "The jade pendant and the pearl were compatible... Their restoration magic resonated, allowing my life force to stabilize and heal. It wasn\'t a miracle. It was the result of forgotten restoration mechanisms working together." Jade: "Now we understand the truth." Sky: "The Dragon Pearl was never just a symbol of power. It is a key to preserving life..." Levi: "...and with this knowledge, we can protect more people in the future. The lost wisdom of the Sunken Kingdom still has so much to teach us." The Dragon Pearl\'s ancient restoration resonance has now been unlocked. The knowledge of the past will help the party protect lives and preserve the future of the Sunken Kingdom.',
  art:'Pages show: the restoration chamber with rings of blue light around a floating pearl, Sky\'s old recovery as a flashback with Yvette\'s jade pendant, and the party gathered around the pearl. This chapter says the pearl is not a Dragonvale royal jewel by origin but an older restoration anchor; the build adds Devon\'s Pearl Resonance skill at this chapter (the quest line "Unlock the pearl\'s ancient restoration resonance").',
  quote:'"The Dragon Pearl was never just a symbol of power. It is a key to preserving life."',
  events:['Maris leads the party to a chamber of ancient restoration mechanisms', 'The Black Dragon Pearl is a restoration anchor, not a weapon or a mere jewel', 'It preserves damaged life force long enough for recovery, but cannot resurrect the dead', 'Sky\'s survival: Yvette\'s jade pendant and the pearl, two ancient restoration traditions, worked together', 'The pearl\'s ancient restoration resonance is unlocked'],
  purpose:['Reveal the pearl\'s true purpose', 'Explain Sky\'s recovery'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Dragon Pearl (5 objectives)', 'Devon: Pearl Resonance'],
  reward:'The pearl\'s restoration resonance is unlocked'},
 177:{ title:'The Drowned Crown', type:'Major Encounter — the Drowned Crown, royal guardians', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the drowned royal palace',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Maris Aurel',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deeper within the Sunken Kingdom, Jade\'s party approaches the drowned royal palace, where the silence of the sea gives way to the authority of a forgotten throne. There an ancient power awakens: not a beast of chaos, but a royal will preserved beneath the waves. Dragonvale\'s histories had named it a destroyer. But in the depths, another truth begins to surface. Jade: "The palace... something has awakened." Devon: "That crown... it isn\'t just a symbol. It\'s the presence itself." Sky: "I can feel an overwhelming royal presence... so many voices, layered together through time." Maris: "Dragonvale called it a cursed monarch, but that was never the whole truth!" "Listen... There are voices... the kings and queens of this kingdom. They\'re still here." A voice: "Leave this place. The sea remembers what the land chose to forget." "This realm is not yours. Turn back, living ones. Disturb not what still rests beneath our care." Jade: "The Drowned Crown... this is one of the Fifteen?" "Royal guardians! Defend yourselves!" Jade: "Then we fight through, and learn what it\'s protecting." Sky: "It\'s warning us... not hunting us. It\'s defending something." "This isn\'t just an attack. It\'s a protection. There must be something here worth keeping safe." When the warning was ignored, the palace answered with the blades of its dead guardians.',
  art:'Pages show: a giant floating crown of blue light over the palace, translucent kings and queens, spectral armoured guardians, Jade with a sword, Devon and Sky casting, two archers. The fight is against the royal guardians, not against the Crown itself; the quest line "Determine whether the entity is genuinely hostile" is left open (the Crown warns rather than hunts). The Drowned Crown is Evil X in the chapter 147 list (10. The Drowned Crown).',
  quote:'"It\'s warning us... not hunting us. It\'s defending something."',
  events:['The party approaches the drowned royal palace; the Crown is a presence, not just a symbol', 'Many layered voices: the kings and queens of the kingdom are still here', 'The Drowned Crown is one of the Fifteen; Dragonvale called it a cursed monarch', 'The Crown warns them to leave; when the warning is ignored, its dead guardians attack', 'The party realises the guardians are defending something'],
  purpose:['Introduce the Drowned Crown as a warning, not a hunt', 'Pose the question: is it hostile?'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Drowned Crown (5 objectives)', 'Register: the Drowned Crown investigating'],
  reward:'The Drowned Crown warns and defends: it is not simply hostile'},
 178:{ title:'Roc\'s Inheritance', type:'Story Chapter — the archives and the maritime authority', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the Deep Archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Maris Aurel and Roc',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep within the preserved archives of the Sunken Kingdom, the party uncovers documents that link Roc\'s bloodline to the kingdom\'s fate: records that had been kept hidden for generations. Roc\'s ancestors inherited maritime authority from the Sunken Kingdom after its submersion. But over time, many of their descendants did not fully preserve the responsibilities tied to those privileges. Maris: "These records tie your house to the drowned realm. After the kingdom\'s submersion, your ancestors were granted maritime authority over these waters. This decree formally transferred maritime jurisdiction to your bloodline... along with the duty to protect what remained of the Sunken Kingdom." Roc: "...So my family profited from a kingdom that vanished?" The records show that some of his ancestors worked to protect the surviving descendants and preserve what remained, but others chose to suppress the kingdom\'s existence, to avoid political disputes over territory, authority and inheritance. "Generations later, the true purpose was forgotten. The privileges remained, but the responsibilities were neglected. Evidence suggests the existence of the Sunken Kingdom was deliberately erased from many records to prevent conflict with other kingdoms." Maris: "Your family gained wealth, trade rights, and influence through this maritime authority. It was a real benefit. And with those benefits came a duty, one that was not upheld by later generations." Jade: "You are not guilty for your ancestors\' choices. But now that you know the truth, you must decide what to do with it." Roc: "...I cannot change what my ancestors did. But I also won\'t defend our name blindly. I will investigate what responsibilities remain, and what can still be set right. The truth is more than my family\'s reputation. It is about the people of the Sunken Kingdom and what justice still matters today." The fate of the Sunken Kingdom became entwined with Dragonvale\'s inheritance, a connection that shaped centuries of maritime power, political alliances and buried truths: the kingdom\'s people, lands and legacy were not simply lost, but absorbed into the histories, privileges and silences of other realms. With the records revealed, the party now seeks to understand the full scope of Roc\'s inheritance: not only the power it brought, but the responsibilities that were left behind.',
  art:'Pages show: the Deep Archives with Maris, Jade, Devon, a bearded dark-haired man in black (Roc, at the centre of the final panel), a golden-haired woman (Seraphina) and the green-ribboned archer. Roc is with the party here although the roadmap left his redemption undecided: his line in 170 is conditional on whether he was purified, so the build treats him as an ally on Dragonvale ground (the existing guest rule) once he has been reborn. The page does not show who among the party Roc has travelled with since 170.',
  quote:'"I cannot change what my ancestors did. But I also won\'t defend our name blindly." — Roc',
  events:['Documents link Roc\'s bloodline to the Sunken Kingdom: his ancestors were granted maritime authority and the duty to protect what remained', 'Some ancestors protected the surviving descendants; others suppressed the kingdom to avoid political disputes', 'Over time the privileges remained and the responsibilities were forgotten', 'The Sunken Kingdom\'s existence was deliberately erased to prevent conflict with other kingdoms', 'Roc will investigate what responsibilities remain and what can be set right'],
  purpose:['Link Roc\'s inheritance to the Sunken Kingdom', 'Raise the question of responsibility'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Roc\'s Inheritance (5 objectives)', 'Lore: the maritime authority'],
  reward:'Roc\'s inheritance: a privilege and a forgotten duty'},
 179:{ title:'A Crown Without a King', type:'Story Chapter — the Crown\'s origin', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the drowned royal palace',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Maris Aurel, Rin and Roc',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Deep within the Sunken Kingdom, Jade\'s party uncovers the truth about the Drowned Crown. It was not the spirit of a single monarch, but a collective magical construct created by the royal council. The Crown holds the final memories, authority and judgments of the Sunken Kingdom\'s rulers; it was made during the ancient crisis to prevent outsiders from reaching the deepest preservation chamber without understanding why the kingdom had submerged itself. Jade: "So it isn\'t a king\'s ghost... but the royal council\'s final command." Devon: "It was never meant to conquer or destroy. It exists to enforce an ancient command." Sky: "Its defensive behavior was misinterpreted as hostility over the centuries." Later historians classified it among the Fifteen Evils because they did not understand its true purpose. Maris: "The Crown\'s rigid interpretation of its command has prevented even the descendants of the Sunken Kingdom from reclaiming their heritage." Levi: "Its purpose may have been justified..." Jade: "...but its methods have become harmful." Roc: "It follows an ancient command without considering what has changed in the present." To reach the deepest chamber the party must understand the council\'s final command and why the kingdom chose to submerge itself. Devon, holding the pearl: "These are their final memories." Sky: "So many voices... Their fears, their decisions, the weight of what they had to do." Jade: "To move forward, we need to learn the truth. Then we must face what remains: the Trial of the Drowned Court." The Crown guards more than a place: it protects the reason for the kingdom\'s disappearance, a truth the world was not ready to understand.',
  art:'Pages show: the glowing crown over the palace, Jade, Devon, Sky, Maris (teal hair), a hooded dark-cloaked man (read as Roc), Levi and the archer in green. Chapter 177 had the fight against the royal guardians while leaving "is it hostile?" open; this chapter answers it (the Crown is a collective construct enforcing a command, harmful in method but justified in purpose). The page labels a dark-hooded man speaking in the Crown panel: the build reads him as Roc.',
  quote:'"So it isn\'t a king\'s ghost... but the royal council\'s final command." — Jade',
  events:['The Drowned Crown is a collective magical construct made by the royal council, not a single monarch\'s ghost', 'It holds the final memories, authority and judgments of the rulers and enforces an ancient command', 'Later historians classed it among the Fifteen Evils because they did not understand its purpose', 'Its rigid reading of the command keeps even the kingdom\'s descendants from their heritage', 'The party must understand the council\'s final command to reach the deepest chamber'],
  purpose:['Reveal what the Drowned Crown is', 'Set up the Trial of the Drowned Court'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Crown Without a King (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'The Crown is a council\'s final command, not a king\'s ghost'},
 180:{ title:'Trial of the Drowned Court', type:'Story Chapter — the three trials and a Major Story Decision', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the Drowned Court',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Roc, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade, Devon and Roc enter the Drowned Court, the deepest chamber of the Sunken Kingdom, where the royal council\'s final judgment still resonates. Ancient guardians and echoes of the royal council await them. Their trials are not battles, but questions: the same questions that once weighed on the rulers of the Sunken Kingdom when the world forced an impossible choice upon them. Trial One, Duty: "What will you protect when everything is at risk?" Devon: "A ruler must sometimes make difficult choices. But duty should never become cruelty." Trial Two, Sacrifice: "Is one kingdom\'s destruction justified if it ensures another\'s survival?" Sky: "The past believed there was no other way..." Trial Three, Rulership: "When two kingdoms cannot both survive, which one will you choose?" Roc: "Inherited power comes with consequences. But must we repeat the same sacrifices as our ancestors?" Jade: "I refuse to accept that one civilization must be destroyed for another to live. There has to be another way." She investigates the ancient magical mechanisms behind the Crown\'s choice and finds that the council\'s preservation system was designed around limitations that no longer necessarily apply. Sky: "Devon\'s pearl and Sky\'s restoration show that different magical traditions can work together. Perhaps the council never considered a solution like this." Roc: "The council chose to submerge the kingdom to protect something more important than territory. It wasn\'t an end... but a safeguard for the future." Jade: "The original command can still be fulfilled. But it does not require more sacrifices. We can preserve both kingdoms." The Crown: "...For the first time in centuries, the Crown recognizes a different path. Its command can be fulfilled without repeating the tragedies of the past." The Drowned Crown acknowledged Jade\'s solution. The trials had not been tests to find a winner, but to determine whether the present generation could understand the truth the royal council had tried to protect. For the first time in centuries, the possibility of change was permitted.',
  art:'Pages show: the Drowned Court with the Crown, three trial panels (Duty, Sacrifice, Rulership with a golden and a dark kingdom on a scale), Jade, Devon, Sky and Roc speaking, the council\'s spectral rulers, the Crown\'s spirit. The Major Story Decision, "Reject the false choice between sacrificing two kingdoms", has one outcome on the page: the build records the decision as made and has no losing branch. The page names Jade, Devon and Roc at the entrance but shows Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin with them in the group panels. Sky is quoted on Devon\'s pearl in the third person; the build reads it as Sky speaking of Devon and himself.',
  quote:'"I refuse to accept that one civilization must be destroyed for another to live. There has to be another way." — Jade',
  events:['The trials of Duty, Sacrifice and Rulership are questions, not battles', 'Jade refuses the false choice between sacrificing two kingdoms', 'The council\'s preservation design had limits that no longer apply; the pearl and Sky\'s restoration show traditions can work together', 'The Drowned Crown recognizes a different path', 'Major Story Decision: Reject the false choice between sacrificing two kingdoms'],
  purpose:['Resolve what the Crown asks', 'Let Jade\'s judgment break an old assumption'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Trial of the Drowned Court (5 objectives)', 'Major Story Decision made: the false choice is rejected', 'Register: the Drowned Crown\'s classification revised'],
  reward:'The Crown permits change'},
 181:{ title:'The Black Tide Returns', type:'Major Boss — The Black Tide: Corrupted Manifestation', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the restoration chambers and the waters above',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Roc, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Rin and Maris',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Before the deepest archive can be reached, the Black Tide returns: stronger than before, swollen by the corruption gathering around the Sunken Kingdom\'s failing preservation magic. The entity, a vast convergence of corrupted water and fractured memory, attacks both the expedition ships above and the submerged ruins below, its strength multiplied by centuries of accumulated magical damage. Roc: "Hold the line above! Keep the vessels away from the black surge!" Levi: "Rin, left passage! Don\'t let them through!" Rin: "On it! I\'ll keep the creatures off the supports!" Sky: "This corruption is layered over something older... The Tide wasn\'t born evil. It\'s a natural spiritual force that has been twisted by centuries of accumulated magical damage." Devon: "The Pearl is resonating with the barriers... I can stabilize them for now!" Seraphina: "I\'ll protect the chamber. Go: stop the central mass!" Jade: "Defensive positions! Protect the chambers and the ships above!" Devon: "Jade, together!" Jade: "Then we end the corruption... not the truth beneath it." The Black Tide was no simple monster, but a natural force and spiritual phenomenon twisted by centuries of magical damage. It had once been a guardian current, part of the kingdom\'s natural balance. The corruption was never its true nature, but a result of the kingdom\'s wounds. Jade: "So it can still be saved... We just need to remove the corruption." Roc: "Destruction may not be the only answer. If we can reach the truth, there may be a way to restore it." The next battle would determine not just the fate of the Sunken Kingdom, but whether the Black Tide could be returned to what it once was.',
  art:'Pages show: the Black Tide as a vast tendrilled mass over the palace, the expedition ships, Roc and the party, Levi and Rin as two green archers, Sky reading the tide, Devon with the pearl, a golden-white haired woman (Seraphina) shielding crew, Jade with a flaming sword. TWO versions of this page were sent (A: this one; B: a different layout and Black Tide design). Version A is built because its dialogue matches 180 and 182; B is not used. The page calls it a Major Boss, but 182 restores rather than destroys it: the build fights the Manifestation, stabilises it, and resolves it in 182.',
  quote:'"Then we end the corruption... not the truth beneath it." — Jade',
  events:['The Black Tide attacks the expedition ships above and the ruins below', 'Roc holds the ships; Levi and Rin guard the passages; Seraphina protects the chamber', 'Sky: the Tide was not born evil, it is a natural spiritual force twisted by centuries of damage', 'Devon\'s pearl stabilises the barriers', 'Jade: end the corruption, not the truth beneath it', 'Major Boss: The Black Tide: Corrupted Manifestation'],
  purpose:['Show the Black Tide as a corrupted guardian', 'Fight the Manifestation without deciding to kill it'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Black Tide Returns (5 objectives)', 'Register: the Black Tide\'s origin understood'],
  reward:'The Black Tide is a wounded guardian: it can still be saved'},
 182:{ title:'The Black Tide Restored', type:'Story Chapter — the restoration ritual', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the restoration chambers',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin (and an unnamed bearded man)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Black Tide returned once more, sweeping through the submerged city. But this time the party did not come to fight: they came to restore what had been lost. The corruption that had endured for centuries began to fracture as the restoration ritual was prepared, linking the Dragon Pearl, the ancient anchors and the kingdom\'s preservation network. Devon activated the Dragon Pearl, awakening its connection to the preservation network. Sky channeled restorative energy through the ancient network, guiding the Black Tide back to its original spiritual nature. Jade led the defense, protecting the ritual from the remaining corrupted creatures. Its true nature slowly emerged: a natural spiritual guardian twisted by centuries of accumulated magical damage. The corrupted marine creatures gradually returned to their original forms or dispersed, and the unnatural darkness began disappearing from the sea. For the first time in generations the waters around the Sunken Kingdom became calm. Sky: "It was always meant to be protected... not destroyed." The Black Tide has been remembered. Jade updates the Fifteen Register: Black Tide: Restored. Drowned Crown: Reclassified as Preservation Construct. Fifteen Register Progress: 5/15 Cases Resolved. The Black Tide is no longer a source of fear, but once again a guardian of the sea. Its restoration proves that not every entity recorded as an Evil was born a monster. With the waters restored, the Sunken Kingdom can begin a new chapter. The sea is calm. But the investigation is far from over.',
  art:'Pages show: the restored whale-like spirit of light among the ruins, Devon with the pearl, Sky in white-and-blue casting, Jade with a sword, the Register page stamped RESOLVED twice (Black Tide, Restored; Drowned Crown, Reclassified as Preservation Construct), Progress 5/15, and the group in the last panel. An earlier render of this page was replaced by this one (the user regenerated it). The Register lists the Drowned Crown as Resolved too, so the build resolves both Evils here (Evil IV Black Tide: Restored; Evil X Drowned Crown: Reclassified), which is why the count is 5/15 (Thorned Widow, Mourning Hart, Hollow King, Black Tide, Drowned Crown).',
  quote:'"It was always meant to be protected... not destroyed." — Sky',
  events:['Devon activates the pearl; Sky guides the Tide back to its spiritual nature; Jade defends the ritual', 'The Black Tide is restored: a guardian of the sea again', 'The corrupted creatures return to their forms or disperse', 'Register: Black Tide Restored; Drowned Crown Reclassified as Preservation Construct', 'Register progress: 5/15 resolved'],
  purpose:['Resolve the Black Tide without killing it', 'Reclassify the Drowned Crown'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Black Tide Restored (5 objectives)', 'Register: Black Tide Restored; Drowned Crown Reclassified (5/15)'],
  reward:'Black Tide restored. Drowned Crown reclassified. Resolved 5/15'},
 183:{ title:'What the Drowned Crown Guarded', type:'Story Chapter — the deepest archive', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the deepest archive',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Rin, Roc and Maris Aurel',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With the Black Tide restored, the Drowned Crown permits Jade\'s party to enter the deepest archive. Within its depths lie records that have remained sealed for centuries. They find records describing an ancient alliance between Dragonvale, Tribute, the Sunken Kingdom and several civilizations that have since vanished: kingdoms that once maintained diplomatic, maritime and magical connections. Maris carefully examines the original records, including documents her family has sought for generations: "These are real... Our family\'s archives mentioned fragments of this, but I never imagined the full records still existed." The records show Dragonvale, Tribute, the Sunken Kingdom and several other civilizations once formed a maritime alliance, particularly important during the Dima/Xima crisis, when corruption threatened to spread across multiple regions. Devon reviews diplomatic correspondence, naval charts and agreements: "They shared knowledge, resources, and spiritual defense systems... This was far more extensive than any single kingdom. It was a true network." Sky finds records on the preservation network\'s original purpose: "This network was not created for war. It was designed to protect people, knowledge, and spiritual resources from catastrophic corruption." Ancient sea routes connected the kingdoms, allowing the exchange of trade, knowledge and magical support. However, following the ancient crisis the participating kingdoms deliberately severed many of their connections: sea routes were erased, records were altered, certain magical traditions disappeared from public knowledge. The archive does not reveal every reason behind these decisions. Rin studies maps showing erased routes and disconnected territories: "These routes didn\'t just fade naturally. They were deliberately removed from navigation records. Someone wanted these connections forgotten." Jade realizes that the history of Tribute\'s curse cannot be understood by examining Tribute alone: "This changes everything. The Fifteen Register cannot be interpreted in isolation. There were forces at work across multiple kingdoms." Many questions remain: why were the connections severed, who decided which records to alter, and how many other kingdoms were involved? The archive provides answers, but also raises new mysteries that will require further investigation. The knowledge recovered will be added to the Fifteen Register and the royal records of Dragonvale. The Sunken Kingdom was not an isolated tragedy, but part of a larger history. The truth may have been hidden, but it was never lost.',
  art:'Pages show: the deepest archive with Jade, Devon, Sky, Seraphina and the green-clad archer in the first panel, Maris reading, a record panel with the alliance\'s sigils, a map linking Dragonvale, Tribute, the Sunken Kingdom and "other civilizations (since vanished)", Rin reading erased routes, Jade, and an open book of the Sunken Kingdom. NOTE (page text): "they also raise how the Dima/Xima crisis fits": the build records an ancient maritime alliance across kingdoms; the page does not say which vanished civilizations. Some page text has rendering errors ("thiy cbr connections", "undersoided"): read as "their connections" and "understanding".',
  quote:'"The Fifteen Register cannot be interpreted in isolation. There were forces at work across multiple kingdoms." — Jade',
  events:['The Crown permits the party into the deepest archive', 'Records of an ancient alliance between Dragonvale, Tribute, the Sunken Kingdom and vanished civilizations', 'The alliance mattered most during the Dima/Xima crisis', 'The preservation network was built to protect people and knowledge, not for war', 'Routes were erased and records altered after the crisis; the reasons are unrecorded', 'Jade: the Register cannot be read in isolation'],
  purpose:['Reveal the larger history behind the Sunken Kingdom', 'Widen the Register beyond Tribute'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: What the Drowned Crown Guarded (5 objectives)', 'Lore: the ancient alliance and the erased routes'],
  reward:'The Sunken Kingdom was part of a larger history'},
 184:{ title:'The Crown Returns the Pearl', type:'Character Chapter — Devon\'s inheritance', loc:'🌊 The Sunken Kingdom: the restoration chamber',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin (and an unnamed bearded man)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Drowned Crown summons Devon to the ancient restoration chamber. Through the preserved memories of the royal council, he learns that his family\'s possession of the Black Dragon Pearl was never intended to be permanent. His ancestors were entrusted with carrying the artifact until the restoration network was needed again; over generations the responsibility was forgotten, and the pearl became a symbol of royal inheritance rather than a tool of preservation. Devon: "So this... was never meant to stay with my family forever." The pearl was not a possession, but a trust inherited from those who sacrificed their kingdom to preserve something greater. Jade: "You\'ve changed so much since our earlier adventures." Devon: "I understand now. This is not just my inheritance... it is a responsibility." Now that the ancient network has begun awakening, the Crown must decide whether Devon is worthy of continuing that responsibility. The Crown: "Rather than reclaiming the pearl, we return its authority to you. The artifact\'s original purpose has resumed." Devon: "I accept this responsibility." The Crown\'s authority settles into the pearl, and the restoration chamber begins glowing once more.',
  art:'Pages show: the pearl floating inside a halo of light, Devon with the pearl, the council\'s spectral rulers, the Crown\'s spirit speaking, Jade, and the party in the last panel. This chapter comes AFTER 183 although it follows 182 in time: the Crown has already recognised the party and the Tide is restored. The Crown speaks in the first person plural to Devon: the build treats the speaker as the Crown\'s council voice.',
  quote:'"I understand now. This is not just my inheritance... it is a responsibility." — Devon',
  events:['The Crown summons Devon to the restoration chamber', 'The council\'s memories show the pearl was entrusted to his ancestors, never given', 'The Crown returns the pearl\'s authority rather than taking it back', 'Devon accepts the responsibility', 'The restoration chamber glows once more'],
  purpose:['Give Devon\'s pearl its purpose and its duty'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Crown Returns the Pearl (5 objectives)', 'Devon: the pearl\'s authority is restored'],
  reward:'Devon accepts the pearl\'s responsibility'},
 185:{ title:'The Sea Remembers', type:'Arc VII Finale — the restoration of the Sunken Kingdom\'s history', loc:'🌊 Dragonvale and the restored Sunken Kingdom',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Rin, Roc, Maris Aurel, Sally Sin (Sally Sun, her noble name) and Adrian Gold (the epilogue, in Tribute)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With the Black Tide restored and the Drowned Crown\'s true purpose revealed, the Sunken Kingdom\'s history can finally be acknowledged. For centuries the kingdom was remembered only as a warning; now its people may finally be remembered for who they were. Dragonvale\'s royal authorities begin restoring the kingdom to their official historical records: "What was erased will be restored. The Sunken Kingdom will be recorded not as a cautionary tale, but as a true part of our shared history." Roc assists in establishing safe maritime contact with the surviving descendants: "We\'ll open the maritime route gradually. Trade, communication and cultural exchange must be done carefully and under protection." Maris Aurel receives access to records her family spent generations trying to recover: "These are real... Our family\'s records... They survived. At last, we can piece together what truly happened." Sally begins distributing the corrected history through her information network: "We\'ll send the verified records to major ports, archives and scholars. Truth spreads further when more people know it." The ancient maritime route is reopened under careful supervision: monitored vessels, registered crews and established routes will ensure the kingdom remains connected safely this time. Jade prepares her final report for Greyson: "The investigation is complete. I\'ll send the report through the royal channel and include all findings, including the changes about the Fifteen Register." The Fifteen Register now contains five resolved cases. Yet the investigation has revealed something more troubling than the existence of corrupted creatures: the names recorded as Evils do not necessarily describe monsters. Some refer to victims. Some to guardians. Others to magical systems whose original purposes were forgotten. The Register itself may have been shaped by political decisions, historical misunderstandings and deliberate alterations. Before departing Dragonvale, Jade looks toward the restored waters. Not every monster was born a monster. Not every darkness must be destroyed. Some truths were lost with time, but now they can be found again. EPILOGUE, "The Register\'s Impossible Entry" (titled "Final Scene" on the page; the author made it an unnumbered epilogue): some time after Jade\'s report reaches Tribute, Adrian discovers a disturbing inconsistency. While comparing records recovered from the Sunken Kingdom against archives from Tribute and Dragonvale, he finds a name appearing in three separate historical accounts: the dates are identical, the locations are not. Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day. According to the records the same entity was active in three different kingdoms at precisely the same time. Adrian checks the translations, then the original documents, then the dates again. There is no obvious copying error. He immediately sends Jade a message: "Jade, there is a problem with the Register. One of the remaining names has appeared in records from three different kingdoms. At the same time." Jade, reading by moonlight over Dragonvale: TO BE CONTINUED, ARC VIII.',
  art:'Three page images are used: (1) the titled "Chapter 185, The Sea Remembers, Arc VII Finale" page (Dragonvale court, Roc, Maris, Sally, ships, the Register, the Evil?/Victim?/Guardian? sketches); (2) a second, untitled page that repeats the same beats with different art and adds the Greyson-reporting panel with a crowned man and the Main Story Objectives; (3) the "Final Scene: The Register\'s Impossible Entry" page (Adrian with spectacles, three records, a triangle map, the message, Jade in the moonlight, "To be continued: Arc VIII"). The first two repeat Maris, Sally, Roc, the route and the Register panels: the build shows them back to back as pages 1 and 2 and treats the beats once. The user\'s doc says the Arc VII record lists 167 to 185 (19 chapters) with 185 as the final chapter. The Arc VII cast sheet was not swapped in (it omits Seraphina and Eira). Names settled by the author: Roc Chadwick is the alias of Prince Roc Chadstone; Sally Sin is Sally\'s original name, and Sun is read as the surname she took on her adoption into nobility.',
  quote:'"Not every monster was born a monster. Not every darkness must be destroyed." — The close of Arc VII',
  events:['Dragonvale restores the Sunken Kingdom to its official records', 'Roc helps open the maritime route to the surviving descendants, carefully and under protection', 'Maris receives the records her family spent generations seeking', 'Sally spreads the corrected history through her network', 'Jade sends her final report to Greyson through the royal channel', 'The Register: five resolved; its names may describe victims, guardians and forgotten systems, not monsters', 'Final scene: Adrian finds one Register name recorded in three kingdoms at the same moment'],
  purpose:['Close Arc VII', 'Hand the Register\'s doubt and a new mystery to Arc VIII'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Sea Remembers (6 objectives)', 'Main Story Quest: The Register\'s Impossible Entry', 'Arc VII complete'],
  reward:'Arc VII complete. Register 5/15. One name in three kingdoms'},
 186:{ title:'Three Kingdoms, One Name', type:'Story Chapter — Arc VIII begins: the impossible entry', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale and the Tribute archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and Adrian Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Some time after Jade\'s report reaches Tribute, Adrian discovers a disturbing inconsistency in the records. While comparing records from the Sunken Kingdom against archives from Tribute and Dragonvale, he finds a name appearing in three separate historical accounts. The dates are identical; the locations are not. According to the records, the same entity was active in three different kingdoms at precisely the same time. Adrian checks the translations, then the original documents, then the dates again. There is no obvious copying error. He immediately sends Jade a message: "Jade, there is a problem with the Register. One of the remaining names has appeared in records from three different kingdoms. At the same time." The message reaches Jade as she reviews the latest findings from the Sunken Kingdom. Jade: "Three kingdoms... And the same name?" The Register\'s impossible entry has been discovered. But this is only the beginning: if the same name appears in three kingdoms, what else is hidden in the records?',
  art:'Pages show: a fleet of sailing ships at sunset (opening panel), Adrian in spectacles and a navy-and-gold robe, three record cards (Tribute, Dragonvale, Sunken Kingdom, each dated "Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day"), Adrian\'s message at 21:14, Jade reading it, and Jade with a dark-haired man (read as Devon) before a glowing map of the world. This chapter retells the epilogue that is page 3 of chapter 185 (same scenes, same message), now as a numbered chapter. DATE: the author\'s canon is Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day; the page image itself still reads "Year 412, 7th Moon" and needs regenerating.',
  quote:'"Jade, there is a problem with the Register." — Adrian',
  events:['Adrian finds one name in three accounts: Tribute, Dragonvale and the Sunken Kingdom', 'The dates are identical and the locations are not', 'Translations, originals and dates are checked: no obvious copying error', 'Adrian messages Jade; she reads it while reviewing the Sunken Kingdom findings', 'The Register\'s impossible entry is discovered'],
  purpose:['Open Arc VIII with the impossible entry', 'Hand the mystery to Jade'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Three Kingdoms, One Name (5 objectives)', 'Register: the Impossible Entry is open'],
  reward:'The impossible entry is discovered'},
 187:{ title:'The Scholar\'s Warning', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian\'s report', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, Rin and Adrian Gold',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After receiving Adrian\'s message, Jade requests a detailed explanation. Later that evening Adrian sends his full report, including translations and original documents. Adrian continues his examination of the historical records from the three kingdoms: "The dates match. The translations are accurate. And the original documents confirm it." The same name appears in all three accounts, recorded on the exact same date (Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day) but in three different locations. He verifies the translations himself in multiple languages and checks the original documents whenever possible: "There is no evidence of copying. The writing styles, calendar systems, and historical contexts are all consistent with each kingdom\'s records." Each record describes the same entity or event, but with different details and from different perspectives. The descriptions do not align, and the locations should be impossible. Adrian searches for additional references in other historical sources, including private archives and diplomatic records: "There is no obvious explanation. But this cannot be a coincidence." If the Register can contain entries that appear in multiple kingdoms at the same time, the remaining names may be more complex than previously assumed. "I should inform Jade immediately. This may change how we approach the remaining entries in the Register." Jade reads Adrian\'s full report, including the translations and document copies: "Three kingdoms. The same date. Different locations. This is bigger than we expected." She calls a meeting with the party to discuss the findings and determine the next steps: "We need to understand what this name really is, and why it appears in three different kingdoms at the same time." The impossible entry suggests that the Fifteen Register may contain linked events, shared identities, or historical figures whose records were deliberately altered. The party prepares to investigate further.',
  art:'Pages show: a Tribute-like skyline at dusk (opening), Adrian in a green-and-gold robe studying the records, three record cards dated "Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day" (Tribute, Dragonvale, Sunken Kingdom), Jade reading the report, and the party meeting around a table at sunset (Jade, Devon, Sky, Seraphina, Levi and a green-clad archer). DATE MISMATCH: ch185 and ch186 say "Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day"; this chapter and 188-190 say "Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day". The build shows the later date once ch187 is reached.',
  quote:'"Three kingdoms. The same date. Different locations. This is bigger than we expected." — Jade',
  events:['Adrian verifies the translations in several languages: the dates match and the originals confirm them', 'The writing styles, calendars and contexts are consistent with each kingdom: no copying', 'Each record describes the same entity or event from a different angle; the locations should be impossible', 'Adrian: the remaining names may be more complex than assumed', 'Jade reads the report and calls the party together', 'The Register may hold linked events, shared identities or figures whose records were altered'],
  purpose:['Prove the records are genuine', 'Make the party commit to investigating'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Scholar\'s Warning (5 objectives)', 'Register mark: the Impossible Entry is Verified'],
  reward:'The three records are genuine'},
 188:{ title:'A Name Without a Body', type:'Story Chapter — the party examines the records', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin (and an unnamed bearded man)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following Adrian\'s report, Jade and the party begin a detailed investigation into the Register entry that appears in three kingdoms at the same time. The party gathers to examine the three records sent by Adrian. The same name appears in records from Tribute, Dragonvale and the Sunken Kingdom, all dated Year 712, 3rd Month, 14th Day. The descriptions vary, but all three accounts refer to the same entity: in Tribute it is "a visitor who arrived without escorts"; in Dragonvale it is "recorded as a natural phenomenon witnessed near the northern border"; in the Sunken Kingdom it is "mentioned as a figure associated with a ritual at the coastal ruins." Jade: "The dates match, but the locations are completely different. It cannot be the same person in all three places... at the same time. The contexts are too different to be a simple case of copied records. We need to understand what each kingdom believed they witnessed." Devon: "It could be a linked event. A single occurrence that was recorded differently depending on the kingdom\'s perspective." Levi: "Or it could be a title, a position, or even a phenomenon that appears in different forms. We shouldn\'t assume it\'s a person yet." Sky: "If it\'s a natural phenomenon, we should look at environmental records from that year. Weather, tides, seismic activity, anything unusual." Seraphina: "If it\'s a title or role, we should examine political records. Someone may have used the same name for different purposes in each kingdom." An unnamed dark-haired bearded man: "And if it\'s something else entirely... then the Register may be recording more than just individual creatures." The party examines the original documents, focusing on the descriptions and surrounding events. Each record uses different terminology; the locations are hundreds of miles apart. And yet the date is identical. There is no evidence that the accounts were copied from one another. The more they investigate, the more it seems that the name\'s presence in three kingdoms was intentional, or part of a larger, hidden pattern. The question is no longer whether the records are accurate. The question is what this name truly represents, and why it appeared in three different kingdoms at the same time. Jade: "This is not an ordinary entry. We need to find out whether these three accounts are connected by a common event, a shared figure, or something much larger." "Whatever the truth is, it\'s beyond what we expected. We will need to look deeper, into history, politics, and perhaps even the nature of the Register itself."',
  art:'Pages show: the party around the three records (Jade, Devon, Seraphina in white, Levi, and Sky in blue), the three record cards with a description under each ("Described as a visitor who arrived without escorts" / "Recorded as a natural phenomenon witnessed near the northern border" / "Mentioned as a figure associated with a ritual at the coastal ruins"), close-ups of each speaker, the original documents and a star chart, and the party on a balcony at dusk with a green-clad archer and a bearded dark-haired man. The bearded man speaks the "something else entirely" line and appears in the group panels. AUTHOR\'S DECISION: he is not canonised as Roc (Roc is not back in Jade\'s travelling party); his identity is left unassigned. The page does not name the entity (the "name" is not given).',
  quote:'"The question is no longer whether the records are accurate. The question is what this name truly represents." — Jade',
  events:['Three accounts: a visitor without escorts (Tribute), a natural phenomenon near the northern border (Dragonvale), a figure at a ritual at the coastal ruins (Sunken Kingdom)', 'Hypotheses: a linked event (Devon), a title or phenomenon (Levi), environmental records (Sky), political records (Seraphina), the Register records more than creatures', 'Each record uses different terminology and the places are hundreds of miles apart; the date is identical', 'No evidence the accounts were copied: the shared presence looks intentional or part of a larger pattern', 'The question becomes what the name represents'],
  purpose:['Frame the mystery as a question of what the name is', 'Give each companion a hypothesis'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Name Without a Body (6 objectives)', 'Register mark: the Impossible Entry is Contradictory'],
  reward:'The three accounts disagree about what the name is'},
 189:{ title:'Beyond the Three Kingdoms', type:'Story Chapter — a lead beyond the three kingdoms', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin; Adrian Gold accompanies the investigation (temporarily); an unnamed bearded man',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following their initial analysis, the party digs deeper into the mysterious entry in the Fifteen Register, looking for connections that could explain how the same name appears in Tribute, Dragonvale and the Sunken Kingdom at the same time. The party gathers to review their findings and discuss possible explanations. Jade: "The same name. The same date. Three kingdoms." A companion: "It cannot be coincidence. There must be a reason why this entry appears in all three records at the same time." The descriptions match in name and date, but the contexts are different in each kingdom. Adrian examines the original documents and translations again, checking for errors in language, dating systems and historical context: "The translations are accurate. The calendar systems have been cross-checked. And the writing styles match each kingdom\'s own records." Sky: "If it\'s the same person, they must have travelled to all three kingdoms within the same time period. That would require extraordinary means, even for someone with powerful magic or connections." An unnamed bearded man: "Or the same name could refer to different people, possibly related by blood, position or title. We shouldn\'t assume it\'s a single individual. There could be a shared identity, a ceremonial title, or a deliberate use of the same name." Seraphina: "The entries describe different events: a visitor, a natural phenomenon, and a ritual figure. Perhaps the same person appeared in different forms or roles, or was recorded from different perspectives." Levi: "We should also check private archives, trade logs and traveller accounts. Official records can be altered, but personal records are harder to change." An unnamed bearded man: "If this is connected to political movements, it may explain why the records appear in all three kingdoms. It could be a person, a group, or an organization operating across borders." The party lists possible areas to investigate further: neutral maritime archives, independent scholarly organizations, nearby kingdoms and trade cities, religious or cultural records, and private collections and family archives. One promising lead is a neutral trade city known for keeping records from multiple kingdoms, including those that were later erased elsewhere. It may contain information that was not influenced by the political changes of Tribute, Dragonvale or the Sunken Kingdom. Jade: "We need to understand what this name really means, and why it appears in three different kingdoms at the same time. Let\'s go there next." The investigation now moves beyond the three kingdoms, as the party follows new leads that may reveal a larger history connecting them all. The name in the Fifteen Register may be more than a single entry: it could be a key to a deeper truth about the past, and the forces that still shape the present.',
  art:'Pages show: the party reviewing findings (Jade, Adrian in a green robe with a topknot, Sky, Levi), the three record cards (same descriptions as ch188), close-ups of Adrian, Sky, an unnamed bearded man, Seraphina, Levi and the bearded man again, a list of areas to investigate, a neutral trade city on a bay at dusk, and the party on a balcony. The "ritual figure" wording is Seraphina\'s: the Sunken Kingdom\'s account. The trade city is not named in this chapter (named Haiyue Port in 190). The page text has typos ("shoud", "Ye:") read as "should" and "Yet:". Adrian accompanies the investigation temporarily as the Royal Scholar (the author\'s decision); he is not a party member.',
  quote:'"We need to understand what this name really means." — Jade',
  events:['Adrian re-checks languages, calendars and writing styles: all accurate', 'If it is one person they travelled three kingdoms at once; or different people sharing a name, a title or a role', 'Possible shared identity, ceremonial title, organisation or political movement across borders', 'The party lists leads: neutral maritime archives, scholarly organisations, nearby cities, religious records, private collections', 'A neutral trade city holds records from several kingdoms, including erased ones: the party will go there'],
  purpose:['Widen the investigation beyond the three kingdoms', 'Choose the neutral trade city as the next lead'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beyond the Three Kingdoms (6 objectives)', 'Lead: a neutral trade city that keeps erased records'],
  reward:'A neutral trade city may hold what was erased'},
 190:{ title:'Traces Across the Water', type:'Story Chapter — the lead to Haiyue Port', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale harbour',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Seraphina and Rin; Adrian Gold accompanies the investigation (temporarily); an unnamed bearded man',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With a possible lead identified, the party begins to investigate the connections between the Fifteen Register, maritime trade, and the missing records that once linked the three kingdoms at the same time. The party gathers again to plan their next steps, reviewing their findings from the three records and the new lead. The trade city seems to appear in all three records, but the roles and descriptions are different. In Tribute\'s records it is Haiyue Port (Sea-Moon Port): a trade hub and neutral city, recording merchant fleets and cultural exchanges. In Dragonvale\'s records it is Moonreach (Moon Bridge): a strategic trading post, with mentions of restricted cargo and closed ledgers. In the Sunken Kingdom\'s records it is Yueluo (Moon Anchorage): a sacred port, referenced in ritual texts as the meeting place of three tides. The name appears with different spellings and titles in each kingdom\'s records, suggesting a place of strategic importance. Jade: "If the same place is recorded so differently, there must be a reason. It could be linked to the missing entries." Adrian compares the linguistic differences and historical contexts, looking for clues in translation choices, titles and calendar references: "The name may refer to the same city, but it was seen very differently by each kingdom." Sky: "Some of the ships listed in the Tribute records match shipping patterns from Dragonvale. But the destinations were altered or omitted in later copies." Levi: "That could mean something happened at this trade city that was deliberately hidden. We need to find out what was being traded, and who was involved." Seraphina: "The ritual references are particularly interesting. They suggest the city was also a place of ceremony, not just trade. If it linked all three kingdoms, it might have been used for more than commercial purposes." The bearded man: "We should also consider the people who controlled the port. A neutral trade city still needs someone to manage it. If there was a shared council, merchant guild, or independent rulers, their records might still exist." Jade: "We also need to look for records outside the official channels. Private merchant logs, family archives and travel journals might contain details that were left out of the main records." The party lists possible sources and contacts: neutral merchant guilds, independent trade families, maritime archives and ship logs, nearby kingdoms and allied cities, scholarly organizations, private collections and personal journals. The next step is to travel to Haiyue Port, to gather more information and see what remains of the city\'s records. The party prepares for the journey, arranging supplies, contacts and a route that avoids drawing unnecessary attention. Before they leave, Adrian makes detailed notes and copies of the relevant entries from the three records, so the party can compare them on the journey. As the sun sets, the party leaves the current city behind and sets sail towards Haiyue Port, the first major lead beyond the three kingdoms. Jade: "This may be the key to understanding how the same name appears in Tribute, Dragonvale, and the Sunken Kingdom, and what really happened there."',
  art:'Pages show: the party at the table, the three record cards (Tribute: Haiyue Port (Sea-Moon Port); Dragonvale: Moonreach (Moon Bridge); Sunken Kingdom: Yueluo (Moon Anchorage)), close-ups of Adrian, Sky, Levi, Seraphina, the bearded man and Jade, a list of sources, a harbour at sunset with ships, Adrian writing copies, and the party sailing. The chapter\'s speakers use "the name" for both the entity and the city: the build reads the three place-names as the same port under three spellings, and keeps the entity\'s name unrevealed. Adrian stays with the party until they sail and copies the records for the journey; he accompanies the investigation temporarily. Haiyue Port is a new location that the next chapter will use: the build records it as the lead and does not open it yet.',
  quote:'"This may be the key to understanding how the same name appears in Tribute, Dragonvale, and the Sunken Kingdom." — Jade',
  events:['The records name a trade city three ways: Haiyue Port, Moonreach and Yueluo', 'Ships in the Tribute records match Dragonvale\'s patterns, but destinations were altered or omitted in later copies', 'The city may also have been a ritual place linking three kingdoms', 'The port\'s rulers or guilds may still keep records; private merchant logs, family archives and journals are the next sources', 'Adrian copies the records; the party sails for Haiyue Port'],
  purpose:['Turn the neutral trade city into a destination', 'Mark the records as altered'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Traces Across the Water (6 objectives)', 'Lead: Haiyue Port', 'Register mark: the Impossible Entry is Deliberately Altered'],
  reward:'The first lead beyond the three kingdoms: Haiyue Port'},
 191:{ title:'A Lady\'s Return', time:'flashback', type:'Story Chapter — Sally\'s return to society and her marriage (a flashback / retelling; the author says 192 onward is the present)', loc:'🏯 The royal court: the social gathering and the wedding',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Sally Sun (Sin) and Lucien Marroway',
  introduced:['Lucien Marroway (a respected nobleman)'],
  sum:'After the turmoil of the past, Sally\'s return to aristocratic society is met with both curiosity and quiet respect. Once a courtesan, she is now a woman of restored status, and this time it is by her own choice. Dressed in an elegant gown and with her head held high, Sally attends the royal court\'s social gathering once again. This time she is no longer a guest of the night: she is a lady of the realm. The noble families welcome her warmly. Many had heard of her past, but it is her grace, maturity and quiet strength that silences the old whispers. A noble: "Lady Sally, your return is a blessing to the court. We are all honoured to see you again." It is here that Sally is formally introduced to Lucien Marroway, a respected nobleman known for his integrity, diplomatic skills and quiet kindness. Their meeting is not a chance encounter, but the result of months of quiet conversations and growing trust. Lucien does not treat her as a fallen woman, but as a partner, a woman with a past and a future, and a heart that deserves happiness. Lucien: "I do not wish to be the man who saves you, Lady Sally. I simply hope to walk beside you... as an equal." Sally: "Then let us build a future together. Not out of obligation, but by choice." Their wedding is a union of respect, trust and love, a new chapter for both of them. Lucien: "From today forward, you are my wife, Sally Marroway." Sally: "And you are my husband, Lucien." Sally\'s past had once been written by others. Now she writes her own story as a wife, a noblewoman, and a woman who chose her own tomorrow. Her marriage to Lucien Marroway marked not only her personal redemption, but also a sign to the court that the past did not define her. She was no longer a shadow of scandal, but a lady of influence, grace and purpose. For Sally, it was not the end of her journey but the beginning of the life she had always deserved. And for Lucien, it was the greatest honour of his life to stand beside her.',
  art:'Pages show: a castle by the sea (opening), Sally in a lilac gown at the royal court\'s gathering, Lucien Marroway (dark hair, navy and gold coat), the wedding in a stained-glass hall (Sally in red and gold with a veil), a sealed invitation, and the couple on a balcony at sunset. The chapter does not name the kingdom or the date: it is the wedding the game\'s time-sensitive events now anchor to (ch191). Lucien\'s public standing is shown as integrity, diplomatic skill and quiet kindness (the dossier\'s \'public standing\').',
  quote:'"I do not wish to be the man who saves you, Lady Sally. I simply hope to walk beside you... as an equal." — Lucien Marroway',
  events:['Sally returns to the court as a lady of the realm', 'The noble families welcome her; her grace silences the old whispers', 'Sally is formally introduced to Lucien Marroway, a respected nobleman known for integrity, diplomacy and quiet kindness', 'Months of quiet conversations and growing trust', 'The wedding: Sally Marroway', 'Her marriage is a sign to the court that the past does not define her'],
  purpose:['Show Sally\'s restored status and her marriage', 'Present Lucien Marroway\'s public standing'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Lady\'s Return (4 objectives)', 'Sally is Lady Marroway: the Marroway case begins'],
  reward:'Sally marries Lucien Marroway'},
 192:{ title:'An Evening at the Tavern', type:'Story Chapter — a rare evening of rest', loc:'🏮 A familiar tavern in Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Sally and Levi',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With the investigation ongoing, the party takes a rare evening of rest at a familiar tavern in Dragonvale (the page text says Tribute; the author says Dragonvale). They did not expect to see a well-known face there. The tavern is livelier than usual, filled with nobles, merchants and travellers. Laughter, music and the clatter of cups create a welcome break from their recent investigations. Jade: "It\'s been a while since we had a proper meal like this." A companion: "A chance to rest doesn\'t happen often." Their evening is interrupted when a familiar figure enters the tavern with a small entourage: Lady Sally Sun, formerly Sally Sin, returns to public life after her recent marriage, her presence drawing attention across the tavern. She is accompanied only by her handmaiden, not her husband. Sally\'s appearance is striking, but different from before: her hair is now worn down, her robes more elegant and free, a reflection of her new position and the freedom she now has. Levi Stanson is also present, having arrived separately. His gaze lingers on Sally, though his expression reveals little. Sally: "It\'s been a long time. So much has changed. But tonight, let\'s simply enjoy the evening, yes?" After some time, Jade, Devon and Sky take their leave, deciding to return to rest and continue their discussions later. Jade: "Take care. We\'ll continue tomorrow." Devon: "Enjoy your evening, Sally." Sally watches them go with a small, thoughtful smile. "Thank you, Jade. You too, Devon and Sky. Rest well." With the others gone, the evening continues, and the conversation between Levi and Sally takes a different turn. Levi: "It really has been a long time, hasn\'t it? Shall we talk?" As the evening continues, old connections and new questions resurface, reminding them that even moments of rest can reveal unexpected information. What begins as a chance encounter may lead to new clues about the past, and the true nature of those around them.',
  art:'Pages show: a lantern-lit tavern on a river at night (opening), Jade in red, Devon with a fur collar, Sky with blue hair and a black-haired man (read as Levi\'s table companion; the text says Levi arrived separately), Sally in purple with her hair down and her handmaiden, Levi close up, and the party leaving. \'Lady Sally Sun, formerly Sally Sin\' is canon for the noble name. The page text says "a familiar tavern in Tribute", but the author says the chapter is in Dragonvale (after the Sunken Crown, with Roc and Delilah back at the palace): the build places it in Dragonvale. Sally is married (\'her recent marriage\') yet alone with her handmaiden. NOTE: this is a tavern scene between Levi and Sally while she is still married; the game\'s separate post-divorce \'one drink\' scene (ch176+) is kept as a different, later moment: the author to confirm.',
  quote:'"It\'s been a long time. So much has changed. But tonight, let\'s simply enjoy the evening, yes?" — Sally',
  events:['The party takes a rare evening of rest at a tavern in Dragonvale', 'Lady Sally Sun, formerly Sally Sin, arrives with her handmaiden, without her husband', 'Levi is also there, arrived separately; his gaze lingers on Sally', 'Jade, Devon and Sky leave; Levi and Sally keep talking', 'Old connections and new questions resurface'],
  purpose:['Reintroduce Sally and Levi in the present', 'Open the thread the handmaiden will voice in ch193'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: An Evening at the Tavern (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sally and Levi talk again'},
 193:{ title:'The Handmaiden\'s Concern', type:'Story Chapter — a quiet conversation', loc:'🏮 A tavern in Dragonvale, late at night',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Sally Sun, her handmaiden and Levi (seen)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the lively evening, when the others had left, Sally remained a little longer at the tavern with her handmaiden. Away from the larger crowd, the cheerful atmosphere gave way to a quieter, more honest conversation. Her handmaiden, who had been with her since before the marriage, finally spoke when they were away from the rest of the party. Handmaiden: "Lady Sally... may I speak freely?" Sally: "Of course. You always may." Handmaiden: "I cannot help but worry about Levi Stanson. He was here tonight, and the way he looked at you... it felt different from before. Has something happened between you two?" Levi Stanson has returned to Tribute with his own purpose. His expression was composed, almost distant, yet there were moments when his gaze lingered on Sally longer than necessary. Handmaiden: "He did not join our table, but I could feel his presence. It made me uneasy, Lady Sally. I am afraid he might still hold feelings for you. Or that others might misunderstand, given your past connection." Sally: "I understand your concern. But please do not worry. Levi and I are from different paths now. I am Lady Sun, and my life is my own to choose. I will remain polite and gracious, but I will not allow the past to define my future." Handmaiden: "Still... men like Levi do not give up easily. He is noble, skilled and respected. If he decides to pursue you again, would it not cause trouble for you and Lord Marroway?" Sally: "If that happens, I will handle it. I am not the timid girl I once was. I have my own position, my own voice, and people who respect me for who I am now." Handmaiden: "I will always be honest with you, Lady Sally. It is my duty to protect you." Sally: "You have always stood by me. That is enough. Thank you. Your concern means a lot to me. No matter what comes next, we will face it together." Their conversation continues late into the night, about the past, the present, and the uncertainties ahead. Even in times of new beginnings, old connections and unanswered questions still cast their shadows. For Sally, this evening is a reminder that freedom comes with its own challenges, and that trust and understanding with those closest to her will be just as important as facing the truths of the past.',
  art:'Pages show: Sally in purple with her handmaiden at the table, Levi (with a quiver) in a close-up, and the tavern\'s river at night. Levi\'s feelings and Sally\'s answer here are stated directly: Sally says she and Levi \'are from different paths now\' and calls herself \'Lady Sun\'. This is a conversation, no romance happens; the game keeps the Levi and Sally bond a quiet one (no romance track).',
  quote:'"I am Lady Sun, and my life is my own to choose." — Sally',
  events:['Sally\'s handmaiden asks to speak freely about Levi', 'She fears Levi still holds feelings for Sally, or that others will misunderstand', 'Sally: they are from different paths now; she will not let the past define her future', 'The handmaiden pledges honesty and protection', 'The conversation continues late into the night'],
  purpose:['Establish where Sally and Levi stand', 'Show the handmaiden\'s loyalty and Sally\'s resolve'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Handmaiden\'s Concern (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sally: freedom has its own challenges'},
 194:{ title:'The Price of Obedience', type:'Story Chapter — a village under Marroway House', loc:'🏘️ A village under the authority of Marroway House',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and the party',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While following up on new information, Jade\'s party visits a nearby village under the authority of Marroway House. What they find is a place living in quiet fear, and people paying a heavy price for obedience. The village appears orderly at first, but the atmosphere feels wrong. Soldiers bearing the Marroway insignia watch the people closely. Villager: "Please... we have already paid the levy. There is nothing left." Jade: "Who collects these levies? Is it Marroway House?" Villager: "Yes, my lady. It is for \'road maintenance\' and \'security\', they say. But the roads are broken, and the soldiers only take more. But they still take our grain... and our children for labour. If we refuse, there are punishments." Devon: "This is more than a simple tax. It is extraction, and it is systematic." Sky: "These people are afraid to speak openly. Someone has made an example of those who resisted." A companion: "The records we saw in the town match this. Marroway controls the supply routes, the grain stores, and the labour. This is not just local greed. It looks like a wider network. There is also increased movement of goods at the docks. Grain, timber... and people." A mother holds her child: "They said my son would work for the house for one season... It has been two years. We have not heard from him since." Jade: "This is the same pattern we saw in the previous town. Different villages, but the same methods: levies, forced labour, disappearances. Marroway\'s influence runs deeper than we thought." Devon: "We should continue our investigation. If this is a wider pattern, there may be more victims, and stronger forces behind it." A companion: "Sally trusted Marroway. But if this is what his house does to these people... there may be more that she does not know." Jade: "For now, we will gather more evidence quietly. These people are already suffering. We must be careful not to put them in greater danger."',
  art:'Pages show: a village at night under red banners with Marroway soldiers, villagers pleading with Jade, Devon (fur collar), Sky (blue hair), a green-ribboned archer and Jade again; a mother and child (\'It has been two years\'). Which companion speaks the archer\'s lines (the records, the docks, \'Sally trusted Marroway\') is not captioned: it may be the \'Carly\' of ch195 or Rin or Levi: flagged. This is the party\'s own discovery of Marroway House\'s levies, forced labour and disappearances, while Sally (in this chapter) still trusts him.',
  quote:'"This is more than a simple tax. It is extraction, and it is systematic." — Devon',
  events:['A village under Marroway House: levies for \'road maintenance\' and \'security\', grain and children taken for labour', 'Punishments for those who refuse; someone made an example of the resisters', 'Marroway controls the supply routes, the grain stores and the labour; movement of grain, timber and people at the docks', 'A boy taken for \'one season\' two years ago has not been heard of since', 'The same methods as the previous town: a wider pattern', 'Jade: gather evidence quietly, without endangering the villagers; Sally may not know'],
  purpose:['Show the cost of Marroway House\'s rule', 'Make it the party\'s investigation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Price of Obedience (5 objectives)', 'Evidence: the levies'],
  reward:'Marroway House\'s levies and forced labour are exposed'},
 195:{ title:'Beneath a Noble Name', type:'Story Chapter — Carly documents what they have learned', loc:'🏘️ The villages and docks under Marroway House',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Carly, Jade and the villagers',
  introduced:['Carly (Sally\'s trusted handmaiden, named in ch198)'],
  sum:'While Levi spends more time with Sally, Carly quietly begins to document what they have learned. Behind the respected name of Marroway House, a different reality is starting to emerge. Carly reviews the accounts from the village and compares them with older trade records and shipping routes. "The taxes are far higher than what is recorded in the official levy tables... and these goods are not reaching the capital at all." What the villagers described matches what Carly sees at the docks: extra levies, diverted goods, and harsh enforcement by Marroway\'s men. The people speak cautiously, fearing punishment if they are found to have talked. Villager: "If we complain, he will take our land..." A mother with her daughter: "Last season, three families disappeared after refusing to pay the new levy..." Carly collects every detail she can, names, dates, locations and witness accounts, and records them in a separate journal: "It is not just isolated incidents. This is a pattern. If I can gather enough evidence, this could support a formal investigation." She cross-references the information with trade manifests, supply ledgers and shipping schedules. Some of the shipments listed as \'grain for the capital\' never left the region. Carly also notes the names of key enforcers, storage sites and intermediaries who seem to be involved: "These warehouse marks... they match the ones at the eastern docks. So the goods are being rerouted through Marroway\'s private stores." She knows she must be careful. For now, she keeps her investigation quiet and shares only the necessary details with Jade and the others. Carly informs Jade of her progress, and they agree to continue gathering information discreetly while remaining in the region a little longer. Jade: "We need more before we present this. If we move too soon, the evidence may disappear. But we cannot ignore what the people are suffering either. Thank you, Carly. Your work is important." Carly: "I will continue. There are still gaps, but the picture is becoming clearer." Carly makes a final note for the night, reminding herself of why this matters: "Behind a noble name, there are people whose voices are not heard. If we can bring the truth to light, perhaps their lives can change." As the night ends, the signs of Marroway\'s power remain visible throughout the region, in the banners, the guards, and the fear in the people\'s eyes. But beneath that power, a different story is taking shape. Carly\'s investigation has only begun, and what lies ahead may reveal far more than they expected.',
  art:'Pages show: a woman in a green-and-gold robe with green ribbons (named \'Carly\' in the text) reading levy tables and trade records, Marroway\'s soldiers at the docks, villagers, a notebook of sketched warehouses, Jade with a green-ribboned woman, and red Marroway banners with a horse emblem. \'Carly\' is a NEW NAME: she is not introduced anywhere earlier. She looks like the green-ribboned archer of ch194 (the game\'s Rin Kaede dresses this way) and acts as the party\'s investigator; the build records her as \'Carly\' exactly as written and does not decide who she is: the author to confirm (Rin? a new ally?). The text opens \'While Levi spends more time with Sally\' (the party and Levi are apart).',
  quote:'"Behind a noble name, there are people whose voices are not heard." — Carly',
  events:['Carly compares the village accounts with trade records and shipping routes: the levies are far higher than recorded and the goods do not reach the capital', 'Villagers fear punishment; three families disappeared last season after refusing the new levy', 'She records names, dates, locations and witness accounts in a separate journal', 'Shipments listed as \'grain for the capital\' never left the region; the warehouse marks match the eastern docks: goods are rerouted to Marroway\'s private stores', 'She keeps the investigation quiet and shares only what is needed with Jade', 'Jade: more evidence before they present it; the evidence may disappear if they move too soon'],
  purpose:['Show the evidence being built', 'Make the pattern a formal case'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beneath a Noble Name (5 objectives)', 'Evidence: diverted goods and Marroway\'s private stores'],
  reward:'A pattern: the grain never reached the capital'},
 196:{ title:'A Woman\'s Testimony', type:'Story Chapter — a survivor speaks', loc:'🏮 A tavern room by the river',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Carly (shown as Sally), her handmaiden and a protected witness',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With enough background information in hand, Carly seeks first-hand testimony. A survivor agrees to speak, on the condition that her identity remains protected. That night, Carly and her handmaiden meet a woman who had once worked at a supply warehouse under Marroway\'s control. The woman is clearly frightened, looking over her shoulder several times before speaking. Woman: "I... I can speak, but please... do not use my real name. If it is discovered that I talked, they will not only punish me, but my family too. We were told the grain shipments were for the capital, but many of the goods were diverted elsewhere. When we asked questions, we were beaten or dismissed. Some of the women who refused to comply were sent away... and we never saw them again." Carly: "Did you see who gave the orders?" Woman: "It always came from Marroway House, through their stewards and military officers. They said it was a noble order, and that disobedience would be treated as treason. There were also new levies. Families were forced to give more labour, including children. Those who could not pay were marked and taken for \'other services\'... Please. I do not want my name to be written. My family is still here." Carly: "You have done a brave thing telling me this. Your identity will remain protected. I will record this carefully, but your name will not be included." Carly notes every detail: dates, locations, names of stewards, shipment routes, and the condition of the people. Carly: "There are others who may be willing to talk, but they are afraid. We must be careful. Marroway\'s men have informants even among the common people." Woman: "Thank you for trusting me." Carly: "There are still many we need to speak to. We will proceed quietly, and with care." One testimony alone is not enough, but it confirms a darker truth. Behind Marroway\'s noble name lies a network of exploitation, intimidation, and silence. Carly will continue gathering voices, so they are no longer lost in the shadows.',
  art:'Pages show: two women in lilac and white (the images look like Sally and her handmaiden, while the text says \'Carly and her handmaiden\'), a hooded woman in tears, a notebook, a river at night. NAME MISMATCH: the captions say Carly, the pictures show Sally (purple robe, flowers in her hair) with her handmaiden; the build keeps the caption name \'Carly\' and records the doubt. The witness is anonymous: she asks that her name never be written. Direct witness, anonymous.',
  quote:'"Please... do not use my real name. If it is discovered that I talked, they will not only punish me, but my family too." — the witness',
  events:['A survivor who once worked at a Marroway-controlled supply warehouse agrees to speak, anonymously', 'The grain for the capital was diverted; questions were met with beatings', 'Women who refused were sent away and never seen again; children were taken under new levies for \'other services\'', 'Orders came from Marroway House through its stewards and military officers, and disobedience was called treason', 'Carly records every detail but not the witness\'s name', 'Marroway\'s men have informants among the common people'],
  purpose:['Give the case a first-hand voice', 'Show why witnesses need protection'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Woman\'s Testimony (5 objectives)', 'Evidence: the first testimony (anonymous, direct)'],
  reward:'The first testimony against Marroway House'},
 197:{ title:'The Marroway Ledger', type:'Story Chapter — the household ledger', loc:'🏯 Marroway House: the household offices',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Carly (shown as Sally) and her handmaiden',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following the woman\'s testimony, Carly gains access to a set of household and trade records connected to Marroway\'s operations. What they find paints a darker picture than expected. The records are kept separately from the main trade ledgers, hidden in a side storeroom beneath the household offices. Handmaiden: "Are you sure these are from Marroway House?" Carly: "Yes. The seal, the format... and look at these names." The ledgers show regular payments labelled as "escort fees," "protection," and "labour relocation", but the amounts do not match the recorded shipments. "These are not normal transport costs. The goods recorded should not require this much payment. And these names... they match the villages we visited. The same month the levies increased, there are also payments listed here." Some payments are made to local enforcers, while others go to individuals outside the region. Several entries are marked with coded notes, likely referring to people rather than goods. "These terms are suspicious. \'Relocation,\' \'transfer,\' \'special handling\'... It looks like people were being moved, and not voluntarily." The household accounts also include unusual expenses: payments to officials, large sums to unknown recipients, and records that have been deliberately altered. "Some of these entries have been crossed out, but the original writing is still visible. Someone tried to hide this." Carly and her handmaiden carefully copy the key information, aware that they may not have long before the missing records are noticed. "We should make copies and keep them in separate places. If they realise these are missing, they might destroy the rest." The more she reads, the clearer it becomes that this is not just about extra taxes. It is a network of intimidation, exploitation and the quiet removal of people who resist. "This goes deeper than we thought. These records prove it wasn\'t isolated incidents. It\'s systematic." Carly selects the most important pages to copy: payment lists, names, dates, warehouse locations and notes that link the accounts to specific villages. "These should be enough to support an investigation if we can get them to the right people." Before leaving, Carly and her handmaiden restore the room as best as they can, leaving no obvious signs of their search. "We cannot be careless. They will be watching for any unusual activity. For now, we keep quiet and continue gathering evidence." As they leave the household, the weight of what they have seen settles heavily on both of them. "That was just one household. I wonder how many others are involved..." The Marroway ledger is more than numbers: it is a record of the people behind the profits, and the cost of obedience paid in silence. But with each piece of evidence, the truth becomes harder to hide.',
  art:'Pages show: two women in lilac and white in a candle-lit storeroom reading a ledger in Chinese-style script (as in the captions: Carly and her handmaiden; the pictures again look like Sally and her handmaiden), a seal with red ink, crossed-out entries, copied pages and the two walking home by the river under a full moon. The ledgers are inside Marroway House itself (\'hidden in a side storeroom beneath the household offices\'), so whoever Carly is has access to the household: the author to confirm whether Carly is Sally or a servant.',
  quote:'"The Marroway ledger is more than numbers: it is a record of the people behind the profits." — the narration',
  events:['Household and trade records are kept separately, in a side storeroom beneath the household offices', 'Payments labelled \'escort fees\', \'protection\' and \'labour relocation\' do not match the recorded shipments and match the villages visited', 'Entries marked \'relocation\', \'transfer\' and \'special handling\' seem to refer to people, moved not voluntarily', 'Payments to officials and unknown recipients; crossed-out entries still legible', 'Key pages are copied and kept in separate places', 'The records prove a systematic network of intimidation, exploitation and the removal of those who resist'],
  purpose:['Give the case its documentary core', 'Prove the pattern is systematic'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Marroway Ledger (5 objectives)', 'Evidence: the Marroway ledger', 'The Marroway files open: masked contracts at the capital'],
  reward:'The Marroway ledger: a systematic network'},
 198:{ title:'A Request for Justice', type:'Story Chapter — Carly asks for help', loc:'🏮 A quiet corner of a Dragonvale tavern',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky and Carly (Sally\'s handmaiden)',
  introduced:['Carly (Sally\'s trusted handmaiden)'],
  sum:'To avoid drawing suspicion, Sally does not attend the meeting. Instead, she sends Carly, her trusted handmaiden, to speak with Jade, Devon and Sky in private. That night Carly meets them at a quiet corner of the tavern. Carly: "Thank you for agreeing to meet me. Lady Sally could not come. It is safer this way." Jade: "Tell us what you need, Carly." Carly: "I have been gathering information quietly, but now the situation is more dangerous than I expected. Lucien\'s men are intimidating the villagers, especially the women. Some have already disappeared. They fear speaking because Marroway House can punish anyone who talks. I am asking for your help to protect the villagers and the women who are still at risk." Jade: "You have done well to gather this much, Carly. Do you know how many are in danger now?" Carly: "From what I can confirm, there are several families. At least three women have disappeared within the last two years. There are also those forced into labour at the docks and the storehouses. Some are not paid, and some are never seen again." Devon: "This is not just a few isolated cases. It looks like a pattern. An organised network using Marroway House\'s status to cover its tracks." Sky: "Do we have any written records? Names, locations, shipments?" Carly: "Yes. I have made copies of some ledgers, payment records and household accounts. I kept them separate and used different locations in case they are discovered. Here are the copies I can give you for now. There are more, but I need time to make additional copies. I cannot risk returning with obvious signs that I have been collecting these. Please... I am not asking for revenge. I just want the villagers and the women to be safe. If Marroway\'s men suspect me, it would put Lady Sally at risk too." Jade: "You have already done more than most would dare, Carly. We will help. But we must be careful and plan this properly. For now, continue gathering information quietly. Do not let them suspect you. If you learn of any immediate danger, send word to us discreetly. We will arrange protection for those who need to leave." Carly: "Thank you... truly, thank you." With Carly\'s request, Jade\'s party steps further into the shadows of Marroway House. What began as an investigation is no longer just about records: it is about real people, and the lives still at risk.',
  art:'Pages show: a lantern-lit tavern, Jade (red), Devon (fur collar), Sky (blue) and a young woman in lilac and white with flowers in her hair: CARLY is Sally\'s trusted handmaiden (the text of this chapter says so). Sally herself is absent. This identifies the \'Carly\' of ch195-197: the author\'s resolution of the earlier question. The pictures of 195 (a green-ribboned woman) and 196-197 (the handmaiden beside a woman in lilac) are inconsistent with this and are read as Carly and her mistress.',
  quote:'"I am not asking for revenge. I just want the villagers and the women to be safe." — Carly',
  events:['Sally stays away to avoid suspicion and sends her trusted handmaiden Carly', 'Lucien\'s men intimidate villagers, especially women; at least three women have disappeared in two years', 'Forced labour at the docks and storehouses; some unpaid, some never seen again', 'Carly gives copies of ledgers, payment records and household accounts, kept in separate places', 'She asks for protection, not revenge; if Marroway\'s men suspect her, Sally is at risk', 'Jade: help, but plan carefully; keep gathering quietly and send word of any immediate danger'],
  purpose:['Turn Carly\'s evidence into a request the party accepts', 'Make protection the goal'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Request for Justice (6 objectives)', 'The Marroway files open: masked contracts in Dragonvale', 'Carly: Sally\'s trusted handmaiden'],
  reward:'The party accepts Carly\'s request'},
 199:{ title:'The Night Investigation', type:'Story Chapter — a separate investigation at Marroway House', loc:'🏯 Marroway House, at night',
  chars:['jade', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Rin and Levi',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While Carly continues to gather information within her limits, Jade, Rin and Levi carry out a separate investigation at Marroway House to find evidence that is kept outside the official household records. After nightfall the three slip into Marroway House through a lesser-used gateway behind the warehouses. Levi: "Keep low. The main halls are this way." Rin: "The guards are changing shifts. We have a short window." They move through servants\' corridors and storage areas, avoiding patrols. At the warehouses they find signs of goods being diverted: crates marked as "grain" contain other supplies, including medicine and high-value items. Levi notes the delivery marks and takes careful copies. Jade: "These marks match the ones in Carly\'s notes. The goods are being sent to other locations." Rin: "Look at this. A token used by Marroway\'s agents. It wasn\'t in the official household records." In a hidden storage room they find lists of payments to local enforcers, travel routes, and names of villagers and women marked for relocation. They collect copies of key documents, traces of delivery seals, and one of the tokens used to identify the shipments. Levi: "This will be enough to prove there is a wider network. But we need to be careful when we use it." Rin: "These records show intimidation, bribes and forced labour. It is far worse than we expected." Jade: "Let\'s take what we have and return to Carly. There are still more places to check, but this is a good start." Rin: "We must move now, before the next patrol."',
  art:'Pages show: three figures in dark clothes (Jade in red, Rin with green ribbons and Levi in black) slipping through a gateway of a lantern-lit manor under a full moon. The chapter names Jade, Rin and Levi: the party\'s field team here. Rin is the green-ribboned woman of 194-196.',
  quote:'"It is far worse than we expected." — Rin',
  events:['Jade, Rin and Levi enter Marroway House by a lesser-used gateway behind the warehouses', 'Crates marked "grain" hold medicine and high-value goods: goods are being diverted', 'Levi copies the delivery marks; Jade matches them to Carly\'s notes', 'A token used by Marroway\'s agents that is not in the household records', 'A hidden storage room: payments to enforcers, travel routes, names of villagers and women marked for relocation', 'Copies, delivery-seal traces and a token are taken; the party withdraws before the next patrol'],
  purpose:['Find evidence outside the official records', 'Prove a wider network'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Night Investigation (6 objectives)', 'Evidence: the agents\' token and the hidden storage room'],
  reward:'Proof of a wider network at Marroway House'},
 200:{ title:'The Aristocrat\'s Mask', type:'Story Chapter — Lucien begins to realise', loc:'🏯 Marroway House',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Lucien Marroway (his chapter)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Lucien begins to realise that someone is investigating him and his carefully maintained public persona begins to fracture. At first it is small things: a missing ledger, a moved document, a question from a steward, and unfamiliar attention around the warehouses. Lucien finds traces that his household records have been viewed or copied. Lucien: "So... there are eyes within my house now?" He begins to suspect that the information is coming from within his own household, most likely through a trusted servant close to Sally. "Is my own domestic staff no longer loyal? ...Or is it Sally?" In public, Lucien maintains his mask: the gracious noble, a devoted husband, and a respectable member of the court. "As always, I am honoured to be among such esteemed guests." But behind the mask, his patience begins to wear thin. He quietly increases surveillance within the household, questioning servants and changing access to key areas. "Find out who is asking questions. Search the storerooms. I want to know everyone who has had access to the records. From now on, no one enters the warehouses or ledgers without my approval. Double the watches." Several servants are warned, transferred, or threatened when Lucien suspects they may have spoken or seen too much. "Remember where your loyalty lies. A careless tongue can ruin lives." Lucien cannot yet prove who is behind the investigation, but the pattern is clear. Someone is deliberately tracing his activities. "They are careful. They know where to look. This is not random." His carefully maintained public persona begins to fracture: the more he searches, the more uneasy he becomes, because someone has seen beyond the image he shows to the world. "Whoever you are... you have made a serious mistake. If you think you can hide from me... you underestimate how far my reach goes." The aristocrat\'s mask is still in place, but cracks have begun to show, and the danger for those investigating him has grown.',
  art:'Pages show: Lucien in a navy-and-gold robe alone with a copied page and a red seal, at a gathering with a goblet, giving orders to guards, threatening a servant, and at a balcony at night. A villain\'s-point-of-view chapter: the party is not present. Lucien suspects a trusted servant close to Sally, or Sally herself.',
  quote:'"If you think you can hide from me... you underestimate how far my reach goes." — Lucien Marroway',
  events:['Lucien finds that his records have been viewed or copied', 'He suspects a trusted servant close to Sally, or Sally herself', 'In public he keeps the mask of the gracious, devoted noble', 'He tightens surveillance: no one enters the warehouses or ledgers without his approval', 'Servants are warned, transferred or threatened', 'His persona begins to fracture; the danger to the investigators grows'],
  purpose:['Show the threat Lucien becomes', 'Raise the stakes for Sally and Carly'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Aristocrat\'s Mask (6 objectives)', 'Lucien is alerted'],
  reward:'Lucien knows someone is investigating him'},
 201:{ title:'The Villagers\' Stand', type:'Story Chapter — a safe meeting place', loc:'🏘️ A safe meeting place outside Lucien\'s control',
  chars:['jade', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Rin, Levi and the villagers',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With evidence in hand, the party moves to protect the villagers and women who are willing to speak. For the first time in a long while, the people of Marroway House\'s lands begin to stand together. Word spreads quietly at first, but once a few speak, others find the courage to come forward. Jade: "You are safe here. You can speak. We will protect you." The party sets up a safe meeting place outside Lucien\'s direct control, where villagers and workers can share what they have witnessed. A man: "We have seen the wagons leave at night. Women from the docks, from the farms... and they never return. Those who ask questions are dismissed, punished, or made to disappear as well." A young woman: "I was sent to Marroway House to work in the storehouses. When I resisted, they said my family\'s grain debts would be seized. There were others. We... we are not the only ones." A companion: "You have been very brave to speak. Your names will be kept confidential. We will make sure you and your families are protected." Jade: "Lucien\'s power depends on fear and silence. But you are not alone. If more people speak, we can stop this." A man in black: "From today, no one who speaks to us will be left unprotected. We will arrange safe houses and escorts for those at risk." Villager: "We will stand together. This ends now. Our village will no longer be a place where people disappear in silence." A woman: "We will speak too. My sister... She never came back. I want the truth. Count on us. There are more who will testify once they see we are not alone." As more villagers come forward, the fear that once kept them apart begins to break. What started as whispers becomes a united stand, a community ready to face Lucien\'s influence and protect one another. With their protection, the villagers find their voices, and the first real challenge to Lucien\'s rule begins.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade, Rin (green) and Levi with villagers and a child in a lantern-lit meeting hall; a crowd of villagers and women; a man in black and gold with a tassel who promises safe houses and escorts (read as Devon or Levi: not named); the village at night under red maple leaves. Direct witnesses, several of them, whose names are protected.',
  quote:'"Lucien\'s power depends on fear and silence. But you are not alone." — Jade',
  events:['A safe meeting place outside Lucien\'s control', 'Villagers and workers describe wagons leaving at night and people who never return', 'A woman forced into the storehouses under threat of seizing her family\'s grain', 'Names kept confidential; safe houses and escorts promised', 'More come forward: the fear that kept them apart begins to break', 'The first real challenge to Lucien\'s rule'],
  purpose:['Give the villagers a protected voice', 'Turn testimony into a community'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Villagers\' Stand (6 objectives)', 'Evidence: several direct witnesses, anonymised', 'Safe houses and escorts'],
  reward:'The villagers stand together'},
 202:{ title:'The Weight of a Name', type:'Story Chapter — Devon', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale',
  chars:['devon', 'jade', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Devon, Jade, Sky and Levi',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Devon confronts the responsibility that comes with noble and royal authority, especially when status has been used to shield wrongdoing. Devon has witnessed the evidence gathered by Sally and Carly, and the testimonies from the villagers. The records show how noble authority, household connections, and official channels have been used to intimidate villagers, silence women, and hide disappearances. Devon: "This is not just one man\'s cruelty. It has continued because people looked away. So many names... All protected by pedigree, wealth or position." As a prince and a noble, Devon cannot ignore what this means for his own world. "If we allow our names and titles to be used as shields for wrongdoing, then we are part of the problem. Authority is not a privilege to protect the guilty. It is a duty to protect the people." Devon speaks openly with Jade, acknowledging the uncomfortable truth that noble families have often enabled people like Lucien to act with impunity. "I have benefited from the same system that lets men like Lucien do as they please." Jade: "It is not enough to punish one person. We must change how this is allowed to happen." He commits to using his position and connections to support the investigation, ensure the victims are protected, and push for reforms within the noble and royal circles where such abuses are ignored or covered up. "I will use what I can: my name, my influence, and the royal channels, to make sure this does not end here. These people deserve more than silence. They deserve justice and a safer future." Sky and Levi support him, reminding him that real authority is shown through action, not just titles. "Your voice matters, Devon. What you do now can protect more people than you realise." Devon: "A name is not just honour and privilege. It is accountability. If we do not live up to that responsibility, then we have no right to be called noble or royal. I will not look away again. Using our names to protect the people: that is the kind of nobility I choose to stand for." From this point forward Devon chooses to be part of the solution, working with Jade\'s party to hold Lucien and his allies accountable and to prevent more people from suffering under the same abuse of power. Jade: "This ends with Lucien, but it must not be the last. We protect these people, and we make it harder for anyone to do this again."',
  art:'Pages show: Devon with a fur collar and a lion-crest cloak, a table of sealed letters, Devon and Jade talking, Sky (blue) and Levi, a balcony at night. A character chapter for Devon: his own place in the system of noble privilege. It does not set up a plot beyond his resolve to push for reform.',
  quote:'"A name is not just honour and privilege. It is accountability." — Devon',
  events:['Devon reviews the evidence and testimonies: noble authority has been used to hide disappearances', '"If we allow our names and titles to be used as shields for wrongdoing, then we are part of the problem"', 'He admits he has benefited from the same system', 'He commits his name, influence and the royal channels to the investigation and to reform', 'Sky and Levi: real authority is action, not titles', 'Jade: it ends with Lucien, but must not be the last'],
  purpose:['Give Devon a stake in the case', 'Raise the question of reform'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Weight of a Name (6 objectives)', 'Devon: accountability for his name'],
  reward:'Devon chooses accountability'},
 203:{ title:'Sally\'s Decision', type:'Story Chapter — Sally leaves Lucien', loc:'🏯 Marroway House',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Sally and Lucien Marroway',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Sally accepts that the marriage cannot continue and decides to leave Lucien. After learning the truth and hearing the villagers\' testimonies, Sally can no longer ignore what has been hidden behind Marroway House\'s polished facade. Sally: "I stayed because I believed things could be different. But silence has only allowed more harm to continue." Lucien tries to dismiss her decision, clinging to reputation, status and control: "You are my wife. Where would you go? Do you think you can simply walk away from Marroway House?" Sally speaks with clarity, refusing to be bound by fear or appearances any longer. "I will not remain in a marriage built on lies and harm. I choose to leave." She tells Lucien that her decision is final, and that she will not stay to protect his image. "You have your name, your influence and your alliances. I will not be used to protect your reputation any longer." Sally prepares to leave, taking only what is hers and what she needs for a new beginning. "I do not need much to start over. What I need most is the freedom to choose my own path." She leaves behind the title of Marroway\'s wife, but takes with her her own identity, dignity and the hope of a safer future. "I was once a wife of Marroway, but that is not who I am anymore. From today, I choose myself." With the support of Jade\'s party and trusted allies, Sally leaves Marroway House and sets out for a new life away from Lucien\'s control. "This is not an end, but a new beginning. I will live without fear, without lies, and without being someone\'s protection for wrongdoing." As Sally departs, she carries with her the strength to rebuild her life, and the knowledge that her decision may help other women and villagers find their voices too.',
  art:'Pages show: Sally in purple with flowers in her hair, Lucien in black and gold, Sally packing a chest, a sunrise terrace over a harbour town, and a carriage at a gate. Sally ends the marriage herself: this is the decision, not a trial.',
  quote:'"I was once a wife of Marroway, but that is not who I am anymore. From today, I choose myself." — Sally',
  events:['Sally can no longer ignore what has been hidden behind the facade', 'Lucien clings to status and control: "Where would you go?"', '"I will not remain in a marriage built on lies and harm. I choose to leave."', 'She takes only what is hers', 'With the support of Jade\'s party she leaves Marroway House', 'Her decision may help other women and villagers find their voices'],
  purpose:['Sally leaves', 'Her agency, not rescue'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Sally\'s Decision (5 objectives)', 'Sally has left Lucien'],
  reward:'Sally leaves Lucien'},
 204:{ title:'The Fall of Marroway', type:'Story Chapter — the evidence is presented', loc:'🏛️ Before the authorities of Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade', 'levi', 'sky'], charsNote:'Jade, Levi, Rin, Sky, Sally and Lucien Marroway',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With undeniable evidence in hand, Jade exposes Lucien\'s crimes and secures protection for those affected by him, bringing an end to his abuse of power. Jade presents the collected evidence: household ledgers, delivery records, testimonies, and the network of cover-ups linking Lucien to the abuse of his authority. At first Lucien tries to maintain his composure, dismissing the claims as lies and manipulation: "Do you truly think these accusations can bring me down? I am Marroway. My word has always been enough." But the evidence is clear and undeniable. Jade exposes the use of noble channels to intimidate villagers, silence women, and hide illegal activities: "These are the records. These are the testimonies. These are the people you harmed. There is no denying it now." Levi stands with Jade, ensuring Lucien is taken into custody and that his crimes are formally recorded: "Your title does not place you above the law. What you did will be answered for." With his power stripped away, Lucien is taken into custody to face formal charges. The villagers, servants and others affected by Lucien finally find the courage to speak: "Thank you... Now we can finally speak the truth." Sally confirms her decision to leave, choosing her own future and a life no longer defined by Lucien: "I will not return. I choose to leave. I want a life where I can be myself, and finally move forward." Rin, Sky and Levi remain by Jade\'s side, helping to secure protection, compensation and new opportunities for those affected by Lucien\'s abuse: "This is not the end. We will make sure these people are safe, and that this never happens again." With Lucien\'s fall, Marroway House descends into turmoil, but for many it marks the end of fear and the start of a safer, fairer future. Justice has been served, and the people\'s voices are no longer in silence. There may be more to uncover, but today a step has been taken toward a brighter future, for Marroway, and for everyone who suffered.',
  art:'Pages show: a court hall with blue banners, Jade reading the evidence, Lucien in navy and gold denying, Levi (black) with the guards, Lucien led away, villagers and servants speaking, Sally in purple and red confirming she leaves, and Jade, Rin, Sky and Levi at the close. THE OUTCOME IS CANON: Lucien is taken into custody to face formal charges (the authorities), not killed. The game\'s final Marroway decision therefore moves to AFTER this chapter (while he awaits judgement).',
  quote:'"Your title does not place you above the law. What you did will be answered for." — Levi',
  events:['Jade presents the ledgers, delivery records, testimonies and the network of cover-ups', 'Lucien: "I am Marroway. My word has always been enough."', 'He is taken into custody to face formal charges', 'The villagers, servants and others find the courage to speak', 'Sally confirms she will not return', 'Protection, compensation and new opportunities for the victims; Marroway House falls into turmoil'],
  purpose:['Resolve the public case', 'Protect the victims'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Fall of Marroway (6 objectives)', 'Lucien Marroway is in custody awaiting judgement'],
  reward:'Lucien Marroway is taken into custody'},
 205:{ title:'Never Again', type:'Story Chapter — the separation and Sally\'s declaration', loc:'🏯 Dragonvale',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Sally, Devon, Jade, Levi and Sky',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After roughly half a year of marriage, Sally completes her separation from Lucien and firmly declares that she does not intend to remarry. After months of proceedings, the separation is finally completed. Sally signs the final documents with a steady hand. What began as a marriage of duty and political convenience now ends in separation. She reclaims her name, her freedom and her future. Lucien accepts the outcome without protest, his carefully maintained public image left in ruins after his crimes are exposed. Sally: "I will not remarry. I choose my own path from now on." Devon stands by her, acknowledging her strength and the difficult journey she has endured: "You have shown courage, Sally. Your decision is respected." Jade, Levi and Sky support her decision, knowing that this marks a new chapter in her life: "You are more than what you went through. This is a new beginning, Sally. You are free to be who you want to be now." For the first time in a long while, Sally feels a sense of peace. She is no longer bound by a title or a man\'s name. "I will build a life of my own, with the people I trust and the work that matters." With the separation complete, Sally returns to Dragonvale as a free woman, no longer Lucien\'s wife but her own person, surrounded by friends and allies who value and respect her. The past cannot be changed, but it no longer defines her. Sally looks ahead, ready to write the next chapter of her life on her own terms. Never again will she give up her name, her voice, or her future for the sake of a title or expectation. Sally steps forward, not as someone\'s wife, but as herself.',
  art:'Pages show: a white castle by the sea (opening), Sally in purple signing papers with a brush, Lucien accepting, Devon (fur collar) beside her, Jade (red), Levi (black) and Sky (blue) around her, and Sally alone among flowers at sunset. Lucien\'s \'complete\' separation here is after his arrest (ch204): the game\'s separate \'one more thing\' decision about his fate is placed after this chapter. \'Roughly half a year of marriage\' matches the game\'s 180 days.',
  quote:'"I will build a life of my own, with the people I trust and the work that matters." — Sally',
  events:['After months of proceedings the separation is complete; Sally signs', 'Lucien accepts without protest; his public image is in ruins', 'Sally: "I will not remarry. I choose my own path from now on."', 'Devon, Jade, Levi and Sky stand by her', 'Sally returns to Dragonvale as a free woman', 'Never again will she give up her name, voice or future for a title or expectation'],
  purpose:['Close Sally\'s marriage', 'Her declaration: never again'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Never Again (5 objectives)', 'Sally is free and will not remarry'],
  reward:'Sally is free: never again'},
 206:{ title:'The Fourth Record', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian finds a fourth record', loc:'📚 The Dragonvale archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'levi'], charsNote:'Adrian, Jade, Devon, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Adrian discovers another reference to the impossible Register entry, proving the anomaly extends beyond the original three records. While reviewing the archives in Dragonvale, Adrian spots an unusual entry in a regional Register from several years earlier. The record references an impossible Register entry: the fourth instance, in a different location and under a different name. Adrian: "...This cannot be another coincidence." The details match the same anomaly found in the first three records: a name that should not exist, a seal that is not recognised, and a reference to the hidden isle. "It\'s not limited to one place... The anomaly is wider than we thought." Adrian shows the entry to Jade, explaining the similarities to the previous three records: "Same seal... same phrasing... and a connection to the hidden isle." Levi studies the details, noting how the fourth record appears in a different region: "This means someone has been using this entry across multiple locations. It\'s a pattern." Rin considers the implications: "Four records... That\'s too many to be a mistake. Whoever did this has a purpose." Devon reflects on the scope of the anomaly: "If there are four, there could be more, perhaps hidden in other archives as well." The party compares all four records, confirming the same impossible entry, seal and hidden isle reference. Jade: "This is not an isolated case. The Register entry is being used deliberately, and across the realm." Adrian decides to expand the search, looking for other archives that might contain similar references: "I will contact my networks in the other regions. We need to find the next record before someone else does." The discovery of the fourth record confirms that the anomaly is part of a larger, coordinated plan, and that the hidden isle is at the centre of it all.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian in a navy robe with a blue ribbon in a library, an old register with a dragon seal and glowing lines, Jade and Adrian, Levi, Rin (green ribbons), Devon (fur collar), the four records compared, and a map on a table. Adrian is in Dragonvale (the chapter says so). \'The hidden isle\' is a name the game\'s player knows as Tribute; the fourth record names it in the same phrasing: the chapter does not say what it means by \'the hidden isle at the centre of it all\': flagged.',
  quote:'"The Register entry is being used deliberately, and across the realm." — Jade',
  events:['Adrian finds a fourth instance in a regional Register from several years earlier: a different place and name', 'Same anomaly: a name that should not exist, an unrecognised seal and a reference to the hidden isle', 'Levi: it appears in a different region, so it is a pattern; Rin: too many to be a mistake', 'Devon: there could be more, hidden in other archives', 'Adrian will contact his networks in the other regions', 'The hidden isle is at the centre of a coordinated plan'],
  purpose:['Expand the anomaly beyond three records', 'Make the hidden isle the centre'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Fourth Record (5 objectives)', 'Register: a fourth record', 'Register mark: the Impossible Entry is Cross-Kingdom, four records'],
  reward:'A fourth record'},
 207:{ title:'Eve Gray\'s Other Face', type:'Story Chapter — the party meets Eve', loc:'📚 The Dragonvale archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin, Adrian and Eve Gray',
  introduced:['Eve Gray (in male disguise)'],
  sum:'The party encounters Eve and sees that she is far more capable and knowledgeable than Adrian understood, from his previous brother-sister conversation with Jade. The party finally meets Eve, who is travelling in a male disguise to keep a low profile. Eve: "You must be the Imperial Guard and her companions. I am a humble scholar passing through Dragonvale." At first Adrian is surprised by her presence, remembering his earlier impressions of Eve as quiet and reserved: "...Eve? I did not expect to see you here." Eve: "There is much I did not say before. And much more I am now able to do." Eve demonstrates her deep knowledge of the archives, hidden networks and long-standing connections across different regions: "This register is only one thread. There are other records, in places most people have forgotten to look. These records link back decades. The same names appear in different forms, across different places. It is not a coincidence." Her understanding goes beyond theory: she has been actively collecting information, tracking movements, and piecing together what others have missed. Jade quickly realises that Eve is far more capable and independent than Adrian had suggested in their previous conversation: "You have done all of this, alone? You are far more capable than we were told." Devon and Sky listen as Eve explains how the pieces connect, people, places and motives that span beyond the original three records: "The pattern is larger than any single incident. Someone has been using different names, different locations, and different facades, but the purpose remains the same." Eve also reveals the risks she has taken to continue her investigation, and why she has chosen to remain in disguise for now: "There are people who would silence me if they knew what I had found. For now, it is safer this way. As a man, I can move more freely and ask questions others would pass me." The party decides to work with Eve, combining her information with their own findings to uncover the full scope of the anomaly. Jade: "Then we move forward together. Your knowledge fills the gaps we have been struggling to reach." Eve: "I may travel under another name, but I choose my own path. There is still much to uncover. I intend to see it through, with you if you will have me." With Eve\'s help the investigation takes a significant step forward, and the truth behind the Register begins to look far more complex than anyone had imagined. Eve Gray is no longer just a name in a conversation, but an active ally in the journey ahead.',
  art:'Pages show: Eve in a dark scholar\'s robe with a blue ribbon and a topknot, as a man; Adrian in green beside her; Jade, Devon (fur collar), Sky (blue) and Levi at the table; a waterfall city at night. Eve is travelling in male disguise as \'a humble scholar\'; the party meets her as Eve Gray. Her real identity beyond the name stays undisclosed (author: keep secret): the build does not say who she is. She is an ally (\'with you if you will have me\'), not yet a party member: the build gives her guest-intelligence prompts in the Register, no party slot.',
  quote:'"I may travel under another name, but I choose my own path." — Eve Gray',
  events:['The party meets Eve Gray, travelling in male disguise as a humble scholar', 'Adrian is surprised: she is far more capable than he had known', 'She shows deep knowledge of archives, hidden networks and connections across regions: the same names in different forms for decades', 'Someone has been using different names, locations and facades for the same purpose', 'She keeps her disguise because there are people who would silence her', 'The party decides to work with Eve: an active ally'],
  purpose:['Bring Eve into the investigation', 'Show her capability'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Eve Gray\'s Other Face (5 objectives)', 'Eve Gray: an active ally (guest intelligence: Ask Eve, Compare Record, Follow Her Lead)'],
  reward:'Eve Gray joins the investigation'},
 208:{ title:'A Pattern Across Kingdoms', type:'Story Chapter — the ancient alliance link', loc:'📚 The Dragonvale royal archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and Adrian',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade links the historical contradictions to the ancient alliance revealed in Chapter 183 and begins to see a larger pattern. In Dragonvale, the party regroups with Adrian to compare their findings with the royal archives. Jade examines the records side by side, events, names, locations and dates, and recognises the same pattern. Jade: "These contradictions keep appearing in different kingdoms. They are not isolated incidents." The historical contradictions point towards the ancient alliance first revealed in Chapter 183, suggesting a long-running network that spans multiple kingdoms. "The dates are different, the names are different, but the purpose is the same. The same symbol. The same oath. Different kingdoms... but the same alliance." Adrian shares additional records from Dragonvale, showing that similar discrepancies exist in their own history: "Even in Dragonvale\'s archives, there are deliberate erasures and conflicting versions of the same events." Devon realises that this is not just about one kingdom, one noble house, or one wrongdoing; it is part of something far larger: "They used different faces, different titles, and different places... but the pattern is consistent." Sky points out that the same methods were used: manipulation of records, control of people, and the use of intermediaries: "It is a system. Not a single person\'s crime. They built it to last, across kingdoms and generations." Levi adds that the scale of the pattern explains why so many unrelated incidents felt strangely similar: "Different kingdoms. Different people. But the same methods, the same goals... and the same victims." Jade begins to see the larger picture: this ancient alliance has shaped the present, and its influence still reaches into the current era. "This explains so much. What we have uncovered so far is only part of a much larger pattern." The evidence from multiple kingdoms points to a coordinated network, with shared symbols, allied houses and hidden records. The party agrees to continue investigating, tracing the connections between the records and identifying which kingdoms and noble houses were involved. "We need to find all the missing pieces. The more we uncover, the closer we get to the truth. This is bigger than we thought. But we are no longer just reacting. We are mapping the whole network." The ancient alliance was not a legend: it was real, and it still leaves traces today.',
  art:'Pages show: the party around candles in an archive (Jade, Sky, Adrian in green, Levi with arrows, Devon with a fur collar), a map of compass symbols and arrows, and a waterfall palace at sunset. Eve is not in this chapter\'s pictures. \'Chapter 183\' is the ancient maritime alliance (Dragonvale, Tribute, the Sunken Kingdom and vanished civilisations). Note: the chapter links the Register contradictions to the alliance, and says the methods (manipulating records, controlling people, using intermediaries) match the Marroway case: \'the same methods... the same victims\'.',
  quote:'"The ancient alliance was not a legend: it was real, and it still leaves traces today." — the narration',
  events:['Contradictory records keep appearing in different kingdoms', 'They point to the ancient alliance of ch183: the same symbol and oath in different kingdoms', 'Dragonvale\'s own archives show deliberate erasures and conflicting versions of events', 'Devon: different faces, titles and places, but a consistent pattern', 'Sky: a system built to last, not one person\'s crime; Levi: the same methods, goals and victims', 'The party will map the whole network'],
  purpose:['Tie the Register to the ancient alliance', 'Turn the case into mapping a network'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Pattern Across Kingdoms (6 objectives)', 'Register: the pattern links to the ancient alliance (ch183)'],
  reward:'The pattern leads to the ancient alliance'},
 209:{ title:'The Name That Travels', type:'Story Chapter — the name is a framework', loc:'📚 The Dragonvale archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and Adrian',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The investigation shows that the Register entry cannot be understood as an ordinary individual creature or a simple single identity. The party continues their research in Dragonvale, comparing the Register entry with records from different kingdoms and archives. The same name appears again, but the descriptions are different in each place. The dates, the locations and even the titles do not match a single person or creature; yet the core name, or something close to it, keeps appearing. Some records treat the name as a creature or entity. Others describe it as a title, a place, or even a role passed between people across generations. Jade: "It changes form, meaning and context... but it is always connected to the same core." Jade overlays maps from Tribute, Dragonvale and other kingdoms (the North Kingdom, the Western Isles, the Southern Ports, the Eastern Coast); the sightings and incidents form a wide network. Levi notes that the pattern does not fit the behaviour of any known demon, evil creature or individual recorded in the Register: "If it were a single creature, its nature and appearance would be consistent. But the records describe different forms, different roles, and different effects." Sky points out that the same methods were used in multiple incidents: manipulation of records, control of people and the use of intermediaries. "The methods are the same, only the faces change. It behaves like a network, not a single being." Adrian compares the Register entry with restricted royal archives and older scholar accounts: "In some records, it is a person. In others, a place. In others, a title. It may be a name that is used, inherited, or passed on... rather than one fixed identity." The party begins to suspect that the Register entry is a framework, a name that can move between people, places, and even bloodlines. "It could be a title, a role, or a function. Something that survives by changing how it appears." Devon suggests that this may explain why similar incidents have appeared in different kingdoms over decades, without a clear source: "It leaves traces behind, then moves elsewhere, taking a different form. That is why so many unrelated events share the same name, but look unrelated on the surface." The party realises that understanding the name requires looking at all the records together, across kingdoms, time periods and different forms: "This is not just an investigation of what it is... but how it moves, how it is used, and why it continues to appear." Jade records their findings, marking this as a key turning point in their investigation: "The name is not a single creature or person. It is a pattern, and understanding that pattern is the next step." The true nature of the Register entry remains hidden, but the party now knows it cannot be understood in simple terms. To uncover the truth they will need to follow the pattern further, beyond Dragonvale, and across the kingdoms it touches.',
  art:'Pages show: the party reading in a candle-lit archive, a map overlaid with the North Kingdom, Western Isles, Dragonvale, Eastern Coast, Southern Ports and \'Related Incidents\' linked by red lines, a star-shaped sigil, and a waterfall city at night. Eve is not shown. The place names \'North Kingdom\', \'Western Isles\', \'Southern Ports\' and \'Eastern Coast\' appear for the first time on this map.',
  quote:'"The name is not a single creature or person. It is a pattern, and understanding that pattern is the next step." — Jade',
  events:['The same name appears in each kingdom, with different descriptions, dates and titles', 'It is a creature in some records, and a title, a place or a role passed between people in others', 'The map: the North Kingdom, the Western Isles, Dragonvale, the Southern Ports and the Eastern Coast form a network of related incidents', 'It behaves like a network, not a single being: the methods are the same, only the faces change', 'The Register entry may be a framework: a name that moves between people, places and bloodlines', 'The party must follow the pattern beyond Dragonvale, across the kingdoms it touches'],
  purpose:['Reframe the entry as a framework', 'Point beyond Dragonvale'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Name That Travels (6 objectives)', 'Register: the name is a pattern, not a being'],
  reward:'The name is a pattern'},
 210:{ title:'Beyond the Fifteen', type:'Arc VIII Finale — the Register records beyond the Fifteen', loc:'📚 The Dragonvale archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and Adrian',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Arc VIII concludes with the discovery that the Register is recording anomalies outside the traditional Fifteen framework, opening the next major investigation. Jade: "All the evidence points to the same conclusion. The Register is not limited to the Fifteen." The page shows the Traditional Fifteen Framework as fifteen categories: Celestial, Abyssal, Infernal, Bestial, Fae, Elemental, Undead, Spiritual, Construct, Aetherial, Vile, Blessed, Human, Draconic and Unknown. The Register contains entries that do not fit any of the Fifteen categories: "These anomalies show different patterns, symbols and behaviours." A companion: "We initially assumed the Fifteen covered all known beings. But the Register is recording entries beyond that system. This explains why so many incidents seemed unrelated at first." Sky: "The patterns are consistent, even if the forms vary. Different places. Different times. Different victims. But the same kind of anomaly, outside the Fifteen." Levi (or a companion): "It is not a single individual, not a single race, and not a single creature type. It is a broader category, or perhaps a different framework entirely. The Register is tracking something older, or something beyond our current understanding." When the records from Tribute, Dragonvale and other kingdoms are overlaid, a clear pattern of anomalies appears across regions; the anomalies are connected through similar symbols, shared effects and a repeating sequence in the Register. "They are not random incidents, but part of a larger, ongoing record." Jade: "The Fifteen were a useful way to understand the world... But the Register reveals that there is more beyond it. This changes everything." Devon: "So what happens now? If the Register can record beyond the Fifteen, there may be many more anomalies we have not encountered. And we cannot treat these as isolated events any longer." The next phase of the investigation will focus on uncovering the source of these beyond-Fifteen entries, identifying the purpose behind the Register, finding the links between past and present anomalies, and determining how this affects Tribute and other kingdoms. Sky: "This is only the beginning. The Register has shown us a larger world, one that reaches beyond the systems we were taught. We now have more questions than answers, but at least we know where to look next." Arc VIII closes not with an answer, but with a new path. The Register is recording anomalies outside the traditional Fifteen framework. The investigation continues...',
  art:'Pages show: a parchment of \'The Traditional Fifteen Framework\' (fifteen round emblems), the party in turn, a map of five regions around a star, a book of anomalies, a list of the next phase\'s four goals, and the party looking at a waterfall city at sunset. MISMATCH TO CONFIRM: the game\'s \'Fifteen\' are the Fifteen Evils (named entities); this chapter\'s \'Traditional Fifteen Framework\' is fifteen CATEGORIES of beings (Celestial ... Unknown). The build keeps both: the Fifteen Evils (the Register\'s named cases) and the Fifteen categories (a framework the Register is now said to exceed). The page prints the next phase\'s objectives. Arc VIII\'s title is \'The Impossible Entry\' (the author\'s canon); the next arc\'s title is not given.',
  quote:'"The Register is not limited to the Fifteen." — Jade',
  events:['The Register contains entries that fit none of the Fifteen categories (Celestial, Abyssal, Infernal, Bestial, Fae, Elemental, Undead, Spiritual, Construct, Aetherial, Vile, Blessed, Human, Draconic, Unknown)', 'The anomalies are connected by symbols, shared effects and a repeating sequence: a larger, ongoing record', '"The Fifteen were a useful way to understand the world... But the Register reveals that there is more beyond it."', 'Next: the source of the beyond-Fifteen entries; the purpose of the Register; links between past and present anomalies; the effect on Tribute and other kingdoms', 'Arc VIII closes with a new path, not an answer'],
  purpose:['Close Arc VIII', 'Open the beyond-Fifteen investigation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beyond the Fifteen (4 objectives)', 'Register: Beyond the Fifteen opens (anomalies)', 'Arc VIII complete'],
  reward:'Arc VIII complete: the Register records beyond the Fifteen'},
 211:{ title:'A Scholar Among Warriors', type:'Story Chapter — Arc IX begins: the old trade route', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale: a district on the old trade route',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and Adrian Gold (guest)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Following their discoveries in Chapter 210, Jade\'s party continues their investigation in Dragonvale, accompanied by Adrian, who has joined them for this mission. The party arrives in a district to investigate records related to the old trade route. Although the area appears peaceful, there are few signs of the route mentioned in the archives. Jade: "Let\'s complete the survey before we return to the palace." Adrian, with the records: "These records are much newer than expected. Something has been deliberately removed..." Jade: "The same pattern as the Register. It could be connected to what we found in the previous investigation." A companion: "Then we should check the forest path behind this district. It may lead to the remnants of the original route." As they move deeper into the area, the party is suddenly ambushed by a group of bandits. "Bandits! Stay alert! They\'re trying to surround us!" Adrian stays towards the rear, using his arts to deflect incoming attacks and protect the others. His focus is on survival, movement, and redirection rather than inflicting harm. When more enemies close in, he throws a smoke pouch. "Smoke! Fall back! They\'ve lost sight of us!" After the fight, the party regroups and recovers several items that may be related to the missing trade route. Jade: "This seal matches the pattern we saw in the Register." Adrian: "Someone didn\'t want this route to be easily traced." The district was quieter than expected, but it has given us new clues. There is definitely more to uncover beyond what has been erased.',
  art:'Pages show: a Dragonvale bridge skyline (labelled \'Dragonvale\'), Jade (red), Adrian (with scrolls), Levi (archer), Sky (blue) and Devon (fur collar) walking a district; bandits in a forest; Adrian deflecting blows with open-handed movement and a green smoke pouch; Jade and Sky fighting; a seal found afterward. This is the REPLACEMENT page (the earlier 211 was a lower-quality format): the story is the same with small changes (the ambush is on a forest path behind the district; several items are recovered; Adrian stays towards the rear). Adrian is shown in dark robes here, not the green-and-gold scholar\'s robes of earlier pages. Eve is not in this chapter.',
  quote:'"Someone didn\'t want this route to be easily traced." — Adrian',
  events:['The investigation of the old trade route continues in Dragonvale with Adrian as a guest', 'The records are much newer than expected: something has been deliberately removed', 'Bandits ambush the party on the forest path; Adrian stays towards the rear, deflecting attacks, then throws a smoke pouch', 'The party recovers several items that may relate to the missing route, among them a seal matching the Register\'s pattern', 'Someone did not want the route easily traced'],
  purpose:['Open Arc IX with the old trade route', 'Show Adrian\'s guest abilities'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Scholar Among Warriors (5 objectives)', 'Adrian: guest ally (Smoke Pouch)', 'Register: the seal on the old route'],
  reward:'The old route was deliberately erased'},
 212:{ title:'The Wanderer\'s Smile', type:'Story Chapter — Eve rejoins the investigation', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale and the old forest trail',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Jade, Adrian and Eve Gray (in male disguise)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Eve Gray rejoins the investigation in her male disguise. Adrian and Eve spend time together, gradually rediscovering the comfortable companionship they once shared. Jade notices their growing affection. Eve arrives at the meeting point, dressed as a travelling man, just as she promised. Eve: "Sorry I\'m late. The checkpoint was more crowded than expected." Adrian: "You made it. I thought you might have changed your mind." Eve: "Not a chance. I\'ve missed travelling with you." As they travel, Adrian and Eve fall back into the easy rhythm they once shared on the road. Adrian: "According to this map, there\'s a trail through the old forest. Much safer and faster than the main road." Eve: "Good. I\'d prefer to avoid the checkpoints if we can." Adrian: "You still have that same smile. It\'s impossible to forget." Eve: "And you... still say the same things." Jade notices the way they look at each other: the unspoken comfort, the effortless closeness. Jade: "They\'re already so close... and they haven\'t even realized it yet." For the first time in a long while, Adrian seems relaxed, and Eve looks genuinely happy. Jade: "I\'m so glad they\'re back together... and I hope this time they won\'t lose each other." Later that evening they share a quiet meal before continuing their investigation. Adrian: "You really are better at this than I expected." Eve: "Years of practice. And a few close calls." Adrian: "Same route tomorrow?" Eve: "I\'m not sure I\'m ready to be apart again."',
  art:'Pages show: Eve in a black travelling cloak with a blue ribbon and a quiver, arriving at a meeting point in a city of spires; Adrian (in black and gold) with a map; the two walking, sharing a meal, and Jade watching them from a viewpoint. TIMELINE: ch207 already had the party meet Eve and Adrian\'s surprise at seeing her; this chapter has Eve arriving at a meeting point \'just as she promised\' and Adrian greeting her as if parting recently: the comic is not in story order (a retrospective, or the meeting that precedes 207): flagged. \'The Wanderer\'s Smile\' is Eve\'s smile.',
  quote:'"I\'m not sure I\'m ready to be apart again." — Eve',
  events:['Eve arrives at the meeting point as a travelling man, as promised', 'Adrian and Eve fall back into the easy rhythm they once shared on the road', 'A safer, faster trail through the old forest; they would rather avoid the checkpoints', 'Jade notices their effortless closeness: "they haven\'t even realized it yet"', 'A quiet meal: "Years of practice. And a few close calls."', 'Eve: "I\'m not sure I\'m ready to be apart again."'],
  purpose:['Reunite Adrian and Eve', 'Show their growing closeness through Jade\'s eyes'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Wanderer\'s Smile (5 objectives)', 'Eve Gray: guest ally (Quick Counter)'],
  reward:'Adrian and Eve are travelling together again'},
 213:{ title:'The Missing Seal', type:'Story Chapter — a royal seal removed from an alliance document', loc:'📚 Dragonvale: the royal archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Adrian and Eve',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party examines a document related to the ancient alliance and discovers that a royal seal has been deliberately removed. During their investigation in Dragonvale, the party gains access to a set of historical documents related to the ancient alliance. A companion: "This looks important. What does it say?" The document bears clear evidence that a royal seal was deliberately removed. Devon: "These markings... this is not from the current system. It matches the older diplomatic seals used by Dragonvale before the alliance fractured." Jade: "So someone intentionally removed the seal. But why?" Sky: "Could it be to hide the document\'s origin? Or to prevent it from being recognized as an official agreement?" Adrian: "If the seal confirmed Dragonvale\'s involvement, removing it would make it easier to deny its authenticity." Eve: "Or perhaps someone wanted to keep the contents hidden... not just the sender." Devon: "The seal belongs to a diplomatic system used between our kingdoms during the early years of the alliance. It would have carried significant legal and political weight." Devon points out distinctive features in the remaining impression: a crest shape consistent with Dragonvale\'s older royal seal; a partial emblem still visible; traces that indicate the seal was forcibly removed rather than naturally lost. Adrian: "The document\'s contents, combined with the missing seal, suggest that this may be a genuine diplomatic agreement, one that was later altered. Someone wanted to preserve the information, but not the evidence of its origin." The discovery raises new questions about what other records may have been altered, and why. Jade: "This is only one document, but it could lead to a much larger network of hidden records." The missing seal is a clear sign that history was deliberately changed, and there may be more documents like this still waiting to be found.',
  art:'Pages show: the party around a table in the archive (Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi-like man, and a hooded figure: Eve), a document with a torn-out round seal, a close-up of the remaining impression annotated with three features, and a library with a gold dragon banner. The hooded figure is Eve in disguise. The gameplay note says the chapter objective is to recover the damaged diplomatic seal.',
  quote:'"Someone wanted to preserve the information, but not the evidence of its origin." — Adrian',
  events:['The party gains access to historical documents on the ancient alliance in Dragonvale', 'A royal seal was deliberately and forcibly removed from one of them', 'Devon: it matches the older diplomatic seals Dragonvale used before the alliance fractured', 'Adrian: a genuine diplomatic agreement, later altered; Eve: perhaps the contents were meant to stay hidden, not only the sender', 'The discovery points to a larger network of hidden records'],
  purpose:['Show that the alliance\'s records were deliberately altered', 'Set the objective: recover the damaged diplomatic seal'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Missing Seal (5 objectives)', 'Objective: recover the damaged diplomatic seal', 'Register mark: records altered'],
  reward:'A royal seal was forcibly removed'},
 214:{ title:'A Gentleman\'s Defence', type:'Story Chapter — an ambush at the warehouse district', loc:'🏮 Dragonvale: a warehouse district',
  chars:['jade', 'devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Adrian and Eve (and the party)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'As the investigation continues, the party follows a lead to a warehouse district in Dragonvale. But before they can examine the records, they are suddenly attacked by a group of unknown assailants. The ambush comes without warning. "Surround them!" Adrian moves to the front, using fluid, defensive movements to deflect the incoming attacks. When the numbers grow, he throws smoke pouches to obscure their vision and give the others time to react. Within the cover of smoke, Adrian focuses on keeping the assailants at bay, redirecting their attacks rather than inflicting harm. "Don\'t let them break through!" Jade and Eve quickly join the fight. Jade: "Over here!" Eve\'s movements are swift and precise, far surpassing what Adrian expected. Adrian: "You... are even stronger than I remembered." Eve: "I had to learn how to protect myself. There were many situations where I could only rely on my own strength." After the assailants retreat, the party takes a moment to rest and tend to minor injuries. Eve: "You handled yourself well today. Those smoke pouches were a clever choice." Adrian: "I prefer solutions that allow everyone to get out safely. Your growth is remarkable, Eve. I\'m glad you\'re here with us again." Eve: "And I\'m glad to fight alongside you too, Adrian. It feels... comfortable, as it always has." Their shared experiences renew the respect between them, and the bond they once shared feels stronger than before.',
  art:'Pages show: hooded assailants advancing on a lantern-lit warehouse street at night, Adrian in black and gold deflecting with open hands and throwing a smoke pouch (blue tassel), Jade (red) joining with a blade, Eve (blue ribbon) moving precisely, and the two resting after the fight. The attackers are unknown. The gameplay note: the encounter is to survive an ambush while protecting Adrian. NOTE: the party that is not named here (Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin) is not shown; only Jade, Adrian and Eve.',
  quote:'"I prefer solutions that allow everyone to get out safely." — Adrian',
  events:['The party follows a lead to a warehouse district; unknown assailants attack before they can examine the records', 'Adrian moves to the front, deflecting blows with fluid movement; smoke pouches obscure their vision', 'Jade and Eve join the fight: Eve is swifter and more precise than Adrian expected', 'Eve: "I had to learn how to protect myself"', 'The two talk after the fight: respect renewed, the old bond stronger'],
  purpose:['Show Adrian and Eve fighting together', 'Survive an ambush while protecting Adrian'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Gentleman\'s Defence (5 objectives)', 'Battle: ambush at the warehouse district (protect Adrian)'],
  reward:'Adrian and Eve fought side by side'},
 215:{ title:'Letters Never Forgotten', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian and Eve talk about their letters', loc:'🌙 Dragonvale, at night',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian and Eve',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the recent ambush, the party rests in Dragonvale. With the immediate dangers at bay, Adrian and Eve find a quiet moment to speak privately. Eve brings out the letters they exchanged during their separation. Eve: "I kept every letter you sent. They were the reason I was never truly alone on the road." Adrian: "I wrote because I wanted you to know I was thinking of you. Even when we were apart, you were still part of my days." Adrian: "You once asked why I did not return sooner..." Eve: "It was not because I did not want to. There were reasons I had to continue travelling. There were people I needed to find, information I needed to gather, and matters I could not leave unfinished. Returning too early would have put you and the investigation at risk, and it would have meant leaving important tasks incomplete. I also needed time to understand myself... and what I could do beyond the life that had been chosen for me. I wanted to return to you as someone strong enough to stand beside you, not as someone who was still running from their past." Adrian: "You have always been stronger than you realize. Even then, you were protecting me in your own way." Through their letters they shared worries, discoveries, and the small moments of their daily lives, words that bridged the distance between them. Eve: "Your letters gave me the courage to keep going. No matter how far I was, it always felt like you were walking beside me." Their conversation slowly turns more personal. Adrian: "I missed you. More than I said in my letters." Eve: "...I missed you too. Every day. I am not sure what the future holds, but I know this... wherever this path leads, I want to face it with you." Adrian: "We do not have to decide everything right now. For now, it is enough to know that we are still here, together." Their journey is far from over, but their bond is stronger than before, shaped by time, distance, and the words that kept them connected. Some paths take longer than expected, but some connections are never truly lost.',
  art:'Pages show: Eve in a dark hooded cloak with the letters, Adrian reading, a bundle of letters and flowers, a harbour town at night, and the two on a bench in the moonlight. \'The life that had been chosen for me\' hints at her royal identity; the characters do not say it. The romance is told in letters and a quiet conversation, with no choice.',
  quote:'"Some paths take longer than expected, but some connections are never truly lost." — the narration',
  events:['Eve has kept every letter Adrian sent: they were why she was never alone on the road', 'Eve explains why she did not return sooner: people to find, information to gather, and a need to become someone strong enough to stand beside him', 'She needed time to understand herself beyond the life that had been chosen for her', 'The letters bridged the distance: worries, discoveries and small daily moments', '"I missed you. More than I said in my letters." "I missed you too. Every day."', 'They do not have to decide everything now: it is enough that they are here together'],
  purpose:['Deepen Adrian and Eve\'s bond', 'Explain Eve\'s long absence'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Letters Never Forgotten (5 objectives)', 'Adrian and Eve: the letters kept'],
  reward:'Adrian and Eve renew their bond'},
 216:{ title:'The Road Between Kingdoms', type:'Story Chapter — an abandoned checkpoint on the old route', loc:'🏔️ The road from Dragonvale to Tribute',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin, Adrian and Eve',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade\'s party returns to Tribute with Adrian and Eve. Along the way they investigate an abandoned checkpoint that once served travellers between the two kingdoms. After several days on the road the party reaches the remains of an old checkpoint. Jade: "This must be the checkpoint mentioned in the old records. It\'s in much worse condition than we expected." The checkpoint is clearly abandoned, its buildings collapsed and overgrown. Judging by the layout, this used to be a major route, not a small post. But there is no trace of it on current maps. Devon: "Someone deliberately removed this route from official records. This was not natural decay. Look at the way the main buildings were dismantled. It was done in an organized manner." Sky: "There are carved markers that match the alliance\'s older symbols. This route connected Tribute and Dragonvale." Faded carvings and stone markers confirm that this checkpoint once belonged to the ancient alliance network. A companion: "These markings are consistent with the older diplomatic system used before the alliance fractured. This route was important enough to be erased completely." Among the ruins they find partial records: travel permits, tax ledgers and correspondence. Sky: "These records show a steady flow of travellers, merchants and messengers between the two kingdoms." Jade: "Then suddenly, it stops. The last entries are years before the alliance broke." Devon: "Whoever removed this route did not just close a road. They removed the evidence that it ever existed." A companion: "That means they wanted future generations to forget about the connection between the two kingdoms." As the sun sets, the party prepares to leave the old checkpoint and continue their journey to Tribute. Jade: "There may be more checkpoints like this along the way. We should keep our eyes open for any other traces that were deliberately hidden. The past may have been buried... but the road between the kingdoms still exists in the people who remember."',
  art:'Pages show: a ruined gate on a mountain road with torn banners, Jade, Devon (fur collar), Sky and an archer (Rin) in a row, a collapsed overgrown building, carved compass-rose markers, travel permits and ledgers, and the four walking away at sunset. Adrian and Eve are named in the opening caption but only four are drawn (Jade, Devon, Sky, Rin/Levi-like archer). The story RELOCATES to Tribute here: the party travels back from Dragonvale. The gameplay note: Players collect fragments of old maps and compare them against modern travel routes (the Old Routes tab).',
  quote:'"The past may have been buried... but the road between the kingdoms still exists in the people who remember." — Jade',
  events:['The party returns to Tribute with Adrian and Eve, investigating an abandoned checkpoint on the way', 'A major route, absent from current maps: dismantled in an organised manner, not natural decay', 'Carved markers match the alliance\'s older symbols: the road once connected Tribute and Dragonvale', 'Permits, tax ledgers and correspondence: a steady flow of travellers, ending years before the alliance broke', 'Someone removed the evidence that the road ever existed, so future generations would forget', 'More checkpoints may lie along the way'],
  purpose:['Show the erased road', 'Start the Historical Route Reconstruction'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Road Between Kingdoms (6 objectives)', 'Historical Route Reconstruction: old map fragments', 'Adrian: back at the Tribute Palace (Research section)'],
  reward:'An alliance road was deliberately erased'},
 217:{ title:'The King\'s Archives', type:'Story Chapter — Greyson opens the sealed records', loc:'👑 Tribute: the royal archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Adrian, Eve and King Greyson',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'King Greyson grants Jade access to restricted historical records. Adrian compares these documents with those recovered in Dragonvale, discovering that several accounts were rewritten during the generations following the Dima–Xima crisis. Within Tribute\'s royal archives Jade and the party are granted access to records that have long been sealed from the public. Greyson: "These records have remained sealed for a reason. Handle them with care." The documents include travel logs, diplomatic correspondence, and accounts from the period surrounding the Dima–Xima crisis. Adrian: "The wording here is different from the records we found in Dragonvale. Entire sections have been altered." Comparing the two sets of documents reveals deliberate inconsistencies: names removed, events reframed, and certain individuals omitted entirely. Sky: "This account places the sole blame on Dima, but the original records suggest Xima was involved as well. The narrative was simplified. Too conveniently." Jade: "So the history we were taught is not the full truth. Someone chose what to remember... and what to erase." Greyson: "History is often shaped by those who survive it. What is recorded depends on what serves the next generation\'s interests. These archives contain many truths, but also many silences." A companion: "Look at this. Even the dates have been adjusted. The alliances, the movements: some of it does not align with the evidence we found." The archives also include records of border routes, missing envoys, and sealed agreements that were later reclassified or destroyed. Adrian: "These revisions began a few years after the crisis. It was a gradual process, not an immediate one. That means the truth was not merely lost: it was deliberately reshaped over time." Greyson: "Your findings confirm that there is more to this history than what was officially recorded. You may continue your research here. But remember: some truths are buried for a reason." With new information in hand, the party begins to see the larger picture, one that spans beyond a single kingdom and reaches deeper into the past. The rewritten records raise new questions, and the search for the full truth is far from over.',
  art:'Pages show: the royal archives with Greyson (a crown, long dark hair), Jade, Sky, Adrian (green) and Devon around a table; two sets of documents compared; a border-route book; and the party before a tall window onto Tribute\'s palace. King Greyson speaks directly. A tension: Greyson warns \'some truths are buried for a reason\', hinting that the crown has its own interest; he does not forbid the research. The Dima-Xima crisis is the curse\'s origin story (Xima is shown to have been involved too).',
  quote:'"These archives contain many truths, but also many silences." — King Greyson',
  events:['Greyson grants access to sealed records: travel logs, diplomatic correspondence and accounts of the Dima–Xima crisis', 'Adrian compares them with Dragonvale\'s copies: entire sections altered, names removed, events reframed, people omitted', 'Sky: the account blames Dima alone, but the originals suggest Xima was involved too: too conveniently simplified', 'Even the dates were adjusted; border routes, missing envoys and sealed agreements were reclassified or destroyed', 'The revisions began a few years after the crisis: gradual and deliberate', 'Greyson: you may continue; "some truths are buried for a reason"'],
  purpose:['Show history was rewritten after the crisis', 'Give the party the royal archive'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The King\'s Archives (6 objectives)', 'Register: records altered after the Dima-Xima crisis', 'Historical Route Reconstruction: border routes'],
  reward:'History was reshaped after the Dima-Xima crisis'},
 218:{ title:'The Woman Who Knows Too Much', type:'Story Chapter — a tavern and Eve\'s knowledge', loc:'🏮 A tavern in Tribute',
  chars:['jade', 'devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Adrian and Eve',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'As the investigation continues, the party takes a temporary rest at a tavern in Tribute, where they review the newly gathered information and cross-check it with the royal records. In a quiet corner of the tavern, Jade, Devon, Adrian and Eve pore over documents late into the night. Eve: "Wait, there is another reference here. This note mentions a secondary envoy who was present during the early negotiations. Their role was not recorded in the official accounts, but the format and phrasing match Tribute\'s court documentation from that era." The reference is subtle, but its wording and seal format align with Tribute\'s older records. It connects to the Dima–Xima crisis and mentions a private meeting that was not included in the later compiled history. Adrian: "...I missed this. This changes the timeline of their communications entirely. It also suggests that someone deliberately removed this part from the official records." Jade: "You noticed this? Even Adrian overlooked it? Your knowledge of Tribute\'s royal history... it goes far beyond what most nobles would know." Eve: "I have spent a long time travelling. I have had to learn how courts work, not just in theory, but in practice. It helps me understand how different kingdoms think, and how they choose what to record or what to hide." Devon: "Your understanding of court administration, diplomatic protocols, and archival systems is remarkably detailed. It is not something one picks up easily on the road." Eve: "There are many reasons for a person to learn. Some are practical. Knowledge is a form of protection, especially for those who cannot rely on their name or status." Adrian: "...That explains a great deal. You see more than most people do, Eve." Jade: "I would like to know more about your travels someday. There is still so much about you that I do not know." The conversation continues late into the night, deepening their understanding of the past and of each other. Devon: "There are still unanswered questions. But this gives us a clearer direction for the next phase of the investigation. And it also leaves new questions about the histories that were rewritten, and the woman who seems to know too much about them."',
  art:'Pages show: a lantern-lit tavern table with Jade (red), Devon (fur collar), Adrian (green and gold) and Eve (dark cloak and blue scarf) over documents; a secondary-envoy note with a seal; close-ups; the four in candlelight. The title says \'woman\': the party knows Eve is a woman in disguise (ch207). Eve notices a record Adrian missed: her knowledge of Tribute\'s royal history exceeds what a traveller or most nobles would know: a clue to her royal identity, which nobody says. The author\'s palace note: Eve can be encountered in the Palace during story investigations, though her true identity remains concealed.',
  quote:'"Knowledge is a form of protection, especially for those who cannot rely on their name or status." — Eve',
  events:['The party cross-checks the gathered records at a tavern in Tribute', 'Eve finds a reference to a secondary envoy at the early negotiations, absent from the official history', 'The wording and seal match Tribute\'s older court documentation; a private meeting was left out of the compiled history', 'Someone removed this part deliberately; Adrian had missed it', 'Jade and Devon notice Eve\'s knowledge of courts and archives far exceeds a traveller\'s', 'Eve: knowledge is protection for those who cannot rely on name or status'],
  purpose:['Show Eve\'s hidden depth', 'Find the missing envoy'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Woman Who Knows Too Much (6 objectives)', 'Eve Gray: contact at the Tribute Palace during investigations (identity concealed)'],
  reward:'A missing envoy, and a woman who knows too much'},
 219:{ title:'A Promise Beneath the Lanterns', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian and Eve speak openly', loc:'🌙 Tribute at night',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian and Eve',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After a long day of investigation, Adrian and Eve find a quiet moment together in Tribute, where they finally speak openly about their feelings. Adrian: "There were times I feared... that I might lose contact with you permanently. I did not know if you were safe, or if I would ever see you again." Eve: "I also feared that you might forget about me in time. You were a prince, and I was just a traveller on the road." Adrian: "I could never forget you. No matter how much time passed, you were always in my thoughts." They speak about the letters they exchanged, the choices they made, and the uncertainty of the road. Eve: "My feelings have never changed. Even when I was far away, even when we could not speak openly, you were always the one I thought of." Adrian: "You have always been honest with me... even when it was difficult. That is one of the reasons I admire you." Eve: "You give me the courage to keep going. No matter where I go or what path I take... I want you to be by my side. Not just in letters. Not just in thought. But in reality." Adrian: "Then let me be clear. I do not want to be apart from you again. I want to walk whatever road comes next... together." Beneath the lanterns of Tribute, they make a promise, not just for today, but for all the days ahead. Different paths, the same future. No more silence. No more distance. Only the road they will walk together.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian (green and gold, a topknot with a green ribbon) and Eve (dark cloak, blue scarf, blue ribbon) among lanterns and white flowers, close in the last panels (a kiss implied), and from behind on a bench by a lantern-lit canal under a full moon. Eve says \'You were a prince, and I was just a traveller on the road\': in this telling she hides her own rank (the character does not say she is a princess). The romance is told, not chosen.',
  quote:'"Different paths, the same future. No more silence. No more distance." — the narration',
  events:['Adrian and Eve speak openly about their fears of losing each other', 'They talk about the letters, the choices they made and the uncertainty of the road', 'Eve: her feelings never changed; Adrian: he never forgot her', 'Each admires the other\'s honesty and courage', 'They promise to walk the next road together, not just in letters but in reality'],
  purpose:['Resolve Adrian and Eve\'s separation', 'Make the promise before the wedding arc'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Promise Beneath the Lanterns (5 objectives)', 'Adrian and Eve: the promise'],
  reward:'Adrian and Eve promise to stay together'},
 220:{ title:'The Hidden Correspondence', type:'Story Chapter — letters before the alliance fractured', loc:'📚 Tribute: the royal archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and the party',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While continuing their research in Tribute\'s archives, the party discovers letters exchanged between officials of Tribute and Dragonvale shortly before the ancient alliance fractured. Among a collection of unclassified records they find a set of letters that had been misfiled and hidden in a separate ledger. Jade: "These letters match the time just before the alliance broke apart. The handwriting and seals are authentic. They were exchanged between high-ranking officials, not personal correspondence." The letters include travel reports, diplomatic discussions, and private assessments of the situation between the two kingdoms. Sky: "They speak of more than just political disagreements. There were concerns about knowledge, specifically knowledge that should not be lost to time." Devon: "Some of the reports mention unrecorded ruins and restricted research sites. It seems both kingdoms were investigating something beyond the alliance itself." Jade: "Look at this letter... It warns that if the alliance\'s knowledge were preserved, it could expose the kingdoms to a danger they did not yet understand. They believed it was safer to divide the records and let some of the truths be forgotten." One letter reads: "If the knowledge kept within the alliance endures, there are forces beyond our sight that may yet take notice. It is the judgment of this office that certain records must be divided, and that some truths are safer left to time, rather than revealed to a world not yet ready." Sky: "So the fracture was not just political. They were trying to hide something: not from each other, but from what might come in the future." Adrian: "Which explains why so many records were rewritten, destroyed, or scattered. They wanted to ensure that even if the alliance fell, the dangerous knowledge would not remain intact in one place. But these letters prove that someone knew the risk. And they were willing to erase parts of history to prevent it from resurfacing." Jade: "That means there may still be more records hidden somewhere. And whatever they were afraid of... it is not a threat of the past."',
  art:'Pages show: the royal archives (blue fleur-de-lis banners), Jade, Devon, Sky and an archer reading letters, a wax seal with a dragon and one with a fleur-de-lis, a letter with the key quotation, and the party in turn. Adrian and Eve are not drawn (Adrian\'s lines may be Devon\'s or an uncaptioned speaker). The letters make the alliance\'s fracture a deliberate act of dividing dangerous knowledge to hide it from \'forces beyond our sight\'. \'The Hidden Correspondence\' sets up the next arc moves.',
  quote:'"Some truths are safer left to time, rather than revealed to a world not yet ready." — a letter of the alliance',
  events:['A set of misfiled letters between Tribute and Dragonvale officials, just before the alliance fractured', 'Authentic seals and handwriting: official correspondence, not personal', 'Concerns about knowledge that should not be lost, and unrecorded ruins and restricted research sites', 'The alliance\'s knowledge could expose the kingdoms to a danger they did not understand: the records were divided and truths left to be forgotten', 'Why so many records were rewritten, destroyed or scattered', 'There may be more records hidden: the threat is not of the past'],
  purpose:['Reveal why the alliance was divided', 'Point to hidden records and a future threat'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Hidden Correspondence (6 objectives)', 'Register: the alliance divided its records on purpose', 'Historical Route Reconstruction: unrecorded ruins and research sites'],
  reward:'The alliance divided its knowledge on purpose'},
 221:{ title:'An Invitation from the King', type:'Story Chapter — a formal court gathering is called', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the party\'s residence and the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin, Adrian and Eve (a separate invitation)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'King Greyson summons Jade, Adrian, and their companions to a formal court gathering concerning the investigation. Eve receives a separate invitation but offers Adrian little explanation. A royal messenger arrives at the party\'s residence with an invitation from King Greyson: "By order of His Majesty King Greyson, Lady Jade Gold and her companions are requested to attend a formal court gathering at the Imperial Palace." Jade: "The timing suggests this is important. The king rarely calls for a formal gathering." Devon: "It must be related to our findings." Sky: "We should prepare our report and evidence." Eve also receives a separate invitation shortly afterward: "You are invited to attend a different gathering at the Imperial Palace. Details will be provided upon arrival." Adrian: "A separate invitation... Will you be joining them as well?" Eve: "I have my own invitation. It is better this way. I will explain later." Jade: "Eve\'s invitation must be related to the same matter. I wonder what role she is being asked to play." Devon: "It could be a meeting with different officials. The king may want information from multiple perspectives." Sky: "Or he is testing how each of us understood the records. We should be prepared for questions we did not expect." A companion: "Whatever the reason, we present the truth clearly and stay consistent. The more they know now, the safer it will be for what comes next." Later, Jade, Adrian and the party head to the Imperial Palace for the formal court gathering. The palace is more heavily guarded than usual, and officials from different departments have been invited. Inside the main audience hall, King Greyson awaits them, seated upon the imperial throne. Jade, Adrian and their companions take their places, ready to present their report and discuss the next phase of the investigation.',
  art:'Pages show: a royal messenger with a sealed letter, Jade, Devon, Sky and an archer reading it, Adrian reading Eve\'s separate invitation, Eve (dark cloak, blue ribbon) declining to say more, the party walking up to a red-and-gold palace with dragon banners, and King Greyson on the throne. The messenger is the person addressing Jade as \'Lady Jade Gold\'. Eve\'s separate invitation is the hint of her identity. Gameplay: none stated for this chapter.',
  quote:'"I have my own invitation. It is better this way. I will explain later." — Eve',
  events:['A royal messenger brings King Greyson\'s invitation to a formal court gathering at the Imperial Palace', 'Jade: the timing is important; the king rarely calls a formal gathering', 'Eve receives a separate invitation and tells Adrian: "I will explain later"', 'The party agrees to prepare the report and evidence and stay consistent', 'The palace is heavily guarded; officials from different departments are invited', 'Greyson waits on the imperial throne; the party takes its place'],
  purpose:['Call the court gathering', 'Plant Eve\'s separate invitation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: An Invitation from the King (6 objectives)'],
  reward:'The party is summoned to the court gathering'},
 222:{ title:'The Princess\'s Grand Entrance', type:'Story Chapter — Evelyne\'s identity is revealed', loc:'👑 Tribute: the Imperial Palace, the audience hall',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin, Adrian, King Greyson and Princess Evelyne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The court gathering begins as King Greyson and the party assemble to discuss the investigation. Just as the meeting is about to start, a familiar figure makes her entrance: the king\'s younger sister, Princess Evelyne Greyson. The palace doors open, and Princess Evelyne Greyson enters the hall, captivating everyone with her graceful presence. Dressed in elegant royal attire, she moves with the confidence and composure of a true princess. Evelyne: "Imperial Brother. It has been some time." Adrian is astonished to see that Eve Gray is none other than the king\'s younger sister. Adrian: "...!" Greyson: "Welcome, Evelyne. You have kept us waiting." Evelyne: "I apologise, Imperial Brother. There were matters I needed to attend to before joining this gathering." Jade finally understands why Eve knew so much about the palace, its history, and the inner workings of the court. Jade: "A princess... So that\'s the reason." Sky: "That explains a lot." A companion: "She really hid her identity this well..." Adrian: "Eve... You are... Princess Evelyne Greyson?" Evelyne: "I chose to travel under a different name for my own reasons. It allowed me to see the world more freely... and to meet all of you." Adrian: "...You never told me." Evelyne: "I wanted to be with you as myself, not as a princess. And now... the time has come for the truth to be known." With Evelyne\'s true identity now revealed, the investigation takes on new weight: not just a matter between kingdoms, but one that reaches the heart of Tribute itself. The party prepares to share their findings, with the princess now standing beside her imperial brother, as both family and key figure in what comes next.',
  art:'Pages show: Evelyne in a pale-green court gown with a flowered headdress and veil entering a red-and-gold hall, Adrian astonished, King Greyson on the throne, Jade, Sky and the archer reacting, and the party facing the throne with the princess beside the king. This is the REVEAL (the author\'s roadmap put it in ch221-225: it is ch222). The second portrait (the princess) applies from here. The game calls her \'Evelyne\' (the king \'Evelyn\' in the author\'s notes; the page spells Evelyne).',
  quote:'"I wanted to be with you as myself, not as a princess." — Evelyne',
  events:['Princess Evelyne Greyson, the king\'s younger sister, enters the court gathering', 'Adrian is astonished: Eve Gray is the princess', 'Greyson: "You have kept us waiting"; Evelyne apologises: matters to attend to first', 'Jade understands why Eve knew so much of the palace and the court', 'Evelyne: she chose a different name for her own reasons, to see the world freely and to meet them', '"The time has come for the truth to be known"; the investigation reaches the heart of Tribute'],
  purpose:['Reveal Eve Gray as Princess Evelyne Greyson', 'Raise the stakes of the investigation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Princess\'s Grand Entrance (6 objectives)', 'Evelyne\'s identity is revealed: her princess portrait and name apply'],
  reward:'Eve Gray is Princess Evelyne Greyson'},
 223:{ title:'You\'re a Princess?', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian speaks to Evelyne privately', loc:'🌙 Tribute: a palace garden at night',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian and Evelyne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Later that evening, Adrian privately confronts Eve, not with anger, but with genuine disbelief. Adrian: "You\'re a princess? Eve Gray... was actually Princess Evelyne Greyson...?" Evelyne: "Yes. I wanted to see the world beyond the palace walls. To meet people without the weight of my title. To understand what kind of person I am, apart from being a princess." Adrian: "You never told me... You travelled, worked, listened... You carried so much on your own. Weren\'t you afraid?" Evelyne: "I was afraid. But it was worth it. Those experiences gave me a perspective I could never have gained within the palace. They helped me understand our people better... and myself. I\'m still the same person you know. The only thing that\'s different is that you now know my full name." Adrian: "...It doesn\'t change anything. Whether you are Eve Gray or Princess Evelyne, you are still the person I care about." Evelyne: "That\'s all I needed to hear. I was afraid this would change the way you see me. But it seems you understand. My title may belong to the crown, but my heart... has always been my own." Adrian: "You can be a princess, and still be free. And I will be by your side, not because of your title, but because of you." Evelyne: "I\'m grateful I could share this with you. There are still many things I want to see, and I hope... you will continue to walk this path with me. Then let me go forward without hiding anymore. As Princess Evelyne... and as myself." Adrian\'s feelings remain unchanged. Eve no longer needs to hide her identity, and the path ahead is one they will face together. A princess, and yet still herself. The same person. The same feelings. And many more journeys to come.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian (green and gold, a green ribbon) and Evelyne (pale-green court gown with flowers) among lanterns and cherry blossom on a palace terrace under a full moon. The chapter is a quiet conversation; the romance is told, not chosen. NOTE: the comic numbers this chapter 223 though it follows the reveal (222) and precedes the garden scene of 225: \'later that evening\' (it and 225 are the same evening or consecutive).',
  quote:'"My title may belong to the crown, but my heart... has always been my own." — Evelyne',
  events:['Adrian confronts Evelyne privately, with disbelief, not anger', 'Evelyne: she wanted to see the world and meet people without the weight of her title', '"I was afraid. But it was worth it."', 'Adrian: it changes nothing; she is still the person he cares about', '"You can be a princess, and still be free"', 'Evelyne: "let me go forward without hiding anymore"'],
  purpose:['Resolve the reveal between Adrian and Evelyne'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: You\'re a Princess? (5 objectives)'],
  reward:'Adrian accepts that Eve is a princess'},
 224:{ title:'A Princess by Choice', type:'Story Chapter — Evelyne announces her future', loc:'👑 Tribute: the Imperial Palace, the audience hall',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin, Adrian, King Greyson and Evelyne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'At the formal court gathering, Princess Evelyne announces her decision for the future: she will serve the kingdom as a government official rather than accept a political marriage. Before the assembled officials, Princess Evelyne Greyson speaks openly about her intentions, capturing the attention of the entire court. Evelyne: "Imperial Brother, I wish to serve Tribute as a government official. I do not wish to enter a political marriage. My position as a princess gives me responsibilities, but it does not mean my future must be decided through marriage. I wish to use my knowledge, my experiences, and what I have learned beyond the palace to serve the kingdom directly." Greyson: "You have my support. You have always seen more than most. Tribute needs people like you: not just as a princess, but as someone who understands its people, its neighbours, and the changing world." Adrian watches Evelyne with new respect, seeing clearly her determination to shape her own path. Jade: "That\'s so like her. Eve has always wanted to do more than what is expected of her." Devon: "She\'s turning her unique knowledge into something meaningful." Sky: "This will be good for Tribute. Her insight into other kingdoms is a great asset." A companion: "She\'s not rejecting her role as a princess. She\'s choosing a different way to fulfil it." Evelyne: "I understand the responsibilities of my position. I will continue to uphold the honour of the royal family and fulfil my duties as a princess. But I ask for the opportunity to serve through official work: through diplomacy, administration, and the strengthening of our alliance with neighbouring kingdoms." Greyson: "You have not only my permission, but my full support. Tribute will benefit from your talents. Your path is your own, and I will stand beside you." Adrian realises that Evelyne is not just a princess bound by tradition, but a person with her own dreams, courage and sense of responsibility. Today, she stands not just as a princess of Tribute, but as herself, choosing her future with clear eyes and an unshakable heart. With the king\'s support, Evelyne begins a new chapter: one where she serves Tribute not through marriage, but through her own choices.',
  art:'Pages show: Evelyne in pale green before the court officials and Greyson on the throne, close-ups of Greyson, Adrian, Jade, Devon, Sky and the archer, and the party before a skyline of pagoda roofs. Greyson publicly supports her. Gameplay (author): after this chapter Evelyne receives a dedicated Palace interaction: political intelligence, diplomatic investigations and access to confidential reports; Adrian keeps historical research and the Register; their responsibilities stay separate.',
  quote:'"She\'s not rejecting her role as a princess. She\'s choosing a different way to fulfil it." — a companion',
  events:['Evelyne asks to serve Tribute as a government official and refuses a political marriage', 'She will uphold the honour of the royal family and her duties, through diplomacy, administration and strengthening the alliance with neighbouring kingdoms', 'Greyson gives his full support: "Your path is your own, and I will stand beside you"', 'Adrian watches with new respect', 'The party sees it as a different way of fulfilling her role', 'Evelyne begins a new chapter, serving Tribute through her own choices'],
  purpose:['Establish Evelyne\'s official role', 'Unlock her Palace interaction'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Princess by Choice (6 objectives)', 'Evelyne: Palace role unlocked (political intelligence, diplomatic investigations, confidential reports)'],
  reward:'Evelyne becomes a royal court official'},
 225:{ title:'The Scholar\'s Answer', type:'Story Chapter — Adrian\'s answer in the garden', loc:'🌸 Tribute: a lantern-lit garden terrace',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian and Evelyne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'That evening, after the court gathering, Adrian asks Evelyne to meet him in a quiet garden terrace overlooking the lantern-lit city of Tribute. Adrian: "Eve... The woman I met on the road, the one who travelled, argued, laughed and trusted me... That is the woman I love. Even now, knowing you are Princess Evelyne Greyson... it does not change my feelings. If anything, I respect you even more." Evelyne: "I was afraid you would see a different person once you knew the truth. But I am still the same Eve. I chose that life because it let me see the world, and it gave me the chance to meet you. You saw me when I was just Eve... not a princess, not a royal title, and you still chose me." Adrian: "I choose you. All of you. Your dreams, your responsibilities, your stubbornness... and even the crown that comes with them." Evelyne: "I choose you too, Adrian. I am a princess, but I am also myself. And I want to go forward with you, openly, honestly, without hiding anymore." Despite the attention their courtship will attract, Adrian and Evelyne decide to pursue their relationship openly, with honesty and mutual respect. Whatever challenges await, they will face them together, as a princess and a scholar, and as the two people who chose each other beyond titles and expectations. For now, beneath the lanterns and the moonlit sky, they allow themselves a rare moment of peace: just Adrian and Evelyne. A new path lies ahead, one that belongs to them both.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian (green and gold) and Evelyne (pale green court gown with flowers) among white blossoms and lanterns, a kiss, and the two before a moonlit canal with a pagoda skyline. The courtship is now open. Adrian says \'I choose you\': the game does not offer a choice here.',
  quote:'"I choose you. All of you. Your dreams, your responsibilities, your stubbornness... and even the crown that comes with them." — Adrian',
  events:['Adrian asks Evelyne to meet him on a quiet garden terrace over the lantern-lit city', '"The woman I met on the road... that is the woman I love": knowing she is a princess changes nothing', 'Evelyne: she is still the same Eve; she chose that life and it let her meet him', 'They choose each other: "I choose you. All of you."', 'They decide to pursue the relationship openly, with honesty and mutual respect', 'A rare moment of peace under the lanterns and the moon'],
  purpose:['Make the courtship open'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Scholar\'s Answer (6 objectives)', 'Adrian and Evelyne: an open courtship'],
  reward:'Adrian and Evelyne choose each other openly'},
 226:{ title:'A Courtship Without Chains', type:'Story Chapter — the palace reacts to the match', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Adrian, Evelyne, King Greyson, Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'News of Adrian and Evelyne\'s relationship spreads quickly through the palace. While many offer their congratulations, others question whether a scholar is a suitable match for a princess. Courtier: "A scholar? For a princess? He is not from a royal family, nor a military house. Is it wise for His Highness to allow this?" Evelyne: "Rank does not determine my worth, nor my future. I will not be married off for political convenience. I choose my own path." Another courtier: "But a princess must think of alliance and stability. Feelings are fleeting. Will a scholar be able to protect her? Provide for her?" Adrian: "I understand their concerns. But I will not disappoint your trust." Greyson: "Evelyne has always been someone who thinks deeply. She sees people for who they are, not for their rank. I support her decision." Evelyne: "I am not asking for special treatment. I only ask to be allowed to choose. I will serve Tribute as a government official. I will continue to learn, investigate and contribute to the kingdom. My relationship with Adrian does not change my duties." Greyson: "You have already done so much for me... and for this kingdom. I am proud to stand beside you." Evelyne: "Whatever challenges come, we will face them together." Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi are glad for them, offering their quiet support. They have both fought for the right to be themselves. And now, they are choosing it, together. Not everyone approves, and there will continue to be obstacles, but Evelyne refuses to let tradition or rank decide her personal future. With the king\'s support and the loyalty of their friends, Adrian and Evelyne move forward as partners in both love and purpose.',
  art:'Pages show: courtiers whispering in red-and-gold halls, Evelyne answering them, Greyson on the throne, Adrian, a hand on a sleeve, Jade (red), Devon, Sky, a green-haired man in green with a quiver (Levi or Rin) and a dark-haired man smiling, and Adrian and Evelyne at a balcony at sunset. The scholar\'s rank question matters later for the wedding: Adrian becomes Imperial Prince Consort through marriage (the author\'s decision). \'His Highness\' in the courtiers\' line is King Greyson.',
  quote:'"I am not asking for special treatment. I only ask to be allowed to choose." — Evelyne',
  events:['News of the relationship spreads; many congratulate, others doubt a scholar is a match for a princess', 'Evelyne: "Rank does not determine my worth, nor my future. I will not be married off for political convenience."', 'Courtiers: a princess must think of alliance and stability; can a scholar protect and provide for her?', 'Greyson supports her decision; Adrian promises not to disappoint his trust', 'Evelyne\'s relationship does not change her duties as a government official', 'Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi offer quiet support; Adrian and Evelyne move forward as partners in love and purpose'],
  purpose:['Show the court\'s doubt and the king\'s support'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Courtship Without Chains (6 objectives)'],
  reward:'The king and friends support Adrian and Evelyne'},
 227:{ title:'The Dragonvale Accord', type:'Story Chapter — a surviving agreement between the ancient kingdoms', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale: the royal archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon'], charsNote:'Jade and Devon',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade and Devon return to Dragonvale to investigate a surviving agreement between the ancient kingdoms. They discover that the alliance originally included safeguards intended to prevent the misuse of magical preservation systems. They return to Dragonvale, following records that mention a surviving alliance agreement between the ancient kingdoms. It has been a long time since Devon last returned. The city still feels familiar, and yet changed. Jade: "These are the original records. Look at the seal and the script. This predates the Dima–Xima crisis." Devon: "The wording is very clear. It was a multi-kingdom agreement, including Tribute, to prevent the misuse of magical preservation systems." Jade: "This is the Dragonvale Accord. It was signed by multiple kingdoms to ensure balance." The accord established three key safeguards: knowledge must be shared among kingdoms; preservation systems cannot be used to control people or manipulate entire populations; any significant use requires multi-kingdom approval and oversight. Jade: "So the preservation systems were never meant to be used for personal power or to manipulate entire populations. There were restrictions, oversight, and a shared custody for a reason." Devon: "Parts of the agreement were deliberately destroyed in later generations. Someone removed these sections. Which means the current records are incomplete on purpose." There are also references to monitoring committees and shared custody locations. The evidence confirms that the ancient alliance included safeguards specifically designed to prevent the misuse of magical preservation technology. Jade and Devon prepare to share what they have found, knowing that the full truth may still be hidden across the other kingdoms.',
  art:'Pages show: Dragonvale\'s waterfall city with blue-and-gold dragon banners, Jade (red) and Devon (fur collar) walking in, the original accord with three circular sigils (a tree, a sun and a dragon) and a red wax seal, and the two reading in the archive. Only Jade and Devon go (the rest of the party stays in Tribute). The three safeguards are listed on the page. The comic says it \'predates the Dima-Xima crisis\'.',
  quote:'"Someone removed these sections. Which means the current records are incomplete on purpose." — Devon',
  events:['Jade and Devon return to Dragonvale to follow records of a surviving alliance agreement', 'The original records predate the Dima–Xima crisis: a multi-kingdom agreement including Tribute, to prevent misuse of magical preservation systems', 'The Dragonvale Accord\'s three safeguards: knowledge shared among kingdoms; no use to control people or manipulate populations; significant use needs multi-kingdom approval and oversight', 'References to monitoring committees and shared custody locations', 'Parts of the accord were deliberately destroyed in later generations', 'The full truth may be hidden across the other kingdoms'],
  purpose:['Reveal the alliance\'s safeguards', 'Prove the records are incomplete on purpose'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Dragonvale Accord (6 objectives)', 'Record: The Dragonvale Accord'],
  reward:'The alliance had safeguards against misuse of preservation systems'},
 228:{ title:'The Price of Silence', type:'Story Chapter — two reasons records were concealed', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale: the royal archives',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party discovers evidence that certain historical records were deliberately concealed to prevent dangerous knowledge from being exploited. However, other alterations appear to have protected powerful families rather than the kingdoms themselves. In Dragonvale\'s royal archives, Jade, Devon, Sky and Levi examine records related to the ancient alliance. Devon: "These records are older than we expected. Parts of the text have been removed. Someone altered these deliberately." Jade: "This section should detail the preservation systems and their restrictions... but it has been deliberately torn out." Certain records were concealed to prevent dangerous knowledge from being exploited. Devon: "The missing information matches the safeguards mentioned in other kingdoms\' records. If this knowledge fell into the wrong hands, it could be misused to preserve people or manipulate entire populations." Sky: "These safeguards were meant to limit how the preservation systems could be used. Removing this information would make the technology far more dangerous." Levi: "But look here. These other sections were altered for a different reason. They are not about safeguards. They protect the interests of specific families." Other alterations appear to have been made to protect powerful families rather than the kingdoms. Jade: "Someone chose what to hide and what to keep, shaping the narrative for their own benefit. The kingdom was protected in part... but powerful families also used these changes to maintain their position. The truth has been buried for a long time. Now we need to understand who made these changes... and what they are still trying to protect today."',
  art:'Pages show: Jade (red), Devon (fur collar), Sky (blue) and an archer (Levi/Rin) at the archive table; a torn record with three sigils (tree, sun, dragon); black bars striking out passages and a leaf-emblem seal of a family; the four in the stacks. Gameplay (author): Diplomatic Investigation: compare official agreements with confidential correspondence to decide which historical decisions were protective and which politically motivated. Built as \'Protective or Political?\' in Evelyne\'s Palace tab.',
  quote:'"Someone chose what to hide and what to keep, shaping the narrative for their own benefit." — Jade',
  events:['Dragonvale\'s archives: older than expected, parts removed, altered deliberately', 'A section on the preservation systems and their restrictions was torn out', 'Some concealment was protective: dangerous knowledge could be exploited if it fell into the wrong hands', 'Other alterations protected the interests of specific families, not the kingdoms', 'Someone chose what to hide and what to keep; powerful families used the changes to hold their position', 'Next: who made the changes, and what they still protect today'],
  purpose:['Separate protective from political concealment', 'Open the Diplomatic Investigation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Price of Silence (6 objectives)', 'Diplomatic Investigation: Protective or Political? (Evelyne\'s Palace tab)'],
  reward:'Some records were hidden to protect, others to protect families'},
 229:{ title:'A Question of Marriage', type:'Story Chapter — the engagement', loc:'📚 Tribute: the imperial library',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian and Evelyne',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Adrian asks Evelyne whether she truly wishes to marry him, knowing that their marriage may attract political scrutiny. Evelyne answers that she has already chosen him. Their engagement is established through mutual agreement rather than royal arrangement. After the palace gathering, Adrian meets Evelyne in a quieter part of the imperial library to speak openly about their future. Adrian: "Evelyne, I want to ask you something plainly. Do you truly wish to marry me? This marriage may attract political scrutiny." Evelyne: "I am aware of that. I understand what it could bring." Adrian: "Some will say a scholar is not a suitable match for a princess. They will question my rank, my influence, and whether I can protect you. Are you certain you still wish to proceed?" Evelyne: "I have already chosen you, Adrian. Not because of your title or position, but because of the person you are: the man who walks beside me, who listens, and who sees me. I am not entering this marriage because it is expected of me, nor because it brings an alliance or political advantage. I choose this because I want you, and because I believe in the future we can build together." Adrian: "Evelyne... Thank you. Your trust means more to me than any position ever could. Then let this be our agreement: not a royal arrangement, but a promise between the two of us. Together, we will face whatever comes, with honesty and as equals. I will stand by you, as your husband, not for what it gives me, but for who you are." Evelyne: "And I will stand beside you, Adrian, not as a princess above you, but as your partner in every step ahead." Their engagement is established through mutual agreement rather than royal arrangement. Though questions and opposition will certainly follow, Evelyne has made her choice, and Adrian has accepted it as a partner, not as a favour from the throne.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian (navy and gold, writing) and Evelyne (pale green) in the imperial library among white blossoms and red pillars, hands joined, foreheads together, and the two in a flowered palace. This is a fixed story development (the author: not a player-choice romance route). Adrian wears navy-and-gold robes here, not his green-and-gold.',
  quote:'"Let this be our agreement: not a royal arrangement, but a promise between the two of us." — Adrian',
  events:['After the palace gathering, Adrian asks Evelyne plainly whether she wishes to marry him, knowing the political scrutiny', 'Evelyne has already chosen him: not for title or position, but for the person he is', '"Not a royal arrangement, but a promise between the two of us"', 'They will face what comes with honesty and as equals', 'The engagement is established by mutual agreement; opposition will follow'],
  purpose:['Establish the engagement as a fixed story milestone'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Question of Marriage (5 objectives)', 'Relationship milestone: Adrian and Evelyne are engaged (fixed story, not a player choice)'],
  reward:'Adrian and Evelyne are engaged'},
 230:{ title:'The King\'s Blessing', type:'Story Chapter — Greyson blesses the marriage; Jade remembers', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Adrian, Evelyne, King Greyson, Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Adrian formally approaches Greyson regarding the marriage. Greyson, already aware of his sister\'s wishes, gives his blessing. Jade shares a warm moment with Adrian as they reflect on how much their lives have changed since childhood. Adrian: "Your Majesty, I wish to formally request your blessing to marry Princess Evelyne." Greyson: "I was already aware of your intentions from Evelyne herself. You have my blessing." Evelyne: "Thank you, Brother." Greyson: "Adrian, I have watched you grow from a serious young scholar into a man of principle. Evelyne has found in you someone who respects her mind, her choices and her path. That is more than I could ask for." Adrian: "Thank you, Your Majesty. I will continue to serve Tribute and support Evelyne, as I always have." Evelyne: "With your blessing, I feel even more certain about the future. Thank you for understanding, Brother." Greyson: "You have always been strong, Eve. Choose the life you truly want. That is what matters most." Jade: "It\'s been a long time, Adrian. I can remember you so much better now." Adrian: "You remember...?" Jade: "Parts of those years were always fuzzy since I nearly drowned, but they\'ve become clearer recently. With Devon\'s help, and the Dragonvale tonics I was given after my marriage, I\'ve been taking herbal tonics and looking after my health. I can remember more of when we were younger, before you left for your studies. I remember copying books with you in the old study, and how you always explained things patiently, even when I asked too many questions." Adrian: "You were always curious and determined, Jade. Even then, you cared about the people around you. Some things don\'t change." Jade: "So much has changed since those days. We were just children then, with different burdens and simpler worries." Now we stand here, as a king, a princess, a scholar, a guard, a healer and a trusted friend, choosing our own paths, and still finding our way back to each other.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian bowing before Greyson on the throne with Evelyne beside him; close-ups of Greyson and Adrian; Evelyne and Jade (red) with Adrian; flashback panels of Jade and Adrian as children copying books in the old study; and the group (Jade, Evelyne, Greyson, Devon, Sky, an archer) at the end. MEMORY: in the comic Jade says she can \'actually remember\' Adrian now. The author confirms this is a slip: the childhood drowning cost her some memories, but never her memory of Adrian. In-game Jade always knew her brother. The drowning (the transmigration, a spoiler kept out of game text) merged her memories with a newcomer\'s, leaving them fuzzy but not lost; Dragonvale tonics, given after her marriage and sometimes sent as royal tribute, are clearing them, so she now remembers Adrian and their childhood better.',
  quote:'"I can remember you so much better now." — Jade',
  events:['Adrian formally asks Greyson for his blessing to marry Evelyne', 'Greyson already knew and blesses the marriage: she has found someone who respects her mind, choices and path', 'Greyson to Evelyne: "Choose the life you truly want"', 'Jade remembers Adrian better: Dragonvale tonics are clearing her fuzzy childhood', 'They recall copying books in the old study as children', 'A king, a princess, a scholar, a guard, a healer and a friend, finding their way back to each other'],
  purpose:['Give the marriage the king\'s blessing', 'Mark Jade\'s clearer childhood memories'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The King\'s Blessing (6 objectives)', 'Greyson\'s blessing: the wedding can be planned', 'Jade: remembers Adrian better'],
  reward:'The king blesses the marriage'},
 231:{ title:'The Last Witness of the Accord', type:'Story Chapter — a testimony preserved outside the official archives', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale: a sealed chamber in the ruins',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While examining a lesser-known section of Dragonvale\'s ruins, Jade finds a sealed storage chamber not listed in the official archives. Party: "This wasn\'t recorded in the main archive. It looks like a private archive. The preservation magic is very old, but still intact. Someone intentionally hid this." Jade discovers an ancient testimony preserved outside the official archives. It is a personal testimony written by a scribe who was present during the later years of the alliance. It says the alliance did not end in a single event. Instead, each kingdom made separate decisions over many years. Some withdrew support due to internal crises. Others reduced cooperation after disputes over the use of preservation systems. By the end, there was no united agreement left, only fragments. Devon: "So it wasn\'t betrayal by one kingdom alone. It was a slow unravelling." Sky: "Each kingdom was facing its own pressure. Some feared the preservation systems were becoming too powerful. They wanted stricter control." Levi: "And some used the situation to protect their own interests. These records make that clear." There are also notes about the safeguards: the alliance originally included restrictions to prevent misuse of the preservation systems, but some kingdoms pushed to weaken those restrictions over time. The final records mention repeated requests to expand access, especially from a few powerful families. When the other kingdoms refused, they began operating separately, and the alliance gradually lost its purpose. Jade: "So the dissolution was not inevitable. It was the result of many choices. Some were made out of fear. Some out of ambition. And some to protect specific families rather than the kingdoms themselves." The testimony provides a new perspective on how the alliance changed, and why the safeguards were no longer enforced. It also raises new questions about which families were involved, and what records may still be hidden in other kingdoms. Jade and the party decide to make copies of the testimony, and to compare it with records from the other kingdoms to understand the full timeline.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade (red), Devon (fur collar), Sky (blue hair) and Levi (green, with arrows) reading in a lit archive with waterfalls behind; the scribe\'s testimony with a drawing of a drowned-looking city; a map of the old kingdoms. The comic says \'Dragonvale\'s ruins\'; the party matches chapters 228 and 232. First-pass note: the earlier pages say records were concealed; this one is the first personal testimony.',
  quote:'"It was not betrayal by one kingdom alone. It was a slow unravelling." — Devon',
  events:['Jade finds a sealed storage chamber not listed in the official archives: a private archive', 'A personal testimony by a scribe present in the alliance\'s later years', 'The alliance ended not in one event but in many separate decisions over many years', 'Some kingdoms withdrew support in crises; others reduced cooperation over the use of preservation systems', 'The alliance originally included restrictions against misuse, but some kingdoms pushed to weaken them', 'Repeated requests to expand access, especially from a few powerful families', 'Jade and the party copy the testimony to compare it with other kingdoms\' records'],
  purpose:['Find testimony preserved outside the official archives', 'Show the dissolution was a series of decisions, not one betrayal'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Last Witness of the Accord (5 objectives)', 'Testimony: the scribe of the alliance\'s later years'],
  reward:'A witness preserved outside the official archives'},
 232:{ title:'What the Kingdoms Forgot', type:'Story Chapter — reconstructing the alliance\'s history', loc:'🐉 Dragonvale: the archive',
  chars:['jade', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade reconstructs part of the ancient alliance\'s history. The kingdoms once cooperated to contain magical corruption and preserve dangerous knowledge, but fear, political ambition and mistrust eventually fractured their cooperation. Using the testimony and fragmentary records, Jade begins to piece together the forgotten history of the ancient alliance. Jade: "So they did work together at the beginning. Their goal was to contain magical corruption and preserve dangerous knowledge. They understood how destructive that knowledge could be. But somewhere along the way... something changed." The early records describe a genuine alliance. They shared resources, research and containment methods across kingdoms. They built preservation systems with safeguards to prevent misuse. They created seals, archives and independent oversight to ensure that no single kingdom could exploit the knowledge. At that time the threat of magical corruption was real. Several regions had already suffered catastrophic incidents; the kingdoms knew that uncontrolled use of certain forms of magic could destroy entire populations and landscapes. But over time, fear grew. Each kingdom began to prioritise its own security and wanted more control over the preserved knowledge. Political ambition also played a role: some kingdoms sought greater access, while others wanted to restrict it from their rivals. Disputes over who should hold certain records and who could authorise their use became more frequent. Mistrust slowly replaced cooperation. Incidents were exaggerated or concealed to justify breaking the existing agreements, and in some cases kingdoms used the threat of corruption for their own political gain. Eventually the alliance began to fracture. There was no single event. It was a series of decisions: withdrawn support, restricted information, separate research and the establishment of independent preservation systems. Each kingdom made choices based on its own fears and ambitions, and over time the united purpose was lost. What remained were fragments of agreements, altered records and selective histories. And some of those alterations were not only to protect the kingdoms. They also served to protect powerful families and their own interests. That is why certain records were concealed or changed. Jade: "They were trying to contain a real danger. But fear and ambition made them forget why they started. In trying to protect the world, they ended up protecting their own power instead. We need to understand this history clearly, because the same fears, ambitions and mistrust still exist today. The more we learn, the better prepared we will be for what comes next."',
  art:'Pages show: the same four at the archive table; the early alliance (a council of robed figures, a drawn compass rose); a dark panel of a magical catastrophe; kings arguing; a stone statue of two figures; a torn compass map; and a sunset over a river-city. This is a chapter of reconstruction and no new location is shown. The text says \'the threat was real\': it is the author\'s counterpoint to the idea that the whole alliance was a scheme.',
  quote:'"In trying to protect the world, they ended up protecting their own power instead." — Jade',
  events:['Jade pieces together the alliance\'s history from the testimony and fragments', 'It began as a real alliance: shared resources, research and containment methods; preservation systems with safeguards; seals, archives and independent oversight', 'The threat of magical corruption was real: several regions had suffered catastrophic incidents', 'Fear, political ambition and mistrust slowly replaced cooperation', 'Incidents were exaggerated or concealed to justify breaking agreements', 'The alliance fractured through a series of decisions, not a single event', 'Some alterations also protected powerful families: that is why certain records were concealed or changed'],
  purpose:['Reconstruct part of the alliance\'s history', 'Show it was a real danger that fear and ambition misused'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: What the Kingdoms Forgot (6 objectives)', 'Alliance board: history partially reconstructed'],
  reward:'Part of the alliance\'s history reconstructed'},
 233:{ title:'The Forgotten Alliance', type:'Story Chapter — Tribute and Dragonvale begin restoring cooperation', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the royal study',
  chars:['jade', 'devon'], charsNote:'Jade, Devon and King Greyson',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade presents her findings to Greyson and Devon. Tribute and Dragonvale agree to begin carefully restoring historical cooperation. However, the impossible Register entry remains unresolved, suggesting that the alliance\'s forgotten systems may still be active. In the royal study, Jade presents the results of her research on the ancient alliance to King Greyson and Devon. Jade: "These records show that the alliance was built over many years. It was a network of agreements, not a single treaty. Each kingdom contributed in different ways." Greyson: "So they worked together to contain magical corruption and preserve dangerous knowledge. A remarkable system... and a fragile one." Jade: "But over time, fear, political ambition and mistrust began to erode their cooperation. Some kingdoms withdrew support due to internal crises. Others restricted information to gain an advantage. In the end, the alliance fractured, not because of a single betrayal, but a series of decisions." Jade pieces together the timeline using testimonies, marginal notes and hidden records. Devon: "This changes how we understand the past. We were taught that the alliance fell suddenly, but the truth is far more complex. It also explains why certain records were altered. The knowledge they were trying to contain was real. Even now, remnants of that corruption still exist. If the old systems are still active, it means the threat has not disappeared." Jade: "That is why I believe Tribute and Dragonvale should begin restoring historical cooperation. We can start with information sharing, joint research, and mutual safeguards. It will not be a full alliance yet, but a first step, built on understanding rather than fear." Greyson: "I agree. Tribute will support this. We will reopen channels for research and discussion, and work with Dragonvale to establish proper guidelines. We cannot undo the past, but we can prevent the same mistakes from happening again." However, one entry in the ancient Register remains impossible to explain. The name, date and recorded event do not match any known history. Jade: "This entry shouldn\'t exist... It describes a meeting that never happened, with people who could not have been there. It suggests that the alliance\'s forgotten systems may still be active... but we don\'t know how, or why." Greyson: "This means there may be more to the alliance than we realise. If these systems are still functioning, we need to find out how to access them, and what their purpose is now. We should proceed carefully, but we cannot ignore this." For now, Tribute and Dragonvale take the first steps toward restoring their historical cooperation, with hope, caution and a shared purpose. But the impossible Register entry remains unresolved: a reminder that the alliance\'s forgotten systems may still be active, and that there are still secrets waiting to be uncovered.',
  art:'Pages show: Jade (red), Devon and King Greyson (crowned, black-and-gold dragon robes) in the royal study with cherry blossoms; a timeline map of connected cities and compass roses; the ancient Register open to the impossible entry; and the three seen from behind at the window at the end. The comic says \'Devon\' here (the fur-collared man); the Register is not shown in numbers: we keep it at 5 of 15 resolved, as the author confirmed.',
  quote:'"We cannot undo the past, but we can prevent the same mistakes from happening again." — Greyson',
  events:['In the royal study, Jade presents her research to Greyson and Devon', 'The alliance was a network of agreements built over many years, not a single treaty', 'Devon: the fall was not sudden, and remnants of that corruption still exist', 'Jade proposes restoring historical cooperation: information sharing, joint research, mutual safeguards', 'Greyson agrees: Tribute will reopen channels and work with Dragonvale on guidelines', 'One Register entry remains impossible: a meeting that never happened, with people who could not have been there', 'The impossible entry suggests the alliance\'s forgotten systems may still be active'],
  purpose:['Begin restoring historical cooperation between Tribute and Dragonvale', 'Leave the impossible Register entry unresolved'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Forgotten Alliance (6 objectives)', 'Tribute and Dragonvale: historical cooperation begins', 'The impossible Register entry: unresolved, carried into Arc X'],
  reward:'Tribute and Dragonvale begin restoring cooperation'},
 234:{ title:'The Wedding Beneath the Blossoms', type:'Story Chapter — the royal wedding of Adrian and Evelyne', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian, Evelyne, King Greyson, Jade and guests from both kingdoms',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Adrian and Evelyne marry in Tribute. The ceremony celebrates their long separation, reunion, and their decision to choose one another freely. Jade and Greyson witness the union. Tribute prepares a grand ceremony for Adrian and Evelyne, a union born not of politics, but of their own choice. After years of separation, misunderstandings and different paths, they have finally found their way back to each other. Adrian: "I choose you. Not for duty, but because I want you." Evelyne: "I choose you too, Adrian. With all that I have learned, with a clear heart, and my own will." Adrian: "Let us face the future together." Evelyne: "No more separation." They exchange vows before the assembled court, witnessed by family, friends and allies from both kingdoms. Their union symbolises a new beginning, not just for themselves, but for the growing friendship between Tribute and Dragonvale. Jade watches the ceremony with a warm heart, knowing how far they have both come. Jade: "They finally have the happiness they deserve." Greyson: "Adrian, you have made a wise choice. Evelyne, you are not only a princess, but also a person of courage and compassion. I give you both my blessing." In choosing each other freely, Adrian and Evelyne prove that love can exist alongside responsibility, and that it can be a source of strength rather than a political constraint. Surrounded by friends, family and allies, they begin this new chapter together. Guests: "May your life together be as bright as these blossoms." "This is a beautiful day. I\'m happy for both of you." "Your happiness brings hope to us all." Adrian and Evelyne: "Thank you, all of you, for being here today." Two people who once walked separate roads have chosen to walk the rest of their lives together. Beneath the blossoms of Tribute, their marriage is not just a union of two hearts, but a promise of a brighter future. With the support of their kingdoms and friends, they step into the future, together, and on their own terms.',
  art:'Pages show: a grand ceremony hall in red and gold under cherry blossoms with a large double-happiness banner; Adrian and Evelyne in red robes with gold dragons, the vows and a close embrace; Jade (red) watching; Greyson (crowned, black-and-gold dragon robes) giving the blessing; and the group seated: Jade, the couple, Greyson, Sky (blue hair), and an archer (Levi) as guests. This page replaces the first quicker version. Jade\'s gown in the group panel looks cream rather than red: not changed in the text.',
  quote:'"I choose you. Not for duty, but because I want you." — Adrian',
  events:['Tribute prepares a grand ceremony: a union born not of politics but of their own choice', 'After years of separation, misunderstandings and different paths, they find their way back to each other', 'Adrian: "I choose you. Not for duty, but because I want you." Evelyne: "I choose you too, Adrian. With all that I have learned, with a clear heart, and my own will."', 'They exchange vows before the assembled court, witnessed by family, friends and allies from both kingdoms', 'Greyson: "Adrian, you have made a wise choice... I give you both my blessing."', 'Love can exist alongside responsibility, a source of strength rather than a political constraint', 'Their union symbolises the growing friendship between Tribute and Dragonvale', 'The kingdom\'s wedding celebrations begin (14 days)'],
  purpose:['Celebrate the royal wedding', 'Mark Evelyne\'s and Adrian\'s freely chosen union'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Wedding Beneath the Blossoms (5 objectives)', 'The royal wedding celebrations: 14 days of drops and decorations', 'Adrian and Evelyne: wedding portraits for 14 days'],
  reward:'The royal wedding of Adrian and Evelyne'},
 235:{ title:'Two Hearts, One Kingdom', type:'Story Chapter — a new chapter at the Tribute Palace; the alliance reaches further', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade'], charsNote:'Adrian, Evelyne, Jade and King Greyson',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the wedding, Adrian and Evelyne begin a new chapter together at the Tribute Palace. Their union does not change who they are, but allows them to support one another while continuing their separate official responsibilities. As husband and wife, Adrian and Evelyne share a home, but they each continue their own duties, bound not by obligation, but by mutual respect and trust. Evelyne resumes her work as a government official, using her insight and experience to strengthen Tribute\'s administration and its place among the island kingdoms. Adrian continues to represent Tribute in diplomatic affairs, working to maintain alliance ties and prepare for the challenges ahead. Amid their busy schedules, they find comfort in the simple moments: sharing meals, quiet conversation, and a home filled with the warmth they once longed for. Meanwhile, Jade receives new information from her visions and research. Jade: "The mechanisms of the forgotten alliance do not end here... There are traces in other regions. So the alliance still has surviving links beyond Tribute and Dragonvale. That means there is more we need to understand." Jade reports her findings to King Greyson, who recognises the significance of the discovery. Jade: "These records suggest the alliance\'s mechanisms may be connected to other kingdoms and regions beyond this island. We will need to investigate further." Greyson: "Then we prepare carefully. This may change more than just Tribute and Dragonvale. You have done well, Jade. Continue your research, and we will look into this together in time." The fragments point to distant lands, old trade routes, and hidden locations once tied to the forgotten alliance. There are still many questions, and this is only the beginning of what lies beyond. For now, Adrian and Evelyne choose to focus on the present, building their life together, serving Tribute in their own ways, and facing the future side by side. Jade knows there is still a long road ahead. The forgotten alliance\'s mechanisms extend beyond this island, and new journeys await. But with family, friends and allies beside her, she is ready to uncover the truth, one step at a time. Two hearts have found one another, and a kingdom steps into a brighter future. Beyond these shores, new chapters wait, with new allies, new challenges, and a world that is far larger than any of them once imagined.',
  art:'Pages show: Adrian and Evelyne in red dragon robes at a desk with a scroll; a cat in Evelyne\'s arms; Evelyne reading and Adrian profiled (the latter in red robes); Jade reading new findings; Jade and Greyson (crowned, black-and-gold robes) discussing; an old map with a compass rose and ships; and the palace terrace at sunset with the couple, Greyson, Sky (blue hair), and an archer seen from behind. This page replaces the first quicker version. Jade says her findings come from \'visions and research\': the cat is unnamed and not built. Greyson\'s line \'beyond this island\' is kept.',
  quote:'"Two hearts have found one another, and a kingdom steps into a brighter future."',
  events:['Adrian and Evelyne begin a new chapter at the Tribute Palace: their union does not change who they are', 'They share a home but each continue their own duties, bound by mutual respect and trust', 'Evelyne resumes her work as a government official; Adrian continues to represent Tribute in diplomatic affairs', 'Simple moments: shared meals, quiet conversation, a home filled with warmth', 'Jade receives new information from her visions and research: the alliance\'s mechanisms do not end at Tribute and Dragonvale', 'Jade reports to Greyson: "We will need to investigate further." Greyson: "Then we prepare carefully."', 'Fragments point to distant lands, old trade routes and hidden locations; this is only the beginning'],
  purpose:['Close Arc IX', 'Open the mystery beyond the Fifteen for Arc X'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Two Hearts, One Kingdom (5 objectives)', 'Palace: Adrian (Royal Scholar) and Evelyne (Court Official) both stay available', 'Arc IX complete'],
  reward:'Arc IX complete; the alliance reaches beyond Tribute and Dragonvale'},
 236:{ title:'The Season She Remembered', type:'Story Chapter — Sera misses home', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera and an unnamed cat',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the wedding, life at the Tribute Palace gradually returns to its usual rhythm. The court is busy, friends and allies remain close, and new preparations begin for the next stage of their journey. As the days pass, Jade notices that Sera has become unusually quiet. Where she once joined every conversation with a smile, she now often falls silent, her gaze distant. Sometimes she lingers by the balcony, watching the mountains, as if listening for something only she can hear. It begins with small things: a seasonal dish she mentions in passing, a type of flower that reminds her of home, and a festival date that is approaching. Sera: "This is similar... but not quite the same as the rice cakes we have in Altan. We usually add osmanthus and preserved fruits. The scent fills the whole town..." She hums an old melody under her breath, stopping when others enter the room. Jade recognises it as a song Sera once mentioned from her homeland. Jade: "Sera... you\'ve been very quiet these past few days. Is something troubling you?" Sera: "...I think I just miss home. It\'s this season. In Altan, we would be preparing for the Spring Lantern Festival. At this time, the streets would be filled with lanterns and music... My mother would be busy with the temple offerings, and my brother would argue with the guards about the parade route again. Even the food... it just tastes different when you\'re home." Sera\'s expression softens as she speaks of her brother, the crown prince, remembering happier times. "My brother always said the lanterns were a symbol that even when we are apart, we are still under the same sky." Jade: "It\'s natural to miss home. You\'ve been with us for so long now, but Altan will always be a part of you." Sera: "Thank you, Jade. I didn\'t realise I\'ve been acting so distant. It\'s just... sometimes the memories come unexpectedly." Jade: "Then let\'s make a plan. When the time is right, we\'ll find a way for you to return to Altan. Until then, we can still celebrate this season here, with our own lanterns, our own food, and our own version of home."',
  art:'Pages show: Sera with silver-white hair in a navy-and-gold robe (see the hair mismatch below), Jade in red, the festival food and a lantern-lit bridge, a grey-and-white cat on the table, and a flashback of Sera as a child laughing with her brother (brown-haired, in gold-and-white). The brother is called the crown prince on this page. HAIR: from this chapter to ch244 Sera is drawn with silver-white hair at rest; ch245-246 say her resting state is golden (white only when she channels the inheritance), and the game portrait is golden: the earlier pages are likely to be regenerated.',
  quote:'"Even when we are apart, we are still under the same sky." — Sera\'s brother',
  events:['After the wedding, life at the palace returns to its usual rhythm', 'Jade notices Sera has become quiet and distant', 'Small things: a seasonal dish, a flower, an approaching festival, a half-hummed melody', 'Sera: "I think I just miss home." Altan would be preparing for the Spring Lantern Festival', 'Her brother, the crown prince: the lanterns are a symbol that even apart, they are under the same sky', 'Jade promises to find a way for her to return to Altan, and to celebrate the season at the palace until then'],
  purpose:['Show that Sera misses home', 'Set up the journey to Altan'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Season She Remembered (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sera misses Altan'},
 237:{ title:'A Letter from Altan', type:'Story Chapter — an ordinary letter from home', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In the days that follow, Sera receives a letter from her family in Altan. It is an ordinary letter, filled with familiar news, and exactly what she needed. A letter arrives from Altan, carried by a merchant caravan. Seeing her family\'s familiar seal, Sera feels her heart quicken. The letter reads: "Dearest Sera, Mother sends her love and hopes you are in good health. The garden peaches have bloomed early this year, and the palace is lively with preparations for the Spring Festival. Your little cousins ask about you often. Father says the new tea from the southern estates would be to your liking... We all look forward to the day you can return home. With love, Mother." The letter is filled with familiar news: family, seasonal events and daily life. There is no mention of danger or urgent matters. And that, more than anything, brings her comfort. Sera: "They sound well... The garden is blooming, my little cousins are as lively as ever, and Mother is still worrying about whether I am eating enough. It\'s such an ordinary letter, but it makes me so happy. I miss them. I miss the palace, the festivals, the food, the songs, and the familiar streets. Sometimes... I just want to be home again." Jade: "Of course you should go. You don\'t need a grand reason. Wanting to see your family is reason enough." Sera: "Thank you, Jade. That means a lot." The party gathers around the table: "It will be good for you to spend time with your family again." Sera: "I\'ve missed Altan\'s food so much. The peach pastries, the spiced lamb, and the jasmine tea..." "Shall we make a list of everything you want to eat?" "Not just the food. I want to walk through the markets, hear the songs, and see the mountains again." "Then let\'s plan our departure." With the decision made, the party begins preparations to travel to Altan. This time, Sera returns home not because of a crisis, but because she genuinely misses her family and the place that has always been part of her. A new journey begins, one filled with familiar faces, long-awaited reunions, and the countless moments Sera has been longing for.',
  art:'Pages show: Sera with the letter (the family seal is a gold wax seal), the handwritten letter itself, and the party at a long table with a map and two cats (one grey, one dark): Devon (black-gold), Jade, Sera, Sky (blue hair) and a green-robed man. The letter says the Spring Festival, the page 236 says the Spring Lantern Festival: treated as one festival. No danger in the letter: kept as written.',
  quote:'"It\'s such an ordinary letter, but it makes me so happy." — Sera',
  events:['A letter arrives from Altan by merchant caravan, with her family\'s seal', 'Familiar news: the garden peaches, palace preparations for the Spring Festival, her little cousins, a new tea', 'No mention of danger or urgent matters: it comforts her', 'Sera: "Sometimes... I just want to be home again." Jade: "Wanting to see your family is reason enough."', 'The party makes a list of Altan food and plans the departure', 'Sera returns home not because of a crisis, but because she misses her family'],
  purpose:['Give Sera a reason to go home that is not a crisis'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Letter from Altan (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The decision to go to Altan'},
 238:{ title:'The Princess Who Left', type:'Story Chapter — Sera tells Jade about her brother', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade and Sera (flashbacks of Sera and her brother)',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'As preparations for the journey to Altan begin, Sera finally tells Jade more about her homeland, and about the older brother who has always been both her greatest support and her greatest headache. Jade: "You\'ve mentioned your brother before, but never in detail. What is he like?" Sera: "He\'s only a year or two older than me, but he\'s always been like a companion rather than just a prince. We grew up together, so in many ways he feels more like a brother than a distant royal figure. He has always looked out for me, no matter how much trouble he gets into. He would sneak me out of the palace to see the gardens, the river, and the spring blossoms when we were younger. He loves adventure, horses and falcons. He would include me in his plans, even if the court thought it inappropriate. He is brilliant, but also impulsive. He is always chasing new ideas. He sees possibilities everywhere, but he also runs into obstacles just as often. He can be frustrating at times. He disappears for weeks with barely a message, or decides to visit remote villages, or gets involved in causes the court dislikes. But he always comes back." Jade: "It sounds like he cares about you a lot." Sera: "Yes. Even when we argue, I know he would do anything to protect me. He may not always show it in the way others expect, but he has always looked out for me. That\'s just who he is." Jade: "No wonder you miss home so much. It sounds like you two have a very special bond." Sera: "Altan is full of memories of him. The palace, the festivals, the mountains... even the food we grew up with together. It\'s not just a place. It\'s the people I love, and the life we shared." Thinking about her brother, and all that she has left behind, Sera feels even more certain that she wants to return to Altan, not because of a crisis, but because she genuinely misses her family and the place that has always been part of her.',
  art:'Pages show: Sera and Jade talking, flashbacks of Sera as a child with her brother (brown tousled hair, gold-and-white robe), the brother on a horse with a falcon overhead, and a sunset palace. The brother is not named on this page. \'He always comes back\' is the setup for ch241.',
  quote:'"He disappears for weeks with barely a message... But he always comes back." — Sera',
  events:['Jade asks about Sera\'s brother; Sera describes a companion more than a prince', 'He is a year or two older, brilliant and impulsive, who loves adventure, horses and falcons', 'He sneaked her out of the palace to see the gardens, the river and the spring blossoms', 'He disappears for weeks, visits remote villages, takes up causes the court dislikes, but always comes back', 'Even when they argue, she knows he would do anything to protect her', 'Altan is full of memories of him: the palace, the festivals, the mountains, the food'],
  purpose:['Establish Sera\'s brother before he goes missing', 'Make the reader fear for him'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Princess Who Left (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sera\'s brother'},
 239:{ title:'Toward Altan', type:'Story Chapter — the party sets sail for Altan', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Levi and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With preparations complete, Jade\'s party agrees to accompany Sera back to Altan. The journey will take them through familiar waters and new territories, as they head toward the kingdom that has always been part of Sera\'s heart. Sera: "Thank you... for coming with me. It will mean a lot to have all of you there." Jade: "Of course we\'re coming. You\'re part of this party. Besides, I want to see your homeland too. There\'s probably so much we can learn: people, customs, and maybe even new leads." Devon: "Altan is an important kingdom. It will be useful for our investigations to understand their current situation and political alliances. And you shouldn\'t be travelling alone." Sky: "I\'ll go too. It\'s a new place. There might be useful information... and good food." The scout: "It\'s a good chance to scout the route and check surrounding areas as well. I\'ll make sure we\'re prepared for any potential risks along the way." Sera: "Thank you. Truly. Having all of you with me makes this feel less like leaving Tribute, and more like returning home together." The route into Altan becomes available. The party reviews maps, gathers supplies, and finalizes their plans before departure. NEW ROUTE UNLOCKED: Altan Route. New Region: Altan Kingdom. Travel route available. New locations, quests, and people. Continue your journey. The party prepares for the journey, arranging supplies, contacts, and any documents that may be useful in Altan. The route will take them across familiar waters, then along the northern passage toward Altan. With everything in place, the party sets sail for Altan. A new journey begins, not just to a kingdom, but to the place that has always been part of Sera\'s story.',
  art:'Pages show: the party agreeing (Sera, Jade, Devon, Sky, an archer), the \'New Route Unlocked: Altan Route\' card over an Altan harbour city, a hand-drawn map showing a sea route from Tribute across open waters to the Altan Kingdom, a blue-sailed ship and the party at the rail at sunset. The route is by SEA (the game\'s Altan Route is a ship passage). Levi is not clearly shown: the archer is read as Rin; the roster for the journey follows the author\'s gameplay notes.',
  quote:'"Having all of you with me makes this feel less like leaving Tribute, and more like returning home together." — Sera',
  events:['The party agrees to accompany Sera: Jade, Devon, Sky and the scout each give a reason', 'Devon: Altan is important for the investigations, and she should not travel alone', 'NEW ROUTE UNLOCKED: Altan Route: a new region, a travel route, new locations, quests and people', 'The party reviews maps and gathers supplies and documents', 'The route crosses familiar waters, then the northern passage toward Altan', 'The party sets sail'],
  purpose:['Open the Altan Route', 'Begin Arc X'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Toward Altan (4 objectives)', 'New route: the Altan Route (a sea passage)', 'New region: Altan Kingdom'],
  reward:'The Altan Route opens'},
 240:{ title:'The Border of Home', type:'Story Chapter — the party reaches the Altan border', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and the Altan border guards',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After days of travel, the party reaches the border of Altan. The familiar banner, architecture, and mountain air bring a wave of recognition, and a sense of home for Sera. Altan\'s border comes into view. The banners are familiar, and Sera recognises the crest from her childhood. As the party approaches, guards at the gate immediately notice Sera and hurry forward. Guards: "Your Highness! Welcome home! We are relieved to see you safe." Sera: "It\'s been a while. Thank you. Everyone looks well." "Your Highness, we were worried. The people of Altan are glad to see you return. Please allow us to escort you into the city." Sera: "Where is my brother? Is he at the palace?" "Your Highness... He... is not at the palace right now. He left some time ago on an official matter." Sera: "He left...? Where did he go?" "I\'m afraid we do not have the full details yet, Your Highness. We were instructed not to disclose his exact location at this time." Jade: "Let\'s head to the city first. We can ask for more information there." Sera: "Yes... I\'d like to see my mother and speak to the court. Perhaps they know more." The party: "We\'ll stay close and support you. If your brother is involved in something important, we\'ll help find out what it is. Until then, let\'s keep moving. It\'s safer to be in the city under Altan\'s protection." With an escort of Altan guards, the party crosses the border and makes their way toward the capital. Sera has returned home, but questions already hang in the air.',
  art:'Pages show: the white-stone border fortress under blue banners with a snowflake crest (see below), Altan guards in blue-and-silver armour (a bearded captain speaks), the party from behind, and the border gate with winged falcon-or-griffin statues. CREST: the banners carry a snowflake-like crest, ch241 shows a gold compass-star, and the Arc VI map gives Altan a golden bird crest: the Altan emblem is inconsistent across pages (the Falcon Banner is Sera\'s signature).',
  quote:'"Sera has returned home, but questions already hang in the air."',
  events:['After days of travel the party reaches the Altan border; Sera recognises the crest from her childhood', 'Guards at the gate hurry to greet her: "Welcome home!"', 'Sera asks for her brother: he left some time ago on an official matter; his location is not to be disclosed', 'The party resolves to go to the city first and ask the court', 'An escort of Altan guards takes them across the border toward the capital', 'Questions already hang in the air'],
  purpose:['Bring the party to Altan', 'Plant the first question about the brother'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Border of Home (4 objectives)', 'Altan: the border region opens to travel'],
  reward:'The party reaches the Altan border'},
 241:{ title:'The Prince Who Is Missing', type:'Story Chapter — Prince Rheon has vanished', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and the Altan royal household',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'At the palace, Sera learns that her older brother disappeared several days earlier while investigating strange activity near an old military road. The royal household has kept the disappearance quiet to avoid panic and political instability. The party is brought into Altan Palace, where they are welcomed by members of the royal household. Sera is escorted to meet with senior officials and trusted guards. Official: "Princess Seraphina. It has been too long. We are relieved to see you safe. Please forgive us for not sending word sooner. There have been... complications." Sera: "Where is my brother? I want to see him right away." "Your Highness... Prince Rheon has not returned. He set out several days ago on a discreet investigation and has not been heard from since." Sera: "Several days...? Why wasn\'t I told?" "The royal household has kept this quiet to avoid causing panic, and to prevent our enemies from taking advantage of the situation." Prince Rheon left around seven days ago with a small escort to investigate unusual movements near an old military road in the northern territory. There were reports of strange sightings (abnormal creatures) and signs of recent activity around an abandoned outpost. He found evidence that someone had recently passed through the old road, heading toward the mountains. His last message mentioned a hidden trail leading deeper into the mountain region. After that, all communication went silent. The royal guards have already sent search teams, but the terrain is dangerous, and the recent weather has made travel difficult. There are also political concerns: if news of the prince\'s disappearance spreads, it could trigger unrest among the nobles and neighbouring kingdoms. Sera: "My brother would never be careless... There must be a reason. I want to join the search." "Your Highness, we understand your feelings, but it is too dangerous for you to go yourself. For now, we ask that you remain in the palace while we gather more information." Jade: "We\'ll help you find him. We can look into the route, gather more information, and speak to the teams already searching the area. You\'re not alone in this." Devon: "Let\'s review the maps and reports first. We\'ll find out what happened and where he might have gone." Sky: "The old military road... There must be something there that drew him in." Rin: "We\'ll help uncover it." To be continued...',
  art:'Pages show: the throne-hall reception under blue-and-gold banners with a gold compass-star crest, the officials (an older white-bearded man and a bearded captain), the prince on the old military road in a dark travelling cloak (brown tousled hair), a misty ruin in the mountains, a map table, and the party (Jade, Devon, Sky, Rin, Sera) agreeing to help. The page ends \'To be continued...\'. The brother is named: PRINCE RHEON. First-pass: the Altan Capital stays closed until ch262; the chapter is played from the Border Garrison and the palace scenes are narrated.',
  quote:'"My brother would never be careless... There must be a reason." — Sera',
  events:['Sera is received at the Altan Palace and learns that Prince Rheon has not returned', 'He left about seven days ago with a small escort to investigate unusual movements near an old military road', 'Strange sightings: abnormal creatures and recent activity around an abandoned outpost', 'His last message mentioned a hidden trail leading deeper into the mountains; then silence', 'The household kept it quiet to avoid panic and to keep enemies from exploiting it', 'Search teams have been sent but the terrain and weather are against them', 'Jade: "You\'re not alone in this." The party takes up the search'],
  purpose:['Reveal that the prince is missing', 'Start the Missing Prince investigation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Prince Who Is Missing (5 objectives)', 'Quest: Find the Missing Altan Prince'],
  reward:'Prince Rheon is missing'},
 242:{ title:'Thank Goodness I Came Back', type:'Story Chapter — Sera takes charge', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and Altan officials',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'In the palace, Sera gathers everything they know about her brother\'s disappearance. She stays calm and asks practical questions. Jade immediately notices how much Sera has matured from the young princess Altan remembers. Sera meets with the royal household and trusted guards to hear the full report. Maps, written accounts, and collected evidence are laid out in the war room. Sera: "When was he last seen? Who travelled with him? Which route did he take? What supplies did he carry? What reports prompted this expedition? Show me the exact location again." On the map: Northern Military Road, Last Known Location, Abandoned Outpost. Prince Rheon left seven days ago with a small escort to investigate unusual movements near an old military road in the northern territory. They followed reports of strange sightings and signs of recent activity around an abandoned outpost. His last message mentioned a hidden trail leading deeper into the mountain region. After that, all communication went silent. He carried standard supplies for a short investigation: rations for a week, cold-weather equipment, and maps. Sera: "Thank goodness I came back. If I had stayed away any longer... There might have been even less information left." Jade sees immediately that Sera is no longer the sheltered young princess Altan remembers. She is calmer, more focused, and thinks like someone who has faced real dangers. Sera: "We should prepare as soon as possible. I want to go to the last known location and see for myself." Devon: "We\'ll review the reports in detail and plan the route. We\'ll make sure it\'s as safe as possible." Sky: "I\'ll check for any magical traces or remaining readings from his last message." Rin: "We\'ll prepare the equipment and be ready to depart once everything is in order."',
  art:'Pages show: the war room with the party, an Altan captain and officials around a map table; Sera\'s list of questions; the map with \'Northern Military Road\', \'Last Known Location\' and \'Abandoned Outpost\'; horse riders in the mountains; the prince\'s gear (a sword and rolled blankets). The silver-haired man at the end of the table in red-brown robes with a quiver is Rin.',
  quote:'"Thank goodness I came back." — Sera',
  events:['Sera hears the full report in the war room: maps, written accounts, collected evidence', 'She asks practical questions: when, who, which route, what supplies, which reports', 'The map: Northern Military Road, Last Known Location, Abandoned Outpost', 'The prince carried rations for a week, cold-weather equipment and maps', 'Jade sees how much Sera has matured: calmer, more focused, someone who has faced real dangers', 'Preparations begin: Devon plans the route, Sky checks for magical traces, Rin readies the equipment'],
  purpose:['Show Sera taking charge', 'Lay out the facts of the disappearance'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Thank Goodness I Came Back (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sera takes charge of the search'},
 243:{ title:'What Home Remembers', type:'Story Chapter — the old servants and the new Sera', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Levi, Rin and the Altan household',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The family reunion continues under the shadow of the missing prince. Old servants and officials still remember Sera as the younger royal sibling, but she is now the one coordinating the investigation. Servants: "Your Highness, welcome home! The palace has been prepared for you. Forgive our fervent welcome, Your Highness. We have missed you greatly." To them, she is still the little princess who used to run through these halls. "Princess Seraphina, when we heard you were back, we were so relieved. You were always such a bright and kind child." The old servants remember her warmth, her laughter, her younger self. Sera: "I\'m here to find my brother. When was he last seen? Who travelled with him? Which route did he take? What supplies did he carry? And what reports prompted this expedition?" Officials: "We... we have kept the matter quiet, Your Highness. The prince\'s disappearance is still under review. Revealing it now could create panic and political instability." The royal household chose silence, not just out of concern, but to protect the kingdom\'s stability. According to the reports, her brother was last seen several days ago, investigating strange activity near an old military road in the northern territory. "He was travelling with a small escort. They took the northern route, carrying basic supplies for a short expedition. The reports came from outlying villages: strange movements, and signs of something unnatural near the old road. He followed up on unusual signs and never returned." Sera listens carefully, asking precise questions, not just as a princess, but as someone who means to find the truth. Sera: "We\'ll check the last known location, review the caravan logs, and speak to the villagers again. I\'ll coordinate with the guards." And this is Princess Seraphina, the heir of Altan, who carries the weight of a kingdom\'s future. To the world, she is the missing prince\'s sister. This is Sera, the travelling companion, who sees, listens and acts. Jade: "She\'s changed... so much more mature than the princess I remember." To Jade, she is something more: a woman who has grown, who has learned to lead, and who is not afraid to fight for what she loves.',
  art:'Pages show: Sera welcomed by an old woman servant and officials in the palace hall (blue banners), an old servant remembering her, Altan officials and a captain explaining the silence, the prince riding with an escort, Sera speaking with a bearded official, and Jade at the end. Sera is called \'the heir of Altan\' here: ch238 and ch236 call her brother the crown prince, so \'heir\' is read as a title she carries beside him (flagged). Sera\'s hair is silver-white again.',
  quote:'"I\'m here to find my brother." — Sera',
  events:['Old servants welcome her home: to them she is still the little princess', 'Sera asks precise questions about the prince\'s last journey', 'The household chose silence, not just from concern but to protect the kingdom\'s stability', 'He was last seen several days ago on the northern route; the reports came from outlying villages', 'Sera will check the last known location, review the caravan logs, and speak to the villagers again', '"To the world, she is the missing prince\'s sister. To Jade, she is a woman who has grown, who has learned to lead."'],
  purpose:['Show how Altan sees Sera and how she has changed', 'Confirm the facts of the disappearance'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: What Home Remembers (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sera leads the investigation'},
 244:{ title:'A Message from Tribute', type:'Story Chapter — Sera reads Greyson\'s letter three times', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera and an Altan official',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'A formal message arrives from Tribute, welcoming Sera home and expressing concern over the missing Altan prince. Sera rereads the message far longer than necessary. Jade notices. A formal message from Tribute arrives at the Altan Palace. Official: "This is a message from the King of Tribute, Princess Seraphina." Sera: "Thank you. I\'ll read it in private." The message conveys a warm welcome, concern for the missing prince, and continued support between the two kingdoms. Sera reads the message once. Then a second time. And again, slower this time. Jade notices. Sera: "His words are always so thoughtful... Even now, with so many concerns of his own, he still remembers to send this... ...He worries about my brother. He always thinks of others first. Just as I remembered... It has been a long time. But his letter still feels the same: steady, reassuring... I\'m glad he\'s well." Jade: "Sera... you\'ve read that at least three times already. Are you going to keep reading it all night?" Sera: "Ah...! I... I just wanted to make sure I didn\'t miss anything important. It\'s been a while since I received news from him." Jade: "I know. It\'s nice that he thinks of you. You looked really happy while reading it." Sera: "...Yes... His letters have always had a way of making me feel calmer. He\'s always so busy, yet he still took the time to write to me... It means a lot." For the first time, it is clear that Sera\'s feelings for the King of Tribute are more than simple admiration.',
  art:'Pages show: a letter with a purple-blue Tribute seal, an official handing it to Sera, Sera reading it three times in three panels, Jade (red) noticing, and Sera with the letter in a library. The letter\'s sender is \'the King of Tribute\' (Greyson). This is the first time her feeling for him is shown: the hidden flags are set here.',
  quote:'"His letters have always had a way of making me feel calmer." — Sera',
  events:['A formal message from the King of Tribute arrives: a warm welcome, concern for the missing prince, continued support between the kingdoms', 'Sera reads it once, then a second time, then again, slower', 'Jade notices: "You\'ve read that at least three times already."', 'Sera: "His letters have always had a way of making me feel calmer."', 'For the first time it is clear that Sera\'s feelings for the King of Tribute are more than simple admiration'],
  purpose:['Show Sera\'s feelings for Greyson without a romance meter'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Message from Tribute (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sera\'s feelings are shown'},
 245:{ title:'Gold in Her Hair', type:'Story Chapter — an elder recognises the mark of the inheritance', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Rin and an Altan elder',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'While reviewing old family and military records connected to her brother\'s route, an Altan elder recognizes Sera\'s golden hair as the mark of an awakened royal martial inheritance. Sera and the party review old records related to the route her brother took. Ancient maps, patrol logs, and reports are brought out from the royal archives. Elder: "Hmm... Let me see this earlier patrol log." Then: "Princess Seraphina... Your hair... may I take a closer look for a moment?" Sera: "?... Of course." Elder: "Yes. This is remarkable. Your hair has a distinctive golden hue. This is the mark of an awakened royal martial inheritance. Only those of the Altan bloodline directly connected to the royal line usually manifest this when their inner power awakens." In the older records, the royal line is described as bearing "golden hair and the light of the martial spirit" when their abilities truly awaken. "It is rare. Not every royal ever reaches this stage." Sera: "I see... So this means my abilities... have awakened? I always thought it was just something unique about my hair." Elder: "It also means you carry the responsibility of the royal martial line, Your Highness. Your brother most likely awakened earlier than you, but your own awakening suggests that the line remains strong. This may be relevant to the strange activity near the old military road. There could be a connection to ancient Altan sites and past seal activity." Jade: "Sera... this explains so many things. You\'ve always been strong, but I didn\'t realize you carried so much more." For Jade, this is a clear sign of how much Sera has grown, not just as a travelling companion, but as Princess Seraphina of Altan.',
  art:'Pages show: the archive table with Jade, Devon, Sera (now golden-haired), an elder with round spectacles and a white beard, Sky and Rin; a close look at her hair; an old drawing of a golden-haired royal figure. HAIR: Sera is golden here, silver-white on pages 236-244: the resting state is golden per this chapter and ch246. Her awakening is the one first shown at ch161 (the white battle hair); the game keeps 161 as the awakening and this chapter and the next explain it.',
  quote:'"Your hair has a distinctive golden hue. This is the mark of an awakened royal martial inheritance." — the Altan elder',
  events:['Sera and the party review old records connected to her brother\'s route', 'An Altan elder asks to look closely at her hair: it has a distinctive golden hue', 'The mark of an awakened royal martial inheritance; only the Altan royal bloodline usually manifests it', 'The old records describe the royal line bearing "golden hair and the light of the martial spirit" when their abilities truly awaken', 'Her brother most likely awakened earlier than she did', 'It may be connected to the strange activity on the old military road: ancient Altan sites and past seal activity'],
  purpose:['Explain Sera\'s golden hair', 'Link the inheritance to the prince\'s disappearance'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Gold in Her Hair (4 objectives)', 'Quest: Legacy of the Golden Falcon'],
  reward:'Sera\'s inheritance is recognised'},
 246:{ title:'The Falcon Lineage', type:'Story Chapter — the three states of the Falcon inheritance', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border and the palace (played from the Border Garrison)',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Devon, Sky, Rin and the Altan elder',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Altan records explain Sera\'s transformation: dark brown was her dormant state, gold is her awakened resting state, and white appears when she channels the Falcon inheritance fully in battle. The royal archives contain detailed records of the Falcon Lineage, a rare martial inheritance within Altan\'s royal bloodline. Elder: "The Falcon Lineage appears only in royal bloodlines, and it rarely awakens in full. Your Highness, your transformation follows the same pattern recorded in these texts." THE THREE STATES OF THE FALCON INHERITANCE. Dormant State (dark brown hair): before awakening, the royal martial bloodline remains dormant; hair appears dark brown, like other Altan royals. Awakened State (golden hair): when the inheritance awakens, the hair turns gold as the new resting state; this signifies that the royal martial spirit is active within the body. Full Manifestation (white hair): when channeling the Falcon inheritance in battle, the hair turns white; this is the state of complete manifestation and maximum power. The Falcon represents clarity, protection, and far-sighted vision. It is both a symbol of royal duty and a reminder that the ruler must see beyond the immediate horizon. Sera: "So my hair changing colour isn\'t just a magical effect... it\'s a sign that the inheritance has truly awakened. I didn\'t understand what was happening before, but the records explain it clearly..." The records also note that the Falcon inheritance often grants enhanced perception, instinct, and agility, especially in times of danger. However, it can be physically and mentally demanding, and must be trained and controlled over time. Sera: "No wonder it feels different now... It\'s not just my appearance, my senses, my reactions, even my strength... they\'ve changed too." Elder: "The inheritance is a gift, Your Highness, but also a responsibility. It connects you to your ancestors, and to the royal martial line that has protected Altan for generations. The fact that it has awakened now may not be a coincidence, especially with the current dangers." Sera: "So this is who I am now... not just the princess they remember from before. I need to learn how to control this properly... for my brother, for my family, and for Altan." Sera realizes that the change in her hair is more than just a visual transformation. It marks her growth from a sheltered princess into the rightful heir of the Falcon Lineage, and someone who must now stand and act for her kingdom.',
  art:'Pages show: the archive with the party and the elder, a three-panel table \'The Three States of the Falcon Inheritance\' (dark brown, golden, white hair) beside a falcon drawing, a sketch of a robed figure with a falcon, and Sera in golden hair. THE KEY CANON: dark brown = dormant (before the awakening), gold = awakened resting state, white = full manifestation while channeling in battle. First-pass reading in the game: the awakening is the one at ch161 (white in battle, golden at rest); the dormant dark-brown portrait has no art yet; from the full-control chapter (257) white is only shown while channeling.',
  quote:'"Dormant: dark brown. Awakened: golden. Full manifestation: white."',
  events:['Altan\'s royal archives hold detailed records of the Falcon Lineage, a rare martial inheritance', 'Dormant State: dark brown hair, before awakening, like other Altan royals', 'Awakened State: golden hair, the new resting state: the royal martial spirit is active', 'Full Manifestation: white hair when channeling the Falcon inheritance in battle: maximum power', 'The Falcon: clarity, protection and far-sighted vision, a symbol of royal duty', 'The inheritance grants perception, instinct and agility, but must be trained and controlled over time', 'Sera: "I need to learn how to control this properly... for my brother, for my family, and for Altan."'],
  purpose:['Explain Sera\'s three hair states', 'Set up her training and the awakening quest'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Falcon Lineage (5 objectives)', 'Lore: The Falcon Lineage and the three states'],
  reward:'The Falcon Lineage explained'},
 247:{ title:'The Banner Before the Crown', type:'Story Chapter — the Falcon inheritance as a battlefield tradition', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border garrison',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The Falcon inheritance is revealed as a battlefield tradition associated with leaders, formation breakers, and protectors of Altan\'s military routes. The missing prince\'s expedition may have unknowingly crossed into territory historically associated with that lineage. Altan\'s royal archives hold detailed records of the Falcon Lineage, not just as a bloodline, but as a battlefield tradition passed down through generations of royal leaders and their chosen heirs. Elder: "The Falcon Lineage has always been tied to more than royalty. It is a martial tradition. Those who bore its mark were expected to lead, break enemy formations, and protect Altan\'s military routes." The Falcon standard was carried by those who opened the way: leaders who could see beyond the immediate battlefield and secure the routes that kept Altan alive. They were formation breakers, route guardians, and protectors of the realm. Historical records mark certain regions as "Falcon Terrains": remote mountain roads, ancient watch routes, and old outposts used in past generations. These areas are known for unstable terrain, strange energy, and reports of unusual activity. The missing prince\'s expedition followed an old military road that passes through one such territory. It is possible that they unknowingly crossed into an area historically associated with the Falcon Lineage. Those of the Falcon Lineage were often sent to the most dangerous regions, where their vision, intuition and instincts could detect threats others might miss. Many did not return. Their names remain in Altan\'s war records as both heroes and warnings. Sera: "So it isn\'t just a royal symbol... It\'s a responsibility that comes with the power to lead, protect, and make difficult decisions." Elder: "That is why your brother\'s route concerns us. The area he entered has a long and complicated history. There are old reports of unusual phenomena, disappearances, and signs of lingering power related to the Falcon Terrains." Sera: "So he may have encountered something connected to the Falcon heritage... And if that\'s true, this is not a simple investigation. It\'s something much larger than we expected." The Falcon inheritance is a source of pride for Altan, but it is also a path of duty, danger and sacrifice. The missing prince\'s expedition may have walked straight into its legacy.',
  art:'Pages show: Sera (golden hair) and the Altan elder at the archive table, a blue Falcon standard over a marching army, the \'Falcon Terrains\' map with the prince\'s route in red, a falcon drawing over a battle scene. Sera\'s hair is golden here (resting state).',
  quote:'"It is a responsibility that comes with the power to lead, protect, and make difficult decisions." — Sera',
  events:['The Falcon Lineage is a battlefield tradition: leaders, formation breakers, protectors of military routes', 'The Falcon standard was carried by those who opened the way', 'Certain regions are marked "Falcon Terrains": remote mountain roads, ancient watch routes, old outposts', 'The prince\'s expedition followed an old road through one such territory', 'Those of the Falcon Lineage were sent to the most dangerous regions; many did not return', 'The area has old reports of unusual phenomena and disappearances'],
  purpose:['Tie the missing prince to Altan\'s history', 'Frame the Falcon inheritance as duty and sacrifice'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Banner Before the Crown (4 objectives)', 'Lore: Falcon Terrains'],
  reward:'The Falcon Terrains'},
 248:{ title:'The Last Known Route', type:'Story Chapter — reconstructing the prince\'s movements', loc:'🦅 Altan: the border garrison',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and the party reconstruct the prince\'s last known movements. His original mission was legitimate: conflicting reports had come from an old military road, and he personally went to verify them rather than send soldiers somewhere he would not go himself. Jade: "These reports came from an old military road used in past generations. They were serious enough for the prince to see with his own eyes. He didn\'t send soldiers. He went himself to verify the truth. This was not a reckless journey. It was a deliberate investigation." On the map: Altan Keep, Last confirmed camp, Old Military Road (Falcon Route), Disputed Region (reports of unusual activity). Conflicting reports had come from an old military road used in past generations. Recent travellers and scouts described strange activity, but the accounts were inconsistent and difficult to verify. Rather than send soldiers into unfamiliar danger, the prince chose to go himself to confirm the truth. Sera: "That makes sense... It would explain why he wanted to come personally." Levi: "If he travelled lightly, with only a small party, he could have been ambushed, or followed without knowing." Sky: "The accounts from travellers are too different. Some describe strange lights. Some heard unusual sounds. And a few reported seeing people who didn\'t match any known faction." Devon: "There\'s also the question of who would benefit from spreading conflicting reports. It feels intentional, like someone wanted to draw him there, or hide what\'s really happening." The old military road was an important route for Altan\'s military routes and trade. It has been used for generations and is now less travelled, with many stretches damaged by time, landslides and past conflicts. His small party travelled lightly, planning to meet local scouts and check several key locations along the road. The prince\'s notes showed several key locations he planned to check, including an old outpost, a collapsed bridge and a disused watchtower. Jade: "We should also look into the conflicting reports: who sent them, who met him along the way, and what exactly they saw." Sera: "Something doesn\'t add up. The prince would have noticed if it were nothing. He isn\'t the type to ignore a clear danger sign." Levi: "We need to check the last camp, the side routes, and any nearby ruins. If they were following the old Falcon Route, there may be hidden paths that are only recorded in older maps." The prince\'s final recorded movements lead deeper into the mountain road, toward a region with a long history, unsettled reports, and a connection to the Falcon Lineage.',
  art:'Pages show: the party (Jade, Sera golden, Levi in green with a quiver, Sky, Devon) at the map table; a parchment map \'Reconstructing the Prince\'s Last Known Route\' (Altan Keep, last confirmed camp, Old Military Road (Falcon Route), Disputed Region); a ruined bridge-viaduct and a small party on horseback; the prince\'s notes (old outpost, collapsed bridge, disused watchtower). The man in purple at the right is Devon, the man in green is Levi.',
  quote:'"This was not a reckless journey. It was a deliberate investigation." — Jade',
  events:['The prince\'s mission was legitimate: conflicting reports from an old military road', 'He chose to verify them himself rather than send soldiers into unfamiliar danger', 'The map: Altan Keep, last confirmed camp, the Falcon Route, the Disputed Region', 'Devon: someone may be spreading conflicting reports to draw him there, or hide the truth', 'His notes listed an old outpost, a collapsed bridge and a disused watchtower', 'The final movements lead toward a region tied to the Falcon Lineage'],
  purpose:['Show the prince\'s mission was deliberate', 'Plan the search'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Last Known Route (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The prince\'s last known route'},
 249:{ title:'Tracks Beyond the Pass', type:'Story Chapter — following the prince\'s trail', loc:'🦅 Altan: the old military road',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party leaves the capital and follows the prince\'s trail. Levi reads physical tracks, Sky checks signs of injury or corruption, and Jade reconstructs the expedition from abandoned camps and broken equipment. The party departs from the capital, following the route the prince took. Levi: "The tracks are recent... This is the prince\'s party. Multiple riders, with pack animals." Levi reads the physical tracks, identifying the number of riders, the direction of travel, and when they passed. Sky: "There are signs of injury here. Someone was bleeding. The trail also shows traces of unnatural corruption..." Sera: "Based on the distance and the state of the camp, they were here about two days ago. They were moving faster than usual." They find the first abandoned camp. Tents are hastily dismantled, equipment left behind, and signs of a sudden departure. Devon: "This equipment wasn\'t abandoned carelessly. It looks deliberately broken... as if they didn\'t want it to be used." Jade: "This matches the prince\'s banner. But why would they leave it behind?" Among the remains, they find personal items, a damaged satchel, and a blood-stained cloth bearing the prince\'s crest. Sky: "The blood is old, but there are traces of corruption mixed in. Someone here was wounded by something unnatural." The trail continues beyond the pass, through a narrow mountain road known for landslides and past conflicts. The terrain becomes more dangerous, with signs of recent rockfalls and unnatural disturbances. Jade: "They didn\'t turn back here. They continued into the mountains. So whatever they discovered ahead was important enough that the prince kept going, despite the risks. Let\'s follow the trail. We may be close to learning what happened."',
  art:'Pages show: the party on horseback leaving the capital under blue-gold falcon banners; Levi reading hoofprints; Sky at a blood-stained trail; the abandoned camp with a falcon banner and a broken weapon; a satchel with a gold crest and a blood-stained cloth; the narrow mountain road. The roles in the game\'s investigations (Levi tracks, Sky residue, Jade reconstructs) are shown directly on the page.',
  quote:'"They didn\'t turn back here. They continued into the mountains." — Jade',
  events:['The party leaves the capital following the prince\'s route', 'Levi reads the tracks: multiple riders with pack animals, recent', 'Sky: signs of injury, with traces of unnatural corruption', 'The first abandoned camp: hastily dismantled, equipment deliberately broken', 'They find a satchel and a blood-stained cloth bearing the prince\'s crest', 'The trail continues beyond the pass, through dangerous terrain'],
  purpose:['Show the party\'s investigation roles', 'Find the first camp'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Tracks Beyond the Pass (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The trail beyond the pass'},
 250:{ title:'Beneath the Fallen Banner', type:'Story Chapter — the surviving escort', loc:'🦅 Altan: the old military road',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party discovers surviving members of the prince\'s escort. They reveal that the prince deliberately drew a supernatural threat away from his soldiers, allowing several of them to escape. He is missing because he protected them, not because he acted foolishly. Following the trail, the party finds a ruined campsite: torn banners, broken equipment, and signs of a violent attack. But they are not alone. Several members of the prince\'s escort are still alive. Escort: "We wouldn\'t be here if it wasn\'t for the prince. When the attack happened, he ordered us to fall back. He stayed behind to draw the creature away. He knew we couldn\'t all escape if we stayed. Someone had to hold it off... and he chose to be that person." Jade: "So this wasn\'t reckless... He made a deliberate decision." Sera: "He protected them..." Levi: "The tracks and battle signs match what they\'re saying." Sky: "Look at the ground here. There are signs of a non-human presence. The damage isn\'t from bandits or ordinary monsters. This was something else." Devon: "He covered their retreat route. You can see it here: the equipment was destroyed to slow pursuit. This was planned, not a chaotic flight." The prince left clear signs that he bought time for his soldiers to escape: destroyed supplies, fallen banners, and a false trail leading in the opposite direction. A soldier: "He told us to run... He said the kingdom still needed us." Sera: "The prince always puts others first. This is just like him." Levi: "If he drew the threat away, he must have gone deeper into the mountains." Sky: "We need to find out what kind of creature this is, and where it might be hiding now." Devon: "There may still be a chance to reach him, if we can follow the signs and avoid walking into the same trap." The survivors\' accounts confirm that the prince is not acting foolishly. He is missing because he chose to protect his soldiers and draw the supernatural threat away from them. The trail leads deeper into the mountains, toward a region where the land itself feels wrong, and the presence of something ancient and dangerous grows stronger.',
  art:'Pages show: a ruined camp under torn blue falcon banners with the party; wounded escort soldiers (bandaged) around a fire; the party reacting; the fallen falcon banner, with a soldier saying \'He told us to run\'; the party around a map; a mountain valley with a faint blue glow. The title says \'Beneath the Fallen Bamer\' (a typo for Banner): the game uses \'Banner\'. \'Surviving escort\' matches the game\'s quest step.',
  quote:'"He told us to run... He said the kingdom still needed us." — a soldier of the escort',
  events:['A ruined campsite: torn banners, broken equipment, signs of a violent attack', 'Several members of the prince\'s escort are alive', 'The prince ordered a retreat and stayed behind to draw the creature away', 'Sky: signs of a non-human presence; Levi: the tracks match their account', 'Devon: the retreat was planned: equipment destroyed to slow pursuit, a false trail laid', 'The prince is missing because he protected his soldiers'],
  purpose:['Find the surviving escort', 'Show why the prince is missing'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Beneath the Fallen Banner (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The surviving escort'},
 251:{ title:'The Prince in the Mountain', type:'Story Chapter — Rheon is found behind an ancient barrier', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party finds Sera\'s older brother alive but injured, trapped, or isolated behind an ancient barrier. Sera reaches him first. Their reunion is affectionate, relieved, and immediately argumentative in a very sibling-like way. Following the trail, the party reaches a secluded mountain region sealed by an ancient barrier. Behind it, they find someone alive. Sera immediately recognizes her brother\'s presence. Against everyone\'s warning, she pushes forward. Sera: "Rheon...! You\'re alive... You\'re really alive..." Rheon: "Sera... You found me." Sera: "Are you insane?! Do you have any idea how worried we were? You just disappeared without a word and ended up like this?!" Rheon: "I knew you would come eventually. And look: you did. Still as fiery as ever. I drew the threat here so it wouldn\'t reach the others. They needed to escape. I couldn\'t let my soldiers die for my sake. It wasn\'t foolish. It was my responsibility as their prince." Sera: "You always take everything on yourself... You haven\'t changed at all. But you should have trusted us. We would have come sooner if we knew." Rheon: "Would you? Knowing you, you\'d probably get yourself killed trying. And you... are still as reckless as ever... But I\'m glad you came." Jade: "Even after everything, he still chose to protect his soldiers first." Levi: "It explains why the trail suddenly ended here." Rheon is alive, but injured and trapped behind the ancient barrier. The party prepares to help him and find a way to break the seal. The reunion brings both relief and new questions. Rheon\'s presence confirms that the prince deliberately led the threat here. But the ancient barrier, his injuries, and the lingering danger mean their journey is far from over.',
  art:'Pages show: the party at the barrier (blue glowing sigils and an arched ruin), Sera embracing a long silver-white-haired man with golden eyes and a black-and-white robe: PRINCE RHEON is silver-haired (not the brown-haired young man in the earlier flashbacks of ch238). The reunion, the party watching, and the barrier at sunset. FLAG: Rheon\'s hair is white here and brown in the childhood flashbacks of 238 and in the 241 page: the white hair is read as the Falcon Lineage full-manifestation (his own awakening), as the elder says he awakened earlier.',
  quote:'"It wasn\'t foolish. It was my responsibility as their prince." — Rheon',
  events:['The party reaches a secluded mountain region sealed by an ancient barrier', 'Behind it they find someone alive: Sera recognises her brother and pushes forward', 'Rheon: "I drew the threat here so it wouldn\'t reach the others. It was my responsibility as their prince."', 'Sera scolds him; he teases her: "Still as fiery as ever"', 'Rheon is alive, injured and trapped behind the barrier', 'The party prepares to find a way to break the seal'],
  purpose:['Reunite Sera and Rheon', 'Make Rheon a temporary guest'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Prince in the Mountain (5 objectives)', 'Guest: Prince Rheon (temporary, never a recruit)'],
  reward:'Prince Rheon is found'},
 252:{ title:'You Are Supposed to Be Older', type:'Story Chapter — Sera scolds her brother', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'After the rescue, Sera scolds her brother for personally chasing danger. He insists the Crown Prince could not order soldiers into a place he was unwilling to enter himself. Sera replies that this principle does not require vanishing for four days. Their relationship becomes clear: he is technically the older sibling, but Sera is often the more mature one. After breaking the ancient barrier, the party rescues Rheon and makes camp to allow him to rest and recover from his injuries. Rheon is injured and exhausted, but otherwise stable. Sera: "You\'re supposed to be older! Who vanishes for days without a single message?!" Rheon: "I had no time to send word. Once I followed the trail, things moved faster than expected." Sera: "You could have died! Do you have any idea how worried I was? You left us with nothing but rumours and a trail of broken camps!" Rheon: "If I hadn\'t gone, more soldiers might have been sent in blindly. The Crown Prince cannot order others into a place he is unwilling to enter himself. It was a legitimate investigation. The reports from this region were serious: unusual activity and disappearances. I needed to see it with my own eyes. I wouldn\'t ask others to face a danger I wasn\'t willing to face myself." Sera: "Your principle doesn\'t require you to vanish for four days. You could have sent someone... a signal... something. You always think about everyone else, but you never think about how your actions affect us." Rheon: "I do think about you. That\'s why I pushed deeper. If the threat had reached the main route, it would have harmed more people... And I knew you would scold me no matter what. So I might as well give you a reason worth scolding me for." Jade: "So the famous principled prince still gets scolded by his little sister." Levi: "Some things never change, no matter how many people you protect." Sky: "It suits you. You look better alive and scolded than missing and chased." Devon: "She\'s right, though. Try leaving a message next time. Even heroes can use a little common sense." Sera: "...You\'re still reckless." Rheon: "And you\'re still worrying too much. That\'s what siblings are for, I suppose." Their reunion makes one thing clear: Rheon is technically the older sibling, but Sera is often the more mature one, keeping him grounded even as he chases danger. The evidence they found confirms that the prince deliberately drew the supernatural threat away from his soldiers, protecting them at great personal risk.',
  art:'Pages show: the camp by the ruins at dusk with the party and Rheon (silver-white hair, a bandaged cheek); Sera scolding him; the party teasing; a ruined tower and the prince\'s blood-stained crest. The page calls Rheon \'the Crown Prince\' once: consistent with ch236 and 238.',
  quote:'"You\'re supposed to be older!" — Sera',
  events:['After breaking the barrier the party rescues Rheon and makes camp', 'Rheon is injured and exhausted, but otherwise stable', 'Sera scolds him: "Who vanishes for days without a single message?!"', 'Rheon: the Crown Prince cannot order others into a place he is unwilling to enter himself', 'Sera: his principle does not require vanishing for four days', 'Rheon is technically the older sibling, but Sera is often the more mature one'],
  purpose:['Show the siblings\' relationship', 'Confirm the prince\'s sacrifice'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: You Are Supposed to Be Older (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The siblings reunited'},
 253:{ title:'What Followed Him Home', type:'Story Chapter — the threat is older than the expedition', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Rescuing the prince reveals that the threat near the old road is larger than expected. His expedition did not cause it; it exposed something Altan had forgotten or sealed away. With the prince safe, the party examines the area more closely and sees the full scale of what lies beyond the old road. Jade: "This is bigger than we expected." Rheon: "My expedition did not cause this. We only exposed what was already here." Sky: "These traces aren\'t recent. They are old, and deep. Something has been moving again." Levi: "The corruption here is not like ordinary monsters. It feels sealed... and now it\'s breaking." Sera: "Look at these symbols. They match the records of an old seal mentioned in Altan\'s archives. It shouldn\'t have reawakened." The old road leads to a site that was sealed away generations ago. The prince\'s expedition uncovered signs that the seal is weakening. Jade: "So this is why you came here... You weren\'t reckless." Rheon: "I came because I needed to know the truth. If something this dangerous is stirring, we cannot afford to remain ignorant." Sky: "This threat is larger than a single expedition. It could affect the whole region if the seal fails." They sense a presence: ancient, powerful, and not fully awakened, but clearly no longer dormant. Devon: "The prince\'s actions gave us something far more important than a simple report. It gave us a warning." Sera: "Which means this is only the beginning. We need to tell the king... and prepare for what comes next." The prince\'s journey did not create the threat; it revealed it. What lies beyond the old road is larger, older, and more dangerous than anyone realized. Something long forgotten in Altan is stirring once more, and its awakening may have consequences far beyond this mountain road.',
  art:'Pages show: the party and Rheon (silver-white hair, from behind) looking down on a night ruin with a glowing blue seal; Sera holding a record with matching symbols; a circular seal in the stone; a purple tentacled shadow over the ruins under a full moon. The title says \'What Followed Him Home\' but nothing follows him home on the page: the title is read as the threat that has followed him out of the old road. \'Tell the king\' is read as Altan\'s king, not Greyson (flagged).',
  quote:'"The prince\'s journey did not create the threat; it revealed it."',
  events:['The threat is bigger than expected; Rheon\'s expedition only exposed what was already there', 'Sky: the traces are old and deep; something has been moving again', 'Levi: the corruption feels sealed, and now it is breaking', 'Sera: the symbols match an old seal in Altan\'s archives; it should not have reawakened', 'The old road leads to a site sealed away generations ago; the seal is weakening', 'A presence: ancient, powerful, not fully awakened, but no longer dormant'],
  purpose:['Reveal the threat as older than the expedition', 'Set up the closed pass'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: What Followed Him Home (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'The seal is weakening'},
 254:{ title:'The Closed Pass', type:'Story Chapter — the lost regiment and the unfinished duty', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party investigates why the route was abandoned and discovers records of an old Altan regiment tied to the Falcon lineage and an unfinished military duty. Following the trail, the party reaches the old mountain pass, once a key military route. Now, it lies in ruins, its gates sealed and its watchtowers destroyed. The symbols here match those in Altan\'s old military records: the Falcon lineage. Sera: "These are records from an old Altan regiment. They operated along this pass, under the Falcon banner." Levi: "Their movements match the terrain. They were stationed here to monitor activity beyond the pass." The regiment was assigned a long-term duty to seal and contain something beyond the pass. But the records end abruptly. Jade: "There\'s no record of their final mission. Just a note that the route was closed shortly after." Sky: "This wasn\'t a simple abandonment. Someone made a deliberate decision to seal the pass, and then never returned to complete it." Rheon: "The language here suggests the duty was unfinished. They managed to contain something, but it was not fully dealt with before the regiment disappeared." Levi: "These notes mention an unnatural presence beyond the pass. Not just monsters, but something older. It aligns with what we\'ve encountered on this route." Devon: "The prince\'s expedition exposed this again. He didn\'t create the threat; he uncovered it. The old seal is weakening, and whatever lies beyond is becoming active." Sera: "This explains why the land beyond the pass feels different. The seal was never complete. The threat was only contained, not ended." Among the ruins, they find a final inscription: a promise left by the regiment that their duty would be completed, even if they fell. Jade: "The Falcon lineage has guarded this place for generations. If the duty remains unfinished, then the threat is still here, and now it is moving again." The closed pass is not just a forgotten route. It is a warning, and a duty that was left unfinished. What lies beyond the old walls may be waking, and its return could affect not only Altan, but the entire region.',
  art:'Pages show: the ruined mountain gate with a falcon banner, the party (Rheon in a white cloak among them); an old regiment record with a black falcon; a stone plaque with a falcon and a glowing pink mark; the gate with falcon statues under a stormy sky. A bandaged-looking white head near the right is Rheon. The \'lost regiment\' matches the game\'s quest \'Legacy of the Golden Falcon\'.',
  quote:'"The closed pass is not just a forgotten route. It is a warning, and a duty that was left unfinished."',
  events:['The old mountain pass: once a key military route, now in ruins, gates sealed, watchtowers destroyed', 'The symbols match the Falcon lineage; records of an old Altan regiment under the Falcon banner', 'The regiment was assigned a long-term duty to seal and contain something beyond the pass', 'The records end abruptly; the duty was unfinished', 'The seal was never complete: the threat was contained, not ended', 'A final inscription: a promise that their duty would be completed, even if they fell'],
  purpose:['Reveal the lost regiment', 'Tie the Falcon lineage to the unfinished duty'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Closed Pass (4 objectives)', 'Lore: The Lost Regiment (expanded)'],
  reward:'The lost regiment\'s unfinished duty'},
 255:{ title:'A Princess Among Soldiers', type:'Story Chapter — Sera takes command', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Sera takes command around Altan officers with surprising ease. Her brother sees clearly how much travelling has changed her. Jade also realizes that Sera understands both royal command and actual field conditions better than many palace officers. At the temporary camp, Altan officers gather to discuss the next steps. Sera speaks with confidence, gaining their attention immediately. Sera: "We need to secure the eastern ridge first. Place scouts here and here. The old watchtowers can still be used if we clear the approach. Our priority is to prevent further movement from below the pass. Not every sign is a monster; some are natural collapses, but they line up with the same source. We cannot split our forces too thin. Maintain a main defensive line here, with a smaller team to investigate the sealed structures. I will lead the scouting unit myself." Rheon: "You\'ve changed, little sister. You used to avoid command meetings. Now look at you, giving orders like a seasoned general." Sera: "Someone has to, when half of you think rank alone is enough to solve everything. I\'m still the same. I just stopped waiting for others to do what needs to be done." Rheon: "You\'re still as sharp as ever. But now you\'re also far more practical. The road has been good to you." Jade: "Sera understands both the chain of command and what actually happens in the field. She speaks the language of the palace, but she also knows what the land, the soldiers, and the supplies can handle." Sera: "The world is different when you travel it. You see what works, what doesn\'t, and who people really are." Levi: "It shows. You lead naturally, because you understand people, not just protocol. That makes all the difference." Sky: "The officers respect you, not just because you\'re the prince\'s sister, but because you know what you\'re talking about." Devon: "Many palace-born nobles have never set foot on a real battlefield, yet they argue as if they know more than the people who have. Sera bridges that gap." Officer: "Understood, Your Highness. We will prepare the units as you\'ve instructed." Sera: "Good. We move at first light. Make sure the scouts rest and check their supplies. We can\'t afford mistakes on this route." Sera\'s ability to command and understand the realities of the field earns the respect of the Altan officers. To Rheon, she is still his younger sister, but now he sees the capable woman she has become. To Jade and the rest of the party, Sera\'s strength lies in her rare balance of royal insight and practical experience, making her a true leader both in title and in action.',
  art:'Pages show: the Altan camp with blue-gold banners, Sera (here with dark brown hair and a red robe: see below) leading Altan officers at a map table, Rheon (white hair), Jade (red), Levi, Sky, Devon; Sera\'s golden-haired self appears in the reaction panels. HAIR: in the command panels Sera is drawn with dark brown hair and a red outfit, in the reaction panels golden: the author\'s \'dormant, golden, white\' states make the brown a flashback to her dormant state or an art slip: flagged for the cleaning pass.',
  quote:'"I just stopped waiting for others to do what needs to be done." — Sera',
  events:['At the temporary camp, Altan officers gather; Sera speaks with confidence', 'Her plan: secure the eastern ridge, scouts, a main defensive line, a smaller team for the sealed structures', 'Rheon: "You used to avoid command meetings. Now look at you."', 'Jade: Sera understands both royal command and field conditions', 'Devon: Sera bridges the gap between palace-born nobles and the people who have fought', 'Sera earns the respect of the Altan officers'],
  purpose:['Show Sera as a leader', 'Prepare for the decisive battle'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Princess Among Soldiers (4 objectives)'],
  reward:'Sera takes command'},
 256:{ title:'The Thing Beyond the Pass', type:'Story Chapter — an ancient battlefield phenomenon', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'The party identifies the buried supernatural threat: an ancient battlefield phenomenon, sealed entity, or forgotten regional danger tied specifically to Altan\'s history. Beyond the closed pass, the party descends into the ruins and discovers the true nature of what lies here: an ancient battlefield, where something was sealed long ago. The ruins contain records of a great battle from Altan\'s early history, an army that never returned, and a power that had to be sealed beneath the pass. Sera: "This matches the Falcon lineage records. It wasn\'t just a battle. It was a containment. They sealed something here, using the battlefield itself." Jade: "The land itself remembers. That\'s why the route became unusable. It isn\'t a natural disaster. Something is still here." Rheon: "The prince\'s expedition did not create this. He disturbed the seals, and whatever is bound here began to stir. It explains the attacks, the corruption, and why the prince was targeted." Sky: "This is an ancient phenomenon: a residual battlefield manifestation, or a sealed entity. It feeds on unresolved conflict. The more attention it receives, the stronger it becomes." Levi: "The seals are failing. If this spreads beyond the pass, it won\'t just affect Altan. It could destabilize the entire region." Devon: "The old Altan regiment was tasked with containing this. Their duty was never completed. That is why the records end abruptly and the route was abandoned." What lies beyond the pass is not just a monster, but the lingering will of a long-dead battlefield: a presence born from war, grief, and unfinished duty. Sera: "So this is what my brother encountered... It wasn\'t just an attack. It was trying to draw him in, to use him. No wonder it separated him from the others." The party confirms that the threat is an ancient battlefield phenomenon, tied directly to Altan\'s history and the Falcon lineage. The seals are weakening, and the route will continue to draw attention unless the root cause is dealt with. Whatever lies beyond the pass is still awake, and it will not remain contained for long.',
  art:'Pages show: the party descending into blue-lit ruins before a giant falcon-banner gate; a carved relief of a great battle; the party reading; a dark giant figure of armoured soldiers among spears. The threat\'s visual is a \'lingering will\' of a battlefield (shadowy colossus with spears): the game\'s boss is \'The Threat Beyond the Pass\' and now has this identity.',
  quote:'"What lies beyond the pass is the lingering will of a long-dead battlefield: a presence born from war, grief, and unfinished duty."',
  events:['Beyond the closed pass the party finds an ancient battlefield where something was sealed long ago', 'The ruins record a great battle: an army that never returned, a power sealed beneath the pass', 'It was a containment, not just a battle: they sealed something using the battlefield itself', 'Sky: a residual battlefield manifestation that feeds on unresolved conflict', 'The seals are failing and the threat could destabilise the entire region', 'The regiment\'s duty was never completed', 'It tried to draw the prince in, to use him'],
  purpose:['Identify the buried threat', 'Set up the decisive battle'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: The Thing Beyond the Pass (4 objectives)', 'Boss identity: the battlefield\'s lingering will'],
  reward:'The threat is identified'},
 257:{ title:'White as Warfire', type:'Story Chapter — Sera\'s full Falcon battle-channelling', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'During the decisive battle, Sera enters full Falcon battle-channeling. Her hair turns white and her awakened combat state is formally established. Her brother participates, but Sera receives the decisive combat spotlight. When the ancient presence fully reveals itself, the buried battlefield stirs, and the sky turns white with Falcon light. Sera: "I am Altan\'s Falcon! This battlefield is not forgotten, and neither are its dead!" Sera\'s Falcon battle-channeling awakens fully, her hair turning white as the power of Altan flows through her. Rheon: "Sera... You\'ve grown so much. But don\'t push yourself too far. You\'re not just a weapon, you\'re my sister." Sera: "I know! And that is why I will finish this!" Jade: "She truly understands both royal command and the realities of the field. Sera is not just a princess. She fights like someone who has lived the truth beyond the palace." Together, Sera and Rheon hold the line, but it is Sera who breaks the enemy\'s core and turns the tide. White as warfire, the Falcon rises, and the buried threat, long sealed, is finally driven back. Sky: "That\'s... the Falcon lineage in its true form." Levi: "No wonder the regiment sealed this place. This isn\'t a normal enemy." Rheon: "You were always strong, but now... you\'re something else entirely." Sera: "I\'m still Sera. Just... a Sera who will not let Altan\'s past swallow its future. We end this here."',
  art:'Pages show: the party before the ancient presence (a purple tentacled mass under a dark sky), Sera in white hair with a glowing sabre and a spectral white falcon, Rheon and Jade reacting, the line held with white wings, and Sera speaking to the party. Sera is white-haired here, as the elders said white is the state of complete manifestation. This is the game\'s chapter 257: Falcon Banner: Awakened and the white-hair battle state.',
  quote:'"I am Altan\'s Falcon! This battlefield is not forgotten, and neither are its dead!" — Sera',
  events:['When the ancient presence fully reveals itself, the buried battlefield stirs and the sky turns white with Falcon light', 'Sera enters full Falcon battle-channelling: her hair turns white', 'Rheon: "You\'re not just a weapon, you\'re my sister."', 'Together Sera and Rheon hold the line, but Sera breaks the enemy\'s core and turns the tide', 'The buried threat, long sealed, is driven back', 'Sera: "A Sera who will not let Altan\'s past swallow its future. We end this here."'],
  purpose:['Show Sera\'s full Falcon manifestation', 'Establish her awakened combat state'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: White as Warfire (5 objectives)', 'Sera: Falcon Banner: Awakened and the white-hair battle state', 'Boss: The Threat Beyond the Pass'],
  reward:'Sera\'s full Falcon manifestation'},
 258:{ title:'A Place at Two Tables', type:'Story Chapter — Sera and Rheon speak privately', loc:'🦅 Altan: the mountain pass',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'Sera and her brother speak privately. He finally accepts that she is no longer merely the younger princess who left home. She belongs both to Altan and to Jade\'s travelling party. After the battle, the camp is quieter. The immediate threat has been driven back, and Altan\'s soldiers begin their recovery. Sera: "You look much better. I\'m glad you\'re really here." Rheon: "It seems my reckless little sister can still worry after all. You\'ve always had a sharp tongue." Sera: "You almost had me fighting a mountain alone. Do you know how angry I was?" Rheon: "I do. And I deserve it. I wanted to draw the threat away from my men. If I had not gone, more would have died." Sera: "I understand why you did it. But you cannot keep disappearing, Brother. Altan needs you, and so do the people who travel with me." Rheon: "You\'re right. You are no longer the younger princess who stays behind. You have seen the world, and you have become someone yourself." Sera: "I am still Altan\'s princess. But I also have a place with Jade and the others. I don\'t want to choose between the two." Rheon: "You don\'t have to. Altan will always be your home. But you also belong where you are needed. That includes Jade\'s party." Sera: "Thank you... for finally seeing me as an equal. I\'ll still listen when you worry. Just don\'t be reckless again, okay?" Rheon: "I\'ll try. On one condition. You promise to come home sometimes." Sera: "I promise. Altan will always have a chair for me. And Jade\'s party will keep a chair too." Sera\'s path does not end at the palace, nor does it end on the road. She now has a place at two tables, and both are part of who she is. For the first time, there is no distance between who Sera was and who she is now. A princess of Altan. A trusted companion on the road. And someone who finally belongs in both worlds.',
  art:'Pages show: Sera (golden) and Rheon (pale silver hair, a black-and-white robe) by a campfire at night under blue falcon banners, talking in close-ups, and a final sunset overlooking a valley. Rheon\'s hair reads pale silver-blond in the close-ups. The title says \'two tables\': Altan and Jade\'s party.',
  quote:'"Altan will always have a chair for me. And Jade\'s party will keep a chair too." — Sera',
  events:['After the battle the camp is quieter; the immediate threat is driven back', 'Sera: "You cannot keep disappearing, Brother. Altan needs you, and so do the people who travel with me."', 'Rheon: "You are no longer the younger princess who stays behind."', 'Sera: "I don\'t want to choose between the two." Rheon: "You don\'t have to."', 'Rheon\'s condition: she promises to come home sometimes', 'She now has a place at two tables'],
  purpose:['Settle Sera\'s belonging to both Altan and the party', 'End the Altan arc\'s main investigation'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: A Place at Two Tables (4 objectives)', 'Sera: a place in Altan and in the party'],
  reward:'Sera belongs in both worlds'},
 259:{ title:'Jade\'s Excellent Idea', type:'Story Chapter — matchmaking failure #1', loc:'🏯 Tribute: the Imperial Palace',
  chars:['jade', 'seraphina', 'devon', 'sky', 'levi'], charsNote:'Jade, Sera, Levi, Sky, Devon and Rin',
  introduced:[],
  sum:'With the prince safely home, Jade decides Sera should personally thank Greyson for his concern. Reluctantly, Sera makes a formal visit to meet Greyson at the palace. Jade: "You should go and thank Greyson in person. He was genuinely worried about you." Sera: "Do I have to? I\'ll just send a message instead..." Greyson: "Princess Sera. Your safe return is a great relief to me. Tribute is grateful for your efforts." Sera: "Thank you, Your Majesty. I appreciate your concern. It was a dangerous situation, but my party is safe now. Thank you for thinking of us." Greyson: "Your presence and support are important to Altan. I trust you will continue to work closely with my council when necessary." Jade: "That went well, didn\'t it? He seems pleased." Later, Sera receives Greyson\'s response: an extremely formal diplomatic message. It is copied to several officials. "To Her Highness Princess Sera Altan, On behalf of the Crown, we acknowledge your safe return and commend your efforts during the recent incident. Tribute is grateful for your efforts. We look forward to continued cooperation for the stability and prosperity of both our realms. King Greyson. Cc: Imperial Council, Foreign Affairs Office, Royal Archives, Military Command, Trade Bureau, Northern Provinces Administration, Altan Embassy to Tribute." Sera: "...He copied... the entire council? This is more formal than a trade agreement." Jade: "Ah... Matchmaking failure #1." Sera: "That is not what I was hoping for..."',
  art:'Pages show: Jade and Sera in the Altan hall (blue falcon banners), Sera meeting Greyson (crowned, black-and-gold dragon robes) in the Tribute palace, a formal letter with a gold double-headed bird seal and a long Cc list, and the three of them reacting. The page is titled and set at the Tribute palace; Sera\'s hair is golden. \'Matchmaking failure #1\' is the first entry of Jade\'s Matchmaking Record. The hidden-flag gameplay plan calls this the \'Private Report Disaster\'.',
  quote:'"Ah... Matchmaking failure #1." — Jade',
  events:['With the prince home, Jade decides Sera should thank Greyson in person', 'Sera: "Do I have to? I\'ll just send a message instead..."', 'A formal audience with Greyson: he is correct and warm, but formal', 'Greyson\'s reply is an extremely formal diplomatic message, copied to the whole council', 'Sera: "This is more formal than a trade agreement."', 'Jade: "Matchmaking failure #1."'],
  purpose:['Start the matchmaking gag', 'Show Greyson\'s formality'],
  unlocks:['Main Story Quest: Jade\'s Excellent Idea (4 objectives)', 'Jade\'s Matchmaking Record: failure #1'],
  reward:'Matchmaking failure #1'},
};
